185	2	@@mMaze - Dead End (east branch)@@N	The eastern passage dead-ends at a wall covered in frenzied carvings.\nSomeone spent a great deal of time here, judging by the depth and\nrepetition of the marks. The carvings appear to be a person slowly\nlosing their sanity in documented stages. The final carving is simply\na pair of eyes, over and over, across the entire wall.\n	8201	11
186	2	@@mMaze - The Whispering Alcove@@N	A small side alcove where the whispers are louder than anywhere else.\nIf you stand here for a moment and focus, you can begin to make out\ndistinct voices giving directions. Unfortunately, several of the voices\nare giving contradictory advice, and at least two of them are clearly\ntrying to lead you in circles.\n	8201	11
187	2	@@mMaze - Western Branch@@N	The western passage splits here. A faint smell of something burned - but\nstrangely sweet - comes from the north. From the south, a rhythmic\nscratching sound can be heard. Both passages look identical in every\nother respect.\n	8201	11
188	2	@@mMaze - The Scorched Room@@N	The source of the burned smell: a chamber where some magical explosion\ntook place long ago. The walls are blasted smooth and the floor is\nfused glass. Charred remnants of what might have been furniture or\nbodies are fused into the glass floor. A passage continues south.\n	8201	11
189	2	@@mMaze - Dead End (north of scorched)@@N	The passage ends abruptly here at a sealed door. The door bears no\nhandle, no keyhole, and no visible means of opening. It is simply\na wall of featureless black metal. Knocking on it produces no sound -\nthe metal absorbs the impact completely, producing not even a vibration.\n	8201	11
190	2	@@mMaze - The Clawed Crossing@@N	The floor here is covered in parallel scratch marks, as if something\nmassive and clawed paced back and forth across this point repeatedly.\nThe grooves are deep enough to catch your foot. Passages lead north,\neast, and west. The western passage smells of blood.\n	8201	11
191	2	@@mMaze - Dead End (blood scent)@@N	The blood scent leads here, to a chamber that clearly served as a lair\nfor something predatory. Bones of various creatures - some of them\nhumanoid - are scattered across the floor. Whatever lived here has moved\non, but not long ago.\n	8201	11
192	2	@@mMaze - The Doubled Passage@@N	This passage appears identical to one you've seen before, but subtle\ndifferences hint that it is not. The scratches on the wall are in\nslightly different positions. The dust has been recently disturbed in\npatterns that suggest careful, deliberate movement.\n	8201	11
193	2	@@mMaze - The Heart of the Labyrinth@@N	You have reached what feels like the center of the maze. The whispers\nhere are almost loud enough to be speech. A single phrase repeats:\n'Remember why you came.' The walls here are clean, unmarked - as if\nnothing dared to touch them. Three passages lead away, each perfectly\nidentical to the others.\n	8201	11
194	2	@@mMaze - The False Exit@@N	This passage seems to lead upward and the air freshens slightly, giving\nfalse hope of escape. But the passage curves and descends again, eventually\nrejoining the maze at a point you've already visited. Several sets of\ndesperate footprints have run this route before you, and the turning-back\nmarks are always at the same point.\n	8201	11
195	2	@@mMaze - Dead End (the pit)@@N	The western passage ends at a pit in the floor, roughly circular and\nabout two meters across. Looking down, you cannot see the bottom. Faint\nlight - greenish and cold - rises from below. The pit makes a sound like\nbreathing.\n	8201	11
196	2	@@mMaze - The Second False Hope@@N	The air freshens even more here, and for a moment the whispers stop entirely.\nThen they return louder than ever, and the passage dead-ends at a blank wall\nbearing a single message: 'There is no shortcut. Only through.'\n	8201	11
197	2	@@mMaze - The Narrowing@@N	The passage narrows here until you must turn sideways to pass. The walls\npress close and the whispering becomes intense - dozens of voices all speaking\nsimultaneously in your ears. The floor is covered in handprints, as if\nprevious travelers crawled this section.\n	8201	11
198	2	@@mMaze - After the Narrowing@@N	Beyond the narrow passage, the corridor opens again. The air is colder\nand the obsidian walls here seem different - slightly transparent, and\nwithin them you can see vague shapes moving. Whether they are reflections\nof the present or visions of the past is impossible to tell.\n	8201	11
199	2	@@mMaze - Dead End (the visions)@@N	The passage ends at a wall that is completely transparent - a window into\nanother place. Beyond it, you see a vast hall filled with the shades of an\narmy, standing at attention before an empty throne. They face the throne\nwith absolute devotion, waiting for a ruler who will never return. They\ncannot see you.\n	8201	11
200	2	@@mMaze - The Crossroads@@N	A four-way junction in the deepest part of the labyrinth. Marks on the\nfloor indicate that hundreds of travelers have stood here before, most\nof them choosing the same directions. The north passage looks fresher,\nless worn. The south passage has been worn smooth by the most footfalls.\n	8201	11
201	2	@@mMaze - Dead End (the most traveled)@@N	The most-traveled path leads here. A chamber full of desperate graffiti\n- names, pleas, curses, prayers. In the center of the room stands a\nmirror that shows not the room itself but instead shows the crossroads\njunction. At least, it shows where you need to go.\n	8201	11
202	2	@@mMaze - The Fresh Passage@@N	The less-traveled northern path. The air here is slightly less stale\nand there are fewer footprints. Whether this indicates it leads somewhere\nnew or simply that fewer reached this far is unclear. A faint light can\nbe seen somewhere ahead to the north.\n	8201	11
203	2	@@mMaze - Dead End (the western spiral)@@N	The western passage spirals inward in a tight coil, bringing you back\nto a point you cannot connect to anywhere else. The spiral itself is\na puzzle of sorts - standing at its center and looking outward, you\ncan see an alignment of symbols on the walls that makes a complete\nsentence. It reads: 'The exit lies where fewer dare to walk.'\n	8201	11
207	2	@@mMaze - The Light at the End@@N	The source of the faint light: a door of black iron, set with a single\nluminous stone of pale blue. The door is locked, but the keyhole is\nshaped like an obsidian shard - as if made for a very specific key.\nBeyond this door, you sense open space and the presence of something\nvery old and very powerful.\n	8201	11
212	2	@@mThe Threshold of the Sanctum@@N	Passing through the iron door, you find yourself in a vast antechamber\nof polished black marble. Your reflection looks back at you from every\nsurface, but each reflection is slightly different - showing you with\ndifferent expressions, wearing different things, or in different poses.\nNone of them quite match what you are actually doing. The air here\ncarries real weight, pressing against you from all sides.\n	8201	11
213	2	@@mThe Corridor of Souls@@N	This corridor is lined with niches, each containing a crystalline container\nthe size of a fist. Inside each container floats a faint light - a\ncaptured soul. The containers number in the hundreds, perhaps thousands.\nEach one bears a name plate. The corridor stretches on ahead for what\nseems like an impossible distance given the size of the structure.\n	8201	11
214	2	@@mThe Hall of Void Studies@@N	Bookshelves of blackened metal line this circular chamber, bearing\nvolumes bound in material you prefer not to identify. Many are chained\nto their shelves. In the center, a lectern holds an open book in which\ntext writes itself - forming observations about the room and its occupants,\nwhich currently includes you.\n	8201	11
215	2	@@mThe Chamber of the Dark Puzzle@@N	A large chamber with a complex mechanical device in its center - a three-\ndimensional puzzle of interlocking void-stone rings, each engraved with\nsymbols. The rings must be aligned in the correct configuration to open\nthe door to the inner sanctum. The door itself is a slab of pure void-\nstone, seamlessly fitted into the wall to the north.\n	8201	11
216	2	@@mThe Overseer's Balcony@@N	A balcony of black stone overlooking an impossibly large chamber below.\nFrom here, the full scale of the inner sanctum becomes apparent - it\nis several stories tall and wide, its ceiling lost in shadow. Below, you\ncan see movement - figures walking in patterns too regular to be random.\nThey haven't noticed you yet.\n	8201	11
217	2	@@yThe Guard Post@@N	A fortified position carved into the corridor wall where it widens.\nArrow slits pierce the outer wall, and the narrow bottleneck forces\nvisitors to pass through a chokepoint. The guards that once manned\nthis post are gone, but the mechanisms they operated - iron gates\nthat can drop to seal the passage - remain functional.\n	8205	11
218	2	@@mThe Inner Sanctum Gate@@N	A wide landing before the innermost doors of Kel'Shadra. The doors\nthemselves are not locked - they stand open, as if inviting entry.\nOr as if something beyond them is not concerned with keeping you out.\nTorches of void-fire flank the entrance, their black flames producing\nlight that seems to make shadows deeper rather than banishing them.\n	8201	11
219	2	@@yThe Throne Room Approach@@N	A grand processional corridor leading to the throne room. The floor\nhere is a mosaic of black and deep purple tiles depicting a battle:\nmortal forces being consumed by a vast darkness that the tile-work\nrenders in breathtaking, terrible detail. On the far side of this\ncorridor, two massive doors stand sealed.\n	8205	11
220	2	@@mThe Throne Room of Void@@N	The throne room of Kel'Shadra is vast and terrible. A throne of solid\ndarkness sits upon a dais at the room's far end - not a throne of dark\nstone or metal, but a throne made of crystallized void itself. Floating\nabove it, a crown of black light hovers without support. The ceiling\nhere appears to be looking back at you - thousands of void-eyes staring\nfrom the stone above.\n	8201	11
221	2	@@mThe Sanctum Archive@@N	A side chamber off the throne room housing the most dangerous knowledge\nin Kel'Shadra. Texts sealed within barriers of void-light, accessible\nonly to those who understand the nature of the void. Several barriers\nhave been broken in the past, their contents removed - by whom, for what\npurpose, no one living knows.\n	8201	11
222	2	@@mThe Preparation Hall@@N	A chamber where Kel'Shadra's chosen prepare for battle. Weapon racks of\nvoid-stone line the walls, and training dummies made from crystallized\ndark matter stand in rows. Several of the dummies appear to have been\nrecently used - their surfaces bear fresh damage.\n	8205	11
223	2	@@yThe Chamber Below@@N	The vast chamber visible from the balcony above. From ground level, the\nscale is even more intimidating. The void priests' ritual patterns become\nclear: they are tracing lines of power that converge on a single point\nat the room's center - a circular sigil of incredible complexity\ninscribed directly into the floor.\n	8205	11
224	2	@@mThe Sanctum Gallery@@N	A long gallery connecting the archive to the chamber below. The walls\nhere are bare stone that has been burned smooth by incredible heat or\ncold at some point in the past. Abstract shapes have formed in the\nstone's surface - shapes that gain meaning only when viewed from\nspecific angles.\n	8201	11
225	2	@@pThe Binding Circle@@N	At the absolute center of Kel'Shadra's power. The sigil here is fully\nvisible - a circle of void-runes forty feet across, glowing with restrained\npower. The air inside the circle shimmers and distorts, and through the\ndistortion you can see something vast and dark pressing against reality\nitself. This is where Kel'Shadra is imprisoned. This is where it waits.\n	8201	11
226	2	@@yThe Ritual Antechamber@@N	Directly adjacent to the binding circle, this room serves as a staging\narea for the maintenance rituals. Spell components of dark power are\nstored here, along with detailed instructions in several languages for\nmaintaining the binding. The instructions assume the reader has ten\nto fifteen years of void-magic training as a baseline.\n	8205	11
227	2	@@yThe Path of Manifestation@@N	A corridor leading to the binding circle that vibrates with contained\nenergy. The floor here glows faintly with the overflow of power from\nthe sigil. Walking this corridor, you feel the entity's consciousness\npressing against the edges of your mind - not attacking, just... noticing.\n	8205	11
232	2	@@pThe Presence Chamber@@N	This is as close as you can come to the direct presence of Kel'Shadra\nwithout entering the binding circle itself. The entity is aware of you\nhere - the walls pulse with its attention, and the shadows cast no\nshapes that match the room's contents. Something vast and ancient is\nlooking at you from the other side of a very thin barrier.\n	8201	11
233	2	@@yThe Final Approach@@N	The last passage before confronting Kel'Shadra's physical manifestation.\nThe air here tears at your clothing and weapons and flesh, not from wind\nbut from the sheer reality-distortion caused by the entity's proximity.\nLight bends visibly. Sound arrives before and after it should. Time\nitself seems unreliable in this corridor.\n	8205	11
237	2	@@eThe Void Sanctum@@N	The ultimate chamber of Kel'Shadra - a space that exists at the\nintersection of material reality and the void. The floor is solid but\nthe walls and ceiling are pure darkness from which forms constantly\nemerge and dissolve. Standing at the center is the physical manifestation\nof Kel'Shadra itself: a towering figure of crystallized void energy,\nwatching your approach with the absolute calm of something that has never\ndoubted its own victory.\nThis is the final battle.\n	8205	11
242	2	@@pThe Chamber of Reflection@@N	A hidden chamber accessible only to those who correctly solved the\nfrozen puzzle in the Frost Sanctum. The chamber is perfectly circular\nand perfectly silent. At its center, a void-fire burns in a stone\nbrazier, illuminating items left by previous challengers who did not\nsurvive their attempt on Kel'Shadra.\n	8205	11
