243	2	@@mThe Sorcerer's Refuge@@N	A hidden room that can only be found by those who paid attention to\nall the environmental clues throughout the citadel. Once a private\nstudy of a sorcerer who served Kel'Shadra before realizing his mistake,\nthis room contains research notes, personal items, and most crucially,\ntactical advice for confronting the void entity. The shelves along the\nwalls are crammed with journals written in increasingly erratic script,\nchronicling the sorcerer's growing horror at what he had helped create.\nA desk in the corner bears a final unfinished letter addressed to no one.\n	8201	11
244	2	@@mThe Memory Pool@@N	A perfectly circular pool of dark water in a hidden alcove. Those who\ndrink from it experience a vivid vision - not of the past, but of the\nmost important moment in their own future. The vision is accurate but\nmay be difficult to interpret. The pool has one cost: a small portion\nof the drinker's life force, permanently given.\n	8201	11
245	2	@@dThe Catacomb Descent@@N	A staircase of cracked black stone descends steeply from the northern\nhall into the earth below Kel'Shadra. The walls narrow as you go deeper,\nand the air grows heavy with the smell of ancient death. Phosphorescent\nmoss provides a sickly blue-green light along the lower steps. Below,\nyou can hear the distant echo of something moving in the dark.\n	8201	11
246	2	@@dThe Upper Catacomb Hall@@N	The catacombs open into a wide vaulted hall whose ceiling is lost in\ndarkness. Niches carved into every wall hold the remains of Kel'Shadra's\nearliest servants - not merely their bones, but their preserved bodies\nstill wearing the armor and vestments they died in. Their eyes are dark,\nbut they feel aware. A long corridor runs deeper into the complex.\n	8201	11
247	2	@@dThe Bone Road@@N	A long passage running deeper into the catacomb complex. The floor here\nis made not of stone but of compressed bones - countless remains that\nhave been ground flat and fused together by decades of foot traffic and\nvoid energy. The passage is wide enough for three to walk abreast and\nruns straight south without deviation or branch.\n	8201	11
248	2	@@dThe Preparation Chamber@@N	Here the dead were prepared before being placed in their niches. Stone\ntables still bear dark stains, and the tools used in preservation\nrituals hang on the walls in neat rows. The tools are sized for\ncreatures much larger than humans. A locked door in the east wall\nbears a symbol of an open eye surrounded by radiating lines.\n	8201	11
