1576	8	@@aInlet Lower Hall@@N	The lower hall is the most spacious section of the cave system at this depth â a wide, irregular chamber with a floor of flat water-smoothed limestone and a ceiling studded with stalactites in various stages of growth.  @@WThe temperature@@N is noticeably cooler here than at the surface.  The acoustic properties of the hall are remarkable â sounds echo in a way that makes whispers audible from one end to the other.  A narrow ledge runs along the east wall at shoulder height, too regular to be natural, suggesting it may have been improved by hand.\n	9	11
