1581	8	@@aInlet Lower Hall East Recess@@N	An east recess off the lower hall contains a feature that has attracted scholars â a series of marks on the wall that are not natural.  @@WThe marks@@N are arranged in rows: circles, lines, and a few more complex symbols.  Their purpose is debated.  They may be ancient tally marks, astronomical notation, or something else entirely.  They have been carefully traced and copied by several parties, and the copies exist in archives in both @@yKiess@@N and @@BMidgaard@@N.  The marks themselves are undisturbed.\n	9	11
