1585	8	@@aInlet Cave Stream Source@@N	The stream source is a pool that wells from the cave floor in the deepest accessible part of the north cave, its water rising through a crack in the limestone from a pressurized aquifer below.  @@WThe water is very cold@@N and perfectly clear, the welling motion visible at the center of the pool where the upwelling keeps the sediment in motion.  This is the source of the stream that runs through the cave in high water, and its existence is the reason the cave has its particular character â water-sculpted, cold, and mineral-clean.\n	9	11
