2244	12	@@lSpring Vent Chamber@@N	@@lThe spring vent chamber east of the Wyrm's antechamber is where one of the three original Deepwell Confluence springs rises â a natural spring vent in the limestone floor that predates all human presence at the oasis, the original source of the water that made the Great Oasis possible.@@N @@lThe spring vent is active.@@N @@aWater rises through the vent continuously, cold and mineral-clear, bubbling up into the chamber and overflowing into the main aquifer channel through a natural sill.@@N @@lThe vent's activity is maintained by the Wyrm's presence: the creature regularly clears the vent of mineral sediment that would otherwise seal it over time,@@N using its body to displace the deposits that accumulate at the spring's emergence point. The clearing is not deliberate stewardship â the Wyrm uses the vent as a temperature reference point and clears it incidentally as it moves through the chamber. The spring does not know or care about the creature's motivation. It simply flows, as it has always flowed, keeping the oasis alive from below.\n	24584	11
2245	12	@@lPre-Lair Approach@@N	@@lThe approach passage south of the alcove narrows and descends sharply,@@N the aquifer channel cutting deeper into the natural limestone as it approaches the Wyrm's primary lair zone. @@lThe walls here carry the densest concentration of physical evidence of the creature's presence:@@N mineral scrape marks overlap in layers, the oldest worn nearly smooth and the newest still showing the raw limestone beneath the removed deposit. The scale impressions in the passage floor are so numerous they cover every square arm-length of the sediment. The current is negligible here â the water is nearly still, suggesting the Wyrm's lair acts as a pressure sink that reduces the hydraulic gradient in the surrounding passages. @@lThe temperature drops another degree in this approach.@@N Something very large is close, and its presence has modified the local environment in ways the geology alone does not explain.\n	24584	11
2246	12	@@lTemperature Plunge Chamber@@N	@@lThe temperature here is the lowest in the entire flooded zone â a cold that reaches through wet clothing in seconds and numbs exposed skin within a minute.@@N @@lThe drop is abrupt: one step south through the passage constriction and the temperature falls sharply,@@N a thermocline marking the boundary of the Wyrm's direct influence on its immediate environment. The creature's body size means it displaces and circulates cold deep-aquifer water through the local environment more effectively than any natural mixing process would achieve. @@lMineral formations on the chamber's walls are elaborate here:@@N ice-like crystal growths in white and pale blue that have built up in the stable, cold conditions the Wyrm has maintained for its habitation period. The chamber itself is short but feels vast because of the silence and the cold â the aquifer sounds from above do not penetrate here. A deep, periodic vibration in the stone is the only sound: the Wyrm breathing, somewhere below.\n	24584	11
