2450	14	The Shattered Gate	The towering iron gates of Kel'Shadra lie shattered and bent, torn from their\nhinges by some ancient and terrible force. Beyond them yawns the darkness of\na crypt that has not seen living feet in centuries. The stonework is cracked\nand weeping with black moisture, and runes of binding have been forcibly\nbroken from the archway overhead. A faint, sickly phosphorescence clings to\nthe walls, just enough to reveal the horror of what lies ahead. The path\nsouth leads deeper into the crypts.\n	8201	11
2451	14	The Entry Hall of Lamentations	The entry hall stretches before you in grim grandeur, its vaulted ceiling\nlost in shadow above. Along the walls are carved bas-reliefs depicting the\nfinal moments of those who were sealed within -- faces frozen in expressions\nof absolute terror. The floor is cracked obsidian, polished by centuries of\ndark rituals. Iron sconces still hold black candles that burn with cold blue\nflame, though no mortal lit them. Exits lead north back to the gate, east\ninto a nave, west toward a vestibule, and south deeper into the complex.\n	8201	11
2452	14	The Western Vestibule	A small antechamber with three iron doors, each marked with a different\nsymbol: a spiral, a broken circle, and an eye. The doors are sealed with\nmechanisms of ancient brass and bone. The floor here is inscribed with a\nwarning in an archaic script. The exit east returns to the entry hall.\n	8201	11
2453	14	The Eastern Nave	A long hall that once served as the nave of a dark chapel. Rows of stone\npews face an altar of black glass at the far end. The pews are occupied\nby skeletal figures in rotted vestments, slumped in eternal congregation.\nCarved into the floor between the pews is a complex circular diagram --\na ritual seal that radiates a faint warmth, as though it still functions\nafter all this time. The exit west returns to the entry hall, and a door\nleads north.\n	8201	11
2454	14	The Dark Chancel	Beyond the nave, the chancel is a place of concentrated malevolence. The\nceiling here is painted with a mural of the night sky, but the stars are\nwrong -- arranged in patterns that suggest terrible geometries. A massive\nobsidian sarcophagus dominates the center of the room, its lid shifted\nslightly to one side, suggesting something crawled out long ago. Heavy chains\nare secured to the sarcophagus but they too have been broken. The path south\nleads back to the nave, and a passage descends down.\n	8201	11
2455	14	The Southern Corridor	A long corridor running south from the entry hall. The walls here are lined\nwith sealed niches, each containing a mummified corpse standing upright,\nwrapped in black linen and bound with silver wire. Their hollow eye sockets\nseem to track your movement. The floor is treacherous -- certain flagstones\nare pressure plates that trigger mechanisms in the walls. The corridor\ncontinues south and branches east.\n	8201	11
2456	14	The Ossuary Alcove	A wide alcove branching east from the southern corridor. The walls here\nare entirely composed of human bones, arranged with grotesque artistry --\npatterns of skulls and femurs interlocking in spiraling designs. At the\ncenter of the far wall is a large skull set into an iron frame. Its eye\nsockets glow with sickly green light. Beneath the skull is a recessed\ncompartment. The exit west returns to the southern corridor.\n	8201	11
2457	14	The Hall of Mirrors	The corridor opens into a wide hall lined with tall mirrors set in tarnished\nsilver frames. The mirrors do not show accurate reflections -- instead, each\none shows a different version of you: one covered in wounds, one standing\nvictorious over a heap of bones, one consumed by shadow, one simply absent,\nthe mirror showing only an empty room. The floor is marked with four symbols.\nYou may exit north back to the corridor or south.\n	8201	11
2458	14	The Chamber of Whispers	A perfectly circular chamber where the acoustics are supernatural. Any sound\nmade here is amplified and distorted, transformed into voices speaking in\nlanguages you do not know. The walls are covered in writing -- not carved but\nburned, as if by dark energy from within. At the center of the chamber is a\nstone pedestal with an indentation shaped like a hand. The exits are north\nand south, and a sealed door to the east.\n	8201	11
2459	14	The Puzzle Antechamber	A square room with four alcoves, each containing a stone statue depicting\none of the cardinal virtues corrupted: Courage shown as reckless slaughter,\nWisdom shown as manipulative scheming, Justice shown as cruel punishment,\nand Mercy shown as weakness. The statues hold objects -- a blade, a tome,\nscales, and an open hand respectively. The north exit is sealed with a\nmassive stone door covered in combination locks. An inscription above it reads\n'Only the one who understands corruption may pass.' The exit south returns to\nthe chamber of whispers.\n	8201	11
2460	14	The Gallery of the Fallen	A long gallery displaying portraits of those who founded the order of\nKel'Shadra, each framed in bone. As you walk past, their painted eyes\nseem to follow you with expressions of sorrow and warning. The floor here\nhas partially given way, and crossing it requires care -- some boards are\nmissing, revealing a darkness below that produces sounds of breathing. A\ndoor stands at the far south end, and the exit north returns to the antechamber.\n	8201	11
2560	16	Within the Public Dungeon of Midgaard.	You are standing within the Public Dungeon, sounds of the inmates deafen you.\n\n	1	11
2461	14	The Threshold of the Abyss	The grand entrance to the lower crypts -- a wide landing at the top of a\nmassive staircase descending into absolute darkness. The architecture here\nchanges: instead of stone, the walls are made of some dark, slightly warm\nmaterial that is not quite rock and not quite bone. The railing along the\nstaircase is carved from a single piece of shadow-iron, depicting writhing\nfigures. The exit north returns to the gallery, and the stairs descend.\n	8201	11
2462	14	The Antechamber of Darkness	The bottom of the great stair opens into an antechamber bathed in total\ndarkness, save for a ring of green-flamed torches that burn waist high.\nThe air here is thick and tastes of iron and old death. The walls press\nclose and the ceiling is very high, lost in shadow. You can feel things\nwatching you from beyond the torch-light. Exits lead up to the threshold,\nnorth into the labyrinth, east and west.\n	8201	11
2463	14	The Labyrinth Entrance	You stand at the entrance to the great labyrinth of Kel'Shadra. The walls\nof the maze rise twenty feet high, carved from volcanic stone worn smooth\nby ages of dark energy. The passages twist immediately in multiple directions,\ndesigned to confuse. Above the entrance arch, a warning is carved: 'The\nlabyrinth remembers all who enter. Not all of what it remembers is friendly.'\nExits lead south back to the antechamber and into the labyrinth north.\n	532489	11
2464	14	The Labyrinth - North Fork	The labyrinth branches here into three passages. The walls are marked with\nfaint scratches left by previous explorers, though many of the marks appear\nto lead in circles. The stone overhead is carved with a repeating motif of\neyes. This section of the maze has a faint sound of dripping water coming\nfrom somewhere to the east. Passages lead south, east, and west.\n	532489	11
2465	14	The Labyrinth - Eastern Passage	A narrow passage that widens slightly as it curves south. The right-hand\nwall is lined with iron spikes, some of which bear scraps of clothing.\nThe floor here is damp and the footing uncertain. The passage continues\neast and returns west.\n	532489	11
2466	14	The Labyrinth - Western Dead End	The western passage terminates in a wall that seems to have been built\nafter the labyrinth was constructed -- the stonework is different, newer,\nand the mortar shows signs of hasty application. Something was walled in\nhere. Faint scratching can be heard from the other side. The only exit\nis east.\n	532489	11
2467	14	The Labyrinth - The Crossroads	The dead center of the labyrinth -- a wider space where four passages meet.\nAt the center of this intersection is a stone column bearing a compass rose\ncarved in relief, but the cardinal directions are wrong: North is marked\n'Below', East is 'Within', South is 'Without', West is 'Above'. The column\nrotates very slowly under its own power. Passages lead north, south, east,\nand west.\n	532489	11
2468	14	The Labyrinth - The False Exit	A passage that seems to lead upward toward light -- but the light is false,\na phosphorescent patch of mold arranged to look like daylight. Beyond it,\nthe passage loops back on itself and deposits you back at the crossroads.\nA small alcove in the wall here contains a dusty skeleton whose hands are\nstill pressed flat against the wall, as though it died pushing futilely\nagainst solid stone. The exit south returns to the crossroads.\n	532489	11
2469	14	The Labyrinth - The Dark Pool	The eastern passage opens into a small chamber containing a black pool whose\nsurface is perfectly still and perfectly dark. The pool reflects nothing --\nnot even light touches its surface. Looking into it too long causes visual\ndistortion and a sensation of vertigo. The exit west returns to the crossroads,\nand a narrow ledge circles the pool to a door on the far side.\n	532489	11
2470	14	The Labyrinth - The Trap Corridor	The western passage is lined with mechanisms that are unfortunately quite\nvisible -- pressure plates in the floor, tripwires across the corridor, and\nsmall apertures in the walls that lead to some unseen mechanism. Either the\ntraps were never reset after previous victims triggered them, or this is\nmeant to make you feel safe. The passage continues west and east back to\nthe crossroads.\n	532489	11
2471	14	The Labyrinth - The Sentinel Room	A chamber at the western end of the labyrinth, guarded by ancient iron\nconstructs that now stand inert, their mechanisms long since failed. They\nare impressive nonetheless: eight feet tall, in the shape of armed knights,\nwith faces made of hammered iron beaten into expressions of grim menace.\nOne construct, in the far corner, may not be entirely inert -- its head\nmoves very slightly when you are not watching it directly. A door leads north\nand the exit east returns to the trap corridor.\n	532489	11
2472	14	The Labyrinth - The Lower Junction	The passage descends and opens into a junction room where the floors are\ncovered in a thin layer of grey dust, unmarked -- meaning nothing has passed\nhere recently. The junction connects several passages and a stairway leading\nfurther down. The exits are south back toward the sentinels, east toward the\npool chamber, west, and down.\n	532489	11
2473	14	The Labyrinth - The Echo Chamber	A roughly spherical chamber where sounds echo with impossible complexity,\ncreating layered harmonics. Speaking aloud here causes your own voice to\nbe returned in fragments over the course of several minutes, mixed with\nother voices that were here long before you. The chamber has no purpose\nthat is immediately apparent, but the echoes themselves seem to contain\ninformation. The exit east returns to the junction.\n	532489	11
2474	14	The Ritual Chamber of Binding	The end goal of those who built the labyrinth: a vast circular chamber with\na ritual circle of power that fills the entire floor, inscribed with thousands\nof runes. At the center stands an altar of pure black stone atop which rests\nan ancient tome sealed with seven locks. The power in this room is palpable\nand crushing. The air shimmers slightly, as though reality itself is under\nstrain here. The exit north returns to the antechamber below.\n	8205	11
