COPY public.help_entries (id, filename, level, keywords, body) FROM stdin;
1	poison_quinine	0	poison:quinine	Syntax: poison:quinine\n\nApplies quinine poison to your currently wielded weapon. Quinine has unique\neffects distinct from the other two weapon poisons (arsenic and nightshade).\nIt is one of three weapon poisons available to rogue-line characters\n(Cipher, Assassin, Warlock, Nightblade).\n\nEach poison interacts differently with rogue openers such as Backstab and\nCircle, producing additional effects on hit.\n\nRestrictions:\n  - Requires a weapon to be wielded.\n  - Must have the skill learned.\n\nSee also: shelp poison:quinine poison:arsenic poison:nightshade poison weapon backstab\n
2	west	0	west	Syntax: west\n\nMoves one room west, if an exit exists.\n
3	cage	1	cage	The cage spell is similar to seal room, but things CAN enter, just not leave.\n\n
4	blight_touch	0	blight touch	Your touch spreads a creeping blight, dealing poison damage and\nleaving a damage-over-time effect on the target.\nDruid spell. Uses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
5	put	0	put	Syntax: put <item> <container>\n\nPlaces an item into a container.\n
6	hide	0	hide	Syntax: hide\n\nAttempts to hide yourself from view.\n
7	ninth_descent	0	ninth descent	@@yNinth Descent@@W                                        Sentinel level 35\n\nSyntax: ninth descent\n\nEnter the focused perceptive state of the silence-court descent ritual.\nFor 4 combat rounds, each successful avoidance (dodge, parry, or block)\ngrants +2 testimony instead of +1. Measured Response procs during Ninth\nDescent also grant +2.\n\n@@yDetails:@@W\n  * Mana cost: 25 (roughly 25% of pool at level 35).\n  * Cooldown: 20 rounds.\n  * Can only be used while fighting.\n  * This is the Sentinel's burst window — pop it, survive 4 rounds of\n    incoming attacks, and reach high verdict tiers in half the time.\n\nNamed for the Khenari Doctrine of Ninth Descent — the nine-stage chant\nstructure of the silence-court ritual where each descent deepened perceptive\nacuity.\n\nSee also: @@mtestimony verdict sentinel@@W\n
8	loot	20	loot	Syntax: loot <corpse>\n\nAttempts to steal one random item from a player corpse.\n\nNotes:\n- You must be level 20+ to use this command.\n- You can only loot player corpses (not NPC corpses or other objects).\n- The corpse must be lootable for your clan/PK status.\n- Loot can fail, and items flagged NOLOOT cannot be taken.\n
9	greeting3	-1	greeting3	@@m    Beyond the veil of ordinary worlds lies ACK!TNG.@@N\n@@m    Steel rings, spells burn bright, and every choice matters.@@N\n\n@@c    Diku Mud was created by Hans Henrik St{rfeldt, Katja Nyboe,\n@@c    Tom Madsen, Michael Seifert and Sebastian Hammer.\n@@c    MERC Modifications made by: Furey, Hatchet, Kahn@@N\n\n@@a    New here or returning veteran, your next chapter starts now.@@N\n@@WEnter your name:@@N\n
10	emote	0	emote	Syntax: emote <action>\n\nPerforms a custom social/action message.\n
11	ironpine_vigor	0	ironpine vigor	The vigor of ironpine surges through the target, increasing maximum\nhit points by 10%.\nDruid spell. Uses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
12	stun	0	stun	Syntax: stun\n\nAttempts to stun your current combat opponent, temporarily incapacitating\nthem and interrupting their actions. Stun targets whoever you are currently\nfighting -- no argument is needed.\n\nA successful stun leaves the target unable to act for a short duration,\ngiving you a window of uncontested attacks.\n\nRestrictions:\n  - Must be in active combat (fighting someone).\n  - Only players (not NPCs) can use the stun command.\n  - Must have the skill learned.\n\nSee also: shelp stun bash trip dirt\n
13	build_stop	-1	build_stop	BUILD HELP : STOP\n-----------------\nTyping STOP will cause you to leave the Builder.\n
14	mana	1	'mana flare'	Mana flare causes a fountain of mana to flood the room, doubling your normal\n\nmana regeneration rate.\n\n
