16	read_opponent	0	read opponent	@@yRead Opponent@@W                                        Sentinel level 10\n\nSyntax: read opponent\n\nStudy your current combat target, instantly granting +2 testimony marks.\nCosts an action — you observe rather than attack.\n\n@@yDetails:@@W\n  * Mana cost: 8\n  * Cooldown: 8 rounds (reduced to 7 at WIS 22).\n  * Can only be used while fighting.\n  * Sets or maintains your testimony target.\n\nUse this to fast-charge toward a verdict threshold when avoidance-based\ntestimony accumulation is too slow.\n\nSee also: @@mtestimony verdict sentinel@@W\n
17	junk	0	junk	Syntax: junk <item>\n\nPermanently destroys an item in your inventory, removing it from the game.\nUnlike sacrifice, junk gives you nothing in return -- use it only for\nitems of no value that you simply want to be rid of.\n\nExample:\n  junk worn rag     -- Destroys the "worn rag" in your inventory.\n\nThe item must be carried (in your inventory), not worn or wielded.\n\nWARNING: Junked items cannot be recovered. Use this command carefully.\n\nSee also: sacrifice donate drop\n
18	assassin	0	assassin	@@dASSASSIN@@W\n\n@@dHistory@@W\n  No guild claims the founding of the Assassin tradition -- that is by\n  design. The earliest known practitioners were royal intelligence agents\n  in a long-dissolved empire, trained to remove obstacles without the\n  political cost of open warfare. Their methods passed from handler to\n  operative in a chain of careful instruction, each generation learning that\n  patience and positioning mattered more than strength. When the empire fell,\n  its agents scattered and sold their expertise piecemeal. Most lineages\n  degraded into common cutthroats; those who kept the original philosophy\n  intact produced something rarer: practitioners who understood that the\n  perfect kill requires as much study as any academic discipline.\n\nAssassins are patient executioners. They win by controlling first contact,\ncreating one lethal opening, and ending the fight before opponents can answer.\n\n@@dPassive class advantages@@W\n  * @@wExtra attack round@@W while Assassin remort is active.\n  * @@wCritical chance@@W bonus (+0.05% per level, up to +5% at 100).\n  * @@wCritical damage@@W bonus (+0.2% per level, up to +20% at 100).\n  * @@wBackstab / circle damage@@W bonus (+1% per level, up to +100% at 100).\n\n@@dUnique Assassin mechanics@@W\n  * Access to @@wAssassin stance@@W and @@wNinja stance@@W at higher remort level.\n  * Core opener class for stealth burst and positional kill windows.\n  * Uses @@wDexterity@@W as prime remort attribute.\n\n@@dAssassin reincarnation bonuses@@W\n  * @@wAssassin + Warlock remort reincarnations >= 20@@W unlocks\n    @@wDual Wield@@W permanently.\n\nSee also: @@mremort stance ninja warlock nightblade reincarnate@@W\n
19	lifesteal	0	lifesteal lifestealer	Lifesteal is a weapon extra flag. It can be id'd.\n\n \n\n
20	build_findmobroom	-1	build_findmobroom	BUILD HELP : FINDMOBROOM\n------------------------\nThe FINDMOBROOM command allows you to find which room a mob is loaded into.\nSyntax:  FINDMOBROOM <mob-vnum>\nYou will be shown a list of any rooms that the mob referenced is loaded in.\n
