24	greeting4	-1	greeting4	@@b~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~@@N\n@@b                    Welcome to ACK!TNG@@N\n@@b~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~@@N\n\n@@c    Diku Mud was created by Hans Henrik St{rfeldt, Katja Nyboe,\n@@c    Tom Madsen, Michael Seifert and Sebastian Hammer.\n@@c    MERC Modifications made by: Furey, Hatchet, Kahn@@N\n\n@@l    Explore dangerous frontiers, ancient powers, and living history.@@N\n@@l    In ACK!TNG, heroes are forged one decision at a time.@@N\n\n@@WWhat is your name?@@N\n
25	fungal_eruption	0	fungal eruption	Poisonous fungi erupt from the ground, damaging all enemies in the room.\nArea spell. Druid spell. Uses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
26	build_findobject	-1	build_findobject	BUILD HELP : FINDOBJECT\n-----------------------\nThe FINDOBJECT command displays certain object vnums.\nSyntax:  FINDOBJECT <string>\nYou will be shown a list of any objects that contain the string within their\nshort description.  Typing 'ALL' for the string will list all the objects.\nThis command will only show details of objects in your current area.\n
27	monk	0	monk	@@gMONK@@W\n\n@@gHistory@@W\n  The Monk tradition originated in the mountain monasteries that predated\n  the great cities, where communities of ascetics developed physical\n  disciplines as a form of living meditation. They discovered that breath\n  control, posture, and movement could be refined to a point where the body\n  itself became the instrument of something beyond ordinary physical\n  capacity. The first combat-capable Monks were not warriors -- they were\n  scholars of the physical form who found, sometimes reluctantly, that their\n  disciplines translated into devastating martial efficiency. They codified\n  their methods in what came to be called the Interior Forms, a system that\n  treated every strike not as aggression but as applied understanding.\n  Pugilists who return to study the Interior Forms find the forms have been\n  waiting for them all along.\n\nMonks are disciplined impact-fighters who convert breath control and posture\nmastery into relentless unarmed pressure.\n\n@@gPassive class advantages@@W\n  * @@wBare-hand direct-hit damage@@W bonus (+1% per level, up to +100% at 100).\n  * @@wMartial strike damage@@W bonus for palmstrike/pummel/aurabolt family\n    (+0.5% per level, up to +50% at 100).\n\n@@gUnique Monk mechanics@@W\n  * Access to @@wMonk stance@@W.\n  * High unarmed scaling and strong chi-path synergy into Martial Artist.\n  * Uses @@wConstitution@@W as prime remort attribute.\n\n@@gMonk reincarnation bonuses@@W\n  * @@wBrawler + Monk remort reincarnations >= 20@@W unlocks\n    @@wEquip Fist@@W and @@wDual Fist@@W permanently.\n\nSee also: @@mremort stance brawler martial_artist chi reincarnate@@W\n
28	tongue	0	tongue	TONGUE is equivalent to SAY, except that only players of your race will\nunderstand what you say.  Anyone else will see gibberish!  Note that the\nRACE command will tell to ALL members of your race (who are on the channel)\neven if they aren't in the same room as you.
29	description	0	description	Syntax: description\n\nEdits or displays your character description.\n
30	rest	0	rest	Syntax: rest\n\nSits down to rest and recover.\n
31	chi	0	chi	Chi is the monk/brawler/martial resource used by several hand-to-hand skills.\n\nChi cap is class-tiered:\n- Base Pugilist (or 20+ Pugilist reincarnations): 15 max chi\n- Monk or Brawler remort path (or 20+ combined remort reincarnations): 20 max chi\n- Martial adept path (or 20+ adept reincarnations): 25 max chi\n\nChi is spent by techniques like chiblock, chakra, and spinfist. Some actions\ngenerate chi (for example, many pugilist-style strikes), while others consume\nit for defense, healing, burst, or multi-hit pressure.\n\nFlurry converts your current chi into repeated immediate attacks until chi is\nexhausted. Some chi skills also become more expensive when used again before\ntheir cooldown fully recovers.\n\nTip: build chi with your basic chi-generating attacks, then spend it on the\nright window (defense, sustain, or finishing pressure).\n
32	human	0	Human	The world's most institutionally dominant people — not through raw power but through\nrelentless institution-building. From the Keeper civilization's road networks to the\nSolar Court's Great Pyramid to the cities of Midgaard and Kowloon, human history is a\nrecord of organizations that amplify both achievement and failure. The Ashfall Era's\nSpirebound Conclave, the Black Ledger, and the sealed warrant records are equally human\nconstructions. Most of what shapes this world, for good and ill, traces back to a human\ndecision made inside a human institution.\n
33	purge_toxin	0	purge toxin	Purges poison from the target's body using natural energy.\nDruid spell. Uses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
34	combat	-1	combat	\n\t\t\t--COMBAT--\nThe following commands are available:\nkill            flee            kick            rescue\ndisarm          backstab        dirt            bash\ntrip            assist\nFor more detailed help, type "HELP <command>".
35	sunken	150	sunken sanctum	The Sunken Sanctum is an ancient ruin buried beneath a collapsed mountain.\n\nThose who delve within will face the remnants of their experiments -- creatures\n\ntwisted by centuries of uncontrolled magic.  Deep within the Sanctum lie hidden\n\nchambers sealed by ancient puzzles.  Those who solve them may discover paths to\n\neven more dangerous areas.  Recommended level: 150-170.\n\n
36	apostle	1	apostle apostles	@@aApostles@@W\n\n \n\nApostles are traditionally the intermediaries between mortals and the elder\n\nGods.\n\n \n\nHere in the Realm you may contact an Apostle with questions you cannot get\n\nanswered from other mortals or for reimbursements, remorting, passing along\n\nof messages, etc.  Simply send a tell to an Apostle and then be patient in\n\ncase they are busy.\n\n \n\nDo not use the pray channel.  Again, this is for emergencies only when you\n\nneed a God and cannot see any visible ones.  If Gods are invisible it usually\n\nmeans they are coding for the mud so please contact Apostles first.\n\n \n\nTip - Type "who staff" to see which staff members are on.\n\n
37	hunt	0	hunt	Syntax: hunt <target>\n\nTracks or hunts for a named target.\n
39	build_doors	-1	build_doors	BUILD HELP : DOORS\n------------------\nUh-oh.  I don't know exactly _how_ doors are handled by the builder.  I'm\nstill working this one out myself.  As far as i know, this method seems to\nwork:\nset the door as type door, and as closed, locked or pickproof, as needed.\nAdd a reset to close/lock the door.\nMake sure you set both sides of the door.\n
40	deltari	0	Deltari	River delta folk of the Kowloon region, the Deltari built the hydraulic infrastructure\n— channels, cisterns, flood defenses, water-quality monitoring — that makes the delta\ncity viable. Direct heirs of the Reed Ledger Wardens, their civilization is organized\naround water-reading and practical record-keeping: the accumulated flow records of a\nDeltari settlement can span centuries of continuous hydraulic observation. The Black\nLedger, Kowloon's sealed census of individuals transferred to the Spirebound Conclave,\nlists Deltari among the transferred; their oral tradition has preserved those names\nacross generations while the official records remain sealed and the Jade Magistracy\ndeclines to discuss the matter.\n
41	build_nedit	-1	build_nedit	BUILD HELP : NEDIT\n------------------\nThe NEDIT command places you in No EDITing mode.\nSyntax:  NEDIT\nThis sets your editing mode to nothing.  \n
42	knight	0	knight	@@cKNIGHT@@W\n\n@@cHistory@@W\n  Knights trace their lineage to the Iron Reformation, when the warlords of\n  the eastern campaigns realized that warrior strength alone could not hold a\n  siege line. The first Knights were heavy infantry officers trained under the\n  Compact of the Seven Chains -- an agreement between warring clans that\n  established mutual rules of engagement. Bound by oath to their standard,\n  they developed a fighting doctrine built around body mechanics, controlled\n  aggression, and formation superiority. Over generations the tradition\n  formalized into academies where recruits underwent years of weapon drill\n  before taking the field. Their creed: break the line, hold the ground,\n  leave no fallen comrade behind.\n\nKnights are disciplined line-breakers: armored tacticians who seize momentum\nthrough relentless body-strike chains and weapon control.\n\n@@cPassive class advantages@@W\n  * @@wExtra attack round@@W while Knight remort is active.\n  * @@wCombo-family strike damage@@W for remort/adept combo attacks\n    (+2% per level, up to +200% at 100).\n\n@@cUnique Knight mechanics@@W\n  * Access to @@wKnight stance@@W.\n  * Strong core scaling for punch/kick/knee/headbutt/charge/holystrike/fleche.\n  * Uses @@wStrength@@W as prime remort attribute.\n\n@@cKnight reincarnation bonuses@@W\n  * @@wKnight + Swordsman remort reincarnations >= 20@@W unlocks\n    @@wTwo-Handed@@W and @@wEquip Buckler@@W permanently.\n\nSee also: @@mremort stance swordsman crusader combo reincarnate@@W\n
43	riposte	0	riposte	Syntax: riposte\n\nPrepares a riposte -- a counter-attack triggered when you successfully\nparry an opponent's strike. Riposte is a Warrior-line finisher skill:\nit can only be activated when your combo counter has reached the required\nthreshold during active combat.\n\nEffects when activated:\n  - Grants a +1 hitroll bonus for (combo_count - 3) combat rounds.\n  - The combo counter is reset after activation.\n  - Skill proficiency improves on successful use.\n\nThe hitroll bonus improves the accuracy of all subsequent attacks during\nits duration. Pair riposte with the parry passive skill for best results.\n\nRequirements:\n  - Must be in combat.\n  - Requires a valid finisher combo count (combo threshold met).\n  - Must have the skill learned.\n\nSee also: shelp riposte parry fleche anti magic shell shieldblock\n
44	poison_nightshade	0	poison:nightshade	Syntax: poison:nightshade\n\nApplies nightshade poison to your currently wielded weapon. Nightshade is\na potent plant-derived poison with powerful debilitating effects. It is\none of three weapon poisons available to rogue-line characters (Cipher,\nAssassin, Warlock, Nightblade).\n\nNightshade's debuffing effects can significantly weaken a target, making\nit valuable for reducing enemy combat effectiveness before or during a\nfight.\n\nRestrictions:\n  - Requires a weapon to be wielded.\n  - Must have the skill learned.\n\nSee also: shelp poison:nightshade poison:arsenic poison:quinine poison weapon backstab\n
45	edit	0	edit	Syntax: edit\n\nStarts/continues line editing for writable text.\n
46	buy	0	buy	Syntax: buy <item>\n\nPurchases an item from a shopkeeper.\n
47	ignore	0	ignore	Syntax: ignore <player>\n\nToggles ignoring communication from a player.\n
48	take	0	take	Syntax: take <item>\n        take <item> <container>\n        take all\n        take all.<keyword>\n\nTake is an alias for the GET command. It picks up an item from the room\nfloor or from an open container.\n\n  take sword          -- Picks up a sword from the room.\n  take all            -- Picks up everything in the room.\n  take sword chest    -- Takes a sword from a chest.\n  take all.iron       -- Takes all items whose name contains "iron".\n\nItems taken from a room go directly into your inventory. If you do not\nhave enough carrying capacity the item cannot be picked up.\n\nSee also: get drop put inventory\n
49	idea	0	idea	Syntax: idea <message>\n\nSubmits an idea/suggestion for staff review.\n
50	zmud	1	zmud client mudclient	@@yMUD CLIENTS@@N\n\nUsing a dedicated MUD client is strongly recommended.  It gives you\nfeatures like triggers, aliases, macros, scrollback, and proper color\nrendering that a plain telnet session cannot match.\n\nPopular free options:\n  @@cMUSHclient@@N  — Windows, highly scriptable\n  @@cTintin++@@N   — Linux/Mac/Windows, lightweight\n  @@cMudlet@@N     — cross-platform, active development\n\n@@yColor Note:@@N\n\nACK!TNG uses ANSI color codes.  Make sure your client has color enabled\nand is set to use the standard 16-color ANSI palette.  Some clients\ndefault to a "bright" scheme that swaps colors — switch to "normal" or\n"dim" if colors look wrong.\n
51	sacrifice	0	sacrifice	Syntax: sacrifice <item>\n        sacrifice <item> <deity>\n\nSacrifices an item to a deity in exchange for gold or alignment adjustment.\nThe amount of gold received depends on the item's value and your character's\nlevel.\n\nDeity options:\n  (none)            -- Neutral sacrifice, gold only.\n  <goodgodname>     -- Sacrifice to the good deity; shifts alignment toward\n                       good. Anti-evil items produce a larger alignment shift.\n  <evilgodname>     -- Sacrifice to the evil deity; shifts alignment toward\n                       evil. Anti-good items produce a larger alignment shift.\n  judge             -- Pays off your criminal sentence (PLR_KILLER/PLR_THIEF\n                       flags). Reduces sentence; when fully paid, criminal\n                       flags are removed. Unique and clan items cannot be\n                       used for fine payment.\n\nRestrictions:\n  - Cannot sacrifice yourself.\n  - Most objects must be in your inventory and droppable.\n  - Corpses of NPCs can be sacrificed; PC corpses cannot.\n  - Quest items and items flagged as NO_SAC cannot be sacrificed.\n  - Some room types prohibit sacrifice.\n\nSee also: junk donate gold worth\n
86	ancient_bark	0	ancient bark	Ancient bark encases your body, providing a large AC bonus and\nthorns that damage attackers.\nSelf-only buff. Druid spell. Uses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
87	players	0	players	Syntax: players\n\nShows currently online player summary.\n
52	paladin	0	paladin	@@aPALADIN@@W\n\n@@aHistory@@W\n  The Paladin order arose from the aftermath of the Sundering Wars, when the\n  gods themselves were said to have wept at the desecration of their temples\n  by mortal armies. Several high clerics, unwilling to leave their sanctuaries\n  defenseless again, forsook pure ministry and took up arms without abandoning\n  their faith. They swore binding oaths -- not to any king or nation, but to\n  the light itself -- and trained in armored combat under the doctrines of\n  advance and sanctification. The first Paladins served as shield-wardens at\n  the great temples, holding every threshold against the dark. Their oath-\n  marks, inscribed in holy silver, are said to burn cold when an enemy of the\n  faith draws near.\n\nPaladins are oathbound vanguards who turn faith into forward pressure. Their\nstyle is direct: close distance, hold formation, and punish evil with sanctified\nsteel.\n\n@@aPassive class advantages@@W\n  * @@wExtra attack round@@W while Paladin remort is active.\n  * @@wPhysical damage@@W bonus from Paladin levels\n    (+0.4% per level, up to +40% at 100).\n  * @@wHealing throughput@@W bonus\n    (+1.5% per level, up to +150% at 100).\n\n@@aUnique Paladin mechanics@@W\n  * Access to @@wPaladin stance@@W (melee + survivability + healing posture).\n  * Hybrid holy/melee kit with strong support crossover into Templar path.\n  * Uses @@wWisdom@@W as prime remort attribute.\n\n@@aPaladin reincarnation bonuses@@W\n  * @@wPaladin + Priest remort reincarnations >= 20@@W unlocks:\n    @@wTwo-Handed@@W, @@wEquip Buckler@@W, and @@wEquip Wand@@W permanently.\n\nSee also: @@mremort stance priest templar reincarnate@@W\n
53	runes	1	runes	Runes are magical effects that you can place in the room you are in.  They\n\nhave varying affects. Experiment!  They are one use spells..once triggered,\n\nthey dissapear.\n\nNOTE: Runes are triggered by the next to enter the room.\n\nNOTE: @@eDO NOT CAST RUNES OR BAD AREA AFFECTS IN NEWBIE AREAS!!!@@N\n\n
54	charge	0	charge	Syntax: charge <target>\n\nPerforms a charging attack against a target, closing distance rapidly and\nstriking with increased force. Charge is a Warrior-line combat skill handled\nby the Warrior attack system.\n\nCharge is available to Warden-class characters and their remort descendants\n(Knight, Swordsman, Crusader).\n\nRequirements:\n  - Must be in combat or initiates combat on the target.\n  - Target must be present in the room.\n  - Must have the skill learned.\n\nSee also: shelp charge bash smash headbutt\n
55	lock	0	lock	Syntax: lock <object|door>\n\nLocks a door/container using an appropriate key.\n
56	rulers	0	rulers	Syntax: rulers\n\nDisplays the current rulers and their affiliations in the game world.\nRulers are named characters who control areas or hold special titles\ngranted by the game's political system. Each ruler is listed with their\nrank title, name, and the group or faction they are affiliated with.\n\nRulers may also control specific areas of the game world, which is listed\nbeneath their entry if applicable.\n\nRuler titles reflect rank and gender (e.g., King/Queen, Lord/Lady).\n\nSee also: politics clan clist\n
57	target	0	target	Syntax: target <victim>\n\nMarks a specific opponent as your priority target and immediately strikes\nthem. Target is a precision skill that forces a single decisive hit on the\nnamed character. If you are currently fighting a different opponent, you\nwill disengage and redirect your attack.\n\nRequirements:\n  - Must have the Target skill at 65% proficiency or higher.\n  - The target must be in the same room.\n  - Cannot target innocent PCs (players without PKill/Thief flags) unless\n    you are in a deathmatch.\n  - Cannot target charmed creatures outside of a deathmatch.\n\nEffects:\n  - Executes one_hit() on the named target.\n  - If you were fighting someone else, combat is re-targeted.\n  - Sets a 1-pulse wait state after use.\n\nSee also: shelp target kill assist\n
58	close	0	close	Syntax: close <object|door>\n\nCloses a door or closeable container.\n
59	cast	0	cast	Syntax: cast <spell> [target]\n\nCasts a known spell, optionally on a target.\n
60	verdict	0	verdict	@@yVerdict@@W                                              Sentinel level 20\n\nSyntax: verdict\n\nConsume all accumulated testimony marks and deliver a single melee strike\nwhose damage and secondary effect scale with marks spent.\n\n@@yVerdict Tiers:@@W\n  @@w1-2 marks@@W: @@yRebuke@@W     — 1.5x damage, no secondary effect.\n  @@w3-4 marks@@W: @@yCensure@@W    — 2.5x damage, target -2 hitroll (3 rds).\n  @@w5-6 marks@@W: @@yBinding@@W    — 4x damage, target speed debuff (4 rds).\n  @@w7-8 marks@@W: @@ySealing@@W    — 6x damage, target silenced (2 rds).\n  @@w9 marks@@W:   @@RFINAL@@W      — 9x damage, target stunned (1 rd).\n\nAll verdicts gain a WIS-scaled damage bonus. Higher tiers include all lower\ntier effects.\n\nAfter spending marks, testimony accumulation pauses for 2 rounds.\n\nNo mana cost — the verdict is powered by observation, not magic.\n\nSee also: @@mtestimony sentinel condemn@@W\n
61	rent	0	rent	Syntax: rent\n\nThis MUD does not use a rent system. There are no inn costs or storage fees\nfor logging out with items.\n\nTo leave the game safely, simply use:\n  save    -- Saves your character to disk immediately.\n  quit    -- Saves and disconnects you from the game.\n\nYour equipment, gold, and character state are automatically saved when you\nquit. There is no need to find an inn or pay rent.\n\nSee also: save quit\n
62	build_bmotd	-1	build_bmotd	-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=- Builder's Message of the Day -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n@@yChanges:@@g Setting details for mobs and rooms has changed.  Typing\n'x' will now list not just the flags set, but those that are not.  To toggle\na flag (or set the room sector) enter it's name.\nAlso, to edit a string, (rooms and mobs) type 'edit <string>' eg edit long.\n@@yBuilders' Board:@@g This is situated west from Midgaard Altar.  Please be\nsure to check this regularly.  Now we have a (very simple) help editor, any\nurgent news can be placed here, in the BMOTD.\n@@RMouse@@g is now the Staff member in charge of building, area theme and \nlinking. If you have any queries, please consult him if possible before\ncoming to another staff member.  \n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=- Updated: 7th October -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-
63	clist	0	clist	Syntax: clist\n\nLists clans and basic clan information.\n
64	consider	0	consider	Syntax: consider <target>\n\nEstimates relative combat danger of a target.\n
65	config	0	config	Syntax: config\n\nDisplays your current configuration toggles.\n
66	rockburst	0	rockburst	A burst of stone shards strikes your enemy, dealing earth damage.\nDruid spell. Uses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
67	build_addmob	-1	build_addmob	BUILD HELP : ADDMOB\n-------------------\nThe ADDMOB command allows you to create new mobiles within the current area.\nSyntax:  ADDMOB <mob-vnum> <name>\nThis will add a new mobile into the area, with the specified vnum and name(s).\nThis will not happen if there is already a mobile with the vnum you supply.\n
164	build_extra	-1	build_extra	BUILD HELP : EXTRA DESCRIPTIONS\n-------------------------------\nExtra descriptions consist of a keyword, and a string.  When the player\n'examines' the keyword, the string will be displayed.\nExtra Descriptions enable you to add more detail to your rooms and objects.\n
68	wizard	0	wizard	@@WWIZARD@@W\n\n@@WHistory@@W\n  The Wizard tradition claims the oldest lineage of any remort path: the\n  Axiomatic Schools, founded when the first mortal arcanists decided that\n  magic was not merely power but a discipline subject to formal proof. They\n  built towers, wrote theorems, and insisted every spell effect could be\n  defined, bounded, and perfected. The most rigorous of their successors\n  became what the Schools called Artificers of Sequence -- practitioners\n  who had reduced combat casting to a precise language of timing, window,\n  and controlled output. When the formal title fell from use the common name\n  that survived was Wizard: not a grand title but a technical one, meaning\n  someone who has made the formless precise. A Magi who returns through the\n  mortal path to study theory rather than raw power earns it honestly.\n\nWizards are precision arcanists: patient theoreticians who break combat into\nangles, timing windows, and controlled spell sequencing. If Sorcerers are\nwildfire, Wizards are the scalpel.\n\n@@WPassive class advantages@@W\n  * @@wSpell critical chance@@W increases with Wizard levels\n    (+0.1% per level, up to +10% at 100).\n  * @@wRemort non-physical damage@@W gains Wizard scaling\n    (+0.5% per level, up to +50% at 100).\n  * @@wArcane healing throughput@@W improves for INT-based arcane healing\n    (+2% per Wizard level, up to +200% at 100).\n\n@@WUnique Wizard mechanics@@W\n  * Access to @@wWizard stance@@W (dual-cast / no-hit caster posture).\n  * Shares high-end arcane synergy with Sorcerer and Grand Magi progression.\n  * Uses @@wIntelligence@@W as prime remort attribute.\n\n@@WWizard reincarnation bonuses@@W\n  * @@wWizard + Sorcerer remort reincarnations >= 20@@W unlocks\n    @@wEquip Wand@@W permanently.\n\nSee also: @@mremort stance sorcerer grand_magi reincarnate@@W\n
69	gold	0	gold	Syntax: gold\n\nDisplays the exact amount of gold you are currently carrying. The game\nuses a single currency (gold coins). Gold is used to buy items from shops,\npay for healing at temples, and is received from selling items, sacrificing\nobjects, and killing monsters.\n\nA quick summary of ways to gain gold:\n  - Kill monsters and loot their corpses (get all corpse / loot)\n  - Sell unwanted items to shopkeepers (list, value, sell)\n  - Sacrifice items at a temple (sacrifice <item>)\n  - Receive gold from other players (split, give)\n\nSee also: worth score split give sacrifice\n
70	pagelength	0	pagelength	Syntax: pagelength <lines>\n\nSets output pagination length for long text.\n
71	fleche	0	fleche	Syntax: fleche <target>\n\nExecutes a fleche, a running thrust attack drawn from classical fencing\ntechnique. The attacker launches forward in a straight line, delivering a\npowerful lunge that is difficult to parry. Fleche is a Warrior-line finisher\nskill: it requires a valid finisher combo count before it can be used.\n\nFleche is available to Warden-class characters and their remort descendants\n(Knight, Swordsman, Crusader).\n\nRequirements:\n  - Must be in combat.\n  - Requires a valid finisher combo count (combo threshold met).\n  - Target must be present in the room.\n  - Must have the skill learned.\n\nSee also: shelp fleche charge riposte holystrike\n
72	build_rflags	-1	build_rflags	ROOM FLAGS:   ( * = To be added! )\n+===============+============================================================+\n| Flag Name\t|\t\t\tDescription\t\t\t     |\n+---------------+------------------------------------------------------------+\n| DARK\t\t| The Room is dark - a light source is needed to see.\t     |\n| REGEN\t\t| Players will regenerate HPs, mana and movement faster.     |\n| NO_MOB\t| No mobiles may enter the room.\t\t\t     |\n| INDOORS\t| The room is indoors; players see no weather messages.\t     |\n| *NO_MAGIC\t| Players may not cast spells here.\t\t\t     |\n| HOT\t\t| Players lose HPs due to the heat.\t\t\t     |\n| COLD\t\t| Players lose Hps due to the cold.\t\t\t     |\n| *PK\t\t| Players may Pkill here without being flagged.\t\t     |\n| *QUIET\t| Players may not talk in this room.\t\t\t     |\n| PRIVATE\t| The room holds only two players maximum.\t\t     |\n| SAFE\t\t| Players are safe from attack here.\t\t\t     |\n| SOLITARY\t| Only one player is allowed into the room at a time.\t     |\n| PET_SHOP\t| Room is a Pet_shop.  Please don't use this flag!\t     |\n| NO_RECALL\t| Players may not recall or use the home command here.\t     |\n| NO_TELEPORT   | Players using teleport cannot appear in this room.\t     |\n+===============+============================================================+\n
73	roothold	0	roothold	Roots grow from your feet, anchoring you firmly in place and\npreventing you from being forced to flee.\nSelf-only buff. Druid spell. Uses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
74	build_strings	-1	build_strings	BUILD HELP : STRINGS\n--------------------\nSTRINGS are collections of characters: i.e. words or sentences.\nThe most visible parts of an area are the descriptions on mobiles, objects, \nand especially rooms.  Please try and bear some thought to how these will\nlook, especially for mobiles and objects that may end up out of their intended\npositions.  Room descriptions should be neutral, and not too short, where\npossible.\n
75	rescue	0	rescue	Syntax: rescue <ally>\n\nAttempts to pull an ally out of combat focus.\n
76	testimonial_guard	0	testimonial guard	@@yTestimonial Guard@@W                                    Sentinel level 12\n\nPassive skill. WIS-scaled resistance to fear, charm, and other mental\neffects. Resistance percentage equals WIS * 3 (66% at WIS 22).\n\nAt 5 or more testimony marks on your current target, grants full immunity\nto fear — your observational focus is too deep to break.\n\nThe silence-court descent ritual trained practitioners to maintain composure\nunder psychic pressure. This is that training expressed as combat discipline.\n\nSee also: @@msentinel testimony@@W\n
77	help_revenant	0	revenant	@@d╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗@@N\n@@d║                   @@WTHE REVENANT SYSTEM@@d                       ║@@N\n@@d╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝@@N\n\nA @@Wrevenant@@N is a permanent undead minion raised from an NPC corpse\nusing the @@Wcast revenant@@N spell (Necromancer 70).\n\n@@WTHE CORPSE IS THE CHASSIS@@N\n  The quality of the corpse determines your revenant's power.\n  A higher-level mob with better combat stats (hitroll, damroll,\n  resistances, spellpower, etc.) produces a stronger revenant.\n  You can then use @@Wtracks@@N to multiply those base stats further.\n\n  @@RBETTER CORPSE = BETTER REVENANT AT EVERY STAGE.@@N\n\n@@WLEVEL CAP@@N\n  Your revenant's level is capped at the @@Wlower@@N of:\n    - The corpse's original mob level\n    - Your pseudo level\n    - 150 (hard cap)\n\n@@WBASIC USAGE@@N\n  1. Kill a strong NPC mob\n  2. @@Wcast revenant <corpse>@@N to raise it\n  3. @@Wrevenant track <name>@@N to choose upgrade paths\n  4. @@Wrevenant infuse <corpse>@@N to feed more corpses for soul points\n  5. @@Wrevenant rankup@@N to spend soul points on track upgrades\n\n@@WCOMMANDS@@N\n  @@Wrevenant status@@N        - View stats, tracks, and soul points\n  @@Wrevenant infuse <corpse>@@N- Feed a corpse for soul points\n  @@Wrevenant track <name>@@N   - Set primary or secondary track\n  @@Wrevenant rankup@@N         - Advance a track rank with soul points\n  @@Wrevenant tracks@@N         - List all available tracks\n\n@@WRELATED HELPS@@N\n  @@Whelp revenant tracks@@N   - Detailed track descriptions\n  @@Whelp revenant infuse@@N   - Soul point feeding system\n  @@Whelp revenant stats@@N    - How corpse stats affect your revenant\n\nlevel 0\nkeywords revenant tracks\n---\n@@d╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗@@N\n@@d║                @@WREVENANT TRACKS@@d                              ║@@N\n@@d╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝@@N\n\nTracks @@Wmultiply@@N your revenant's base stats from the corpse.\nA track upgrade on a powerful corpse yields much bigger gains\nthan the same upgrade on a weak corpse.\n\n@@W── PRIMARY TRACKS ──@@N (5 ranks, active combat abilities)\n\n  @@Wdread@@N   - Offensive melee.  Multiplies hitroll, damroll, crit.\n            Best on corpses with high hr_mod and dr_mod.\n\n  @@Wshadow@@N  - Evasion and ambush.  Multiplies dodge, parry, pierce.\n            Best on corpses with high dodge/parry stats.\n\n  @@Wbone@@N    - Tanking and defense.  Multiplies AC, block, HP.\n            Best on corpses with high ac_mod and hp_mod.\n\n  @@Wsoul@@N    - Spellcasting.  Multiplies spellpower, spell crit.\n            Best on corpses with casting abilities and high spellpower.\n\n  @@Wplague@@N  - DoTs and debuffs.  Level drives save DCs for\n            poison, weaken, and curse effects.\n            Best on high-level corpses.\n\n  @@Wblood@@N   - Lifesteal and sustain.  Multiplies healing, hitroll.\n            Best on corpses with high healing_mod and hr_mod.\n\n@@W── SECONDARY TRACKS ──@@N (3 ranks, passive aura on master)\n\n  @@Wwrath@@N   - Damage aura.  Master gains bonus damroll\n            scaled to revenant's base damroll.\n\n  @@Wward@@N    - Protection aura.  Master gains AC bonus\n            scaled to revenant's base AC modifier.\n\n  @@Whunger@@N  - Mana siphon.  Master regenerates mana each tick\n            scaled to revenant's spellpower.\n\n  @@Wspite@@N   - Retribution.  When master is hit, revenant\n            retaliates for damage scaled to hitroll.\n\n  @@Wwhisper@@N - Buff support.  Periodic minor buffs to master\n            scaled to revenant's level.\n\n  @@Wdecay@@N   - Debuff aura.  Enemies in combat near the\n            revenant are weakened, scaled to level.\n\n@@WTRACK MULTIPLIERS@@N\n\n  @@WPrimary Track:@@N\n    Rank 1:  x1.00  (base)\n    Rank 2:  x1.10   (25 soul points)\n    Rank 3:  x1.20   (75 soul points)\n    Rank 4:  x1.35  (150 soul points)\n    Rank 5:  x1.50  (300 soul points)\n\n  @@WSecondary Track:@@N\n    Rank 1:   5%% of stat shared to master  (free)\n    Rank 2:  10%% of stat shared to master  (50 soul points)\n    Rank 3:  15%% of stat shared to master (150 soul points)\n\n@@WEXAMPLE@@N\n  A dragon corpse with dr_mod=60:\n    Dread rank 1: 60 damroll\n    Dread rank 5: 90 damroll (x1.50)\n\n  A rat corpse with dr_mod=3:\n    Dread rank 1: 3 damroll\n    Dread rank 5: 4 damroll (x1.50)\n\n  @@RTHE CORPSE MATTERS MORE THAN THE TRACK.@@N\n\n@@WSWITCHING TRACKS@@N\n  You can switch tracks at any time, but switching @@Rresets@@N\n  the rank to 1 and @@Rforfeits@@N invested soul points.\n  Choose wisely!\n\nlevel 0\nkeywords revenant infuse\n---\n@@d╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗@@N\n@@d║              @@WREVENANT SOUL FEEDING@@d                          ║@@N\n@@d╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝@@N\n\nFeed NPC corpses to your revenant to gain @@Wsoul points@@N.\nSoul points are spent to advance track ranks.\n\n@@WUSAGE@@N\n  @@Wrevenant infuse <corpse>@@N\n\n@@WSOUL POINTS GAINED@@N\n  Formula: @@W(corpse level - revenant level) / 10@@N\n\n  Corpses weaker than your revenant yield @@Rnothing@@N.\n  You must feed corpses at or above your revenant's level.\n\n  Examples (revenant level 100):\n    Level  90 corpse = 0 soul points (too weak)\n    Level 100 corpse = 0 soul points (no difference)\n    Level 110 corpse = 1 soul point\n    Level 150 corpse = 5 soul points\n\n@@WSOUL POINT COSTS@@N\n  @@WPrimary Track Ranks:@@N\n    Rank 1:  Free (starting rank)\n    Rank 2:   25 soul points\n    Rank 3:   75 soul points\n    Rank 4:  150 soul points\n    Rank 5:  300 soul points\n    Total for max rank: 550 soul points\n\n  @@WSecondary Track Ranks:@@N\n    Rank 1:  Free (starting rank)\n    Rank 2:   50 soul points\n    Rank 3:  150 soul points\n    Total for max rank: 200 soul points\n\n  @@WMaximizing both tracks requires 750 total soul points.@@N\n\n@@WTIPS@@N\n  - Farm high-level mobs for efficient soul point gain.\n  - Use @@Wrevenant rankup@@N to spend accumulated soul points.\n  - Use @@Wrevenant status@@N to check your current soul point total.\n\nlevel 0\nkeywords revenant stats\n---\n@@d╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗@@N\n@@d║           @@WREVENANT STAT INHERITANCE@@d                         ║@@N\n@@d╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝@@N\n\nWhen you raise a revenant, it inherits the original mob's stats:\n\n@@WSTAT               INHERITANCE@@N\n  Level              Capped at your pseudo_level (max 150)\n  Hitroll (hr_mod)   Inherited directly from mob template\n  Damroll (dr_mod)   Inherited directly from mob template\n  AC Mod (ac_mod)    Inherited directly from mob template\n  HP Mod (hp_mod)    Scaled by level ratio\n  Spellpower         Inherited directly from mob template\n  Healing Mod        Inherited directly from mob template\n  Crit / Spell Crit  Inherited directly from mob template\n  Dodge / Parry      Inherited directly from mob template\n  Block / Pierce     Inherited directly from mob template\n  Resistances        Inherited + poison immunity added\n  Susceptibilities   Inherited + holy susceptibility added\n  Combat Skills      Inherited (skills, cast, def flags)\n  Combat Class       Inherited (determines spell AI)\n\n@@WUNDEAD OVERLAY@@N\n  All revenants receive:\n  - Poison resistance (undead immunity)\n  - Holy susceptibility (undead weakness)\n  - ACT_UNDEAD and ACT_PET flags\n  - Permanent duration (no extract timer)\n\n@@WWHY CORPSE QUALITY MATTERS@@N\n  Track multipliers amplify the base stats.  Example:\n\n  Dragon (hr_mod=80, dr_mod=60, ac_mod=200):\n    Dread rank 5: hr=120, dr=90 — devastating melee\n    Bone rank 5:  ac=300 — nearly impenetrable tank\n    Wrath rank 3: master gets +9 damroll aura\n\n  Rat (hr_mod=2, dr_mod=1, ac_mod=5):\n    Dread rank 5: hr=3, dr=1 — trivial improvement\n    Bone rank 5:  ac=7 — marginal defense\n    Wrath rank 3: master gets +0 damroll aura\n\n  Hunt the best corpse you can find. @@RThe corpse IS the loot.@@N\n
78	movement	-1	movement	        \n\t\t\t--MOVEMENT--\nThe following commands are available:\nnorth           east            south           west\nup              down            exits           recall (or /)\nFor more detailed help, type "HELP <command>".
79	knee	0	knee	Syntax: knee <target>\n\nDelivers a knee strike to an opponent, targeting the midsection or legs.\nKnee is a Warrior-line combat skill handled by the Warrior attack system.\nIt is available to Warden-class characters and their remort descendants\n(Knight, Swordsman, Crusader).\n\nRequirements:\n  - Must be in combat or initiates combat on the target.\n  - Target must be present in the room.\n  - Must have the skill learned.\n\nSee also: shelp knee kick bash headbutt\n
80	donate	0	donate	DONATE allows you to transfer a piece of equipment in your inventory\nto the "Donation Room", situated close to your race's Temple.
81	fill	0	fill	Syntax: fill <container> <source>\n\nFills a container from a liquid source.\n
82	creeping_blight	0	creeping blight	A creeping blight ravages your target, reducing STR by 3 and CON by 3,\nand reducing healing effectiveness.\nDruid spell. Uses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
83	templar	0	templar	@@aHISTORY@@W\n\nThe Templar title descends from the Solar Court's temple-guard auxiliaries\n-- wardens who stood at the boundary between battle-clergy and ceremonial\nministry, responsible for neither pure combat nor pure healing but both at\nonce. After the Sundering Wars, the Paladin vanguard and the Priest ward-\nkeepers settled into deliberately separate roles, one advancing and one\nsustaining. The synthesis was forced by necessity during the garrison\ncrisis of the Violet Compact's founding years, when a combined Paladin-\nPriest force found itself too few to maintain separate functions and began\ntraining across doctrinal lines. They revived the old Solar Court title\nfor what it meant: standing between two callings at once. The Violet\nCompact eventually absorbed the resulting Corps as a sanctioned order,\ncodifying what had begun as improvised wartime necessity into a formal\ndiscipline -- and into the adept path for those who had mastered either the\noath-vanguard or the restorative minister.\n\n@@aTEMPLAR@@W\n\nTemplars are the oathforged convergence of @@aPaladin@@W resolve and @@aPriest@@W\ndevotion. They are front-line hierophants: part battle-cleric, part relentless\nwarding engine, sustaining allies while grinding down darkness with holy force.\n\nTo become a Templar, you must master either @@aPaladin@@W or @@aPriest@@W\n(remort prerequisites for the adept path).\n\n@@aPassive class advantages@@W\nTemplar grants always-on scaling as adept levels rise:\n\n  1) @@wPhysical damage bonus@@W\n     - Your physical damage gains a passive Templar multiplier.\n     - Scaling: +1% physical damage per Templar adept level (up to +20% at 20).\n\n  2) @@wHoly damage bonus@@W\n     - Holy-element attacks gain additional damage from Templar level.\n     - Scaling: +2% holy damage per Templar adept level (up to +40% at 20).\n\n  3) @@wHealing output bonus@@W\n     - Healing spells and effects are strengthened by Templar level.\n     - Scaling: +4% healing per Templar adept level (up to +80% at 20).\n\n  4) @@wSpell critical damage bonus@@W\n     - Templar adds passive spell critical multiplier scaling with Wisdom.\n\n  5) @@wExtra attack round@@W\n     - Having any Templar adept level grants an additional melee hit in the\n       multi-hit calculation.\n\n@@aUnique Templar mechanics@@W\n  * @@wTemplar stance@@W becomes available with the adept path.\n  * @@wEnhanced Heal@@W is learned at Templar level 1.\n  * Casting @@wheal@@W as a Templar also attempts @@wcure blindness@@W,\n    @@wremove curse@@W, and @@wcure poison@@W on the target.\n  * Templar contributes to the @@wHoly Power@@W progression family.\n  * Templar uses @@wWisdom@@W as its adept prime attribute.\n\n@@aTemplar reincarnation bonuses@@W\nEach Templar adept reincarnation grants passive scaling:\n\n  * @@wHoly damage@@W: +2% per Templar adept reincarnation.\n  * @@wPhysical damage@@W: +1% per Templar adept reincarnation.\n  * @@wHealing output@@W: +1% per Templar adept reincarnation.\n\nIn short: Templar is the holy sustain adept—blending strong healing throughput,\nstatus-cleansing utility, and reliable holy/physical pressure in one class.\n\nSee also: @@mremort heal enhanced heal holy wrath holy light stance prompt@@W\n
84	split	0	split	Syntax: split <amount>\n\nSplits carried coins among your group members.\n
