88	objects	-1	objects	\n\t\t\t--OBJECTS--\nThe following commands are available:\nget             put             drop            give\nsacrifice       wear            wield           hold\ndonate          recite          quaff           zap\nbrandish        lock            unlock          open\nclose           pick            inventory       equipment\nlook            compare         eat             drink\nfill            list            buy             sell\nvalue           adapt\nFor more detailed help, type "HELP <command>".
89	measured_response	0	measured response	@@yMeasured Response@@W                                    Sentinel level 30\n\nPassive skill. After a successful parry or dodge, chance to deliver an\nautomatic counter-strike at 75% weapon damage. The proc also generates\n+1 testimony mark (+2 during Ninth Descent).\n\nProc rate: WIS * 2 percent (44% at WIS 22).\n\nUnlike Counter (CON 22 racial passive), Measured Response fires only on\nparry and dodge (not block) and deals reduced damage — but it generates\ntestimony, creating a defensive feedback loop: avoid, counter-hit, build\ntoward verdict.\n\nSee also: @@msentinel testimony verdict@@W\n
90	build_delobject	-1	build_delobject	BUILD HELP : DELOBJECT\n----------------------\nThe DELOBJECT allows you to delete an object.\nSyntax:  DELOBJECT <obj-vnum>\nIf an object is found with the specified vnum in the current area, it will be\nflagged for deletion, and you will be asked to enter DELOBJECT OK in order for\nit to be actually deleted.\n
91	greeting5	-1	greeting5	@@y               [ ACK!TNG Transmission Online ]@@N\n@@y         Realms synchronized. Adventurer channel open.@@N\n\n@@c    Diku Mud was created by Hans Henrik St{rfeldt, Katja Nyboe,\n@@c    Tom Madsen, Michael Seifert and Sebastian Hammer.\n@@c    MERC Modifications made by: Furey, Hatchet, Kahn@@N\n\n@@g    From quiet villages to world-shaking battlegrounds,\n@@g    your path is yours to choose.@@N\n\n@@WState your name and begin.@@N\n
92	rmlist	0	rmlist	Syntax: rmlist list\n        rmlist <modifier name>\n\nDisplays information about racial modifiers -- permanent enhancements that\ncan be purchased for your race using reincarnation points (RP).\n\n  rmlist list       -- Shows all available racial modifiers with their RP\n                       costs and any prerequisite racial traits required\n                       before purchase.\n  rmlist <name>     -- Shows detailed information about a specific modifier:\n                       name, RP cost, prerequisite, and the affect it grants.\n\nRacial modifiers are permanent and persist through reincarnations. They\nrepresent deep enhancements to your racial nature beyond what class training\nprovides.\n\nExamples:\n  rmlist list\n  rmlist toughskin\n\nSee also: reincarnate rlist qpspend\n
93	typo	0	typo	Syntax: typo <message>\n\nSubmits a typo report for staff review.\n
94	avoidance	0	avoidance dodge block parry	Avoidance, in total, is capped to 75%. This is a value that is a combined\n\nvalue of parry, block, and dodge in that order of precedence. If you have 50%\n\nparry and 25% block, you are capped at 75% avoidance. If you have 50% block,\n\n25% block, and 25% dodge, you only get the first 75%, and do not get any dodge\n\n\n Note that for every 2 levels above the victim, each avoidance is reduced by\n\n1%.\n\n
95	berserk	0	berserk	Syntax: berserk\n\nAttempts to enter a berserk combat state.\n
96	build_objects	-1	build_objects	BUILD HELP : OBJECTS\n--------------------\nThe following information is needed for each object:\nNAME\tThe name(s) that it is referenced by, from commands like give, etc.\nSHORT   The short description, used when getting or wielding, for example.\nLONG    The long description - seen when object is on the floor.\nEXTRA   Flags used to set special properties for the object.\nWEAR    Flags which determine where the object can be worn, if at all.\nAFF     Affects, such as HitRoll + 5, mana +50. etc.\nWEIGHT  The weight of the object - 1:light 5:heavy 10:Very Heavy!\nTYPE    The item type for the object, eg weapon, armor or fountain.\nED      Extra description - see 'HELP extra'\n
97	build_showroom	-1	build_showroom	BUILD HELP : SHOWROOM\n---------------------\nThe SHOWROOM command displays details about the room you are currently in.\nSytnax:  SHOWROOM\n
98	recite	0	recite	Syntax: recite <scroll>\n        recite <scroll> <target>\n\nReads aloud a magical scroll, releasing the spells inscribed upon it. Scrolls\nhold up to three spell effects. All effects are released simultaneously and\nthe scroll is consumed in the process.\n\nWithout a target argument, spells are cast on yourself. With a target, the\nscroll's effects are directed at the named character or object in the room.\n\nExamples:\n  recite identify     -- Recites a scroll of identify on yourself.\n  recite curse goblin -- Recites a curse scroll targeting a goblin.\n\nRestrictions:\n  - The item must be in your inventory (carried, not worn).\n  - The item must be of type SCROLL.\n  - Target (if specified) must be in the same room.\n\nSee also: quaff brandish identify\n
99	swordsman	0	swordsman	@@cSWORDSMAN@@W\n\n@@cHistory@@W\n  The Swordsman tradition was born in the dueling courts of the old city-\n  states, where legal disputes and matters of honor were settled at blade-\n  point. Unlike the mass-formation doctrine of the Knight, Swordsmen trained\n  for one-on-one excellence -- footwork, measure, and the half-second timing\n  window that separates a cut from a counter. The great masters wrote down\n  their art in codified manuals called the Cutting Books, each school\n  preserving its own blade theory jealously. Warriors who had mastered all\n  mortal fundamentals and returned to study the sword as art rather than\n  instrument became the first true Swordsmen -- technicians for whom the\n  blade was not a weapon but a language.\n\nSwordsmen are technical duelists who optimize edge control, timing, and clean\nfollow-through. They convert disciplined fundamentals into repeatable burst.\n\n@@cPassive class advantages@@W\n  * @@wExtra attack round@@W while Swordsman remort is active.\n  * @@wCombo-family strike damage@@W for remort/adept combo attacks\n    (+2% per level, up to +200% at 100).\n  * Additional sword-specific critical and damage interactions when using\n    sword-enhancement skills.\n\n@@cUnique Swordsman mechanics@@W\n  * Access to @@wSwordsman stance@@W.\n  * High synergy with weapon-based crit chains and Crusader progression.\n  * Uses @@wStrength@@W as prime remort attribute.\n\n@@cSwordsman reincarnation bonuses@@W\n  * @@wKnight + Swordsman remort reincarnations >= 20@@W unlocks\n    @@wTwo-Handed@@W and @@wEquip Buckler@@W permanently.\n\nSee also: @@mremort stance knight crusader combo reincarnate@@W\n
100	extra	0	extra extra_attacks extraattacks autoattack	In TNG, attacks are no longer gained from stats. Rather, attacks are gained\n\nfrom class levels.\n\n If you have levels in a physical-based remort class, that will give you one\n\nextra attack. If your primary class is 10 and a physical class, you will\n\nreceive an additional extra attack. Secondary class at 20. Tertiary class at\n\n40. 4th class at 80.\n\n
165	build_redit	-1	build_redit	BUILD HELP : REDIT\n------------------\nThe REDIT command places you in Room EDITing mode.\nSyntax:  REDIT\nThis will allow you to edit information concerning rooms.  The room you are\nworking on is ALWAYS the room your character is currently in.\nAnything you type will be checked to see if it applies to rooms, and if so, \nthe value, flag or string will be set.\n
101	holystrike	0	holystrike	Syntax: holystrike <target>\n\nChannels holy energy into a powerful weapon strike, dealing additional holy\ndamage to the target. Holystrike is a Warrior-line finisher skill: it\nrequires a valid finisher combo count before it can be activated.\n\nHolystrike is available to Warden-class characters and their remort\ndescendants, particularly Paladin and Crusader who have strong holy-damage\nsynergies.\n\nRequirements:\n  - Must be in combat.\n  - Requires a valid finisher combo count (combo threshold met).\n  - Target must be present in the room.\n  - Must have the skill learned.\n\nSee also: shelp holystrike fleche charge riposte\n
102	wither	0	wither	Withering energy saps the vitality from your target.\nDruid spell. Uses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
103	kick	0	kick	Syntax: kick <target>\n\nPerforms a kick attack in combat.\n
104	quest	1	quest quests	\n@@YQuests@@N are personal postman-issued tasks that can be completed for\nrewards. You can hold up to @@Y3@@N quests at once.\n\n@@WCommands@@N\n  quest request\n    Ask a postman for a random dynamic quest and place it in a free slot.\n\n  quest list\n    While with a mob that offers static quests, view available static\n    quests and their pseudo-level range requirements.\n\n  quest accept <number>\n    While with the offering mob, accept the numbered static quest from\n    @@Yquest list@@N into a free slot.\n\n  quest status\n    View progress for every active quest slot.\n\n  quest complete\n    Turn in one completed quest for rewards.\n    Dynamic quests require a postman; static quests require the\n    same mob that offered them.\n\n  quest cancel <slot#>\n    Cancel the quest in the given slot (1-3).\n\n@@WQuest types@@N\n  1) Kill Variety\n     Defeat several distinct target mobs.\n\n  2) Collect Items\n     Obtain listed items (credit is granted when they enter inventory).\n\n  3) Kill Count\n     Defeat a specific number of one target mob type.\n\n@@WStatic quest behavior@@N\n- Static quests are predefined templates offered by specific mobs.\n- Each static quest is tied to a specific NPC.\n- Each static quest has minimum and maximum pseudo-level requirements.\n- After a static quest is completed and turned in, it is marked complete\n  for that character.\n- Completed static quests no longer appear in @@Yquest list@@N and\n  cannot be accepted again.\n\n@@WRewards@@N\n- Dynamic quests reward gold, experience, and quest points based on pseudo level.\n- Static quests can define fixed gold/quest-point rewards.\n- Static quests may also grant item rewards on completion.\n\n@@WNotes@@N\n- You must be with a postman for @@Yrequest@@N and dynamic @@Ycomplete@@N turn-ins.\n- @@Ylist@@N/@@Yaccept@@N require the matching static-offerer mob to be present.\n- Static @@Ycomplete@@N turn-ins require the same offering mob.\n- @@Ystatus@@N and @@Ycancel@@N can be used anywhere.\n- Cancelling a @@Ydynamic@@N quest adds a 15 minute cooldown before\n  you can request another dynamic quest.\n- Static quests can still be accepted during this cooldown.\n
105	phantomfist	0	phantomfist	Syntax: phantomfist\n\nChannels chi into a burst of speed, allowing your strikes to land before\nopponents can react. Phantomfist is a chi-based buff skill available to\nPugilist-line characters (Monk, Brawler, Martial Artist).\n\nEffects when activated:\n  - Adds +2 to your chi pool.\n  - Applies a +3 speed bonus for 2 combat rounds.\n  - Activates a 10-round cooldown preventing reuse.\n\nSpeed improves how often your attacks land and your combat effectiveness.\nThe chi generated can feed into other chi-dependent skills.\n\nRequirements:\n  - Must be in combat.\n  - Must have the Phantomfist skill learned.\n\nSee also: shelp phantomfist chakra flurry spinfist\n
106	shadowform	0	shadowform	Syntax: shadowform\n\nAttempts to meld your body with the ambient shadows, granting an enhanced\nform of the sneak effect. Shadow Form is a high-level stealth skill that\nimproves on basic sneak by providing a deeper concealment affect tied to\nyour Shadowform skill level rather than generic sneak.\n\nEffects when successful:\n  - Applies the AFF_SNEAK bitvector affect at your character level.\n  - Duration scales with your level.\n  - Any existing sneak affect is first removed before Shadowform is applied.\n\nIf the skill check fails, the attempt is announced to the room but no\nbenefit is gained.\n\nShadowform is available to rogue-line characters who have reached a\nsufficient level in the Cipher, Assassin, or Warlock class lines.\n\nRequirements:\n  - Must have the Shadowform skill learned.\n  - Must not be in a room that explicitly prevents hiding.\n\nSee also: shelp shadowform sneak hide disguise visible\n
107	build_maff	-1	build_maff	MOB AFFECTED_BY FLAGS:\nBlind\t\tInvisible\tDetect_Evil\tDetect_Invis\nDetect_Magic\tDetect_Hidden\tSanctuary\tFaerie_Fire\nInfrared\tCurse\t\tPoison\t\tProtection\nSneak\t\tHide\t\tSleep\t\tFlying\nPass_Door\tAnti_Magic\tDetect_Undead\n*Anti_Magic protects the Mobile from magical attacks.\n
108	where	0	where	Syntax: where [name]\n\nShows nearby players/mobs or a specific target location.\n
109	pdelete	2	pdelete	Syntax: pdelete <password>\n\nPermanently deletes your player character.  Your save file is removed and your\nconnection is closed immediately.  This action cannot be undone.\n\nYou must supply your current password to confirm the deletion.  A wrong\npassword imposes a 10-second wait before you can try again.\n\nIf your account has no password set, the command may be used without an\nargument.\n
110	reincarnate	0	REINCARNATE REINCARNATION	@@aREINCARNATION@@W\n\nReincarnation is the endgame progression system for Realm Lords — characters\nwho have reached adept level 20 in any adept class. When you reincarnate, you\nare reborn as a level 1 character of your chosen race and class order, but\ncarry forward permanent bonuses earned from your previous lives.\n\n@@ySyntax:@@W\n  reincarnate information\n  reincarnate buy help\n  reincarnate buy damcap\n  reincarnate buy statcap\n  reincarnate set show\n  reincarnate set race <race>\n  reincarnate set order <class1> <class2> <class3> <class4>\n  reincarnate set confirm\n  reincarnate set done\n\n@@yRequirements:@@W\n  You must have an adept class level of 20 (Realm Lord) to use\n  reincarnate set. Use @@Wreincarnate information@@W at any level to view\n  your accumulated bonuses.\n\n@@yThe Reincarnation Process:@@W\n  1. Choose your new race: @@Wreincarnate set race <race>@@W\n     Any player-allowed race is valid. See @@Wrlist@@W for options.\n\n  2. Choose your new class order: @@Wreincarnate set order <c1> <c2> <c3> <c4>@@W\n     Specify all four mortal class slots. Example:\n       reincarnate set order War Cle Cip Psi\n\n  3. Confirm your selections: @@Wreincarnate set confirm@@W\n     Review first with @@Wreincarnate set show@@W.\n\n  4. Execute: @@Wreincarnate set done@@W\n     This is irreversible. Your character is reborn at level 1.\n\n@@yWhat Happens When You Reincarnate:@@W\n  - All equipped items are removed.\n  - Your experience is converted to quest points: (exp / 100000) + 1.\n  - Your level, class levels, remort levels, and adept levels all reset to 0.\n  - Your HP/Mana/Move gains from leveling are banked as permanent bonuses.\n  - You receive 1 reincarnation point to spend on upgrades.\n  - Your reincarnation history is updated (mortal, remort, and adept counts).\n  - You begin again at level 1 with your chosen race and class order.\n\n@@yPersistent Bonuses — HP, Mana, and Move:@@W\n  The HP, mana, and move you gained from leveling are permanently banked.\n  These bonuses apply every level in future lives, scaled with diminishing\n  returns. Each reincarnation adds to this pool, so the bonus grows over\n  multiple lives. Buying a higher statcap (see below) raises the threshold\n  before diminishing returns kick in.\n\n@@yPersistent Bonuses — Stat Caps:@@W\n  Each mortal class reincarnation raises the stat cap for that class's\n  prime attribute by 1 point for every 2 reincarnations in that class\n  (rounds up). The stat cap is normally @@W30@@W.\n  - @@cWarden@@W reincarnations increase max Strength.\n  - @@pMagi@@W and @@GPsionicist@@W reincarnations increase max Intelligence.\n  - @@aClerical@@W reincarnations increase max Wisdom.\n  - @@dCipher@@W reincarnations increase max Dexterity.\n  - @@gPugilist@@W reincarnations increase max Constitution.\n\n@@yPersistent Bonuses — Skill Unlocks (Mortal):@@W\n  Having at least 1 reincarnation in a mortal class permanently unlocks\n  a skill regardless of your current class:\n  - @@cWarden@@W    -> Enhanced Damage\n  - @@dCipher@@W      -> Enhanced Critical\n  - @@gPugilist@@W   -> Counter\n  - @@pMagi@@W       -> Potency\n  - @@GPsionicist@@W -> Spell Critical\n  - @@aCleric@@W     -> Spell Critical Damage\n\n@@yPersistent Bonuses — Skill Unlocks (Remort):@@W\n  Combined remort reincarnation totals of 20 or more unlock skills:\n  - Assassin + Warlock >= 20     -> Dual Wield\n  - Knight + Swordsman >= 20     -> Two-Handed, Equip Buckler\n  - Paladin + Priest >= 20       -> Two-Handed, Equip Buckler, Equip Wand\n  - Brawler + Monk >= 20         -> Equip Fist, Dual Fist\n  - Wizard + Sorcerer >= 20      -> Equip Wand\n  - Necromancer + Egomancer >= 20 -> Equip Wand\n\n@@yPersistent Bonuses — Damage Cap:@@W\n  The base damage cap is @@W2500@@W (adepts gain +500 while adept). Each\n  purchased damcap upgrade adds a permanent @@W+500@@W to your damage cap.\n\n@@yReincarnation Points — Spending:@@W\n  Each reincarnation grants 1 reincarnation point. Use @@Wreincarnate buy@@W\n  to spend them on permanent upgrades. Use @@Wreincarnate buy help@@W to see\n  the cost for your next upgrade.\n\n  @@wreincarnate buy damcap@@W\n    Permanently increases your damage cap by 500.\n    Cost: (current damcap bonus * 2) + 1 points.\n    Example: 1st upgrade costs 1 point, 2nd costs 3 points, 3rd costs 5.\n\n  @@wreincarnate buy statcap@@W\n    Raises the threshold before diminishing returns apply to your\n    accumulated HP/Mana/Move reincarnation bonuses.\n    Cost: (current statcap bonus)^2 + 1 points.\n    Example: 1st upgrade costs 1 point, 2nd costs 2 points, 3rd costs 5.\n\n@@yViewing Your Reincarnation Status:@@W\n  @@Wreincarnate information@@W — Shows all reincarnation counts by class\n  (mortal, remort, adept) and your current banked HP/Mana/Move bonuses,\n  statcap bonus, damcap bonus, and available reincarnation points.\n
