146	multi	0	multi multiclass	Ack! Mud now supports players having more than one class.\nEg, a player may chose to be Magi/Conjuerer or Cipher/Warden.\nWHO and SCORE now report the levels gained.  A ' - ' character means that\nthe specified class is not available, eg:\nMag:23 Cle: - Cip: - , etc.  This means that player can advance in Magi levels,\nbut not in Cleric or Cipher.\nSkills and spells become available when ANY class' level meets the minimum\nlevel required to use it.  The max level of the player is not used.\nWhen casting spells, like above, the maximum level of THE CLASS THAT HAS ACCESS\nTO THAT SPELL is used.  This way a char who is Mag:2 and War:50 won't be able\nto cast 50th level Magi spells.\nLevel gain is no longer automatic.  The GAIN command must now be used instead,\nto advance in the specified class.  See 'HELP GAIN' for more details.
119	staffrules	82	STAFFRULES	@@YACK!MUD TNG — Staff Conduct@@N\n\nAs a staff member on ACK!TNG you are staff, not a player.  The same three\nrules that govern players apply to you — and then some.  Players see you\nas a representative of the game.  Act accordingly.\n\n@@RDON'T:@@N\n\n  a) KILL, HARM, or HARASS PLAYERS — this includes:\n       - Changing titles, stats, sex, or class without consent\n       - Using SWITCH, FORCE, or spells against players\n       - Misusing channels (emote, say, gossip, echo) to belittle players\n       - Being deliberately unhelpful or condescending\n\n  b) GIVE UNFAIR ADVANTAGES — this includes:\n       - Using OLOAD or MLOAD to give players equipment or easy kills\n       - Using MSET or OSET to enhance items or weaken mobs for players\n       - Handing out gold, exp, or items outside of sanctioned events\n\n  c) ACT ON PERSONAL BIAS — treat all players equally.  The moment you\n     start helping friends and ignoring strangers, you have failed at\n     the job.\n\n@@GSHOULD:@@N\n\n  a) BE HELPFUL.  If you are online and not building, you are available.\n     A player asking a genuine question deserves a genuine answer.\n\n  b) BE FAIR.  Apply rules and consequences consistently.  No favorites.\n\n  c) USE FREEZE SPARINGLY.  It is a last resort, not an expression of\n     frustration.  Prefer DENY or NUKE for serious violations after\n     consulting with senior staff.\n\n  d) LOG ACTIONS.  Nearly everything you do is logged.  Behave as though\n     every command will be reviewed.\n\n@@RIMPORTANT:@@N\n\n  Staff status on ACK!TNG is not a reward.  It is a responsibility.\n  Abuse it and it will be removed.  Repeated violations will result in\n  deletion.  No warnings, no appeals.\n\n  See also:  @@cHELP RULES@@N\n
