121	trip	0	trip	Syntax: trip <target>\n\nAttempts to sweep an opponent's legs out from under them, knocking them to\nthe ground. A tripped target is left in a vulnerable position for follow-up\nattacks. Success is based on your learned proficiency in the trip skill.\n\nThe target must already be engaged in combat (fighting someone) for trip\nto work. Trip also costs energy via the energy system.\n\nA successful trip initiates combat between you and the target if you were\nnot already fighting. The knockdown effect reduces the target's ability to\nfight back temporarily.\n\nRequirements:\n  - Target must be fighting someone (already in combat).\n  - Must have energy available.\n  - Must have the skill learned.\n\nSee also: shelp trip bash dirt stun\n
122	build_mobiles	-1	build_mobiles	BUILD HELP : MOBILES\n--------------------\nThe following information is need for each mobile:\nNAME\tKeywords for the Mobile.\nSHORT\tThe short description of the mobile.\nLONG    The long description, used on 'LOOK'.\nDESC\tThe Mobile's description.\nSPEC\tAny SPECial functions the Mobile uses.\nSEX\tThe Mobile's gender.\nLEVEL\tThe Mobile's level.\nALIGN\tThe Mobile's alignment.\nAFF\tFlags determining what spells, etc the Mobile is affected by.\nACT\tFlags determining how the Mobile acts, eg: Scavenger, Hunter, etc.\nHR_MOD\tHitRoll Modifier.\nDR_MOD\tDamRoll Modifier.\nAC_MOD\tArmorClass Modifier.\nSHOP\tShop information.  See 'HELP shops'.\n
