128	motd	-1	MOTD	@@R        +----------------------------------------------------------+\n@@R        |   @@eA C K ! M U D   T N G@@R  --  Message of the Day   |\n@@R        +----------------------------------------------------------+@@N\n\n@@YWelcome to the crossroads.@@N  Lamp your bearings.  Ledger your intent.\n\n@@b---------------------------------------------------------------------@@N\n@@gWORLD EVENTS@@N\n\n  Cinderteeth seismic activity is elevated.  The Temple of the Resounding\n  Heart has the watch.  Road warden patrols on northern routes are up.\n\n  Blight from the Withered Depths is disrupting northern timber and herb\n  shipments.  Midgaard herbalists are paying well for expedition stock.\n\n@@b---------------------------------------------------------------------@@N\n@@YRULES — read them.  There are no pardons for ignorance.@@N\n\n  Type @@cHELP RULES@@N for the full text.  Short version:\n  don't be a dick, don't make staff step in, max 3 characters,\n  no automated play.\n\n@@gGETTING STARTED@@N\n\n  @@cHELP NEWBIE@@N   — orientation and essential commands\n  @@cHELP RULES@@N    — the rules\n  @@cHELP IMM@@N      — staff and how to reach them\n\n  Report bugs in Discord.\n\n@@b---------------------------------------------------------------------@@N\n@@N  @@eNo ward unlit.  No traveler uncounted.  No judgment hidden.@@N\n
129	headbutt	0	headbutt	Syntax: headbutt <target>\n\nDelivers a headbutt to an opponent, striking with the forehead or helm.\nHeadbutt is a Warrior-line combat skill handled by the Warrior attack\nsystem. It is available to Warden-class characters and their remort\ndescendants (Knight, Swordsman, Crusader).\n\nThe attack can potentially disrupt the target's combat rhythm and deals\nphysical damage.\n\nRequirements:\n  - Must be in combat or initiates combat on the target.\n  - Target must be present in the room.\n  - Must have the skill learned.\n\nSee also: shelp headbutt bash smash knee charge\n
130	game	0	game	Syntax: game <message>\n\nSends a message on the game channel, which is visible to all connected\nplayers. The channel is prefixed with a colored [GAME] tag.\n\nExample:\n  game Anyone up for the dungeon run tonight?\n\nTo disable or enable receiving game channel messages, use the CHANNELS\ncommand to toggle the channel.\n\nThis channel is intended for in-game discussion such as grouping, trade\nannouncements, and general game-related conversation.\n\nSee also: channels gossip newbie ooc invasion\n
131	quaff	0	quaff	Syntax: quaff <potion>\n\nDrinks a potion from your inventory, triggering the magical spells stored\nwithin it. Potions hold up to three spell effects which are all released\nsimultaneously when quaffed. The potion is always consumed in the process.\n\nThe spell effects are cast at the potion's stored level, not your character\nlevel. Higher-level potions produce stronger effects.\n\nExamples:\n  quaff healing   -- Drinks a healing potion.\n  quaff red       -- Drinks a red-colored potion.\n\nRestrictions:\n  - The item must be in your inventory (carried, not worn).\n  - The item must be of type POTION.\n  - You cannot quaff scrolls, staves, or wands -- use recite or brandish.\n\nSee also: recite brandish inventory\n
