132	cipher	0	cipher	@@dHISTORY@@W\n\nWhen the Ninth Meridian Rite failed and the charter road system collapsed, the\nlegitimate caravan economy fragmented into reaver strongholds, cult toll courts,\nand abandoned cistern vaults. In that breakdown a different kind of operator\nflourished: those who moved through institutional seams, traded in what\nregistries could not see, and survived by knowing which doors had been bricked\nover and which still opened from the inside. The cipher tradition crystallized\namong these figures — route guides who sold rival convoy routes, fence operators\nmanaging contraband between the Saltglass Reach and the Five Cities, private\nintelligence dealers who made the post-collapse road network navigable for those\nwho could pay. The current generation inherits a craft older than any guild,\nbuilt on the principle that every system of control creates its own perimeter,\nand every perimeter has a gap.\n\n@@dCIPHER@@W\n\nCiphers are opportunists of motion and timing, winning through angles,\nmisdirection, and surgical violence. They strike where armor and awareness are\nweakest.\n\n@@dPassive class abilities@@W\n  * @@wCipher precision scaling@@W: backstab and circle gain\n    @@w+1% damage per Cipher level@@W.\n  * @@wEnhanced Critical@@W (unlocked at mortal level 20):\n    - Adds extra critical chance based on Dexterity.\n    - Adds extra critical multiplier based on Dexterity.\n\n@@dUnique Cipher mechanics@@W\n  * Prime mortal attribute is @@wDexterity@@W.\n  * Strong synergy with critical-hit focused combat and precision burst windows.\n\n@@dCipher reincarnation bonuses@@W\n  * Every @@w2 Cipher reincarnations@@W (rounded up) increases max\n    @@wDexterity@@W by 1.\n  * At @@w1+ Cipher reincarnation@@W, @@wEnhanced Critical@@W is permanently\n    unlocked for all future class paths.\n\nSee also: @@mreincarnate remort assassin warlock@@W\n
133	get	0	get	Syntax: get <item>\n\nPicks up an item from the room or container.\n
