135	vigilance	0	vigilance	@@yVigilance@@W                                    Racial passive (WIS 22)\n\nVigilance is a racial passive skill granted to characters with WIS 22 or\nhigher. It increases dodge and parry chance based on Wisdom, representing\ncombat anticipation through perceptive depth.\n\n@@yEffect:@@W +WIS*2/5 to dodge and parry chance (@@w+8 at WIS 22@@W).\n\n@@yRaces with Vigilance:@@W Khenari, Deltari, Ushabti, Kethari.\n\nVigilance is not Sentinel-specific — any class with WIS 22 benefits.\nA Cleric with Vigilance dodges more. A Paladin with Vigilance parries more.\nA Sentinel with Vigilance dodges more @@wand@@W builds testimony faster from\nthe increased avoidance.\n\n@@yStat-22 melee passives:@@W\n  @@wSTR 22@@W: Enhanced Damage    — hit harder.\n  @@wDEX 22@@W: Enhanced Critical  — hit sharper.\n  @@wCON 22@@W: Counter            — hit back.\n  @@wWIS 22@@W: Vigilance          — @@wget hit less@@W.\n\nSee also: @@msentinel testimony@@W\n
136	sap_mend	0	sap mend	Warm sap flows through your veins, mending minor wounds.\nA basic Druid healing spell.\nUses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
137	overgrowth	0	overgrowth	@@aOvergrowth@@N is the core mechanic of the Druid class.\n\nDruid spells cost @@eHP@@N instead of mana. Each cast adds Overgrowth stacks\nbased on the spell's growth value, up to a maximum of 100.\n\n@@WEffects of Overgrowth:@@N\n - @@eCost increase@@N: HP cost rises by 2% per stack\n - @@aDamage bonus@@N: Druid spell damage increases by 3% per stack\n - @@WDecay@@N: Out of combat, decays by 1/tick (2/tick if resting/sleeping)\n - @@eDeath protection@@N: If a spell would kill you, HP is set to 1 and\n   Overgrowth is maxed at 100\n - @@WDeath reset@@N: Overgrowth resets to 0 on death\n\nThe Druid walks a razor's edge between destruction and self-destruction.\n
