139	summary	-1	SUMMARY	The help pages for ACK! MUD have been updated, rewritten and reformatted.\nThe following topics now have sub-pages, and then sub-sub-pages!\nThese are the main sub-pages available:\n\tMOVEMENT        GROUP           OBJECTS\n\tINFORMATION     COMMUNICATION   COMBAT\n\tOTHER\nAnd also, other help pages of interest:\n\tDAMAGE          DEATH           EXPERIENCE \n\tNEWS            TICK            WIZLIST \n\tCHANGES         THANKS          BOARDS\n\tMULTI           GAIN\nSo, to view the list of GROUP related commands, type "HELP GROUP".\n   Or, to view the help page for Damage, type "HELP DAMAGE".
140	priest	0	priest	@@CPRIEST@@W\n\n@@CHistory@@W\n  The Priest as a formal remort path emerged from the schism within the\n  Cleric councils known as the Hour of Quiet Thunder, when a faction of\n  senior clerics argued that battlefield ministry had diluted the faith's\n  true purpose. These purists withdrew from combat theology and devoted\n  themselves entirely to restoration, consecration, and the slow patient work\n  of keeping the living alive. They developed healing rites of extraordinary\n  sophistication, learned to sustain miracle-channels for hours at a stretch,\n  and built the great ward-networks that still shelter pilgrims across the old\n  cities. A Priest who has walked back through the mortal disciplines carries\n  that reservoir of worldly experience into the sacred work -- they heal not\n  from ignorance but from hard-won knowledge of what breaks a body.\n\nPriests are ward-keepers and miracle-callers, trained to outlast chaos through\nrestoration, sanctification, and relentless holy attrition.\n\n@@CPassive class advantages@@W\n  * @@wHoly damage@@W bonus from Priest levels\n    (+1% per level, up to +100% at 100).\n  * @@wHealing throughput@@W bonus\n    (+2% per level, up to +200% at 100).\n\n@@CUnique Priest mechanics@@W\n  * Access to @@wPriest stance@@W (high healing posture).\n  * Strongest remort-side baseline scaling for sustained holy healing play.\n  * Uses @@wWisdom@@W as prime remort attribute.\n\n@@CPriest reincarnation bonuses@@W\n  * @@wPaladin + Priest remort reincarnations >= 20@@W unlocks:\n    @@wTwo-Handed@@W, @@wEquip Buckler@@W, and @@wEquip Wand@@W permanently.\n\nSee also: @@mremort stance paladin templar reincarnate@@W\n
141	build_dig	-1	build_dig	BUILD HELP : DIG\n----------------\nThe DIG command allows you to add a room to an area.\nSyntax:  DIG <direction> <room-vnum>\nThis will add an exit in the direction given,  to the room you are currently in,\nconnected to a new room, which will have the vnum specified.  There are two\nobvious limitations:  There can't already be a door in the direction you give,\nor a room that already has the vnum you give.\n
