155	invasion	1	invasion invasions quartermaster emblems gertrude	Invasions are realm-wide defense events against a mythic boss and endless waves.\n\nHow invasions start\n- Invasions can start only when at least one non-staff player is online.\n- The system checks once per invasion tick after cooldown.\n- Each check has a 5% chance to start an invasion.\n- After an invasion ends (win/loss/cleanup), a cooldown is applied before another can start.\n\nCore objective\n- Defend Gertrude in room vnum 1209 (The Temple of Midgaard).\n- Kill the invasion boss before Gertrude takes too many invasion hits.\n- If the boss dies: defenders win.\n- If Gertrude dies (or reaches the explosion failure threshold): defenders lose.\n\nScaling and spawn behavior\n- Boss level is based on the highest online player's pseudo level + 20.\n- Regular wave mobs scale from online player pseudo levels.\n- Spawn counts scale with player count (more players = more invaders).\n- Boss pressure increases over time: while the boss survives, extra mobs are spawned.\n- Wave durability/difficulty also rises with prolonged respawns.\n\nInvader behavior\n- Non-boss invasion mobs path toward Gertrude every room update tick.\n- They are not naturally aggressive, but they march relentlessly.\n- They can unlock/open doors while pathing.\n- If they reach Gertrude's room, they explode and are removed.\n- If an invader cannot path to Gertrude, it crumbles away.\n\nGertrude pressure system\n- Each tick where invaders detonate at Gertrude increments invasion pressure.\n- Gertrude issues warning invasion channel messages at 10, 15, and 19 hits.\n- At 20 hits, Gertrude falls and the invasion is lost.\n\nRewards\nOn invasion success:\n- Every online non-staff player receives:\n  - 25 quest points\n  - 1 invasion point\n\nOn killing invasion mobs:\n- Killers can receive invasion reward tokens by mob level:\n  - Commendation: invader level <= 100\n  - Ribbon: invader level 101-149\n  - Medal: invader level >= 150\n- Boss kills end the invasion and trigger the global success reward.\n\nTracking your invasion progression\n- SCORE displays:\n  - Invasion points\n  - Invasion rewards (commendations/ribbons/medals) when you have any\n\nQuartermaster and invasion emblems\n- A quartermaster NPC can exchange invasion currency for wearable invasion emblems.\n- Use LIST near a quartermaster to view emblem tiers/styles and prices.\n- Buy syntax: BUY <tier> <style>\n- Tiers: common, magic, rare\n- Styles: caster, melee, tank\n\nCurrent emblem costs\n- common caster/melee/tank: 1 invasion point + 5 commendations\n- magic caster/melee/tank: 10 invasion points + 50 commendations + 5 ribbons\n- rare caster/melee/tank: 100 invasion points + 500 commendations + 50 ribbons + 5 medals\n\nStaff control\n- Staff can use: iinvasion <start|stop|status|bosses>\n\nTips\n- Focus boss pressure first, but do not ignore marching waves.\n- In larger player populations, expect significantly heavier spawn volume.\n- Keep routes open when possible; invaders will force doors when needed.\n
156	poison_arsenic	0	poison:arsenic	Syntax: poison:arsenic\n\nApplies arsenic poison to your currently wielded weapon. Arsenic is a\nslow-acting inorganic poison that deals damage over time when a poisoned\nattack lands. It is one of three weapon poisons available to rogue-line\ncharacters (Cipher, Assassin, Warlock, Nightblade).\n\nEach poison type has distinct effects that interact with Backstab and Circle\nwhen applied. Arsenic's damage-over-time profile makes it effective for\nsustained pressure in extended fights.\n\nAcquiring poison skills:\n  Poison weapon skills are learned through the rogue class progression.\n  Use SHELP POISON:ARSENIC for full acquisition details.\n\nRestrictions:\n  - Requires a weapon to be wielded.\n  - Must have the skill learned.\n\nSee also: shelp poison:arsenic poison:quinine poison:nightshade poison weapon backstab\n
157	beep	0	beep	Syntax: beep <player>\n\nSends an audible/page notification to another player.\n
158	spinfist	0	spinfist	Syntax: spinfist\n\nExecutes a spinning fist technique that strikes all enemies in the room\nsimultaneously. Unlike most targeted attacks, spinfist hits every opponent\npresent (excluding grouped allies and your master). This makes it highly\neffective against multiple enemies.\n\nEffects:\n  - Attempts one_hit() against each eligible target in the room.\n  - Costs chi (scales with cooldown if recently used).\n  - Activates a 10-round cooldown preventing reuse.\n\nEach target is checked individually -- enemies that are immune or protected\nmay not be affected. Grouped or following characters are not hit.\n\nRequirements:\n  - Must be in combat.\n  - Must have chi available.\n  - Must have the Spinfist skill learned.\n\nSee also: shelp spinfist flurry aurabolt phantomfist\n
159	combo	0	combo combos finisher finishers	Combo is the warrior-style chained attack system.\n\nAs you land combo-tagged skills (like punch, kick, knee, headbutt, bash,\ncharge, and some finishers), your combo track fills. Repeating the same\nskill in one sequence breaks the chain.\n\nCombo size (max chain slots) is class-tiered:\n- Base Warden (or 20+ Warden reincarnations): 4 max combo\n- +1 if Crusader adept path is active (or equivalent adept reincarnation tier)\n- +1 if Knight or Swordsman remort path is active (or equivalent remort tier)\nSo practical finisher tiers are usually 4 / 5 / 6 max combo.\n\nFinisher-ready happens at one slot before max (max-1):\n- 4 max combo -> finisher-ready at 3\n- 5 max combo -> finisher-ready at 4\n- 6 max combo -> finisher-ready at 5\n\nWhen finisher-ready, you can use actions such as fleche, holystrike, riposte,\nshieldblock, or anti-magic shell (if your class can use them).\n\nIf your combo reaches full readiness, the combo system can trigger extra\nfollow-up attacks based on the skills in your chain.\n
160	quit	0	quit	Syntax: quit\n\nExits the game and returns to the login screen.\n
161	build_set	-1	build_set	BUILD HELP : SET\n----------------\nSet allows you to set some value, string or flag, depending upon which editing\nmode you are currently in.  It is not really needed any more, as you can drop\nthe 'SET' part of the command now.  Eg: SET level 100 (when editing mobs) could\nbe entered as 'level 100' instead.\nTyping 'SET' on it's own displays the values, flags or strings you can set.\n
