172	unlock	0	unlock	Syntax: unlock <object|door>\n\nUnlocks a door/container with a key.\n
173	bond	0	bond weapon bond swordsman bond	Syntax: bond <weapon>              - Bond to a sword\n        bond status                - View bond details\n        bond track <name>          - Choose a track (edge/guard/keen/spirit)\n        bond track <name> confirm  - Switch tracks (resets rank and points)\n        bond rankup                - Spend bond points to advance rank\n        bond mastery               - Unlock mastery at max rank (100 qp)\n        bond name <new name>       - Rename your bonded weapon\n        bond tracks                - List all available tracks\n\nA swordsman can forge a soul-bond with a sword, creating a weapon that\ngrows alongside them. The bonded weapon automatically scales to the\nwielder's current level, but its power budget is determined by the\noriginal weapon's level at the time of bonding. A level 150 sword\nproduces a far more powerful bond than a level 1 sword.\n\nOnly one weapon can be bonded at a time. Bonding a new weapon destroys\nthe old one and inflicts a "Broken Bond" debuff (reduced hitroll and\ndamroll for several ticks). All accumulated bond points and track\nprogress are lost.\n\nBonded weapons cannot be dropped, given away, disarmed, or lost on\ndeath. They remain equipped through death.\n\nRequirements:\n  - Must be a Swordsman (any level).\n  - Weapon must be a sword (slash type).\n  - Must be holding the weapon.\n\nBond points are earned by killing mobs while wielding the bonded\nweapon. Higher-level mobs relative to the wielder yield more points.\nUse bond points to advance your chosen track's rank.\n\nSee also: bond tracks bond mastery\n
174	order	1	order charmies charmed	The number of charmed creatures you can control is set by default to 3. Those\n\nwith intelligence or wisdom over 21 receive a 1 bonus towards it, and is given\n\nan additional 1 bonus if you have the unit tactics skill.\n\n
175	brandish	0	brandish	Syntax: brandish\n\nBrandishes a magical staff held in your hand, releasing one charge of its\nstored spell. The staff must be equipped in a hold slot (left or right hand)\nand must have charges remaining.\n\nWhen brandished, the staff's stored spell is cast, targeting appropriate\ncharacters in the room based on the spell type:\n  - Offensive spells target enemies in the room.\n  - Defensive spells target allies and the caster.\n  - Self-only spells affect only the caster.\n\nThe staff loses one charge per use. When all charges are exhausted the staff\nbecomes empty and can no longer be brandished.\n\nBrandish imposes a 2-pulse wait state regardless of success.\n\nRestrictions:\n  - Must be holding a STAFF-type item.\n  - Staff must have at least one charge remaining (value[2] > 0).\n\nSee also: recite quaff\n
176	greeting2	-1	greeting2	@@d         _    ____ _  __ _   _ _____ _   _  ____ @@N\n@@d        / \\  / ___| |/ /| \\ | |_   _| \\ | |/ ___|@@N\n@@d       / _ \\| |   | ' / |  \\| | | | |  \\| | |  _ @@N\n@@d      / ___ \\ |___| . \\ | |\\  | | | | |\\  | |_| |@@N\n@@d     /_/   \\_\\____|_|\\_\\|_| \\_| |_| |_| \\_|\\____|@@N\n@@d                         @@yTNG@@N\n\n@@c    Diku Mud was created by Hans Henrik St{rfeldt, Katja Nyboe,\n@@c    Tom Madsen, Michael Seifert and Sebastian Hammer.\n@@c    MERC Modifications made by: Furey, Hatchet, Kahn@@N\n\n@@g    Gather allies. Hunt relics. Challenge the unknown.@@N\n@@WBy what name do you wish to be known?@@N\n
177	build_delroom	-1	build_delroom	BUILD HELP : DELROOM\n--------------------\nThe DELROOM command allows you to delete a room.\nSyntax:  DELROOM <room-vnum>\nIf the room-vnum is found in your current area, and no one is currently in it,\nthe room will be flagged for deletion, and you will be asked to enter DELROOM OK\nto actually delete it.\n
178	umbral	0	Umbral	Shadow given permanent form, the Umbral are humanoids whose bodies incorporated\nanti-light over generations of habitation in zones adjacent to the Black Sun Shard.\nTheir substance is as much darkness as flesh: partially insubstantial, difficult to\nperceive clearly, and healing most efficiently in shadow rather than light. The\nGloamvault beneath Midgaard is their most ancient habitation — the city was built\nabove them, not the other way around. They maintain shadow-archives whose parallel\nrecords document what the human institutions above them would rather suppress, and\nboth Midgaard's factions treat them as simultaneously a resource and a threat.\n
