180	sentinel	0	sentinel	@@yHISTORY@@W\n\nThe Sentinel tradition descends from the Jackal Tribunal's sentence enforcers\n— practitioners who carried out verdicts through disciplined physical\nintervention rather than priestly magic. When the Solar Court collapsed, the\nTribunal's intellectual methods were absorbed by the Cleric tradition and its\nmilitant remnants devolved into the Jackal Synod. But the sentence enforcers\npreserved a third path: the Tribunal's embodied practice of reading subjects,\napplying measured restraining force, and ending confrontations through precise\nphysical action informed by deep observation.\n\n@@ySENTINEL@@W\n\nSentinels are WIS-based melee combatants who fight through perceptive judgment\nrather than raw power. Their combat methodology descends from the Tribunal's\ncore competency: reading multiple signals (posture, breath, weapon angle,\nfooting) and synthesizing them into a predictive model of the opponent's intent.\n\n@@yPassive class abilities@@W\n  * @@wTestimonial Guard@@W (level 12): WIS-scaled resistance to fear, charm,\n    and mental effects. At 5+ testimony marks, immunity to fear.\n  * @@wMeasured Response@@W (level 30): chance to counter-attack after a\n    successful parry or dodge. Generates testimony on proc.\n\n@@yUnique Sentinel mechanics@@W\n  * Prime mortal attribute is @@wWisdom@@W.\n  * @@wTestimony@@W: marks accumulated on a single target through successful\n    defensive reading (dodge, parry, block). See @@mhelp testimony@@W.\n  * @@wVerdict@@W: spend testimony marks for a single devastating strike whose\n    damage and debuff scale with marks. See @@mhelp verdict@@W.\n  * Best against tough, durable targets — the Sentinel's power increases the\n    longer they fight the same opponent.\n  * 6 HP / 1 Mana per level — medium durability, survives through avoidance.\n\nSee also: @@mtestimony verdict vigilance read opponent binding strike\nninth descent condemn seal testimony@@W\n
