185	forestsight	0	forestsight	Your eyes attune to the forest, granting the ability to detect hidden.\nDruid spell. Uses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
186	build_building	-1	build_building	BUILD HELP : BUILDING\n---------------------\nBUILDING is a term used to refer to adding Rooms, Mobiles or Objects to the\nmud, whilst still playing it, allowing possibly instant inclusion of the\nrooms/mobs/objects into gameplay.\nThe builder allows to you to add new mobiles, rooms or objects.  It is up to\nyou how they look and act.  You have complete control over how your area looks.\nBear in mind that if you make objects that are too powerful, you may be asked\nto tone them down in power.  If this does not happen, then a staff member will\nhave to do it.... \nYou should decide a level range for your area, and build your mobs ABOVE that\nrange.  It is usually wise to check with a Creator about the theme of your\narea, AND the level range.\n
187	caravan	0	caravan	Syntax: caravan <city>\n\nBoards a departing caravan wagon at the Caravan Square in Midgaard and\ntravels directly to another city's caravan quarter.\n\nAvailable destinations:\n  Kiess    - The forest-edge trade hub on Roc Road\n  Kowloon  - The delta port city to the south\n  Mafdet   - The desert harbor city\n  Rakuen   - The eastern Canopy Compact city\n\nRequirements:\n  - You must be standing at the Caravan Square in Midgaard (the central\n    plaza of Midgaard's caravan quarter).\n  - You must have completed the cartographic survey quest for the target\n    city. Each city's postmaster in Midgaard offers a city district survey\n    commission; completing and turning in that quest records your knowledge\n    of the city's layout in the caravan routing records.\n  - You cannot board a caravan while engaged in combat.\n\nThe caravan master consults the transit authority's navigation records\nbefore accepting passengers. Without a completed survey on file, the\nrouting office cannot confirm safe arrival, and passage is refused.\n\nPartial city names are accepted (e.g. 'caravan kow' for Kowloon).\n\nSee also: recall, quest\n
188	kill	0	kill	Syntax: kill <target>\n\nStarts combat against a target.\n
189	condemn	0	condemn	@@yCondemn@@W                                              Sentinel level 45\n\nSyntax: condemn\n\nFormally denounce your current target, applying a WIS-scaled debuff that\nreduces saves and AC for 5 rounds. Requires 3 or more testimony marks\nagainst the target — you need sufficient observation before pronouncing\njudgment.\n\n@@yDetails:@@W\n  * Mana cost: 15\n  * Saves penalty: WIS / 3 (7 at WIS 22).\n  * AC penalty: WIS / 2 (11 at WIS 22).\n  * Does NOT consume testimony marks — they remain for a future verdict.\n  * Cannot stack (one condemn at a time per target).\n\nThe condemn-then-verdict sequence is the Sentinel's peak burst: condemn to\nlower saves, then deliver a high-mark verdict for maximum impact.\n\nSee also: @@msentinel verdict testimony@@W\n
190	cleric	0	cleric	@@aHISTORY@@W\n\nThe cleric tradition descends from the five-office priesthood of the Solar\nCourt of the Undivided Disk, whose Dawn Liturgists and Seal College priests\nmaintained the cosmological machinery that kept the Black Sun Shard dormant\nbeneath the Great Pyramid. As the Solar Court fractured after the Ninth\nMeridian Catastrophe, surviving covenant-keepers fled the desert and sought\nalignment with the civic institutions of the crossroads cities. The Violet\nCompact era gave them formal standing: clerics became the civic-sanctioned\nchannel for divine covenant, their rites documented under registry supervision\nand their shrines positioned at watched squares within city walls. The tradition\nholds that faith is not sentiment but infrastructure — a binding that holds the\nworld's deeper catastrophes at bay, and must be maintained with the same\nprecision the Keepers once applied to water and shadow.\n\n@@aCLERIC@@W\n\nClerics are keepers of sacred covenant, shaping divine force through faith and\nrite. They stand between ruin and renewal, turning conviction into miracles.\n\n@@aPassive class abilities@@W\n  * @@wSpell Critical Damage@@W (unlocked at mortal level 20): increases\n    spell critical multiplier by @@w2 x Wisdom@@W.\n\n@@aUnique Cleric mechanics@@W\n  * Prime mortal attribute is @@wWisdom@@W.\n  * Excels at high-impact spell spikes when criticals land, making Cleric a\n    strong base for holy and support-caster progressions.\n\n@@aCleric reincarnation bonuses@@W\n  * Every @@w2 Cleric reincarnations@@W (rounded up) increases max\n    @@wWisdom@@W by 1.\n  * At @@w1+ Cleric reincarnation@@W, @@wSpell Critical Damage@@W is\n    permanently unlocked for all future class paths.\n\nSee also: @@mreincarnate remort paladin priest@@W\n
191	greensight	0	greensight	Your eyes glow with verdant light, granting both infravision and detect hidden.\nDruid spell. Uses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
192	build_otypes	-1	build_otypes	OBJECT TYPES:\n+===============+=======================================================+\n| Object Type\t|\t\t\tDescription\t\t\t|\n+---------------+-------------------------------------------------------+\n| LIGHT\t\t| Object provides light for the room it is held in.\t|\n| SCROLL\t| 3-spells, affects one target.\t\t\t\t| \n| WAND\t\t| One spell, usually aggresive; one target.\t\t|\n| STAFF\t\t| One spell, affects each character in room.\t\t|\n| WEAPON\t| Can be wielded, and used in combat.\t\t\t|\n| TREASURE\t| Item is treasure, usually jewels, etc.\t\t|\n| ARMOR\t\t| Can be worn to protect the player.\t\t\t|\n| POTION\t| Can be quaffed to affect the user only. (no_save)\t|\n| CLUTCH\t| Reserved for special objects.  Ask before using!\t|\n| FURNITURE\t| Players may rest on these objects.\t\t\t|\n| TRASH\t\t| Object doesn't really do anything at all :)\t\t|\n| CONTAINER\t| Can be used to put items in.\t\t\t\t|\n| DRINK_CON\t| Drink Container.\t\t\t\t\t|\n| KEY\t\t| Opens a certain door. (no_save)\t\t\t|\n| FOOD\t\t| Object may be eaten.\t\t\t\t\t|\n| MONEY\t\t| Object is converted to GP when picked up.\t\t|\n| BOAT\t\t| Can be used to cross water.\t\t\t\t|\n| CORPSE\t| Object is a corpse...\t\t\t\t\t|\n| FOUNTAIN\t| Players may drink from this.\t\t\t\t|\n| PILL\t\t| Like a potion, but eaten.\t\t\t\t|\n| BOARD\t\t| Bulletin Board.  Ask before using, please!\t\t|\n+===============+=======================================================+\n
193	stance	0	stance	Syntax: stance [name]\n\nChanges or displays your current combat stance.\n
194	psionicist	0	psionicist	@@GHISTORY@@W\n\nThe psionicist tradition has the most contested origin in the world. The\nSpirebound Conclave's Pale Ledger faction — practitioners of spirit imprinting\nand iterative memory extraction — are the most documented predecessors, though\npsionicists themselves rarely claim that lineage openly. A parallel thread runs\nthrough the Void Citadel's recurrence technology, which weaponized testimony\nreplay to dissolve resistance by collapsing the distinction between memory and\npresent experience. Whatever the genealogy, the practical discipline emerged in\neras when the most dangerous institutions were those that controlled what could\nbe known and remembered: the Kel'Shadra witness order, the Great Pyramid's\nSeal College, the Conclave's cognitive programs. Psionicists are the inheritors\nof that contested space — minds trained to reach past surface resistance into\nthe architecture of will itself, turning thought into force the way earlier\ninstitutions turned record-keeping into control.\n\n@@GPSIONICIST@@W\n\nPsionicists turn thought into weapon and ward, overwhelming enemies through\nfocused will, mental pressure, and disciplined control of unseen force.\n\n@@GPassive class abilities@@W\n  * @@wPsionic lifesteal potency scaling@@W: lifesteal amount gains\n    @@w+0.1% per Psionicist level@@W (before final lifesteal multiplier).\n  * @@wSpell Critical@@W (unlocked at mortal level 20): grants a flat\n    @@w+5% spell critical chance@@W.\n\n@@GUnique Psionicist mechanics@@W\n  * Prime mortal attribute is @@wIntelligence@@W.\n  * Establishes a high-consistency spell-crit baseline for caster paths that\n    value frequent critical procs over single-hit spikes.\n\n@@GPsionicist reincarnation bonuses@@W\n  * Every @@w2 Psionicist reincarnations@@W (rounded up) increases max\n    @@wIntelligence@@W by 1.\n  * At @@w1+ Psionicist reincarnation@@W, @@wSpell Critical@@W is permanently\n    unlocked for all future class paths.\n\nSee also: @@mreincarnate remort necromancer egomancer@@W\n
