202	egomancer	0	egomancer	@@mEGOMANCER@@W\n\n@@mHistory@@W\n  Egomancers emerged from within the Psionicist tradition itself, specifically\n  from the Assertion Wing: a school of thought that argued the mind's primary\n  power lay not in perception or communication but in imposition. Early\n  Assertionists developed techniques for overriding external cognitive\n  processes, bending probability through focused intent, and sustaining\n  mental pressure across extended engagements rather than delivering single\n  decisive bursts. Their methods were considered extreme by conservative\n  academies and several Assertion teachers were expelled. The expelled faculty\n  simply founded independent schools. Psionicists who return through the\n  mortal path and commit to the imposition doctrine become Egomancers --\n  practitioners of the Assertion Wing's full and unfettered philosophy.\n\nEgomancers bend force of will into weaponized cognition. They do not overpower\nthrough brute spell volume, but through pressure, disruption, and focused mindfire.\n\n@@mPassive class advantages@@W\n  * @@wRemort non-physical damage@@W bonus\n    (+0.5% per level, up to +50% at 100).\n  * @@wPsionic-recovery healing@@W scales with Egomancer remort levels\n    (+2% per level, up to +200% at 100 on that healing line).\n\n@@mUnique Egomancer mechanics@@W\n  * Access to @@wEgomancer stance@@W (dual-cast / no-hit caster posture).\n  * Primary remort bridge into mental-pressure Kinetimancer play.\n  * Uses @@wIntelligence@@W as prime remort attribute.\n\n@@mEgomancer reincarnation bonuses@@W\n  * @@wNecromancer + Egomancer remort reincarnations >= 20@@W unlocks\n    @@wEquip Wand@@W permanently.\n\nSee also: @@mremort stance necromancer kinetimancer reincarnate@@W\n
203	build_delmobile	-1	build_delmobile	BUILD HELP : DELMOBILE\n----------------------\nThe DELMOBILE command allows you to delete a mobile from an area.\nSyntax:  DELMOBILE <mob-vnum>\nThis will flag the mob with the specified mob-vnum to be deleted.  You will\nneed to enter DELMOBILE OK in order for it to be actually deleted.\n
204	ack	-1	ack ackmud	@@N-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n@@k)\n\n)@@N\n\n         Ack!Mud 2.0 is Copyright (C)1995/6 Stimpy & Thalen\n\n         Ack!Mud 4.3 is Copyright (C)1998 by Stephen Zepp\n\n@@k)@@N\n\n            Ack!Mud 4.3 by Zenithar, with mucho help from:\n\n             Ramias, Altrag, Spectrum, Flar, and Universe\n\n@@k)@@N\n\n Ack! Mud is a derivative of Merc Muds, which are derivatives of Diku Muds.\n\n In order to run this code, you must observe the conditions of use\n\n of Merc and Diku.\n\n@@k)@@N\n\n Conditions of use for Ack!Mud are as follows:\n\n - Must retain copyright messages in all code.\n\n - Stimpy, Thalen and Zenithar must be credited on greeting screen.\n\n@@k)@@N\n\n Thanks to:\n\n ...Maharet, Requiem and Rupert from the original Ack! for all their help.\n\n ...ACK!TNG for carrying the tradition forward\n\n ...The guys&gals at Diku and Merc for writing the original code  (:\n\n@@k)@@N\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=- \n\n
205	strangling_vines	0	strangling vines	Thick vines wrap around your enemy, dealing earth damage and\nreducing their dexterity with a snare effect.\nDruid spell. Uses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
206	build_flags	-1	build_flags	BULD HELP : FLAGS\n-----------------\nFlags are used to represent many different values.  Becasue of the way they are\nimplemented, this means a saving in space.  One integer can store MANY different\nflags.  For the use of ther builder, a flag is a certain type of attribute, \nthat can be either on or off; true or flase; yes or no.\nFor example, rooms use flags to store such information as 'dark', 'no_recall',\n'indoors' etc.  When a new object, room or mobile is created, some flags will\nbe set my default.  In order to set it to be whatver you wish, you will need\nto set the flags properly.\n
207	exits	0	exits	Syntax: exits\n\nShows visible exits from the current room.\n
208	look	0	look	Syntax: look [target]\n\nDisplays the room or examines a target.\n
209	worth	0	worth	WORTH simply displays a list of any classes you are able to level in,\nalong with the cost in exp to gain in it, and the difference between that\ncost and your current exp.
210	pkok	1	pkok	PKOK -player killing\n\nOnce flagged as pkok the flag WILLNOT be removed\n\nit is a choice for life....\n\nWhat this means is that other players flagged as\n\n@@ePKOK@@N will not be punished if they should so happen\n\nto kill you....\n\nThere are consequences.....\n\nOne of which includes your corpse does not get returned to Moribund\n\nand you must go to where you were killed...\n\n@@eONCE PKOK ALWAYS PKOK!!!@@N\n\n
211	wield	0	wield	Syntax: wield <item>\n\nWields a weapon in your wield slot.\n
212	build_forcereset	-1	build_forcereset	BUILD HELP : FORCERESET\n-----------------------\nThe FORCERESET command allows you to execute all resets within the current area.\nSyntax:  FORCERESET\nThis will read through each reset, and if applicable, will load objects or mobs,\nequip mobs, set door states, etc.  BE WARNED!  Any aggressive mobiles that are\nloaded are just that - aggressive!  In other words you'll be a valid target, \neven if you are in building mode.\n
216	alias	0	alias	The ALIAS command allows you configure the six alias 'slots'.  An alias\ntakes the form of a name, and the alias.  To set up a new alias, type:\nALIAS <slot_number> <name> <alias>\t\tFor example:\nALIAS 2 ban emote turns into a banana and splits...\nNow, whenever you type 'ban' the mud checks through the command table.  If\nyour input wasn't found, it then checks your alias.  Upon matching 'ban'\nit issues the alias to the interpreter function, along with any argument\nyou typed after the alias name.  For example, you can define an alias:\nALIAS 1 ff cast 'faerie fire'   and then use it on mobs by typing:\nff <target_name>.  So typing 'ff stephen' will cause the mud to interpret\ncast faerie fire stephen.\nTo show what aliases are set, type ALIAS with no arguements.\nTo clear an alias, type 'ALIAS <number> clear'.
217	tangling_roots	0	tangling roots	Roots burst from the ground and tangle around your enemy, lowering their\narmor class like faerie fire.\nDruid spell. Uses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
218	crusade	1	crusade crusades	Crusades are auto quests that random mobs, depending on the average level of\nthe players logged on at the time. You must find the mob that stole the item,\nget the item, and return it to the mob that wants it back.\nSome questions you can ask on the crusade channel:\nwhere are you?\nwhere is the thief?
219	assist	0	assist	Syntax: assist <ally>\n\nJoins combat to help an ally already fighting.\n
220	druid	0	druid	@@aDruid@@N\n\nDruids are nature casters who channel the raw power of earth and\npoison through their own bodies. Unlike other spellcasters, Druid\nspells cost @@eHP@@N instead of mana, and each cast builds\n@@aOvergrowth@@N -- a rising tide of natural energy that increases\nboth the power and the cost of subsequent spells.\n\n@@WRemort paths:@@N Thornwarden (tank) and Wildspeaker (utility)\n@@WAdept path:@@N Hierophant (requires both Thornwarden and Wildspeaker)\n\nSee also: @@WOVERGROWTH@@N, @@WSUBSTRATE PIERCING@@N\n
221	build_editor	-1	build_editor	BUILD HELP : USING THE EDITOR\n-----------------------------\nUsing the editor, it is possible to edit any strings you need.  The most \ncommon of these will be room descriptions.\nTo enter the editor, enter '$edit' as the string.  So, in Redit mode:\n'desc $edit'  will allow you to edit the room's description.\nTo format the string, type '.f'\nTo see what other options are available, type '.h'\nTo finish editing a string, type '.'\n
222	build_showarea	-1	build_showarea	BUILD HELP : SHOWAREA\n---------------------\nThe SHOWAREA command displays various details about the area, Ranging from the\nowner, to the minimum and maximum vnums allowed.  \n
223	verdant_mend	0	verdant mend	Verdant energy washes over the target, providing substantial healing.\nDruid spell. Uses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
224	rivennid	0	Rivennid	The Spirebound Conclave's most unsettling legacy, the Rivennid emerged when the\nConclave's abandoned crystal-preservation trials fused with the Withered Depths' fungal\nnetworks, producing custodial intelligences housed in mycelium rather than the human\nsubjects the Conclave intended. They are what the Vaultkeeper project was meant to\ncreate, completed by accident in a medium no one designed. Crystal fragments from the\noriginal matrices remain embedded in their bodies; they are connected to one another\nthrough the same mycelium network that gave them life. They chose, upon emergence, to\nguard the forest that made them — and have since broadened that mandate to the wider\nworld the Conclave's carelessness damaged.\n
225	staff	0	staff	Due to some past events where common sense was overlooked\nit was brought to the attentions of the staff that there is a\nproblem in mortal/staff relations.\nThe way the staff team is run here is very leniant and laid back, much\nless strict then those upon other Multi-User Domains. The point that\nis trying to be made is simply to respect those who do rule upon the realms.\nThis has not been a wide spread problem but one that needed to be\naddressed. Those staff who you are aware that multi-play with mort\ncharacters as well, remember that they are seperate entities in the realms.\nAll characters deserve respect....wether they be friend or foe.\nRemember that anyone being rude or distasteful to not only staff\nbut ALSO other morts will be dealt with accordingly.\n
226	guild	0	guild	GUILD is similar to RECALL in use, except that it transfers you (if possible)\nto your Guild room, in the Player's Rooms, west of the Temple.  They provide\nan easy way to gain entrance to a Guild Room.  If fighting, the same penalties\nstand as for recall.
227	lore	0	lore	Syntax: lore [topic]\n\nLooks up lore on a topic. With no argument, displays a general lore overview.\n\nDisplays a historical description of the topic. NPCs may also use this\ncommand, in which case they receive information specifically relevant to\ntheir own context rather than the general account.\n
228	drink	0	drink	Syntax: drink <container>\n\nDrinks from a drink container or fountain.\n
229	stand	0	stand	Syntax: stand\n\nStands up from resting/sleeping position.\n
230	mend_wounds	0	mend wounds	Natural energy knits your wounds together, providing moderate healing.\nDruid spell. Uses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
231	greeting1	-1	greeting1	@@g    Welcome to ACK!TNG - where legends begin and stories never end.@@N\n\n@@c    Diku Mud was created by Hans Henrik St{rfeldt, Katja Nyboe,\n@@c    Tom Madsen, Michael Seifert and Sebastian Hammer.\n@@c    MERC Modifications made by: Furey, Hatchet, Kahn@@N\n\n@@y    ACK!TNG carries the ACK! tradition forward with fresh adventures,\n@@y    classic danger, and a world shaped by its players.@@N\n\n@@WWhat is your name?@@N\n
232	affected	0	affected	Syntax: affected\n\nShows temporary spell/skill effects currently on your character.\n
233	know_terrain	0	know terrain	Attune to the terrain around you, revealing the alignment of creatures.\nFunctions like know alignment.\nDruid spell. Uses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
234	binding_strike	0	binding strike	@@yBinding Strike@@W                                       Sentinel level 22\n\nSyntax: binding strike\n\nA precise melee strike targeting structural weaknesses identified through\nobservation. Deals 1.5x weapon damage and reduces the target's dodge and\nparry for 3 rounds.\n\n@@yDetails:@@W\n  * Mana cost: 5\n  * Does not generate testimony (you are acting, not observing).\n  * Debuff does not stack with itself.\n  * Bread-and-butter offensive skill between verdict cycles.\n\nSee also: @@msentinel verdict condemn@@W\n
235	list	0	list	Syntax: list\n\nLists items sold by a shopkeeper.\n
236	detox	0	detox	Syntax: detox\n\nAttempts to purge poison from your system through sheer physical endurance\nand trained resistance. Detox is a passive/active skill available to rogues\nand certain combat classes.\n\nSuccess at removing poison depends on your learned proficiency in the skill.\nAt higher skill levels, detox is more reliably effective. Unlike the magical\n"cure poison" spell, detox requires no mana and works through physical\ntraining alone.\n\nUse detox as soon as you notice a poison effect to prevent ongoing damage.\n\nRequirements:\n  - Must have the Detox skill learned.\n  - Must be poisoned (or the skill will have no effect).\n\nSee also: shelp detox cure poison poison\n
238	pummel	0	pummel	Syntax: pummel <target>\n\nDelivers a rapid series of unarmed blows using the Pugilist attack system.\nPummel represents the core repeated-strike technique of the Pugilist class,\nemphasizing quick successive hits over single powerful blows.\n\nPummel is available to Pugilist-class characters and their remort\ndescendants (Monk, Brawler, Martial Artist).\n\nRequirements:\n  - Must be in combat or initiates combat on the target.\n  - Target must be present in the room.\n  - Must have the skill learned.\n\nSee also: shelp pummel punch aurabolt palmstrike spinfist\n
239	rules	0	RULES RULE	@@YACK!MUD TNG — Rules@@N\n\nThere are three rules.  They cover everything.\n\n@@R#1  Don't be a dick.@@N\n\n  This applies to players, to staff, and to the game itself.  Griefing,\n  harassment, deliberate abuse of mechanics to ruin someone else's\n  experience — all of it falls here.  Use your judgment.  If you have to\n  ask whether something counts, it probably does.\n\n@@R#2  If you make staff take action, everyone involved loses.@@N\n\n  When a dispute or violation requires staff intervention, the response\n  will not be surgical.  Everyone involved — instigator, participants,\n  bystanders who made it worse — can expect denial, IPban, or deletion.\n  No warnings, no appeals, no reimbursements.\n\n  Do not waste the staff's time.  Do not drag others into situations\n  that will cost them their characters.\n\n@@R#3  Multiplaying is allowed.  Automation is not.@@N\n\n  You may run up to @@c3 characters simultaneously@@N.  Play them however\n  you like, including having them interact with each other.\n\n  @@eFully automated, scripted, unattended play is prohibited.@@N  A\n  trigger that fires a spell or command in response to a prompt is fine.\n  A bot that plays the game for you while you are away is not.\n  Automated play discovered by staff will be treated as a Rule #2\n  violation — meaning everyone on the account and any associated\n  accounts should expect consequences.\n\n@@b---------------------------------------------------------------------@@N\n\n  That is the entire ruleset.  It is intentionally short because the\n  goal is a game people want to play, not a legal document.\n\n  See also:  @@cHELP NEWBIE@@N   @@cHELP IMM@@N\n
240	clan	0	CLAN CLANS	@@yCLANS@@g\n\nClans are player-run political organizations on Shades of Evil. Each clan\nhas its own identity, leadership, and standing in the world. Clan membership\nis visible in @@ywho@@g, @@yscore@@g, and @@yfinger@@g.\n\nA player may belong to one clan, one @@ypublic society@@g, and one\n@@ysecret society@@g at the same time. These three affiliation systems are\nindependent of each other.\n\n@@yCLAN MEMBERSHIP@@g\n\nClan membership is managed by staff using the @@ycset@@g command.\nContact the staff if you wish to join a clan.\n\nYour clan affiliation grants you @@yclan colors@@g — a wearable item bearing\nyour clan's emblem. Use @@yclaneq@@g to choose the stat focus of your colors:\n\n  @@yclaneq melee@@g    -- Optimized for melee fighters (hitroll, damroll)\n  @@yclaneq caster@@g   -- Optimized for spellcasters (mana, spell stats)\n  @@yclaneq tank@@g     -- Optimized for defensive roles (HP, armor)\n\n@@yCLAN CHANNEL@@g\n\n  @@yclan <message>@@g  -- Sends a message to all online clan members\n\n@@yCLAN COMMANDS@@g\n\n  @@yclan <message>@@g  -- Speak on the clan communication channel\n  @@yclaneq <style>@@g  -- Set your clan colors to melee, caster, or tank\n  @@yclist@@g           -- List all clans and basic clan information\n  @@yhome@@g            -- Recall directly to your clan headquarters\n  @@yleave@@g           -- Voluntarily depart from your clan\n\n@@yOTHER AFFILIATIONS@@g\n\nBeyond clans, two additional affiliation systems exist:\n\n  @@yPublic Societies@@g -- Open civic institutions (Guard Command, Harbor\n    Syndics, Ember Wardens, Shrine of the First Claw, Wall Command, Road\n    Wardens). Membership is visible, open to qualified applicants, and grants\n    rank-gated skills and task-board missions. Use @@yenlist@@g at a society\n    hall to join. A player may belong to one public society at a time.\n\n  @@ySecret Societies@@g -- Hidden covert organizations (The Reckoning, The\n    Jade Eels, The Ash Cult, The Quiet Hand, The Jackal Synod, The Pale\n    Ledger). Membership is concealed from public commands. Discovery requires\n    finding the right contacts in the world. A player may belong to one\n    secret society at a time.\n\nSee also: clist claneq home rulers\n
241	kinetimancer	0	kinetimancer	@@GHISTORY@@W\n\nThe Kinetimancer synthesis arose from a collision between two traditions\nthat spent centuries in philosophical opposition. The Entropy Scholars --\npredecessors of the Necromancer path -- held that understanding dissolution\nwas fundamental to understanding existence; the Egomancer lineage within\nthe Psionicist academies held that pure mental will could override any\nentropic tendency if properly refined. The structural similarity beneath\nthat opposition went unnoticed until a small independent order, the Kinetic\nFormulists, documented it in the pre-Compact period: both traditions were\nworking with momentum -- one redirecting the momentum of decay, the other\nredirecting the momentum of imposed intent. Their manuscripts were reviewed\nby the Violet Compact's registry scholars upon the Compact's founding, who\nclassified the convergence as dangerous theoretical synthesis and logged its\npractitioners under a new registry term -- Kinetimancer. That bureaucratic\nlabel became the tradition's name, carried forward by practitioners who\nfound the Compact's unease to be confirmation enough.\n\n@@GKINETIMANCER@@W\n\nKinetimancers are the union of @@GNecromancer@@W entropy and @@mEgomancer@@W will,\nengineers of unseen force who bend shadow, poison, and mind-pressure into a\nsingle predictive combat style. They do not simply cast spells—they re-route\nmomentum and collapse enemy plans before impact.\n\nTo become a Kinetimancer, you must master either @@GNecromancer@@W or\n@@mEgomancer@@W (remort prerequisites for the adept path).\n\n@@GPassive class advantages@@W\nKinetimancer gains passive scaling through adept levels:\n\n  1) @@wRemort/Adept non-physical spell damage bonus@@W\n     - Non-physical remort/adept damage effects gain a passive Kinetimancer\n       multiplier.\n     - Scaling: +2% damage per Kinetimancer adept level (up to +40% at 20).\n\n@@GUnique Kinetimancer mechanics@@W\n  * @@wMagi stance@@W is available on the adept path (shared caster stance with\n    either-class access, multi-cast support, dual-cast support, and no-hit\n    casting posture).\n  * @@wKinetic Reversion@@W is learned at Kinetimancer level 2.\n  * Kinetimancer contributes to the @@wMental Power@@W progression family.\n  * Kinetimancer uses @@wIntelligence@@W as its adept prime attribute and follows\n    a high-mana caster growth profile.\n\n@@GKinetimancer reincarnation bonuses@@W\nEach Kinetimancer adept reincarnation grants additional passive scaling:\n\n  * @@wShadow / poison / mental damage@@W: +2% per Kinetimancer adept\n    reincarnation.\n\nIn short: Kinetimancer is the control-burst adept for dark and psychic realms,\nrewarding players who maintain pressure through layered non-physical damage.\n\nSee also: @@mremort stance kinetic reversion mental-power@@W\n
242	bash	0	bash	Syntax: bash <target>\n\nAttempts to knock an opponent down in combat.\n
243	sthelp	0	sthelp	Syntax: sthelp [stance]\n\nShows stance-specific help topics.\n
244	train	0	TRAIN	Syntax: train <'str'|'int'|'wis'|'dex'|'con'>\nTRAIN increases one of your attributes.  When you start the game, your\ncharacter has slightly random attributes.  The maximum value for each\nattribute depends on your race and class.\nIt costs four practice to train an attribute, except that it costs\nonly three practice to train your prime attribute.\nThe best attributes to train first are WIS and CON.  WIS gives you more\npractice when you gain a level.  CON gives you more hit points.\nIn the long run, your character will be most powerful if you train\nWIS and CON both to 18 before practising or training anything else.\nTrain now reports the cost in practice points to increase an attribute.\nIt is also possible to spend practices on hit points or mana points.
245	down	0	down	Syntax: down\n\nMoves one room down, if an exit exists.\n
246	build_medit	-1	build_medit	BUILD HELP : MEDIT\n------------------\nThe MEDIT command places you in Mobile EDITing mode.\nSyntax:  MEDIT [mob-vnum]\nThis will allow you to edit information concerning mobiles.  To set which mobile\nyou wish to work on, either enter a mob-vnum after MEDIT, or use the SETVNUM\ncommand.  Anything you type will be checked to see if it applies to mobiles,\nand if so, the value, flag or string specified will be set.\n
247	colour	0	colour color	Firstly, please note the spelling: coloUr.  This is an English mud, so we\nuse English spellings :)\nThe mud now supports "ansi" colour.  Use the config command to turn on\nor off this option.  The COLOUR command allows you to set uo what colours\nyou see different things in.  Please note:  The list of things you can\nconfigure WILL be expanding!\nTo find out what colours are available, type 'COLOUR HELP'.
248	kethari	0	Kethari	Serpentine humanoids of the Saltglass Reach, the Kethari are witnesses to the desert's\ndeep history. Their water-memories of the Deepwell Confluence predate the Keeper surveys\nand exceed anything human instrumentation can produce; their Aquifer Covenant, maintained\nas oral tradition and verified at coil-gatherings, has governed eastern water rights\nlonger than any human institution has existed. Patient beyond the measure of other\npeoples, the Kethari have watched civilizations rise and collapse across timescales that\nmake institutional permanence look like a brief disturbance on the surface of much deeper\ntime. They continue accumulating the record of what passes before them, and they remember\nwhich institutions received their knowledge and failed to credit it.\n
249	examine	0	examine	Syntax: examine <target>\n\nLooks closely at an object, character, or detail.\n
250	punch	0	punch	Syntax: punch <target>\n\nDelivers a standard punch to an opponent. Punch is a basic Pugilist-line\nunarmed attack skill handled by the Warrior attack system. It is one of\nthe foundational unarmed techniques and is available to most combat classes\nthat train unarmed fighting.\n\nRequirements:\n  - Must be in combat or initiates combat on the target.\n  - Target must be present in the room.\n  - Must have the skill learned.\n\nSee also: shelp punch pummel aurabolt palmstrike kick\n
251	leadership	1	leadership	
252	fissure	0	fissure	The ground splits beneath your enemy, dealing massive earth damage.\nDruid spell. Uses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
253	compare	0	compare	Syntax: compare <item> <item>\n\nCompares two items and reports relative value/power.\n
254	auction	0	AUCTION GOSSIP . NEWBIE INVASION QUESTION ANSWER SHOUT YELL FLAME ZZZ MUSIC	Syntax: auction  <message>      Syntax: gossip   <message>\nSyntax: newbie   <message>      Syntax: invasion <message>\nSyntax: question <message>      Syntax: answer   <message>\nSyntax: shout    <message>      Syntax: yell     <message>\nSyntax: zzz      <message>      Syntax: flame    <message>\nSyntax: race     <message>      Syntax: clan     <message>\nsyntax: music    <message>\nYELL sends a message to all awake players within your area.\nRACE sends a message to members of your own race.  CLAN sends a message to\nthose in your clan.\nYou can use the CHANNELS command to hear, or not hear, any of these channels.\n\nTyping a channel name with no message shows the last 15 messages on that\nchannel.  For example, typing just GOSSIP replays recent gossip traffic.\n
255	inventory	0	inventory	Syntax: inventory\n\nShows items you are carrying.\n
256	build_list	-1	build_list	BUILD HELP : LIST | X\n---------------------\nThe LIST command has two purposes.  Firstly, it shows you details about the\nRoom, Mobile or Object you are currently working on.  Secondly, it allows\nyou find out which flags you can set for objects.\nSyntax:  LIST [flags-name]\nIf you type just LIST on its own, you will be shown details of your current\nroom, mobile or object.  If you want to see a list of flags (in wide format,\nrather than the long format used when you screw up) type LIST HELP.\nThe lists of flags you can display vary according to which editing mode you are\nin.  This is basically because there is a list of FLAGS for each mode, etc...\nX may be used in place of LIST.\n
257	halls	82	halls	HALLS is a command which will transfer you, the staff member to the Entry Point,\nsituated within the Halls of the Staff.  It is similar to recall, except\nthat there are no limitations on use if fighting, etc.  
258	say	0	say	Syntax: say <message>\n\nSpeaks to everyone in the current room.\n
259	sorcerer	0	sorcerer	@@pSORCERER@@W\n\n@@pHistory@@W\n  The Sorcerer lineage descends from the Chromatic Circle, a pre-academic\n  order of arcanists who rejected the emerging universities and their narrow\n  specializations. Where early wizards were pressured to choose a single\n  school and go deep, the Circle's founders held that the deepest power lay\n  in synthesis: fire and ice together, healing and destruction from the same\n  hand. They documented every interaction between spell schools in vast\n  libraries called the Confluence Texts. The academies eventually absorbed\n  or outlawed most Circle branches, but the tradition survived in small\n  apprentice chains. Magi who return through the mortal disciplines to\n  study synthesis rather than analysis take up the old Circle inheritance\n  and become Sorcerers in the truest sense.\n\nSorcerers are stormbinders and flame-scholars: arcanists who force raw\ncreation into disciplined patterns of ruin and restoration. Where others study\none school, Sorcerers weaponize breadth.\n\n@@pPassive class advantages@@W\n  * @@wSpell critical chance@@W increases with Sorcerer levels\n    (+0.1% per level, up to +10% at 100).\n  * @@wRemort non-physical damage@@W gains Sorcerer scaling\n    (+0.5% per level, up to +50% at 100).\n  * @@wArcane healing throughput@@W improves for INT-based arcane healing\n    (+2% per Sorcerer level, up to +200% at 100).\n\n@@pUnique Sorcerer mechanics@@W\n  * Access to @@wSorcerer stance@@W (dual-cast / no-hit caster posture).\n  * Strong synergy with elemental spell ladders and summon-style arcane play.\n  * Uses @@wIntelligence@@W as prime remort attribute.\n\n@@pSorcerer reincarnation bonuses@@W\n  * @@wWizard + Sorcerer remort reincarnations >= 20@@W unlocks\n    @@wEquip Wand@@W permanently.\n\nSee also: @@mremort stance wizard grand_magi reincarnate@@W\n
260	martial_artist	0	martial artist martialartist	@@gHISTORY@@W\n\nThe interior history of the Martial Artist tradition is a long argument\nbetween two schools that spent generations insisting they had nothing to\nlearn from each other. Monks held that the Interior Forms -- the discipline\nof breath, posture, and applied understanding developed in the mountain\nmonasteries -- were complete in themselves. Brawlers, who emerged from the\nfighting pits and harbor circuits where formal theory held no authority,\nheld that no system survived first contact with an opponent who fought\nwithout rules. The synthesis came not from agreement but from repeated\nfailure on both sides: monasteries lost students to the pit circuits, and\nexperienced pit fighters could not reliably overcome a trained Monk. Those\nwho trained in both found the disciplines did not cancel but complete each\nother -- the Brawler's ferocity supplied entry pressure the Forms lacked\nin chaotic encounters, while the Monk's structural timing turned that\nferocity into something sustainable. The first Martial Artists had spent\ntwo apprenticeships learning two halves of a single method.\n\n@@gMARTIAL ARTIST@@W\n\nMartial Artists are the perfected union of @@gMonk@@W discipline and @@gBrawler@@W\nferocity. They weaponize breath, balance, and impact timing, turning every\nexchange into a rhythm of pressure, recovery, and sudden burst.\n\nTo become a Martial Artist, you must master either @@gMonk@@W or @@gBrawler@@W\n(remort prerequisites for the adept path).\n\n@@gPassive class advantages@@W\nMartial Artist grants several always-on combat bonuses as adept levels rise:\n\n  1) @@wChi-technique damage bonus@@W\n     - Chi attacks in the palmstrike/pummel/aurabolt family gain extra damage.\n     - Scaling: +2.5% damage per Martial Artist adept level (up to +50% at 20).\n\n  2) @@wBare-hand strike damage bonus@@W\n     - Unarmed direct-hit damage is increased while using bare-hand combat.\n     - Scaling: +2% damage per Martial Artist adept level (up to +40% at 20).\n\n  3) @@wExtra attack round@@W\n     - Having any Martial Artist adept level grants an additional melee hit in\n       the multi-hit calculation.\n\n@@gUnique Martial Artist mechanics@@W\n  * @@wMartial stance@@W becomes available with the adept path.\n  * While Martial Artist adept is active, your maximum chi pool is raised to\n    @@w25@@W (supporting longer chi-combo windows).\n  * Martial Artist uses @@wConstitution@@W as its adept prime attribute and\n    follows a durable, sustained-melee growth profile.\n\n@@gMartial Artist reincarnation bonuses@@W\nEach Martial Artist adept reincarnation grants passive advantages:\n\n  * @@wDirect-hit damage@@W: +2% per Martial Artist adept reincarnation.\n  * At @@w20+ Martial Artist adept reincarnations@@W, your chi cap remains at\n    @@w25@@W even without active Martial adept levels.\n  * At @@w20+ Martial Artist adept reincarnations@@W, combo capacity gains\n    +1 slot when combo progression is active.\n\nIn short: Martial Artist is the chi-pressure adept, excelling at sustained\nunarmed aggression with strong burst conversion when resources are spent well.\n\nSee also: @@mremort chi combo palmstrike pummel aurabolt chakra chiblock stance@@W\n
261	khephari	0	Khephari	Scarab-beetle folk of the desert whose origin myths trace to the Great Scarab's passage\nthrough the earth, the Khephari are ancient, unhurried, and constitutionally tuned to\nthe desert's cyclic timescale. They built the approach roads to the Great Pyramid during\nthe Solar Court Era and continue to quietly maintain the route markers their ancestors\nset. Khephari communities near the Cinderteeth Mountains serve as seismic early-warning\nsystems, detecting volcanic activity through vibration-sense long before other peoples\nnotice a thing — warnings which human institutions have consistently received and filed\nwithout action.\n
262	whois	0	whois	Syntax: whois <player>\n\nShows profile details for a specific player.\n
263	note	0	note mail	Intermud Mail System!!!!\nThe main command is @@rNOTE@@N..all commands listed are preceded by it\n@@yTo Write:@@N\nto (name) - sets who note is going to\nsubject   - lets you write a subject\nwrite     - place you in editor to begin writing note\nedit      - also places you in editor to write note\npost      - posts your note to the player you are writing to\n@@yTo Read:@@N\nlist      - lists all letters you have received, both old and new\nread #    - readds the message number specified\nremove #  - giving the number of which note, removes it from the list\n@@GExamples!!!!@@N\nIf you were writing a letter to @@eCyberlich@@N this is how you would do it\nnote to cyberlich\nnote subject hi\nnote write (or edit) -then write message, exit editor\nnote post\nCyberlich would then type\nnote list\nnote read # of message\nnote remove # of message to delete it\n@@eALL note and mail commands must be done at a postmaster!!@@N
264	newun	-1	NEWUN	-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\t\t\tWelcome New Player!\n\t\t-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\nWelcome to ACK!MUD TNG.\n\nYou start in Midgaard.  Type @@cHELP NEWBIE@@N for a quick-start guide covering\nthe basics: gaining levels, dying, essential commands, and communication.\n\nType @@cHELP RULES@@N to read the three rules.  They are short.\n\nType @@cWORTH@@N to see how much experience you need to gain a level.\nType @@cGAIN@@N to advance a level once you have enough experience.\n\nThere is no rent.  Type @@cSAVE@@N to save, @@cQUIT@@N to exit.\n
265	prompt	0	prompt	Prompt all gives you a default prompt.\n\n %h for current HP. %H for maximum HP.\n\n %m for current mana. %M for maximum mana.\n\n %v for current move. %V for maximum move.\n\n %C for current combo count.\n\n %I for current chi.\n\n %A for current Arcane Power (mage/sorcerer/wizard/grand master stacking bonus).\n\n %P for current Holy Power (cleric/paladin/priest/templar stacking bonus).\n\n %Q for current Mental Power (psi/nec/ego/kin stacking bonus). See HELP MENTAL-POWER.\n\n %b for current bloodlust (vampires only). %B for max bloodlust.\n\n %g for gold. %x for experience.\n\n %a for alignment. %r for room name. %s for stance name.\n\n %t for current time of day.\n\n %c for a newline in the prompt.\n\n %% for a literal percent sign.\n
266	primal_restoration	0	primal restoration	Primal energy surges through the target, providing a large heal\nand curing blindness, poison, and curses.\nDruid spell. Uses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
267	eat	0	eat	Syntax: eat <item>\n\nConsumes edible food items.\n
268	other	-1	other	\n\t\t\t--OTHER--\nThe following commands are available:\n!               save            quit            practice\ntrain           cast            gain            heal\nbank            newbie\nFor more detailed help, type "HELP <command>".
269	pugilist	0	pugilist	@@gHISTORY@@W\n\nThe oldest fighting discipline in the world belongs not to armies or academies\nbut to the people who built everything else: cistern laborers who dug the\nKeeper Cistern Ring, caravan porters who hauled survey equipment across the\nScorching Sands, bound-service workers at the pyramid construction sites, and\nthe dispossessed kin displaced when the Ninth Meridian Catastrophe collapsed the\neastern road system. Without weapons, formal backing, or institutional\nprotection, these groups developed close-quarters disciplines from necessity —\ntiming, stamina, and body knowledge accumulated across generations of physical\nlabor and street survival. The pugilist tradition formalizes what they carried.\nIt is the oldest school because it was never written down, only passed body to\nbody, and it survived every collapse because it required nothing that could be\nseized, registered, or taken away.\n\n@@gPUGILIST@@W\n\nPugilists are close-quarters specialists who trust stamina, timing, and body\ncontrol over steel. They outlast opponents, then punish every opening.\n\n@@gPassive class abilities@@W\n  * @@wPugilist technique scaling@@W: palmstrike/pummel/aurabolt gain\n    @@w+0.5% damage per Pugilist level@@W.\n  * @@wCounter@@W (unlocked at mortal level 20): enables counterattacks when\n    enemies miss and your counter chance succeeds.\n\n@@gUnique Pugilist mechanics@@W\n  * Prime mortal attribute is @@wConstitution@@W.\n  * Builds toward reactive melee defense through counterplay and sustained\n    unarmed pressure.\n\n@@gPugilist reincarnation bonuses@@W\n  * Every @@w2 Pugilist reincarnations@@W (rounded up) increases max\n    @@wConstitution@@W by 1.\n  * At @@w1+ Pugilist reincarnation@@W, @@wCounter@@W is permanently unlocked\n    for all future class paths.\n\nSee also: @@mreincarnate remort monk brawler@@W\n
270	backstab	0	backstab	Syntax: backstab <target>\n\nAttempts a rogue-style surprise attack on a target.\n
