283	living_bridge	0	living bridge	You grow a living bridge of vines and roots to another location.\nFunctions like portal.\nDruid spell. Uses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
315	visible	0	visible	Syntax: visible\n\nRemoves all invisibility, concealment, and stealth effects from your\ncharacter, making you fully visible to everyone in the room. This is useful\nwhen you want to be seen after sneaking, hiding, or using invisibility spells.\n\nEffects removed by VISIBLE:\n  - Sneak (AFF_SNEAK)\n  - Invisibility (AFF_INVISIBLE)\n  - Mass Invisibility (AFF_MASS_INVIS)\n  - Hide status\n\nMessage: "You become more visible again."\n\nNote: Some effects may be reapplied by spells or skills -- for example,\nif a permanent-duration invisibility spell is active, you may need to\ndispel it specifically or allow it to wear off naturally.\n\nSee also: hide sneak shadowform invis cast dispel magic\n
284	testimony	0	testimony marks	@@yTestimony@@W is the Sentinel's class-specific combat resource — marks\naccumulated on a single target through successful defensive reading.\n\n@@yBuilding Testimony:@@W\n  * @@wDodge, Parry, or Block@@W: +1 mark per successful avoidance.\n  * @@wRead Opponent@@W (skill): instantly grants +2 marks.\n  * @@wPassive tick@@W: +1 mark every 3 combat rounds against the same target.\n  * @@wMeasured Response@@W procs: +1 mark on counter-attack.\n  * @@wNinth Descent@@W (buff): doubles all testimony gain for 4 rounds.\n  * Cap: @@w9 marks@@W maximum.\n\n@@yLosing Testimony:@@W\n  * @@wTarget switch@@W: resets to 0 (observations are specific to one foe).\n  * @@wTarget death@@W: resets to 0.\n  * @@wStun@@W: lose half marks (rounded down). @@wSeal Testimony@@W reduces\n    this to losing only 1 mark.\n  * @@wFlee/recall@@W: resets to 0.\n  * @@wOut of combat@@W: decays by 1 per tick (not instant reset).\n\n@@ySpending Testimony:@@W\n  * Use the @@wverdict@@W command to consume all marks for a single strike.\n  * Damage multiplier and secondary effects scale with marks spent.\n  * After verdict, a 2-round cooldown before testimony accumulates again.\n\n@@yKey difference from other resources:@@W\n  * Chi (Monk) builds on @@woffense@@W — +1 per successful attack.\n  * Combo (Warden) builds on @@wvaried offense@@W — auto-finisher when full.\n  * Testimony builds on @@wdefense@@W — +1 per avoidance, spend when ready.\n\nSee also: @@mverdict sentinel ninth descent seal testimony read opponent@@W\n
285	enter	0	enter	Syntax: enter <portal>\n        enter <exit keyword>\n\nMoves your character through a portal object or a specially named exit.\n\nPortal usage:\n  A portal is an object of type ITEM_PORTAL placed in the room. Entering a\n  portal teleports you to the destination room stored in the portal's data.\n  Some portals are one-way; others allow return travel.\n  - Portals cannot be used in rooms flagged as NO PORTAL.\n  - In anti-magic zones, there is a chance a portal explodes when entered.\n\nNamed exit usage:\n  Some doors or passages have keyword names beyond the standard compass\n  directions (north/south/east/west/up/down). You can pass through these\n  using 'enter <keyword>' instead of a directional command.\n\nExamples:\n  enter gate        -- Enters a portal or passage named "gate"\n  enter vortex      -- Enters a portal object called "vortex"\n\nSee also: recall gate travel portal\n
286	build_rsector	-1	build_rsector	SECTOR TYPES:\n+===============+===============+\t+===============+===============+\n| Sector Type\t| Movement Loss\t|\t| Sector Type\t| Movement Loss\t|\n+---------------+---------------+\t+---------------+---------------+\n| INSIDE\t|        1\t|\t| WATER_SWIM\t|        4\t|\n| CITY\t\t|        2\t|\t| WATER_NOSWIM\t|        1\t|\n| FIELD\t\t|        2\t|\t| UNUSED\t|        6\t|\n| FOREST\t|        3\t|\t| AIR\t\t|       10\t|\n| HILLS\t\t|        4\t|\t| DESERT\t|        6\t|\n| MOUNTAIN\t|        6\t|\t+===============+===============+\t+===============+===============+\n*WATER_NOSWIM Sectors require a boat, or a 'fly' spell.\n*AIR Sectors require the player to be affected by 'fly'.\n
287	boards	0	boards	There are now a number of _main_ boards on the game:\nINFO Board - 5 rooms west of Midgaard Temple, this is used to hold rules and\n\t     general information.  Only staff can write on this board.\nIDEA Board - In Midgaard Temple, this is intended to be used by players to\n\t     leave ideas for the mud.\nThere is also a board for players to use, for personal messages, etc.  It is\nlocated 4 rooms west, 2 rooms south of Midgaard Temple.\nTo use the boards, you must be in a room with one :)\nType: WRITE <header> to leave a message, with the specified header/title.\n      WRITE to:<name> to leave a private message.\n      READ <number> to read a message.\nTo find out what messages are on a board, simply look at it.\nThere are also several other boards in the game, for clan and race use, as\nwell as various other use.
288	brawler	0	brawler	@@gBRAWLER@@W\n\n@@gHistory@@W\n  The Brawler path has no founding text, no academy, and no claim to ancient\n  wisdom -- it arose from the fighting pits of the harbor districts, where\n  survival demanded adaptation rather than theory. Early Brawlers were simply\n  the best fighters in contested spaces: people who had learned through\n  accumulated hard experience exactly how much punishment a body could absorb\n  and deliver, and who had mastered by instinct the grinding attrition that\n  breaks opponents the mind alone cannot. Over time the best survivors passed\n  their methods to apprentices not through formal instruction but through\n  demonstration. Every technique in the Brawler's arsenal has been tested at\n  full force against opponents who were trying to kill someone. The ones that\n  survived that test are the only ones still taught.\n\nBrawlers are ruthless close-range enforcers who overwhelm opponents through\nrepetition, pressure, and punishing body mechanics.\n\n@@gPassive class advantages@@W\n  * @@wBare-hand direct-hit damage@@W bonus (+0.75% per level, up to +75% at 100).\n  * @@wCombo-family strike damage@@W bonus on remort/adept combo attacks\n    (+1.5% per level, up to +150% at 100).\n  * @@wMartial strike damage@@W bonus for palmstrike/pummel/aurabolt family\n    (+0.375% per level, up to +37.5% at 100).\n\n@@gUnique Brawler mechanics@@W\n  * Access to @@wBrawler stance@@W.\n  * Excellent bridge between combo pressure and unarmed sustained damage.\n  * Uses @@wConstitution@@W as prime remort attribute.\n\n@@gBrawler reincarnation bonuses@@W\n  * @@wBrawler + Monk remort reincarnations >= 20@@W unlocks\n    @@wEquip Fist@@W and @@wDual Fist@@W permanently.\n\nSee also: @@mremort stance monk martial_artist combo chi reincarnate@@W\n
289	finger	86	finger	Syntax: finger <player>\n\nShows account/profile details about a player.\nThis command is restricted to level 86+.\n
290	build_weapons	-1	build_weapons	BUILD HELP : WEAPONS\n--------------------\nThe WEAPONS command displays the weapon numbers.\nSyntax:  WEAPONS\nFor objects of type WEAPON, the last value (value3) determines which sort of\nweapon it is - hit, crush, slash, etc.  This command displays a numbered list\nof the weapon types.  Note:  For backstabbing weapons, the weapon type must be\n11 (pierce).\n
291	show_showobject	-1	show_showobject	BUILD HELP : SHOWOBJECT\n-----------------------\nThe SHOWOBJECT command displays various details about a given object.\nSyntax:  SHOWOBJECT <object-vnum>\n
