350	murder	5	murder	Syntax: murder <target>\n\nInitiates lethal combat against a player or mob.\nThis command is level-gated to 5.\n
296	bond_mastery	0	bond mastery	Syntax: bond mastery\n\nAt maximum rank (5) in any track, you can unlock mastery for 100 quest\npoints. This grants your bonded weapon a special passive ability that\nactivates periodically during combat.\n\n  Edge Mastery: "Bloodthirst"\n    Your blade hungers for blood. It occasionally lashes out with a bonus\n    slash attack against your opponent, dealing damage based on your\n    damroll. ~8% chance per combat tick.\n\n  Guard Mastery: "Aegis Ward"\n    Your blade projects a shimmering ward. It periodically heals you for\n    5% of your maximum HP during combat. ~10% chance per combat tick.\n    Out of combat, the blade hums with protective resonance.\n\n  Keen Mastery: "Deep Wound"\n    Your blade whispers of weak points. It occasionally inflicts a\n    bleeding wound on foes, applying a weakening effect. ~6% chance\n    per combat tick.\n\n  Spirit Mastery: "Living Steel"\n    Your blade breathes with living energy. It periodically restores\n    4% of max HP and 4% of max mana during combat. ~8% chance per\n    combat tick.\n\nMastery persists through death, track changes (if you re-achieve rank 5),\nand logout. It is a permanent upgrade once activated.\n\nSee also: bond bond tracks\n
297	build	2	build	Syntax: build\n        build <subcommand>\n\nEnter and use the building command set for area editing.\nUse @@Yhelp build_summary@@N for the full list of builder subcommands.\n
298	build_showresets	-1	build_showresets	BUILD HELP : SHOWRESETS\n-----------------------\nThe SHOWRESETS command displays any resets for the room you are currently in.\nSyntax:  SHOWRESETS\n
299	smash	0	smash	Syntax: smash <door>\n\nSmashes open a door by force, bypassing its lock entirely. Both the closed\nand locked flags are removed from the door, and the reverse side is also\nunlocked if it exists. No key is required.\n\nIf the door was already unlocked, your character tumbles through\ncomically rather than smashing it open.\n\nUnlike pick (which requires lockpicking skill and care), smash is a brute-\nforce approach. It is available to strong warrior-type characters.\n\nExample:\n  smash north      -- Smashes open the door to the north.\n  smash iron gate  -- Smashes open the iron gate.\n\nNote: smash the *door* -- it does not attack a target in combat. For combat\nuse, see bash or charge.\n\nSee also: bash open close lock unlock pick\n
300	upheaval	0	upheaval	The earth itself rises in fury, dealing devastating area earth damage\nto all enemies in the room.\nDruid spell. Uses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
301	palmstrike	0	palmstrike	Syntax: palmstrike <target>\n\nDelivers a powerful open-hand palm strike. Palmstrike is a Pugilist-line\nunarmed attack skill that uses the heel of the palm for maximum impact.\nIt is handled by the Pugilist attack system alongside aurabolt and other\nunarmed techniques.\n\nPalmstrike is available to Pugilist-class characters and their remort\ndescendants (Monk, Brawler, and the Martial Artist adept class).\n\nRequirements:\n  - Must be in combat or initiates combat on the target.\n  - Target must be present in the room.\n  - Must have the skill learned.\n\nSee also: shelp palmstrike aurabolt punch pummel spinfist\n
302	pemote	0	pemote	PEMOTE acts in the same way as emote, except that where emote adds your name\nbefore the argument, PEMOTE adds you name PLUS the characters 's\nEg PEMOTE feeling rather annoyed with Staff         would be shown as:\nStephen's feeling rather annoyed with Staff.
303	map	0	map	Syntax: map\n\nDisplays the local automap.\n
304	passage	0	passage	You phase through doors and barriers using natural energy.\nFunctions like pass door.\nDruid spell. Uses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
305	read	0	read	Syntax: read <object|note>\n\nReads readable objects such as notes/signs/books.\n
306	adapt	0	adapt	ADAPT allows you to have a weapon adapted for your use, if it's level is higher\nthan yours.  Adapt can only be used when in the room with a NPC that offers\nhis/her services for adapting.  Typing ADAPT with no argument reports the cost\nof having a weapon adapted.\nOnce the weapon has been adapted, it's damage will have been lowered in line\nwith the decrease in the weapon's level to your's.  Any affects on the weapon\n(Eg affects HITROLL) will be heavily reduced, and probably cancelled.\nIf, once a weapon has been adapted, it's attributes indicate it will cause NO\ndamage, it will crumble into dust, and you will lose it.  
307	build_shops	-1	build_shops	BUILD HELP : SHOPS\n------------------\nShops are basically mobiles with a few extras.  To make a shop, simply create\na mobile, and set the 'shopspec' part of the mobile.\ntrade0 - trade4 are the item types that the monile will buy or sell.\nIf you don't want 5 different item types bought/sold, leave some entries blank.\nprofbuy is the profit the shopkeeper makes when you buy an item.  100 = 100% =\nno profit.  150 = 150% = a fifty percent increae in price.\nprofsell is the loss you make when selling.  100 = 100% = no loss.  50 = 50% =\nyou only get half the item's price from the shopkeeper.\nprofbuy should be no smaller than 100\nprofsell should be no larger than 100\nopenhour is the time the shop is 'open'\nclosehour is the time the shop is 'shut'\nFor a 24-hr shop, set openhour to 0 and closehour to 23.\n
308	build_oedit	-1	build_oedit	BUILD HELP : OEDIT\n------------------\nThe OEDIT command places you in Object EDITing mode.\nSyntax:  OEDIT [object-vnum]\nThis will allow you to edit onformation concerning objects.  To set which object\nyou wish to work on, either enter an object-vnum after OEDIT, or use the SETVNUM\ncommand.  Anything you type will be checked to see if it applies to mobiles,\nand if so, the value, flag or string specified will be set.\n
309	tell	0	tell	Syntax: tell <player> <message>\n\nSends a private message to another player.\n
310	weather	0	weather	Syntax: weather\n\nShows current weather conditions.\n
311	bond_tracks	0	bond tracks bond track edge guard keen spirit	Syntax: bond track <edge|guard|keen|spirit>\n        bond track <name> confirm  - Switch tracks (resets rank!)\n        bond tracks                - List all tracks\n\nThere are four bond tracks, each emphasizing a different combat role.\nChoose a track with 'bond track <name>'. Once chosen, spend bond points\nwith 'bond rankup' to advance through 5 ranks.\n\n  Edge   - The path of destruction.\n           Increases damroll and raw weapon damage.\n           Scaled by weapon base level.\n           Mastery: blade lashes out with bonus slash attacks in combat.\n\n  Guard  - The path of the defender.\n           Adds armor class (scales with base level) and parry (flat).\n           Mastery: blade projects a damage-absorbing ward, periodically\n           healing the wielder during combat.\n\n  Keen   - The path of precision.\n           Increases hitroll (scaled), critical chance and critical\n           multiplier (flat bonuses per rank).\n           Mastery: strikes inflict bleeding wounds on foes.\n\n  Spirit - The path of endurance.\n           Increases hit points and spellpower.\n           Scaled by weapon base level.\n           Mastery: weapon periodically restores HP and mana.\n\nRank costs (bond points):\n  Rank 1:    0 (free on track selection)\n  Rank 2:  125\n  Rank 3:  375\n  Rank 4:  750\n  Rank 5: 1500\n\nWARNING: Switching tracks resets rank to 1 and forfeits all invested\nbond points. Use 'bond track <name> confirm' to confirm a switch.\n\nSee also: bond bond mastery\n
