316	warlock	0	warlock	@@dWARLOCK@@W\n\n@@dHistory@@W\n  The first Warlocks were thieves and shadow-workers who had always sensed\n  something more moving in the dark spaces between their strikes -- a\n  resonance in the moment before a lock clicked open or a pocket emptied.\n  Some pursued this sense deliberately, pressing their skills past what pure\n  physical discipline could explain. They found it in old compacts: pacts\n  with entities that trafficked in shadow, entropy, and the fine art of\n  undoing. The Warlock tradition was never written down formally; it was\n  transmitted through apprenticeship and the hard understanding that every\n  hex carries a price. Thieves who return through the mortal disciplines\n  carry that resonance fully awakened -- curse-weavers who blur the line\n  between shadowcraft and sorcery.\n\nWarlocks are hexblades and curse-weavers, blending shadowcraft with precision\nstrikes to convert attrition into sudden collapse.\n\n@@dPassive class advantages@@W\n  * @@wExtra attack round@@W while Warlock remort is active.\n  * @@wSpell critical chance@@W bonus (+0.075% per level, up to +7.5% at 100).\n  * @@wCritical chance@@W bonus (+0.0375% per level, up to +3.75% at 100).\n  * @@wCritical damage@@W bonus (+0.15% per level, up to +15% at 100).\n  * @@wBackstab / circle damage@@W bonus (+0.75% per level, up to +75% at 100).\n  * @@wRemort non-physical damage@@W bonus (+0.375% per level, up to +37.5% at 100).\n\n@@dUnique Warlock mechanics@@W\n  * Access to @@wWarlock stance@@W (hybrid melee/caster pressure).\n  * Bridges stealth burst and spell pressure toward Nightblade progression.\n  * Uses @@wDexterity@@W as prime remort attribute.\n\n@@dWarlock reincarnation bonuses@@W\n  * @@wAssassin + Warlock remort reincarnations >= 20@@W unlocks\n    @@wDual Wield@@W permanently.\n\nSee also: @@mremort stance assassin nightblade reincarnate@@W\n
