338	assemble	0	assemble	Syntax: assemble <piece1> <piece2>\n\nAssembles two compatible item pieces into a single complete object. Both\nitems must be PIECE-type objects that reference each other as matching\ncomponents. When successfully assembled, both piece items are consumed and\nreplaced with the completed object in your inventory.\n\nA piece item's description will usually indicate what it combines with.\nThe resulting object is created at your current level.\n\nExample:\n  assemble hilt blade\n  -- If "hilt" and "blade" are matching pieces, they combine into a sword.\n\nRestrictions:\n  - Both items must be in your inventory.\n  - Both items must be of the PIECE item type.\n  - The pieces must be specifically designed to combine with each other.\n\nSee also: inventory get put\n
339	build_delreset	-1	build_delreset	BUILD HELP : DELRESET\n---------------------\nThe DELRESET command allows you to remove resets from a room.\nSyntax:  DELRESET <reset-number>\nThis will delete reset-number from the reset list in the current room.\nTo find out the number for each reset, type SHOWRESETS.\n
