343	rootway	0	rootway	You travel through the root network of trees, teleporting to a random location.\nFunctions like teleport.\nDruid spell. Uses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
344	ashborn	0	Ashborn	Born of the Ashfall Era's volcanic catastrophe, the Ashborn are people whose bodies\nabsorbed the Cinderteeth's fire and mineral particulate rather than dying in it. The\ntransformation proved heritable: children of ashfall survivors are born already threaded\nwith volcanic mineral, running hot, and sealed by mineral crust when injured. Midgaard's\npost-Ashfall institutions denied the Ashborn separate civic standing to simplify property\ndisputes during reconstruction — a bad-faith reclassification the Reckoning faction still\nargues against. The Ashborn remain in foundry districts across the corridor, essential\nto the metalwork economy and still classified in some records as a subcategory of human.\n
345	necromancer	0	necromancer	@@GNECROMANCER@@W\n\n@@GHistory@@W\n  The Necromancer tradition is older than the Psionicist academies that now\n  claim jurisdiction over the mind arts. Before the academies there were the\n  Entropy Scholars -- independent practitioners who studied decay and\n  dissolution because they believed that understanding endings was essential\n  to understanding existence. Over centuries their research drifted into\n  practical application: sustaining the departed past their natural terminus,\n  drawing on residual spiritual energy as a power source, weaponizing the\n  same processes that unravel living systems. The academies branded them\n  heretics; the Scholars noted that death itself cannot be outlawed by\n  institutional consensus. Psionicists who return to study entropy rather\n  than enhancement carry on that ancient, unsanctioned tradition.\n\nNecromancers are entropy architects who weaponize decay, shadow, and attrition.\nTheir power grows as enemies lose tempo and control.\n\n@@GPassive class advantages@@W\n  * @@wRemort non-physical damage@@W bonus\n    (+0.5% per level, up to +50% at 100).\n\n@@GUnique Necromancer mechanics@@W\n  * Access to @@wNecromancer stance@@W (dual-cast / no-hit caster posture).\n  * Strong dark-magic summon and drain interactions throughout remort spell kits.\n  * Uses @@wIntelligence@@W as prime remort attribute.\n\n@@GNecromancer reincarnation bonuses@@W\n  * @@wNecromancer + Egomancer remort reincarnations >= 20@@W unlocks\n    @@wEquip Wand@@W permanently.\n\nSee also: @@mremort stance egomancer kinetimancer reincarnate@@W\n
346	status	0	status	Syntax: status\n\nShows world/system status information.\n
347	gain	0	gain	GAIN increases one of your levels.  Level gain is no longer automatic, due\nto the 'semi' multiclass system.  Typing GAIN with no argument will report\nwhich levels you are able to gain in, and the cost to do so (in xp).\nTyping GAIN with the 3-letter abreviation for a class will advance your level\nin the given class, if you can level in it, and if you have enough xp.\nEg: GAIN cip    will advance your cipher level, if you are able to level cipher.\nSee also:MULTI WORTH TRAIN
348	spells	0	spells	Syntax: spells\n\nLists all spells currently available to your character (spells with a mana\ncost of 2 or more), along with their mana cost. The output is formatted in\nthree columns showing spell name and mana requirement.\n\nOnly spells your character can currently cast are listed -- spells you do\nnot have access to via class and level are excluded.\n\nFor all skills including non-mana skills, use LEARNED instead.\nFor a full class-by-class breakdown of available spells at each level,\nuse SLIST.\n\n  spells    -- Shows usable spells and their mana costs.\n  learned   -- Shows all usable skills/spells with proficiency.\n  slist     -- Full spell/skill list by class and level.\n\nSee also: learned slist cast shelp\n
351	help	0	help	Syntax: help [topic]\n\nDisplays the help entry for a given topic. If no topic is provided, the\nsummary help page is shown.\n\nHelp lookup first tries an exact match, then a prefix match. So "help ba"\nwill find "bash" if no exact match exists for "ba".\n\nRelated help commands:\n  shelp <topic>   -- Staff reference for skills and spells (detailed\n                     mechanical information, class acquisition, effects).\n  rhelp <topic>   -- Help on races and racial traits.\n  sthelp          -- Help on combat stances and their effects.\n  rmlist          -- List and describe racial modifiers.\n  lore <object>   -- Lore information about items found in the world.\n\nTopic categories you can explore:\n  commands        -- Lists available commands by category.\n  slist           -- Full list of spells and skills by class.\n  rlist           -- Lists available races.\n  socials         -- Lists available social commands.\n  summary         -- Overview of the game and newbie guidance.\n\nSee also: commands slist rlist socials summary\n
352	time	0	time	Syntax: time\n\nShows current in-game time/date.\n
353	warden	0	warden	@@cHISTORY@@W\n\nThe warden tradition traces to the road warden companies of the Keeper Era —\nprofessional escorts who protected charter caravans across the desert road\nnetwork. After the Ninth Meridian Catastrophe shattered the eastern road\nsystem, surviving militias reorganized as the Reaver Confederates and later\nmercenary brotherhoods, carrying forward a doctrine forged by figures like\nWarden-Sergeant Caleph Dunmar, who held the Seven Shade Arches forty-three\ndays against the Ashbound siege with nothing but defensive ground and\ndiscipline. The Ash-and-Iron Decades further hardened the tradition: as\nMidgaard's civic order militarized in response to the Ashfall Monsoon and the\nfall of Evermeet, warden training was systematized through requisition offices\nand reserve depots. Modern wardens carry this layered inheritance — part road\nguardian, part civic soldier, part mercenary craftsman of force.\n\n@@cWARDEN@@W\n\nWardens are masters of direct force: relentless front-line fighters trained to\nbreak defenses, absorb pressure, and end conflicts in steel and momentum.\n\n@@cPassive class abilities@@W\n  * @@wWarden combat-technique scaling@@W: kick/punch/knee/headbutt/charge\n    style attacks gain @@w+1% damage per Warden level@@W.\n  * @@wEnhanced Damage@@W (unlocked at mortal level 20): increases physical\n    damage by @@w3% per point of Strength@@W.\n\n@@cUnique Warden mechanics@@W\n  * Prime mortal attribute is @@wStrength@@W.\n  * Delivers reliable scaling for weapon and physical-skill damage, making\n    Warden a premier chassis for melee progression.\n\n@@cWarden reincarnation bonuses@@W\n  * Every @@w2 Warden reincarnations@@W (rounded up) increases max\n    @@wStrength@@W by 1.\n  * At @@w1+ Warden reincarnation@@W, @@wEnhanced Damage@@W is permanently\n    unlocked for all future class paths.\n\nSee also: @@mreincarnate remort knight swordsman@@W\n
