355	staffmotd	81	STAFFMOTD	@@a[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]\n|                   @@mStaff Message of the Day@@a                    |\n[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]\n@@y\n    * Please Note:\n@@b\n    o "HELP STAFFRULES" is mandatory reading for ALL staff.\n    o If someone wishes to be PKOK, comfirm it with them first.\n      (i.e. explain the PKOK flag will never be removed, etc.)\n    o Please don't give away the identities of Wizinvis staff!\n@@y\n    * Reminder:\n@@b\n    o Remember that staff of higher level than you are\n      technically senior to you but we must treat ALL staff with\n      respect, especially whilst inhabiting your mort.\n    o Reimbs are no longer given, except for extreme circumstances.\n      o New Quest Point System.  For More Info, Type:\n           o  'help uniques'\n           o  'help uq'  OR  'help unique-rules'\n@@r\n    o WE NO LONGER BUILD ON THIS MUD..LOG ON TO PORT @@e6969@@r INSTEAD!\n @@mFinally, you are all doing a great job, keep up the good work!\n@@a[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]-[]@@N\n
356	pose	86	pose	Syntax: pose [message]\n\nSet or display your custom pose/social output.\nThis command is restricted to level 86+.\n
357	death	0	DEATH	When your character dies, your corpse is magically transported to the \nMorgue of Moribound - an establishment which serves all the realms of this \nland.  You are given a new body to use, and placed in the lands of \nMoribound.\nThe only task you must complete is to get to your corpse is find your way to\nthe morgue - a task set as a rather sick joke by the morgue's management.\nAny spells which were affecting you are canceled by death.\nFollowing and groups are not affected by death.\nYou lose HALF of the experience points you have.\nCorpses decay after time, and the objects inside corpses decay with them.\nOnly the player who died may take items from his/her/it's corpse.
358	sneak	0	sneak	Syntax: sneak\n\nAttempts to move stealthily.\n
359	qp	0	QP QUESTPOINTS	Quest Points\nQuest points are used to reward players for completing quests, helping\nmortals or anything else that the Gods can think of :)\n        QP's     What you can get\n        ----     ----------------\n         4       Transfer -         in case you get lost in a norecall area.\n        10       Corpse Retrieval - For those with the PKOK flag, when\n                                    they cannot find their corpse\n        25       EQU Rename -       Rename a piece of your equ to something\n                                    unique.\n       100       Player House -     A house is created for you in the MUD.\n                                    Type "Help House".\n       *50       Unique Equipment - Staff will make you a peice of\n                                    equipment that is unique to your\n                                    character. See "Help Unique" for details.
360	law	0	law wanted lawless	@@lShades @@dof @@eEvil@@N system of laws and punishments:\n  Within the game, the major cities of the realm have a system of enforcing\nrules of player behavior, by having certain players known to the realm as\nbeing WANTED.  The system is simple, once you understand it's perspective.\n  The civilized states of the realm enforce peaceful interaction between\ncitizens of the various states.  Killing and stealing from other citizens is\nconsidered unlawful, and anyone that falls under the protection of the Law is\nprotected by these actions.\n  There are three states that a citizen can have: Civilized, Wanted, and\nLawless.  Citizens that are Civilized are protected within the legal system\nfrom being attacked by other citizens, and also from having things stolen from\nthem. If a Civilized citizen is attacked or stolen from, the Law will label\nthe attacker with Wanted, and deal with them accordingly.  In addition, if a\nCivilized citizen breaks the Laws of the Realm, they also will be Wanted.\n  Wanted citizens are no longer protected under the Law, and Civilized\ncitizens are authorized to kill or steal from them.  In addition, non-player\ncharacters will interact with them violently.\n  If you wish to become Lawless, this will your protection under the Law.\nHowever, both actors in an interaction must be Lawless for the Law to ignore\ntheir actions between each other.  If a Lawless attacks someone Civilized, the\nLaw will seek retribution on the Lawless.  If a Civilized citizen attacks a\nLawless, the Law doesn't protect the Lawless, it punishes the Civilized by\nmaking them Wanted.  To become a Lawless, you may request a PKOK flag from an\nStaff.  Once you have chosen to be Lawless, the Law will never again place\nyou under its protection.\n  Many hidden and unknown events in the game may take the protection of the\nLaw away from you, either permanently, or temporarily.  Some of these are\nobvious, some not so obvious. A few of these events may even make you Persecuted,\nwhich has several unforseen circumstances.\n  When you become WANTED, either from breaking a law or other actions, you are\ngiven a sentence based on your crime.  Sentences may only be reduced by\nsacrificing valuable objects to the Law, by using the command sacrifice\n<object> judge.  The judge will examine your sacrifice, and reduce your\nsentence appropriately.\n  The Law is omnicient in some ways, and becoming Wanted or Lawless may have\nsome unforseen repercussions, so consider your actions well before commiting\nto them!
361	seal	1	seal seal_room web cage	Seal room and cage are spells used for the purpose of literally sealing a room\n\neither to keep pcs and npcs in or out. There are both positive and negative\n\naffects to those spells. There are limits though.\n\n                      \n\n@@eDO NOT CAST SEAL IN TOWN!!!!!@@N\n\n@@eDO NOT CAST SEAL IN A NEWBIE PRONE AREA!!!!@@N\n\nANYONE seen doing one of these two things or anything else of not common sense will be PUNISHED!!!\n\n
362	credits	0	credits	Syntax: credits\n\nShows credits for the codebase and contributors.\n
363	frenzy	1	frenzy	Frenzy is a skill that let's you go into a fighting frenzy.  You will take\n\nsome damage, but will attempt to hit every enemy in the room!\n\n
364	wimpy	0	wimpy	Syntax: wimpy <percent>\n\nSets auto-flee threshold hit points.\n
365	delete	0	delete	Syntax: delete <number>\n\nDeletes a message from a bulletin board in the current room.  You must be\nstanding in a room that contains a board.  Specify the message number as shown\nby the READ or LIST commands.\n\nYou may only delete a message if you are the author, a recipient, the clan\nleader for a clan board, or staff.\n\nSee also: NOTE, READ\n
366	build_addreset	-1	build_addreset	BUILD HELP : ADDRESET\n---------------------\nThe ADDRESET command adds a new entry to the reset list.\nSyntax: ADDRESET  mob <mob-vnum> <limit>\nLoad the mob with mob-vnum into the present room.  Don't load more than limit.\nEG: ADDRESET mob 1010 1\nSyntax:  ADDRESET obj <obj-vnum>\nLoad the object with obj-vnum into the present room.\nEG: ADDRESET obj 1020\nSyntax:  ADDRESET equip <mob-vnum> <obj-vnum> <location>\nMake the mob with mob-vnum wear the object with obj-vnum in location.                  EG: ADDRESET equip 1010 1020 wield\nSyntax:  ADDRESET give <mob-vnum> <obj-vnum>\nGive the mob with mob-vnum the object with obj-vnum.\nEG:  ADDRESET give 1010 1021                  \nSyntax:  ADDRESET door <direction> <state>\nSet the flag specified by state to the door in a certain direction.\nEG:  ADDRESET door n closed\nSyntax:  ADDRESET rand <num-dirs>\nRandomise the first num-dirs exits in the room.  Exits are number 0 (North), \n1 (East), 2 (South), 3 (West), 4 (Up), and 5 (Down).  \nEG:  ADDRESET rand 3\nSyntax:  ADDRESET message <text>\nAdds an auto-message to the room, which is displayed periodically.\nEG:  ADDRESET message You hear the screams of the Ogre Kings.\n
367	crusader	0	crusader	@@cHISTORY@@W\n\nThe term Crusader appears in Solar Court records as a campaign-honor title\nfor warriors who served successive engagements without rotation, accruing\nfield honors in place of relief. It predates both the Knight academies\nformalized under the Iron Reformation and the dueling courts where the\nSwordsman tradition was codified. The convergence of those two paths was\nforged during the Ash-and-Iron Decades, when Midgaard's militarization\ndrove Knight and Swordsman training into the same reserve depots. The two\ntraditions had long existed in competitive tension -- formation discipline\nagainst individual momentum, controlled body-strikes against escalating\nblade pressure -- but campaigns during the Ashfall aftermath proved\nrepeatedly that the most effective fighters could do both. Informal cross-\ntraining units calling themselves Crusader Corps arose within the depots,\ndeliberately reclaiming the old campaign title. Their doctrine: chain the\nKnight's body-strikes into the Swordsman's building momentum, and the\naccumulated force exceeds what either path sustains alone.\n\n@@cCRUSADER@@W\n\nCrusaders are battlefield zealots forged from @@cKnight@@W discipline and\n@@cSwordsman@@W momentum. Where others fight to survive, Crusaders fight to\noverwhelm: chaining relentless martial pressure into decisive finishing blows.\n\nTo become a Crusader, you must master either @@cKnight@@W or @@cSwordsman@@W\n(remort prerequisites for the adept path).\n\n@@cPassive class advantages@@W\nCrusader grants always-on combat scaling as adept levels rise:\n\n  1) @@wCombo-skill damage bonus@@W\n     - Crusader increases damage for Crusader-relevant remort/adept combo\n       attacks (notably @@wholystrike@@W and @@wfleche@@W, plus other remort/adept\n       entries in that family).\n     - Scaling: +5% damage per Crusader adept level (up to +100% at 20).\n\n  2) @@wExtra attack round@@W\n     - Having any Crusader adept level grants an additional melee hit in the\n       multi-hit calculation.\n\n@@cUnique Crusader mechanics@@W\n  * @@wCrusader stance@@W is available once the adept path is active.\n  * @@wAnti Magic Shell@@W is learned at Crusader level 2.\n  * Crusader uses @@wStrength@@W as its adept prime attribute and follows a\n    heavy melee-oriented adept growth profile.\n\n@@cCrusader reincarnation bonus@@W\nEach Crusader adept reincarnation grants an additional passive bonus:\n\n  * @@wCombo-family strike damage@@W: +2% per Crusader adept reincarnation for\n    punch, kick, knee, headbutt, charge, holystrike, and fleche.\n  * At @@w20+ Crusader adept reincarnations@@W, combo capacity gains +1 slot\n    when combo progression is active.\n\nIn short: Crusader is the pressure-and-finisher adept, rewarding players who\nchain weapon and body-strike sequences into explosive melee bursts.\n\nSee also: @@mremort combo stance anti magic shell holystrike fleche charge@@W\n
368	aurabolt	0	aurabolt	Syntax: aurabolt <target>\n\nFires a concentrated bolt of chi/aura energy at an opponent. Aurabolt is a\nPugilist-line unarmed attack skill that channels internal energy into a\nsingle powerful strike. It is handled by the Pugilist attack system (alongside\npalmstrike and other unarmed techniques).\n\nAurabolt is available to Pugilist-class characters and their remort\ndescendants (Monk, Brawler, and the Martial Artist adept class).\n\nRequirements:\n  - Must be in combat or initiates combat on the target.\n  - Target must be present in the room.\n  - Must have the skill learned.\n\nSee also: shelp aurabolt palmstrike punch pummel\n
369	equipment	0	equipment	Syntax: equipment\n\nShows currently equipped gear.\n
370	magi	0	magi	@@pHISTORY@@W\n\nArcane tradition in this world cannot be separated from its worst catastrophe:\nthe Spirebound Conclave, a mountain academy chartered to preserve dangerous\nmagical knowledge, which turned containment doctrine into prisoner\nexperimentation and collapsed in internal sabotage and seismic ruin. The\nWizard's Keep was founded as its institutional correction — regulated under the\nViolet Compact's registry law, militarized by frontier necessity, and governed\nby the Triple-Ledger Rule that requires every operation to be witnessed,\nrecorded, and audited. Magi trained through this tradition carry that double\ninheritance: they bend elemental law through the precision learned in controlled\nhalls, with the Conclave's catastrophe woven structurally into every curriculum.\nWhere the Conclave sought singular mastery at any cost, the Keep demands\nreproducible competence under civic oversight — and it is this institutional\ndiscipline, as much as raw talent, that defines the modern arcane tradition.\n\n@@pMAGI@@W\n\nMagi are arcanists who study the raw architecture of power. Where others pray,\nbargain, or brawl, a Magi bends elemental law through discipline, theory, and\nprecision.\n\n@@pPassive class abilities@@W\n  * @@wMagi lifesteal chance scaling@@W: lifesteal trigger chance gains\n    @@w+0.05% per Magi level@@W.\n  * @@wMystical Potency@@W (unlocked at mortal level 20): increases your\n    non-physical damage by @@w2% per point of Intelligence@@W.\n\n@@pUnique Magi mechanics@@W\n  * Prime mortal attribute is @@wIntelligence@@W.\n  * Naturally synergizes with spellpower scaling, making Magi one of the best\n    mortal foundations for sustained arcane damage builds.\n\n@@pMagi reincarnation bonuses@@W\n  * Every @@w2 Magi reincarnations@@W (rounded up) increases max\n    @@wIntelligence@@W by 1.\n  * At @@w1+ Magi reincarnation@@W, @@wMystical Potency@@W is permanently\n    unlocked for all future class paths.\n\nSee also: @@mreincarnate remort wizard sorcerer@@W\n
371	chiblock	0	chiblock	Syntax: chiblock\n\nChannels chi energy into a defensive barrier that improves your armor class\nduring combat. Unlike the finisher-based shieldblock, chiblock draws directly\nfrom your chi reserves and can be used independently of combo state.\n\nEffects when activated:\n  - Applies a -1 AC (armor class) bonus for (combo_count - 3) combat rounds.\n  - Activates a 10-round cooldown preventing reuse.\n  - Skill proficiency improves on successful use.\n\nThe chi cost increases if used while the cooldown is active. The lower your\narmor class number, the harder you are to hit.\n\nRequirements:\n  - Must be in combat.\n  - Must have chi available (cost varies with cooldown).\n  - Must have the Chiblock skill learned.\n\nSee also: shelp chiblock shieldblock chakra dodge parry\n
373	chakra	0	chakra	Syntax: chakra\n\nFocuses your internal chi energy to activate the Chakra skill, simultaneously\nhealing your wounds and boosting your combat damage. This skill is available\nto Monk and Martial Artist class characters.\n\nEffects when activated:\n  - Heals a portion of your hit points based on your Monk and Martial Artist\n    class levels: approximately (Monk + Martial Artist levels) * 5-7 HP.\n  - Applies a damroll bonus equal to (Monk + Martial Artist levels) * 5,\n    lasting 1 combat round (2 rounds if you have Martial Artist levels).\n  - Activates a 10-round cooldown preventing reuse.\n\nThe skill costs chi energy. If you have recently used chakra the cost\nincreases due to the cooldown penalty.\n\nRequirements:\n  - Must be in combat.\n  - Must have chi available.\n  - Must have the Chakra skill learned.\n\nSee also: shelp chakra chiblock phantomfist spinfist\n
374	mana__3	1	mana drain	
375	anti_magic_shell	0	anti magic shell	Syntax: anti magic shell\n\nTriggers the Anti Magic Shell finisher skill, surrounding yourself with a\nfield that disrupts incoming magical attacks. This is a finisher-tier combat\nskill: it can only be activated when your combo counter has reached the\nrequired threshold during active combat.\n\nEffects when activated:\n  - Grants a +1 hitroll bonus for (combo_count - 3) combat rounds.\n  - The combo counter is reset after activation.\n  - Skill proficiency improves on successful use.\n\nThis is a defensive finisher that improves your attack accuracy rather than\ndirectly reducing damage taken. It is distinct from the Anti Magic Shell\npassive/spell effect that grants magical absorption.\n\nRequirements:\n  - Must be in combat.\n  - Requires a valid finisher combo count.\n  - Must have the skill learned.\n\nSee also: shelp anti magic shell bash dirt trip\n
376	build_findmob	-1	build_findmob	BUILD HELP : FINDMOB\n--------------------\nThe FINDMOB command allows you to find the vnum of a given mobile.\nSyntax:  FINDMOB <mob-name | ALL >\nIf a mob-name is supllied, the vnums of any mobiles whose names match that\ngiven will be displayed.  If ALL is entered, then all the mobiles will\nbe displayed.  This command only shows the vnums for mobiles in the same\narea as you.\n
377	enchant	0	enchant	Syntax: enchant show\n        enchant buy <enchantment>\n\nPermanently enchants a wearable item using a spell matrix and enchantment\nobjects from your inventory. This system allows players to customize\nequipment with stat bonuses at a quest-point cost.\n\nSetup required before enchanting:\n  1. Obtain a spell matrix object (ITEM_SPELL_MATRIX) and hold it.\n  2. Place one wearable item (weapon, armor, or light) in your inventory.\n  3. Place one or more enchantment objects (ITEM_ENCHANTMENT) in the matrix.\n\n  enchant show    -- Preview what the enchantment would do: displays current\n                     stats, proposed stats, total costs, and whether the\n                     combination is legal.\n  enchant buy     -- Commits the enchantment, deducts quest points from your\n                     total, consumes the enchantment items, and permanently\n                     modifies the target item.\n\nStat limits and rules:\n  - Ability stats (STR/INT/DEX/WIS/CON): Combined total must not exceed +1.\n  - Maximum HP/mana bonus: 480. Maximum move bonus: 240.\n  - Maximum hitroll/damroll: 50 each.\n  - Minimum armor class: -480. Minimum saves: -36.\n  - Base cost: 20 quest points.  Unique items cost 20 QP less.\n  - You must be at least the item's level to enchant it.\n\nRestrictions:\n  - Clan equipment cannot be enchanted.\n  - All transactions are logged via the brands system.\n\nSee also: qpspend worth appraise\n
378	build_vnums	-1	build_vnums	BUILD HELP : VNUMS\n------------------\n"VNUMS" stands for "Virtual Numbers".  They are arbitary numbers used to identify either Rooms, Objects or Mobiles on the mud.  Each object, room and\nmobile must have a unique vnum, for their type.  That is, you can't have two\nmobiles with the same vnum, but you could have a mobile and an object using the\nsame vnum.  Think of each of the three "users" of vnums as being completely\nsperate:  Mobile vnums have to be unique, but only for mobs.  Object vnums must\nalso be unique, but also only for objects.  Room vnums must be unique, but only\nfor rooms.  \nEach area consists of: rooms, mobiles and objects, principally.  Each area has\na vnum range associated with it.  So, for example, the range is vnums 100 to 199\n(Kiess area).  There are rooms with vnums 101 - 195, objects with vnums \n101 - 143, and mobiles with vnums 101 - 135.  It is normal to use consecutive\nvnums starting at the lowest vnum, for all objects, rooms and mobiles in an area.  Please try to conform to this usage of vnums!\n
379	ooc	0	ooc	Syntax: ooc <message>\n\nSends a message on the out-of-character channel.\n
380	mental_power	0	MENTAL POWER MENTAL-POWER	@@mMENTAL POWER@@N\n\nMental Power is a stacking combat mechanic for psionic, necromancer, ego, and\nkinetic spellcasters (PSI, NEC, EGO, KIN spells).\n\n@@WBuilding the Stack:@@N\n  Each time you successfully cast a PSI, NEC, EGO, or KIN spell, your Mental\n  Power increases by 1. The stack persists as long as you remain in combat.\n  It resets to 0 when you leave combat.\n\n@@WBenefits:@@N\n  For every point of Mental Power, the mana cost of PSI, NEC, EGO, and KIN\n  spells is reduced by @@y2%@@N per stack. For example, 10 stacks grants a 20%\n  mana cost reduction on those spells.\n\n@@WRisk - Mental Overload:@@N\n  Each time you cast a PSI, NEC, EGO, or KIN spell while you have Mental Power\n  stacked, there is a @@r1% chance per stack@@N that your mental focus will\n  shatter. If this occurs:\n    - The spell does not fire.\n    - Your Mental Power stack is reset to 0.\n    - No mana is spent.\n\n  At higher stacks this risk grows quickly. At 20 stacks there is a 20% chance\n  of collapse on each cast, so managing your stack is crucial.\n\n@@WPrompt Code:@@N\n  Use @@y%Q@@N in your prompt to display your current Mental Power. See HELP PROMPT.\n
381	wake	0	wake	Syntax: wake [target]\n\nWakes yourself or another sleeping character.\n
382	heal	0	heal	HEAL reports which spells you are able to buy, along with the cost.  This can\nonly be done if with a NPC which offers spells - usually healers.\nHEAL followed by a single character 'buys' that spell.\nEg: HEAL H  buys a heal spell.\nAll spells are only cast on the buyer.  No one else.
