399	build_mflags	-1	build_mflags	MOBILE (ACT) FLAGS:\n+===============+=======================================================+\n| Act Flag\t|\t\t\tDescription\t\t\t|\n+---------------+-------------------------------------------------------+\n| IS_NPC\t| Auto-set for Mobiles.\t\t\t\t\t|\n| SENTINEL\t| The Mobile will stay in the room it is loaded into.\t|\n| SCAVENGER\t| Will pick up any objects lying on the floor.\t\t|\n| REMEMBER\t| Will attack the last player to try and kill it.\t|\n| NO_FLEE\t| Players are unable to flee from this Mobile.\t\t|\n| AGGRESSIVE\t| Attacks any players that it encounters.\t\t|\n| STAY_AREA\t| Will not leave the area it was loaded into.\t\t|\n| WIMPY\t\t| Wimps out of fights.\t\t\t\t\t|\n| PET\t\t| Is a Pet.  (Don't use!)\t\t\t\t|\n| TRAIN\t\t| Can train players.\t\t\t\t\t|\n| PRACTICE\t| Players can practice skills/spells at this Mobile\t|\n| MERCENARY\t| Will assassinate players for a price.\t\t\t|\n| HEAL\t\t| Mobile sells heals and other spells.\t\t\t|\n| ADAPT\t\t| Will adapt weapon levels for players.\t\t\t|\n| UNDEAD\t| Mob is undead; may be summoned by spec_undead.\t|\t\n| BANK\t\t| Offers banking services to players.\t\t\t|\n| NO_BODY\t| Has no solid body; can't bs.\t\t\t        |\n| HUNTER\t| Hunts anyone who attacks it, or it attacks.\t\t|\n+===============+=======================================================+\n
384	remort	0	REMORT ADEPT	@@aREMORT@@W\nYour @@yfirst@@W remort class requires the matching mortal\npre-requisite class at @@y100@@W.\nYour @@ysecond@@W remort class requires:\n  - your first remort class at @@y100@@W,\n  - all mortal classes at @@y100@@W, and\n  - the matching mortal pre-requisite class for that second remort\n    at @@y100@@W.\nWhen you are ready to remort, type gain <class shorthand shown below>.\nRemort classes and mortal pre-requisites are:\n        -@@pSorcerer@@W [@@ySor@@W] (Magi)\n        -@@WWizard@@W [@@yWiz@@W] (Magi)\n        -@@aPaladin@@W [@@yPal@@W] (Cleric)\n        -@@CPriest@@W [@@yPri@@W] (Cleric)\n        -@@dAssassin@@W [@@yAss@@W] (Cipher)\n        -@@dWarlock@@W [@@yWlk@@W] (Cipher)\n        -@@cKnight@@W [@@yKni@@W] (Warden)\n        -@@cSwordsman@@W [@@ySwo@@W] (Warden)\n        -@@GNecromancer@@W [@@yNec@@W] (Psionicist)\n        -@@mEgomancer@@W [@@yEgo@@W] (Psionicist)\n        -@@gMonk@@W [@@yMon@@W] (Pugilist)\n        -@@gBrawler@@W [@@yBra@@W] (Pugilist)\n\n@@aADEPT@@W\nAdept classes are a third tier of progression beyond remort. To unlock\nadepts, you must have at least @@y2@@W remort classes at level @@y100@@W.\nEach adept class requires one of its matching remort classes at @@y100@@W.\nWhen you are ready to adept, type gain <class shorthand shown below>.\nAdept classes and their remort pre-requisites are:\n        -@@pGrand Magi@@W [@@yGra@@W] (Sorcerer or Wizard)\n        -@@aTemplar@@W [@@yTem@@W] (Paladin or Priest)\n        -@@dNightblade@@W [@@yNig@@W] (Assassin or Warlock)\n        -@@cCrusader@@W [@@yCru@@W] (Knight or Swordsman)\n        -@@GKinetimancer@@W [@@yKin@@W] (Necromancer or Egomancer)\n        -@@gMartial Artist@@W [@@yMar@@W] (Monk or Brawler)\n
385	bid	0	bid	Syntax: bid <amount>\n\nPlaces an auction bid on the current auction item.\n
386	briar_volley	0	briar volley	A volley of thorny briars pelts your enemy with earth damage.\nDruid spell. Uses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
387	save	0	save	Syntax: save\n\nSaves your character data to disk.\n
388	disguise	0	disguise	Syntax: disguise <description text>\n        disguise reset\n\nChanges your character's visible long description (the line others see when\nyou are in the same room as them) to arbitrary text of your choosing. This\nallows you to conceal your identity or alter how you appear in a room.\n\n  disguise reset        -- Restores your original character description.\n  disguise <any text>   -- Sets your room description to the provided text.\n                           A newline is added automatically.\n\nExample:\n  disguise A cloaked figure leans against the wall.\n  -- Other players in the room will see this instead of your normal\n     character description.\n\nRequirements:\n  - Must have the Disguise skill learned (learned[gsn_disguise] > 0).\n\nDisguise only changes your room description. Your name when targeted, your\nWHO entry, and your score are unaffected. Careful observers may still\nidentify you by your actions or the name that appears when you speak.\n\nSee also: shelp disguise shadowform sneak hide\n
389	rot	0	rot	A massive bolt of rotting energy strikes your target for heavy poison damage.\nDruid spell. Uses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
390	give	0	give	Syntax: give <item> <target>\n\nGives an item (or coins) to another character.\n
391	greeting6	-1	greeting6	@@r    The gates of ACK!TNG stand open.@@N\n@@r    Fortune favors the bold, and danger waits for the unready.@@N\n\n@@c    Diku Mud was created by Hans Henrik St{rfeldt, Katja Nyboe,\n@@c    Tom Madsen, Michael Seifert and Sebastian Hammer.\n@@c    MERC Modifications made by: Furey, Hatchet, Kahn@@N\n\n@@p    Bring your wit, your courage, and your will to endure.@@N\n@@p    The world remembers every name.@@N\n\n@@WWho are you?@@N\n
392	build_x	-1	build_x	BUILD HELP : LIST | X\n---------------------\nThe LIST command has two purposes.  Firstly, it shows you details about the\nRoom, Mobile or Object you are currently working on.  Secondly, it allows\nyou find out which flags you can set for objects.\nSyntax:  LIST [flags-name]\nIf you type just LIST on its own, you will be shown details of your current\nroom, mobile or object.  If you want to see a list of flags (in wide format,\nrather than the long format used when you screw up) type LIST HELP.\nThe lists of flags you can display vary according to which editing mode you are\nin.  This is basically because there is a list of FLAGS for each mode, etc...\nX may be used in place of LIST.\n
393	warcry	0	warcry	WARCRY is a Warden-only spell, which acts the same as the 'bless' spell.
394	thornhide	0	thornhide	Sharp thorns sprout from your skin, reflecting damage to melee attackers.\nSelf-only buff. Druid spell. Uses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
395	grand_magi	0	grand magi grandmagi	@@pHISTORY@@W\n\nThe Grand Magi title appears in pre-academic records as a civic honorific\nfor arcanists capable of invoking and sustaining multiple elemental forms\nin parallel -- a feat long regarded as ceremonial rather than combat-\npractical. Its roots lie in the tension between the Chromatic Circle and\nthe Axiomatic Schools: the Circle prized synthesis, the Schools prized\nformal proof, and for most of their shared era the two traditions treated\neach other as opponents. A small Circle faction, the Confluent Theorists,\ndocumented what happened when practitioners trained in both approached the\nelemental domains together, producing manuscripts called the Convergence\nCodices that the academies largely suppressed when they absorbed the\nCircle's remnants. The title was reclaimed during the Ash-and-Iron\nDecades, when several practitioners used overlapping elemental disruption\nto redirect ash-laden storm fronts during the Ashfall Monsoon. What had\nbeen an honorific became a designation: the adept path for those who had\ncompleted either line and earned the convergence.\n\n@@pGRAND MAGI@@W\n\nGrand Magi are the apex synthesis of @@pSorcerer@@W breadth and @@WWizard@@W\nprecision: arcane generals who command fire, storm, tide, and stone as a\nsingle disciplined doctrine. Where lesser casters specialize, Grand Magi\nlayer elemental pressure to dominate long fights.\n\nTo become a Grand Magi, you must master either @@pSorcerer@@W or @@WWizard@@W\n(remort prerequisites for the adept path).\n\n@@pPassive class advantages@@W\nGrand Magi gains passive scaling through adept levels:\n\n  1) @@wRemort/Adept non-physical spell damage bonus@@W\n     - Non-physical remort/adept damage effects gain a passive Grand Magi\n       multiplier.\n     - Scaling: +2% damage per Grand Magi adept level (up to +40% at 20).\n\n@@pUnique Grand Magi mechanics@@W\n  * @@wMagi stance@@W is available on the adept path and carries caster-focused\n    stance flags (either-class access, multi-cast support, dual-cast support,\n    and no-hit casting posture).\n  * Grand Magi gains a dedicated elemental spell ladder:\n      - @@wElemental Inferno@@W (level 1)\n      - @@wElemental Shock@@W (level 5)\n      - @@wElemental Deluge@@W (level 10)\n      - @@wElemental Rupture@@W (level 15)\n  * Grand Magi uses @@wIntelligence@@W as its adept prime attribute and follows\n    a high-mana caster growth profile.\n\n@@pGrand Magi reincarnation bonuses@@W\nEach Grand Magi adept reincarnation grants additional passive scaling:\n\n  * @@wElemental realm damage@@W (fire/air/water/earth): +2% per Grand Magi\n    adept reincarnation.\n\nIn short: Grand Magi is the sustained elemental adept, turning advanced arcane\nprogression into consistent, scaling spell pressure across elemental domains.\n\nSee also: @@mremort stance elemental inferno elemental shock elemental deluge elemental rupture@@W\n
396	circle	0	circle	Syntax: circle <target>\n\nAttempts a circling combat maneuver.\n
397	tremor	0	tremor	The earth trembles beneath your enemy, dealing heavy earth damage.\nDruid spell. Uses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
398	influx	0	influx	When successfully cast, this will heal all players in the room.
400	experience	0	EXPERIENCE LEVEL XP	Your character advances in power by gaining experience.  The amount of exp\nyou need to gain a level is determined by your race.  To gain a level, use\nthe GAIN command.\nYou gain experience by:\n    Being part of a group that kills a monster,\n    or by killing monsters on your own.\nYou lose experience by:\n    Fleeing from combat\n    Recalling out of combat\n    Being the target of certain spells\n    Dying\nThe experience you get from a kill depends on several things: how many players\nare in your group; your level versus the level of the monster; your alignment\nversus the monster's alignment; how many of this monster have been killed\nlately; and some random variation.
401	pick	0	pick	Syntax: pick <container>\n        pick <door keyword>\n\nAttempts to pick the lock on a locked container or door using your\nlockpicking skill. A successful pick unlocks the target without a key.\nWhen picking a door, both sides of the door are unlocked simultaneously.\n\nSuccess depends on your learned proficiency in the Pick Lock skill.\nHigher skill levels give a better chance of success.\n\nRestrictions:\n  - The target must be closed, locked, and not pick-proof.\n  - You cannot pick locks if a guard 5 or more levels above you is present\n    in the room.\n  - The item/door must be visible to you.\n\nExample:\n  pick chest          -- Attempts to pick the lock on a chest.\n  pick north          -- Attempts to pick the lock on the north door.\n\nSee also: shelp pick lock open unlock close\n
402	build_rooms	-1	build_rooms	BUILD HELP : ROOMS\n------------------\nThe following information is needed for each room:\nNAME\tThe name of the room, eg "The Temple of Midgaard"\nDESC    The description\nFLAGS\tFlags which determine the room's attributes, eg no_recall, dark, etc.\nSECTOR\tThe kind of terrain, eg city, field, hills, etc.\nDOOR\tInformation about exits, etc.  See 'HELP doors'.\nEXTRA\tExtra descriptions - see 'HELP extra'\n
403	serathi	0	Serathi	Avian humanoids of the western sky-roads, the Serathi predate the Keeper surveyors by\ngenerations and navigate by sky-lines — the horizon profiles of ridges and canopies\nthat form a map legible only from altitude. They maintain roost-chronicles of continuous\naerial observation older than most human cities, and the Roc Road was built along a\ncorridor the Serathi had been flying for centuries before it was named. Their\nrelationship with every ground-bound civilization follows the same pattern: their courier\nservices and aerial intelligence are valued, their territorial claims over the sky-roads\nthey have used since before memory are perpetually deferred. The negotiations continue.\nThe sky-readers do not appear to be in a hurry.\n
404	afk	0	afk	Syntax: afk\n\nToggles your AFK (Away From Keyboard) flag on or off. When the flag is active,\nother players can see that you are temporarily unavailable. Your character\nremains in the world while you are away; you can still receive tells and be\nattacked.\n\n  AFK flag turned on.   -- flag is now active\n  AFK flag turned off.  -- flag has been removed\n\nYour AFK status is visible on the WHO list and to players who examine you.\nThe flag does not protect you from combat or other in-game events; it is\na courtesy indicator only.\n\nSee also: visible save quit\n
405	diagnose	0	diagnose	DIAGNOSE allows you to check on the condition of a player or mob.\nThe condition is shown on a scale 5(best) to 1(worst) 
406	clutch	0	clutch	Syntax: clutch\n\nActivates a clutch item held in your left hand. Clutch items are rare,\nspecially crafted objects with powerful one-time or limited-use magical\neffects. Holding the item and typing "clutch" triggers its stored ability.\n\nClutch item types and their effects:\n  - Portal clutch: Opens a portal to a specific room, transporting you\n    instantly. The item is consumed on use.\n  - Gate clutch: Summons a creature to your location. There is a percentage\n    chance the creature will follow you. The item is consumed on use.\n  - Some clutch items are not consumed and can be used again.\n\nRestrictions:\n  - The clutch item must be worn in the LEFT HAND hold slot.\n  - Cannot be used in rooms flagged as NO PORTAL.\n  - The item must have a valid clutch type stored in it.\n\nThe item must be of type ITEM_CLUTCH. Ordinary held items cannot be\nactivated with this command.\n\nSee also: hold wear remove\n
407	call_of_the_wild	0	call of the wild	You call upon the wild to bring a creature to your side.\nFunctions like summon.\nDruid spell. Uses HP instead of mana and builds Overgrowth.\n
408	khenari	0	Khenari	Jackal-headed humanoids who emerged from the mortuary-legal culture of Akh'enet, the\nKhenari are psychopomps and death-administrators whose entire civilization is organized\naround managing the threshold between life and death as a civic institution. Their\nmeticulous death-ledgers form the connective tissue of inheritance, water-rights, and\nroad-law. The Bellwind Collapse scattered their court families outward along caravan\nroutes, and Khenari communities now serve as notaries, estate administrators, and\ndeath-record keepers wherever civilization requires incorruptible accuracy.\n
409	commands	0	commands	Syntax: commands [category]\n\nShows commands available to your character.\n
410	diplomat	-1	diplomat	Syntax: diplomat <message>\n\nClan diplomat communication channel.\nOnly players with diplomat access in a clan may use this command.\n
411	nightblade	0	nightblade	@@dHISTORY@@W\n\nThe Nightblade tradition has no guild and no formal founding -- traits\ninherited directly from the Assassin lineage that forms half its ancestry.\nFragmented records suggest the synthesis emerged in the post-empire margins,\nwhere agents who had preserved the original Assassin philosophy found\nthemselves operating alongside practitioners of the dark binding arts:\nWarlocks and their precursors, curse-weavers who trafficked in shadow-\ncompacts and the entropy of hexed intent. The combination was pragmatic\nbefore it was principled -- a blade guided by shadow-reading, a strike\ntimed to the window that a hex opened in an opponent's defense. Over\ngenerations it refined into something with its own doctrine. Where the\nAssassin tradition held that the perfect kill required patience and\npositioning, the Nightblade synthesis added a third condition: the ability\nto strip the target's resistance before contact, leaving them open to a\nblow they cannot answer.\n\n@@dNIGHTBLADE@@W\n\nBorn where moonlight fails and steel whispers, Nightblades are the perfected\nfusion of @@dAssassin@@W precision and @@dWarlock@@W cruelty. They are not mere\nkillers; they are executioners of the unseen hour, striking from angles most\nfoes never learn to fear until it is too late.\n\nTo become a Nightblade, you must master either @@dAssassin@@W or @@dWarlock@@W\n(remort prerequisites for the adept path).\n\n@@dPassive class advantages@@W\nNightblade grants several always-on combat bonuses as your adept level rises:\n\n  1) @@wCritical chance bonus@@W\n     - You gain passive critical-hit chance from Nightblade level.\n     - Scaling: +0.25% crit chance per Nightblade level (up to +5% at 20).\n\n  2) @@wCritical damage bonus@@W\n     - Your critical strikes deal more damage.\n     - Scaling: +0.5% crit multiplier per Nightblade level (up to +10% at 20).\n\n  3) @@wBackstab / circle damage bonus@@W\n     - Backstab and circle gain a direct Nightblade damage multiplier.\n     - Scaling: +2% damage per Nightblade level (up to +40% at 20).\n\n  4) @@wExtra attack round@@W\n     - Having any Nightblade adept level grants an additional melee hit in the\n       multi-hit calculation.\n\n@@dUnique Nightblade mechanics@@W\n  * @@wNightblade stance@@W becomes available, including the @@ddual backstab@@W\n    stance flag for high-pressure opener play.\n  * @@wPoison:nightshade@@W is learned at Nightblade level 2.\n  * Nightblade uses @@wDexterity@@W as its adept prime attribute and follows the\n    adept progression profile for survivability and mana growth.\n\n@@dNightblade reincarnation bonus@@W\nEach Nightblade adept reincarnation grants an additional passive bonus:\n\n  * @@wBackstab / circle damage@@W: +2% per Nightblade adept reincarnation.\n    This stacks with the normal Nightblade adept level scaling above.\n\nIn short: Nightblade is the apex stealth-damage adept, specializing in\ncritical lethality and empowered backstab/circle kill windows.\n\nSee also: @@mremort assassinate backstab circle poison:nightshade stance@@W\n
412	learned	0	learned	Syntax: learned\n\nDisplays all skills and spells that your character currently has access to,\nalong with your proficiency level in each. Skills you can use are filtered\nfrom the full skill list based on your class and level.\n\nThe proficiency column shows how well-trained you are in each skill, ranging\nfrom untrained to master levels. Higher proficiency means more reliable and\nmore effective use.\n\nOutput is shown in three columns for readability.\n\n  learned         -- Shows all usable skills/spells and their proficiency.\n\nFor information about a specific skill, type:\n  shelp <skill name>\n\nSee also: slist spells shelp train gain\n
413	colist	0	colist	Syntax: colist\n\nDisplays a complete reference list of all available color codes. Color codes\ncan be used in your title, description, and anywhere the game accepts\nplayer-formatted text.\n\nTo use a color code, type @@ followed immediately by the letter (no spaces):\n  @@r  -- Red        @@g  -- Green\n  @@b  -- Blue       @@y  -- Yellow\n  @@c  -- Cyan       @@m  -- Magenta\n  @@w  -- White      @@k  -- Dark/Black\n  @@N  -- Reset to normal color\n  @@W  -- Bright white (bold)\n\nExample:  Your title set to "@@rMighty@@N Warrior" would display as:\n  (red)Mighty(reset) Warrior\n\nColor display requires the COLOR setting to be enabled. Use the CONFIG or\nCOLOR command to toggle color support on or off.\n\nSee also: color config title description\n
414	keep	0	keep	  keep\n  keep create\n  keep title <string>\n  keep desc <string>\n  keep regen\n  keep inside\n  keep storage\n  keep healer\nUsing @@ykeep@@N will recall you to your keep.\nUsing @@ykeep create@@N creates your keep with @@yno_teleport@@N, @@yno_bloodwalk@@N,\n@@yno_portal@@N, @@yno_mob@@N, and @@ysafe@@N flags.\nUsing @@ykeep title <string>@@N while inside your keep will update your keep's\ntitle.\nUsing @@ykeep desc <string>@@N while inside your keep will update your keep's\ndescription.\nUsing @@ykeep regen@@N while inside your keep adds the @@yregen@@N room flag for\n@@Y100@@N quest points.\nUsing @@ykeep inside@@N while inside your keep adds the @@yinside@@N room flag for\n@@Y50@@N quest points.\nUsing @@ykeep storage@@N while inside your keep expands keep chest capacity by\n@@Y5@@N slots. Cost is tiered at @@Y50@@N quest points per tier: @@Y50->55 = 50@@N,\n@@Y55->60 = 100@@N, @@Y60->65 = 150@@N, and so on.\nUsing @@ykeep healer@@N while inside your keep purchases a personal healer for\n@@Y250@@N quest points. This purchase is permanent and can only be done once.
415	flurry	0	flurry	Syntax: flurry <target>\n\nChannels all remaining chi energy into a rapid sequence of strikes against\na single target. Each point of chi spent produces one additional attack,\nmaking flurry highly damaging when your chi pool is full.\n\nEffects:\n  - Repeatedly executes one_hit() against the target, once per chi point.\n  - Drains your entire chi pool in the process.\n  - Activates a 30-round cooldown preventing reuse.\n\nBecause flurry consumes all your chi, activating it when your chi pool is\nlow produces few hits. Maximize effectiveness by building chi before use.\n\nRequirements:\n  - Must be in combat.\n  - Must have at least 5 chi points available.\n  - Must have the Flurry skill learned.\n\nSee also: shelp flurry chakra spinfist phantomfist\n
416	mindoverbody	0	mindoverbody	Syntax: mindoverbody\n\nUses focused mental discipline to trigger healing over time during combat.\nBy concentrating your mind on physical recovery, you can sustain yourself\nthrough ongoing damage. This skill is available to Pugilist-line characters\n(Monk, Brawler, Martial Artist).\n\nEffects when activated:\n  - Costs energy (via the energy system, cost is higher if cooldown is active).\n  - Grants +1 chi.\n  - Applies a healing-over-time (HOT) affect lasting 3 combat rounds.\n    Healing amount is based on: Pugilist level + (Monk * 2) + (Brawler * 2)\n    + (Martial Artist * 5).\n  - Activates a 15-round cooldown preventing reuse.\n\nRequirements:\n  - Must be in combat.\n  - Must have energy available.\n  - Must have the Mind Over Body skill learned.\n\nSee also: shelp mind over body chakra healing light restoration\n
417	flee	0	flee	Syntax: flee\n\nAttempts to escape from combat.\n
418	remove	0	remove	Syntax: remove <item>\n\nRemoves worn equipment.\n
419	diku	-1	diku	                    Original game idea, concept, and design:\n\n          Katja Nyboe               [Superwoman] (katz@freja.diku.dk)\n\n          Tom Madsen              [Stormbringer] (noop@freja.diku.dk)\n\n          Hans Henrik Staerfeldt           [God] (bombman@freja.diku.dk)\n\n          Michael Seifert                 [Papi] (seifert@freja.diku.dk)\n\n          Sebastian Hammer               [Quinn] (quinn@freja.diku.dk)\n\n                     Additional contributions from:\n\nMichael Curran  - the player title collection and additional locations.\n\nRagnar Loenn    - the bulletin board.\n\nBill Wisner     - for being the first to successfully port the game,\n\n                  uncovering several old bugs, uh, inconsistencies,\n\n                  in the process.\n\nAnd: Mads Haar and Stephan Dahl for additional locations.\n\nDeveloped at: DIKU -- The Department of Computer Science\n\n                      at the University of Copenhagen.\n\n
420	password	0	password	Syntax: password <old> <new>\n\nChanges your account password.\n
421	newbie	0	NEWBIE NEW_PLAYER	@@YWelcome to ACK!MUD TNG.@@N  Here is what you need to know to get started.\n\n@@gTHE BASICS@@N\n\n  This is a multiclass MUD.  Your character belongs to several classes at\n  once.  Levels are gained manually — type @@cGAIN@@N to see which classes\n  you can advance and what it costs in experience points.\n  See also:  @@cHELP GAIN@@N   @@cHELP MULTI@@N\n\n  @@cRecall@@N anytime to return to the Temple in Midgaard — it is free.\n  There is no rent.  Type @@cSAVE@@N to save your character, @@cQUIT@@N to exit.\n  There are no deathtraps.\n\n@@gWHEN YOU DIE@@N\n\n  Your corpse is transported to the Morgue of Moribound.  Only you can\n  loot your own corpse.  Corpses decay over time — retrieve yours promptly.\n  You lose half your experience points on death.\n  See also:  @@cHELP DEATH@@N\n\n@@gESSENTIAL COMMANDS@@N\n\n  @@cSCORE@@N       — your stats, level, gold, and condition\n  @@cWORTH@@N       — experience progress toward your next gain\n  @@cINVENTORY@@N   — items you are carrying\n  @@cEQUIPMENT@@N   — items you are wearing or holding\n  @@cTRAIN@@N       — spend trains to raise base attributes\n  @@cWHO@@N         — see who else is online\n  @@cHELP <topic>@@N — look up anything\n\n@@gCOLOR@@N\n\n  Color is configurable.  Type @@cCOLOUR HELP@@N to see available colors and\n  how to set them.  Use @@cCONFIG@@N to toggle ANSI color on or off.\n  See also:  @@cHELP COLOUR@@N\n\n@@gCOMMUNICATION@@N\n\n  @@cSAY <text>@@N      — speak to people in your room\n  @@cGOSSIP <text>@@N   — public channel heard by everyone\n  @@cTELL <name> <text>@@N — private message to one player\n  @@cYELL <text>@@N     — heard in adjacent rooms\n  @@cAFK@@N            — flag yourself as away from keyboard\n\n@@gRULES@@N\n\n  Type @@cHELP RULES@@N before you do anything else.  They are short.\n\n@@gASKING FOR HELP@@N\n\n  Use @@cGOSSIP@@N or @@cTELL@@N to ask other players questions.\n  Staff — address them politely and only when needed.\n  Use the @@cPRAY@@N command for genuine staff attention; do not spam it.\n
422	substrate_piercing	0	substrate piercing	A passive Druid skill that allows your earth and poison spells to\nbypass elemental resistance. Unlocked through reincarnation.\n
