317	39	1	0	The Binder Collegium was the necromancer-clerk faction that consolidated control over Shadowmere's\nossuary archives, mirror testimony corridors, and binding cells after the frontier march's\nemergency governance framework dissolved. Collegium members—necromancer-clerics, lich-adjacent\nadepts, and record-wraiths—treated souls as administrative entries requiring categorization,\ncustody, and binding within Shadowmere's classification hierarchy. Their intellectual foundation\nwas the Crownward Compact's original principle that uniform recordkeeping prevents panic and\nfalse-claim wars. The Collegium took this to its logical extreme, maintaining legal forms with\nperfect precision after the governance those forms were meant to serve had collapsed. Mirrored\nadjudication rites extracted and mirrored confessions for cross-reference. Null-absolution\ncircles recorded that absolution was formally withheld and why. Name-seizure reliquaries held\nclassified identities as physical objects in custody. The Collegium did not seize power—it\ncontinued its functions after power ceased to be coherent in the march. Emergency administrative\ninfrastructure became permanent institutional identity.
