513	63	3	4	Kowloon's Umbral communities are smaller and less institutionally significant than Midgaard's, organized primarily around the undercity cistern networks where the Black Ledger is believed to be stored. Umbral shadow-archivists in Kowloon maintain records of the cistern network's development and current physical state — records that have the practical side-effect of providing the most detailed available map of where the Black Ledger's storage vault is located. The Jade Magistracy's relationship with Umbral communities is transactional and mutually uncomfortable: the Magistracy values Umbral intelligence capabilities; the Umbral communities' knowledge of where the Black Ledger is stored creates a persistent leverage dynamic that neither party fully acknowledges. Both cities have shadow-archives maintained by Umbral communities that contain records of what the official archives suppress. Both cities have chosen, in different ways, not to formally confront what those shadow-archives contain.
