516	63	6	16	Mafdet's attestation system creates a functional mechanism for Umbral civic standing without requiring anatomical classification that accommodates their semi-substantial nature. The Claw Mark Registry processes Umbral through conduct-based attestation: what has this person done, who has witnessed it, what are the terms of attested commitments. The semi-substantial nature of Umbral bodies creates specific complications for the physical attestation process — the standard witnessed handclasp requires tactile confirmation that Umbral presence sometimes fails to provide clearly. The Swift Court has developed alternative attestation protocols for Umbral: formal declaration before three witnesses counts as attestation where physical contact is uncertain. Umbral-carried documents are technically shadow-archive format — legible only in near-total darkness with appropriate sensory adaptation — creating a specific professional niche: Umbral archivists as custodians of documents requiring specific handling protocols.
517	63	7	513	An Umbral living in Midgaard's deep levels occupies the position that their philosophy most fully describes: necessary presence defined by institutional absence. The shadow-archives contain the actual record; the Gloamvault predates the city above it; the records that Continuity suppresses are accessible in the dark below. The Reckoning faction cultivates Umbral archive access because the archives contain what the official record lacks. The Continuity faction tolerates this because suppression has consistently failed and Umbral intelligence function is genuinely useful. An Umbral in Midgaard is simultaneously the city's most valuable archival resource and its most persistent institutional inconvenience: their records prove the official records are incomplete, and their existence proves that the city cannot successfully suppress what exists in its own foundations. The city was built above the Gloamvault. The Umbral remain.
