524	64	6	16	Mafdet's Quarantine Ledger maintains a special category for Kel'Shadra-provenance relics: items whose legal history includes periods of coercive record manipulation. The Sealed Names Apparatus review protocols reference the Night as the example motivating redundant independent witness requirements. Mafdet's Harbor Wardens maintain awareness that several surviving Kel'Shadra institutional functions operate in the current era under changed names. Mafdet's Claw Mark Registry notes that the Gloamvault's continued operation after the Night is not evidence of reformed function. It is evidence of structural persistence despite ethical collapse.
