527	65	1	0	The Spirebound Conclave was a mountain academy in the Cinderteeth Range chartered to preserve\ndangerous magical knowledge under the doctrine of Continuance: no discovery, oath, or lesson\nshould die with its keeper. Three internal factions embodied three approaches to this mission:\nthe Ember Canon, which held that will expressed through fire was the most fundamental\ntransformative force; the Prism Thesis, which held that memory could be preserved through\ncrystal-binding; and the Pale Ledger, which held that testimony could be imprinted into\nspirit-mediums for indefinite preservation. The Conclave became the condemned-debtor transfer\napparatus—a mechanism that transferred populations as debt payment to fund the Conclave's\ncontinued operation. This apparatus involved at minimum three of the five current cities:\nMidgaard's trade ledgers contain the payment records, Kowloon's proto-delta settlements made\ncorresponding transfers whose records the Black Ledger is said to hold, and Kiess recovered\nan obsidian disc with the Conclave's triune seal during its foundation excavations of Evermeet's\nruins. The Prism Thesis's field trials produced the unintended Rivennid—mycelial humanoids\nwho emerged from abandoned crystal-preservation experiment sites in the Withered Depths when\nConclave preservation magic fused with fungal networks and bound nature spirits into new forms.\nThe Conclave itself collapsed, but its institutional guilt chain continues structuring the\nfive-city network's deepest political tensions.
