559	69	1	0	The Northern Pyramid is the state-monument of the Sand Sovereign, a dynastic heir claiming descent from the Solar Court's Dawn Liturgists.\nBuilt not merely as a tomb but as a political machine in stone, its geometry, procession routes, and celestial alignments make one unavoidable argument: authority over water, trade, death rites, and timekeeping belongs to the sovereign who can harmonize desert survival with the heavens.\nOasis-trained engineers from the Great Oasis Measuring House built the core geometry, bringing Measuring House precision, Water Court legal phrasebooks, and charter road methodology. The pyramid is a downstream expression of oasis science.\nThe ascending floor doctrine encodes administrative logic: lower levels handle containment and adjudication, while higher tiers become increasingly ceremonial, restricted, and astronomically coded.\nThree intertwined functions: funerary legitimacy (dynastic remains and oath-sealed preservation wards), astronomical governance (calibration chambers and star-table alcoves), and revenue theology (inscription programs equating levy collection with cosmic maintenance).\nSeven guardian spirits are bound to ascending floors: Crypt Pharaoh (undercroft), Desert Gate Guardian (ground), Scarab Colossus (Floor 1), High Priest of the Ancient Sands (Floor 2), Eternal Mummy Lord (Floor 3), Pyramid Drake (Floor 4), and the Sand Sovereign itself (Floor 5).\nThe binding mathematics were copied from the Great Pyramid's Seal College — geometries designed to contain the Black Sun Shard, repurposed as spirit-binding lattices.\nThe pyramid was built as a backup containment ring: the Sand Sovereign understood that the Great Pyramid's containment was degrading and designed the Northern Pyramid's seven guardian floors as concentric ritual barriers to slow anti-light radiation if the Great Pyramid's seals failed.\nThe ascending astronomical alignment passages are more precise than funerary tradition requires — they serve as monitoring instruments tracking celestial configurations used by the Seal College to calculate containment degradation rates.\nAstronomical sight-line from the apex summit is oriented toward the Great Pyramid's location on the horizon, functioning as a resonance channel the Sand Sovereign believed could transfer containment energy between structures.\nThe pyramid's cistern systems in the undercroft were originally fed by a canal from the Iseth Reach; when the Reach dried, the internal water supply failed and priestly factions competed for a shrinking supply, accelerating the pyramid's social collapse.\nThe Sand Sovereign and Moon Sovereign were twin siblings — their pyramids are physical arguments in a sibling cosmological debate about whether authority flows from above or from below.
