604	74	1	0	Umbra Heartspire is a failed judicial-religious archive: a satellite complex chartered during Midgaard's containment era to hold materials unsuited for market courts and common notice squares — sealed witness statements, disputed noble titles, war-crime depositions, and ritual contracts.\nIt began as an extension of Midgaard's record culture, absorbed Kiess's funerary rites and inheritance testimonies after Evermeet's fall, and was finally consumed by a shadow creed that mistook preservation for dominion.\nThree institutional inheritances became three corruptions: law as ritual (Midgaard's archive culture), death as continuity (Kiess/Evermeet inheritance), and shadow as infrastructure (Umbra transformation).\nFive institutional wings: Processional Spine (chain-of-custody halls, solemn intake), Mirror-Archive Wing (Kiess memory politics, mirror oath rites, acoustic cross-witnessing), Iron-Wake Bastion (enforcement architecture, execution infrastructure embedded in judicial space), Astral-Orrery Wing (prophecy engines, fate machinery, null-sigil galleries), Root-Crown Finale (convergence where all branches feed one office).\nAbbot Noctivar's Ebon Pulse creed teaches: all testimony decays, all memory fragments, only curated shadow can keep civilization from tearing itself apart. Under this creed, falsification is mercy. The institution no longer stores truth; it manufactures survivable narratives.\nThe Thorned Throne in the Processional Spine formalizes the first institutional lie: that judgment here is impartial.\nThe Mirror Wing's cracked reliquaries symbolize edited lineages; the Harrowed Duchess embodies noble memory trapped in institutional script.\nThe Astral Orrery faction claimed stellar patterns could pre-authorize verdicts; appeal rights collapsed because outcomes were framed as cosmically ratified.\nThe Oathbound Remnant hides corrective annotations in side-ledgers and bell timing marks; the Mirror Court Survivors preserve etiquette as resistance;