617	75	6	16	The catastrophe's most direct effect on Mafdet is the Glasswind Belt: glass-fused terrain creating the Saltglass Reach's most dangerous transit zone.\nGlass color varies with distance from the epicenter; milky glass is stable, amber is thermally proximate, violet marks eclipse-rite residue areas that behave unpredictably under load.\nThe Quarantine Ledger maintains a geological advisory for Reach transit operators: avoid violet-glass zones without certified Glasswalk Guide escort.\nMafdet's three-route system across the Reach was partly designed around the catastrophe's terrain modification, routing around violet-glass concentrations where possible.\nThe Shoreward Assessors treat the Ninth Meridian's territorial consequences as active legal context, not historical background.\nThe Claw Mark Registry's oldest entries reference the post-catastrophe terrain as the reason the Shoreward Assessor profession became necessary; before the catastrophe, the Reach required standard desert navigation skills.
618	75	7	16400	Kethari water-memory preserves the most detailed pre-institutional record of the catastrophe's hydrological effects on the Saltglass Reach.\nPre-catastrophe water-memory describes different mineral content, different aquifer-to-surface flow ratios, and different seasonal variation patterns than post-catastrophe records show.\nPost-catastrophe shift: increased silica saturation, altered salt concentration in the Mirror Flats' underlying deposits, and an unsounded depth zone where water-memory becomes unreliable.\nKethari analysis places the unsounded depth's origin in the thermal pulse propagating through the subsurface along an ancient water-bearing stratum, partially fusing it.\nKethari water-readers have submitted this analysis to Mafdet's Quarantine Ledger and Kiess's frontier cartography office; both submissions were accepted as primary source material.\nKethari position: the catastrophe did not end when the thermal pulse stopped. It continues in the aquifer. The water still carries the wound.
619	75	8	66	Khenari descent-records across nine cycles document the catastrophe's mortuary consequences as the largest event of unrecorded death in corridor history.\nMass death in the thermal zone occurred faster than any mortuary institution could process; bodies consumed, records destroyed, lineages severed.\nNine cycles of descent-record review have not closed this debt because the missing persons cannot be identified without the destroyed records.\nKhenari in Kiess's witness registry filed a formal notation: the Ninth Meridian represents a gap in the corridor's legal death-record constituting an ongoing administrative emergency.\nThe notation has been acknowledged but not acted upon; no institution has authority to close mortuary records for deaths predating the current governance framework.\nKiess's three-power charter has no mechanism for assigning liability to defunct institutions. The advisory remains on file as an acknowledged open debt. It has not closed in nine descent-cycles.
620	76	1	0	Egomancers are offensive psionic practitioners who emerged from the Assertion Wing of the Psionicist tradition — a school of thought arguing the mind's primary power lies in imposition rather than perception or communication. The Assertion Wing's foundational dispute with the academic mainstream concerned directionality: mainstream practice emphasized inward focus (self-knowledge, self-protection, mental clarity under pressure) while Assertionists held that refusing to develop outward imposition technique produces practitioners with untested theoretical models of cognitive force. The Assertion Wing's argument — that understanding imposition is necessary for effective defense against imposition — was philosophically coherent but ethically contested. Several Assertion teachers were expelled from affiliated academies for crossing ethical thresholds; they established independent schools framing their work as continuation of research the academies had declined to support. The Egomancer tradition's primary combat methodology is weaponized cognition: sustained mental pressure that prevents coherent opponent response across extended engagements, ranging from subtle attention redirection to overriding decision-making processes and fragmenting situational awareness. Preference for sustained pressure over single decisive bursts reflects both operational effectiveness and the theoretical commitment that continuous real-time cognitive modeling is a distinct and superior skill. The Kinetimancer adept synthesis combines Egomancer will-imposition with Necromancer entropy-redirection, a convergence the Kinetic Formulists identified theoretically before practitioners systematized it. Registry documentation is minimal or absent in most jurisdictions — the effects occur in cognitive architecture invisible to registry verification.
