636	78	1	0	High Priest Amenhotep was the architect of the doctrine that merged worship, taxation, and surveillance under the Solar Court of the Undivided Disk.\nTraditionally cast as Ramesses's faithful steward, he was in practice the designer of total ritual administration as governing philosophy.\nHis core belief: only comprehensive administrative ritual could prevent civil collapse under the Black Sun Shard's memory-plague conditions.\nHe developed the five-office priesthood structure: Dawn Liturgists, Ledger Priests, Embalmer Houses, Jackal Tribunal, and Seal College — each with distinct jurisdiction, together constituting total governance.\nHis reforms merged surveillance functions with religious observation, making every act of worship simultaneously an act of documentation.\nHe adopted the Keepers' Measure Script as a sacred administrative language, fusing two systems (administrative record and religious inscription) that the Keepers had kept separate.\nAmenhotep's doctrine saved the state from collapse during the Black Sun Shard's worst active period, and it normalized cruelty as a governance tool.\nThe five-office structure survived Ramesses's death; it survived the Archive Schism in fragments; elements appear in multiple current institutional lineages.\nHe is not a figure of heroic reputation in any of the Five Cities — he is a cautionary precedent.\nCurrent institutional lineages tracing to his designs include the cleric tradition's inner technical inheritance, the templar institutional origin, and several Midgaard charter oversight functions.\nThe Ledger Priests he shaped became the diaspora practitioners who carried cleric doctrine when the Solar Court fractured.\nHis philosophical legacy: effective governance and cruel governance are not opposites; they can coexist in the same institution.
637	78	2	1	Midgaard studies Amenhotep as an example of effective and dangerous institutional design. His five-office structure is the historical ancestor of multi-oversight governance — correct principle, oppressive application. The Violet Compact's occult oversight traces through the Seal College office he formalized. Continuity faction: his innovations were sound engineering; the ethical problem was absent external accountability, not the administrative structure itself. Reckoning faction: a structure designed to prevent external accountability cannot be rehabilitated; the structure is the failure. Midgaard's position: Amenhotep is the reason multi-institution oversight exists as a governance model and the reason it requires external accountability to function ethically.
