947	116	1	0	Wardens are defensive melee fighters descended from the road warden companies of the Keeper Era — professional escorts chartered to protect caravans across the desert road network under contracts that bounded them to assigned corridors and prohibited action outside their commission. This constraint shaped the tradition's foundational doctrine: holding assigned ground, not conquest; patience under pressure, positional awareness, capacity to absorb damage without breaking. Warden-Sergeant Caleph Dunmar's forty-three day defense of the Seven Shade Arches waystation — holding a water convoy with nothing but defensive ground and discipline against an Ashbound siege during the Ninth Meridian Catastrophe's aftermath — produced the foundational Ember Warden combat doctrine: fight near shade infrastructure, target logistics first, hold until the principal objective is secured. The Reaver Confederates, road warden companies who outlived their employers when the charter network collapsed, carried forward warden doctrine through the chaos of the Catastrophe, establishing that force without institutional context is not automatically illegitimate but requires continuous re-justification through conduct. The Ash-and-Iron Decades militarization produced the requisition office system, which formalized warden training under civic authority at the cost of the tradition's autonomous professional judgment — the defining internal tension between the Dunmar School (doctrine and discipline supersede orders when orders would violate fundamental protective purpose) and the Registry School (civic legitimacy requires institutional obedience, and wardens who act outside commission become Reaver Confederates by another name). The Crusader adept synthesis, emerging from the Ash-and-Iron Decades reserve depots where Knight and Warden-descended Swordsman training shared institutional space, chains Knight body-strike sequences into Swordsman momentum accumulation for combined force neith