1016	124	3	4	Kowloon's northern survey records contain pre-formal-survey route entries in the Cinderteeth passes attributed to Retha An. These entries do not carry the Kowloon survey seal but a chant-notation transliterated from oral transmission.\nThe Neon Covenant's Black Ledger records Retha An's attestations as pre-crisis route preservation: the passes existed, were used, were named, and survived institutional collapse.\nFrom Kowloon's perspective, this is exactly what crisis protocol is supposed to produce: function preserved when formal systems fail.\nAn individual held the route network together during the post-Conclave gap — impressive and institutionally inconvenient, as Kowloon's authority over those passes rests partly on Retha An's attestation chain.\nAcknowledging her is acknowledging that Kowloon's authority is derivative of an individual who preceded it. Kowloon acknowledges this quietly.\nWithout Retha An's attestation work, three northern passes would have been lost to competing claims during the gap.
