1111	136	1	0	The Verdant Depths lie beneath and beyond the Forest of Confusion — an ancient, sentient woodland where the trees are older than every human institution in the known world.\nThe trees are not separate organisms but nodes in a single interconnected root network spanning the entire area. Damage to one tree triggers responses hundreds of paces away within minutes. The forest has distributed intelligence, not individual thought.\nThree functional aspects: Growth (Rootmother aspect, aggressive expansion, territory colonization), Decay (Blightwood aspect, accelerated breakdown of dead matter, feeds nutrients back to root network), and Predation (Thornfang aspect, territorial enforcement, resident predators optimized by millennia of selective pressure).\nThree Heartwood Guardians embody these aspects: the Rootmother (growth focal point, does not move but grows, reshapes chamber terrain during combat), the Blightwood Ancient (decay incarnate, a biome-entity that processes corrupted matter from the Withered Depths boundary), and the Thornfang Alpha (predation incarnate, connected to root-network chemical signaling, strikes only when the forest identifies a threat lesser predators cannot handle).\nThe Forest of Confusion is not a separate phenomenon but the forest's outermost defense: volatile compounds released by the root network interfere with spatial memory, new vegetation closes paths that existed hours ago, game trails redirect away from the interior.\nThe Verdant Depths are in active ecological conflict with the Withered Depths' blight: growth response piles up biomass at the contamination boundary, decay response redirects toward corrupted matter, predation response has made territorial creatures more aggressive than comparable creatures in the Great Northern Forest.\nPre-civilizational peoples recognized the Verdant Depths as a zone that did not accept human stewardship: Everkeepers' planting rings are absent from the interior. The Cairn-Keepers' deepest