COPY public.room_extra_descs (id, room_vnum, keyword, description) FROM stdin;
1	152	gate	The iron gate bears countless ancient runes. You recognize some as\nwards against the living, others as bindings to prevent whatever is\ninside from escaping. Someone - or something - has partially broken\nseveral of the wards from the inside.\n
2	153	fountain	The dark liquid in the fountain has the consistency of old blood but\nsmells of nothing at all. Where it touches the stone basin, the stone\nhas turned black and cracked. You sense that drinking from it would be\nvery unwise.\n
3	154	banners	The banners bear the crest of Kel'Shadra - a void eye ringed by\nseven black stars. The fabric is impossibly cold to the touch and\nseems to absorb light rather than merely blocking it.\n
4	155	puzzle pedestal rings	The three obsidian rings can each be rotated. If you study the symbols\ncarefully, you notice that each ring depicts phases of some celestial body.\nThe correct sequence will unlock a hidden door. Type 'solve puzzle' to\nattempt to align the rings. (Hint: full, crescent, new)\n
5	156	gem crystal wall	The gem is embedded deeply in the wall and cannot be removed without\nshattering it. It pulses with a slow, rhythmic light - almost like breathing.\n
6	157	frost crystals marks	The frost crystals have formed into patterns that almost resemble runes.\nYou notice that the drag marks lead deeper into the complex, not toward\nthe exit. Whatever was dragged came from deeper within.\n
7	158	thrones rubble	The thrones were clearly once places of great authority. The carvings\non them depict three figures: a warrior, a sorcerer, and a figure with\nno face at all. The faceless figure's throne is the one least damaged.\n
8	159	altar void-stone	The altar hums with dangerous energy. Carved into its surface are the\nwords: 'Only the blood of the willing opens the path.' Below this,\nsomeone has scratched in more recent script: 'I was willing. Do not follow.'\n
9	160	ice faces frozen	The faces within the ice are too numerous to count. Men, women, creatures\nof various races - all showing expressions of absolute terror. One face\nnear the floor has eyes that seem to follow you as you move.\n
10	161	names walls whispers	Scanning the names, you notice they begin in an ancient script and\ngradually evolve toward more modern writing. The most recent names are\nfrom people you might recognize. The very last name scratched appears\nto have been left unfinished - only the first three letters carved before\nwhatever was doing the carving stopped.\n
11	162	ashes ash floor	The ash on the floor forms patterns when disturbed - not the random patterns\nof settling dust, but deliberate shapes that reform within seconds of being\ndisrupted. Circles within circles, over and over again, endlessly.\n
12	163	portraits plaques names	Some of the names on the plaques match names from the Chamber of Whispers.\nThe most recent plaque has a blank space where the name should be - the\ndate upon it is contemporary. Whoever was meant to be remembered here\neither has not yet failed, or their failure is too recent to be chronicled.\n
13	164	figure key ice frozen	The frozen figure's eyes are open. You notice with a start that they are\ntracking your movements. The key in its hand appears to be obsidian, deeply\ncarved with void runes. If you could thaw the ice without shattering the key...\nThe puzzle: the temperature runes on the walls suggest the ice responds to\nheat runes arranged in the correct order. Examine the walls for guidance.\n
14	165	mirrors reflections	If you stare at your reflection long enough, it seems to try to communicate\nwith you - mouthing words, pointing in various directions. It looks frightened\nof something behind you, though nothing is there when you turn.\n
15	166	scorch marks ceiling symbols	The symbols on the ceiling are not the same as the runes elsewhere in\nKel'Shadra. They are older, cruder - suggesting this part of the keep\nwas built before the void entity arrived, by the original mortal builders.\n
16	167	alcoves objects bell mirror	The objects in the alcoves are personal items - things with emotional weight.\nSomeone collected these deliberately. The dried flower is pressed flat but\nstill faintly fragrant; the child's toy is painted with a name that has\nsince faded. These are memories made physical.\n
17	168	crystals formations walls	The crystals appear to be condensed void-energy that has taken on a\nsemi-solid state due to the extreme cold nearby. They are beautiful and\ncompletely inert, responding only to body heat by briefly brightening\nwhen touched, then fading back to their dim glow.\n
18	169	names inscriptions wall	The inscriptions are in dozens of languages, spanning what appears to be\nseveral centuries. Some names have been scratched out with apparent fury.\nOthers have small symbols next to them - not words, but marks suggesting\na category or fate. Most symbols repeat, suggesting they have meaning.\n
19	170	arrow slits quiver horn	The arrows have corroded over time; the tips remain sharp but the fletching\nhas long since rotted away. The signaling horn still gleams - made of some\nmaterial that resists tarnish. You suspect blowing it would be unwise.\n
20	171	orb experiment wire gems	The experiment appears to be some kind of resonance device - each small\ngem vibrates at a different frequency, and the silver wire transmits these\nvibrations to the orb, which integrates them into the pulsing light. It\nis either beautiful mathematics or someone's attempt to hear the void.\n
21	172	mirrors obsidian reflections corridor	The obsidian mirrors are seamlessly fitted and perfectly smooth. Whatever\ncraftsmen created them were masters of their art. The reflections within\nare not quite accurate - there is always a slight lag, a slight wrongness\nthat makes extended gazing uncomfortable. Best to navigate by touch.\n
22	185	carvings eyes wall	Looking carefully at the eyes, you notice some have pupils shaped like\ndirectional arrows. Following them in sequence: north, west, west, north.\nThis may be a clue to navigating the labyrinth.\n
23	195	pit bottom	The pit goes down further than any light can reach. The breathing sound\nhas a rhythm to it - slow and patient, like something very large and very\nold sleeping fitfully. You decide not to jump in.\n
24	199	window vision army shades	You watch for a while, transfixed. One of the shades near the back slowly\nturns its head in your direction. It can't possibly see you through this\nmagical barrier. It stares directly at you. It raises one hand in what\nmight be a warning gesture.\n
25	207	door keyhole stone	The door is solid iron, cold to the touch, bearing no decoration except\nthe glowing stone. The stone's light pulses slowly, as if in reaction\nto your presence. The keyhole is deep and its shape precise - only the\nright key will work.\n
26	212	reflections marble floor	The reflections... if you watch closely, they are not showing alternate\nversions of you. They are showing your past - moments from your life,\nreplayed on the polished surfaces. The citadel is watching. It knows\nwho you are.\n
469	2842	patrol web	Carved arrows preserve a linear route with deliberate side links for rapid patrol rotation.
27	213	souls containers niches names	You read a few names on the containers: adventurers, knights, scholars,\nall who dared enter Kel'Shadra and were taken. Some containers are empty\nand dark. Perhaps their owners escaped. Perhaps something else happened.\n
28	214	book lectern writing	The book is writing about you in real time: your appearance, your equipment,\nyour visible emotional state. The writing is precise and clinical, lacking\nany judgment. Disturbingly, it also describes the thoughts it believes you\nare currently thinking. It is more accurate than it should be.\n
29	215	puzzle rings mechanism door	The puzzle has twelve rings arranged in a three-by-four grid pattern,\neach capable of rotating independently. The engravings on each ring\ncorrespond to the phases of multiple celestial bodies. A faded inscription\nnear the base of the mechanism reads: 'As above in darkness, so below in\nlight. Align the void's own stars to open the way.' The key you found\nearlier bears symbols that match the alignment needed.\n
30	216	below chamber figures	The figures below move in precise, ritualistic patterns. They are\nvoid priests, chanting in their silent language, maintaining some\nenchantment that keeps the inner sanctum stable. If their patterns\nwere disrupted, something would change. You suspect it would not\nbe an improvement.\n
31	219	mosaic battle history	The mosaic tells the story of Kel'Shadra's rise - a void entity drawn\nto the material plane by the ambitions of mortal sorcerers who sought\nto harness its power. The final tiles show the sorcerers' expressions\nof horrified realization as the entity turned on its summoners. The\nartist made sure to capture that moment in great detail.\n
32	220	throne crown void-eyes ceiling	The crown above the throne is the focus of the room's power. It bears\nan inscription: 'Only the worthy may unseat the void.' This room is\na test as much as a destination. The void-eyes above seem to evaluate\nevery choice you make.\n
33	221	archive barriers texts void-light	The intact barriers hum with suppressed power. The texts within float\nfreely, their pages turning as if being read by invisible scholars.\nThe knowledge here is too dangerous to take, and you suspect that\nattempting to break a barrier would attract significant attention.\n
34	222	racks dummies battle preparation	The weapons on the racks are not for mortals - they are void-touched\nimplements of war, their edges able to cut spirit as easily as flesh.\nThe training dummies regenerate damage at a visible rate, reforming\nfrom whatever attack left them broken.\n
35	223	sigil circle patterns ritual	The sigil at the center of the chamber is the binding seal that contains\nKel'Shadra's consciousness within this plane. It was inscribed by the\noriginal sorcerers who summoned the entity and then realized their mistake.\nThe void priests maintain it - not to honor the void, but because without\nit, Kel'Shadra would not be contained to this citadel.\n
36	225	sigil binding runes circle void	The binding is ancient but still strong - barely. Cracks have appeared\nin several of the runes, and the energy seeping through those cracks is\nintense. The circle was designed to hold the entity indefinitely, but\n'indefinitely' is a relative term when measured against the patience of\na void entity.\n
37	226	instructions components ritual maintenance	Skimming the instructions, the key steps appear to involve regular\nreinforcement of the outer runes, quarterly replacement of certain\ncrystallized components, and an annual grand ritual that requires\na significant sacrifice. The instructions note that failure to\nmaintain the schedule could allow partial manifestation.\n
38	227	floor glow energy mind	The presence in the back of your mind is curious rather than malicious.\nIt seems to be cataloging you, filing you away in some vast mental archive\nalongside all the other mortals who have walked this path. You are\nnot the first. You will not be the last.\n
39	232	presence void entity shadow	Kel'Shadra does not speak - it has no need for such crude communication.\nBut impressions filter through the barrier: curiosity, hunger, patience,\nand something that might, in a void entity, be called satisfaction.\nIt has been waiting a long time for a worthy challenge.\n
40	237	kel'shadra entity manifestation void battle	Kel'Shadra regards you with something like interest. It has faced countless\nchallengers over the centuries, and every single one has fallen. Its form\nshifts and moves, displaying weapons and abilities chosen specifically to\ncounter what it has observed of your fighting style during your journey\nthrough the citadel. It has been watching since you entered the gate.\n
41	242	brazier void-fire items relics	The void-fire burns cold and does not consume what it touches. The items\naround the brazier are not random - they have been deliberately placed here\nas offerings or warnings. A note in several languages reads:\n'Leave what you do not need. Take what you can carry. Do not linger.'\n
42	243	study notes research sorcerer advice	The sorcerer's notes are extensive and well-organized despite being\ncenturies old. The critical section is titled 'Weaknesses of the Void':\napparently the entity can be damaged significantly more effectively\nif attacked while it is maintaining one of its secondary abilities.\nThe notes also mention that the sorcerer hid his best weapons here.\n
43	244	pool water vision memory	The pool's surface is absolutely still. Looking into it, you can see\nyour own reflection clearly - but it changes, aging rapidly, then\nreversing, then stopping at a specific moment. The pool shows you\nsomething you will do. Whether it is a warning or a gift depends\nentirely on what you do with the knowledge.\n
44	246	niches bodies preserved	The preserved dead line every available surface. Unlike simple mummies,\nthese show signs of continuous void-energy infusion: faint dark light\npulses beneath their skin, and their expressions appear to change when\nyou look away. The oldest are nearly unrecognizable as humanoid.\n
45	248	tools tables preparation	The preservation tools include implements for extracting vital essence,\ncontainers for storing void-energy, and what appears to be a ritual\nguide. The guide is written in a cipher, but diagrams suggest the\nprocess involved extracting the soul partially and binding it to the\nbody rather than allowing full departure.\n
46	249	sarcophagi carvings honored dead	Reading the carved histories: a great warlord who conquered three\nnations for Kel'Shadra's glory; a sorceress who sacrificed herself\nto seal a breach in the binding circle; a spy who infiltrated enemy\ncourts for decades. These were extraordinary people who served an\nextraordinary evil with complete devotion.\n
47	251	grates iron below movement	Peering through the grates, you can see a lower level of the catacombs\npopulated with the less-honored dead - those who served but did not\ndistinguish themselves. They move with the mindless patience of the\nlong-dead, following patterns laid down when they were first interred.\n
48	252	warriors weapons martial instincts	The champions' formation is perfect even in death: overlapping fields\nof defense, clear lines of attack, coordinated positioning. Whoever\ntrained these warriors when they lived was a genius of battlefield\ntactics. Death has not diminished their formation one iota.\n
49	253	pool fluid black	The pool's surface is absolutely unreflective, absorbing all light.\nDropping a stone in produces no splash - the stone simply vanishes\nwithout a sound. The pool may not be liquid at all. It may be\nsomething else entirely that happens to occupy this space.\n
50	255	murals battles deaths	The murals extend around all four walls and onto the ceiling. Hundreds\nof moments of death, each unique, each rendered with the specificity\nof a witness account. The painter must have been present for some of\nthese moments. The most recent mural depicts a death from only fifty\nyears ago.\n
51	256	roots stone anchor pulse	The roots are too large to move and too well-anchored to damage.\nThey carry the void energy like veins carry blood, the pulse traveling\nupward to the citadel's ritual spaces. Disrupting them would require\npower enough to shake the foundations of the building - and doing so\nwould certainly attract significant attention.\n
52	258	trophies weapons armor enchantments	The enchantments on the displayed weapons are still active, maintaining\nthemselves without user intent. Some call to adventurers - magical\nweapons have a will of their own. A wise voice in the back of your\nmind notes that taking a displayed trophy from a dedicated collection\nin an active citadel would provoke a response.\n
53	259	decor bones candles carpet	The arrangement of bones in the antechamber is not random decoration:\nit is a formal language of display that announces the rank and power of\nwhoever lies beyond. Reading it: a being of great age, great power, and\nabsolute authority over the dead within this complex. A statement of\ndominance directed at any who approach.\n
54	260	files documents archive maintenance	Skimming the archive: it is organized by seniority of service, not\nby date of death. The most prominent file belongs to the Catacomb Lord,\nwho appears to maintain the archive personally. The file contains self-\nassessments of its own power and capabilities that are deeply concerning\nto read.\n
55	261	chains prisoners suspension	The prisoners are from many races and many eras. Some of the oldest\nappear to have been here for centuries. Their eyes follow you with\ndesperate intelligence. You have no way to free them quickly - the\nvoid-seals require specific counter-magic - but you note their\npresence for future reference.\n
56	262	throne bones canopy power	The throne is a masterpiece of dark artistry and a terrifying statement\nof power. Every bone in its construction belonged to someone powerful.\nThe arrangement is deliberate: greater power displayed in more\nprominent positions, like a hierarchy made permanent in death.\n
57	273	laboratory research circles workbenches	The ritual circles on the floor show multiple layers of inscription -\neach new circle added over the previous ones as the research progressed.\nThe progression tells a story of escalating ambition: early circles\nare for basic void-energy collection; later ones are attempts to\ncommunicate directly with the entity. The final layer was never\ncompleted.\n
58	274	library shelves volumes iron-bound	The surviving volumes are written in an academic magical shorthand\nthat would take years to fully decode. Skimming them: they are\nresearch journals tracking experiments in void-energy manipulation.\nThe final entries grow increasingly frantic, describing an experiment\nthat had begun to 'respond' in ways they had not anticipated.\n
59	275	observatory instruments dome	The instruments are still functioning, their needles moving in slow\narcs as they track void-energy concentrations. At the center of the\ndome, a point of greatest concentration is marked: it is directly\nbelow this level, in the spire's foundations. Whatever began here\nhas not ended.\n
60	276	quarters rooms abandoned	The personal effects tell individual stories: a collection of pressed\nflowers from some distant garden, a set of children's toys kept by\nsomeone who missed their family, annotated books in a dozen languages.\nThese were people with lives before they became servants of void magic.\n
