9	shelp_cloak_drain	-1	cloak:drain	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Cloak:drain\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 550\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: @@NThe @@rcloak@@N around your body fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Necromancer: level 48\nDescription:\n   Cloak:drain is the Necromancer's signature remort cloak. It wraps the\n   caster in a dark, life-siphoning aura. When struck in melee combat, there\n   is a 35% chance that the cloak will activate, draining hit points from the\n   attacker equal to the caster's pseudo-level. The caster is healed for half\n   of the drained amount, up to their maximum hit points.\n\n   The cloak does a small amount of damage, but its primary value is the\n   lifedrain effect -- sustaining the Necromancer through prolonged fights.\n   The attacker's hit points cannot be drained below 10.\n\n   Duration scales with pseudo-level (pseudo_level / 8 rounds).\n*******************************************************************************\n
10	shelp_cloak_adept	-1	cloak:adept	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Cloak:adept\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 500\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: @@NThe @@Wcloak@@N around your body fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Not learnable by player classes.\nDescription:\n   Cloak:adept is a powerful cloak available to adept-tier characters. It\n   surrounds the caster in a brilliant aura that provides three offensive\n   bonuses:\n\n     - Hitroll: +2 per pseudo-level (e.g. +200 at pseudo-level 100)\n     - Defense: +5 AC bonus\n     - Damage: All damage dealt is multiplied by 1.2x (20% increase)\n\n   This cloak is primarily an offensive buff rather than a defensive one,\n   making it ideal for adept characters who want to maximize their damage\n   output.\n\n   Duration scales with pseudo-level (pseudo_level / 5 rounds).\n*******************************************************************************\n
11	shelp_shadow_reading	-1	shadow reading	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Shadow Reading\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE (self-buff)\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: Your shadow-sight fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Nightblade: level 5\nDescription:\n   Shadow Reading activates the Warlock compact's perception to assess the\n   target's "defensive energy distribution," granting a hitroll bonus that\n   represents reading the opponent's defensive orientation in real time.\n\n   Costs: Movement (via subtract_energy_cost)\n   Cooldown: 15 rounds\n   Duration: 4 + (Nightblade level / 4) rounds\n   Hitroll modifier: Nightblade level * 3 + Assassin level * 2\n                     + Warlock level * 2\n\n   Named explicitly in the Nightblade lore as a core technique: "a\n   practitioner with shadow reading can assess in real time which defensive\n   orientations the target is maintaining and which angles are consequently\n   underdefended."\n*******************************************************************************\n
12	shelp_divine_strike	-1	divine strike	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Divine Strike\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 15\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: divine strike\n   Wear-Off: !Divine Strike!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 4\nDescription:\n   Divine Strike channels concentrated holy power into a direct damaging\n   strike at a single target. Base damage is 3d10 + level/3 holy elemental\n   damage. Against evil targets (alignment < -350), damage is increased by\n   50%. An accessible early-level offensive spell for Clerics, providing\n   reliable single-target holy damage throughout the leveling progression.\n   Pairs well with Dispel Evil for sustained holy offense.\n*******************************************************************************\n
13	shelp_know_item	-1	know item	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Know Item\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_OBJ_INV\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 20\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Know Item!\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 9\nDescription:\n   Know Item Provides immediate lore-style insight into an item's purpose and notable traits.\n*******************************************************************************\n
14	shelp_calm	-1	calm	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Calm\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 30\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Calm!\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 52\nDescription:\n   Calm Pacifies aggression in the target, reducing hostile behavior and helping de-escalate fights.\n*******************************************************************************\n
15	shelp_solar_precision	-1	solar precision	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Solar Precision\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Solar Precision!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 20\nDescription:\n   Solar Precision is a passive divine discipline mastered by experienced\n   Clerics. Through meditation on Disk's clarity and unwavering judgment,\n   the Cleric aligns their divine conduit with solar principles of exactness.\n   This alignment improves the critical strike rate of the Cleric's spells,\n   allowing their divine attacks to land with far greater force when the\n   moment of clarity arrives.\n\n   When Solar Precision triggers, the critical hit also deals bonus damage\n   beyond the normal critical multiplier, as the Cleric's perfectly aligned\n   divine energy sears through the target with unusual intensity. The\n   passive is always active once learned and synergizes with all of the\n   Cleric's offensive spell repertoire.\n*******************************************************************************\n
