28	shelp_mind_bolt	-1	mind bolt	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Mind Bolt\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 40\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Mind Bolt\n   Wear-Off: !MindBolt!\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 12\nDescription:\n   Mind Bolt is an offensive spell that inflicts psychic damage on an enemy target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
29	shelp_pain	-1	pain	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Pain\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 25\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: psychic pain\n   Wear-Off: !Pain!\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 28\nDescription:\n   Pain floods the target's nervous system with psychic agony, bypassing\n   physical defenses entirely. Deals mental elemental damage (4d(level/4\n   + 3)) with NO_REFLECT and NO_ABSORB flags, meaning the damage cannot\n   be reflected by barrier spells or absorbed by magical protections.\n   A reliable mid-level offensive spell that provides consistent damage\n   output regardless of the target's physical armor or absorption\n   abilities.\n*******************************************************************************\n
31	shelp_shockshield	-1	shockshield	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Shockshield\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 400\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: None\nAcquisition:\n   - Sorcerer: level 55\n   - Wizard: level 55\nDescription:\n   Shockshield surrounds the caster in a crackling electric field. It is a\n   balanced shield that provides moderate absorption while also dealing\n   reactive air-element damage to attackers.\n\n   Shield properties:\n     - Type: SHOCK_SHIELD (cannot stack with other non-coexisting shields)\n     - Reactive Damage: 25% of incoming damage dealt back as air damage\n     - Absorption: 25% + (pseudo_level / 9)% of incoming damage absorbed\n     - Hit Points: 7,000 + (pseudo_level * 20) -- shield breaks when depleted\n     - Duration: pseudo_level / 7 rounds (halved on login)\n\n   The reactive air damage bypasses cloak reflection and absorption effects.\n   Only one non-coexisting shield may be active at a time.\n*******************************************************************************\n
32	shelp_veterans_cadence	-1	veteran's cadence	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Veteran's Cadence\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: Your campaign cadence breaks.\nAcquisition:\n   - Crusader: level 10\nDescription:\n   Veteran's Cadence is a Crusader passive combat rhythm technique. Through\n   extensive campaign experience, the Crusader has internalized an optimal\n   attack rhythm that sustains high offensive output over long engagements.\n   Each successful attack in the cadence builds momentum, slightly improving\n   the speed and power of subsequent attacks.\n\n   The cadence is a flowing pattern of attacks — not a fixed sequence, but\n   an adaptive rhythm that the Crusader maintains instinctively. It improves\n   attack speed and serves as the foundation for the Crusader's combo system.\n   Maintaining the cadence through a long fight gives Crusaders a significant\n   endurance advantage over opponents whose combat intensity fades over time.\n   The cadence breaks if the Crusader is stunned or forced to halt their\n   attack rhythm.\n*******************************************************************************\n
33	shelp_fire_blast	-1	fire blast	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Fire Blast\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 80\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Fire Blast\n   Wear-Off: !Fire Blast!\nAcquisition:\n   - Sorcerer: level 34\n   - Necromancer: level 55\nDescription:\n   Fire Blast is an offensive spell that inflicts fire damage on an enemy target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
34	shelp_soul_thief	-1	soul thief	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Soul Thief\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 900\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !SOUL THIEF!\nAcquisition:\n   - Necromancer: level 67\n   - Egomancer: level 67\nDescription:\n   Soul Thief Steals a portion of the target's soul power, weakening them and empowering the caster.\n*******************************************************************************\n
35	shelp_flare	-1	flare	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Flare\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 18\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: flare\n   Wear-Off: Your vision returns.\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 20\nDescription:\n   Flare is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
36	shelp_weaken	-1	weaken	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Weaken\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 20\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: spell\n   Wear-Off: You feel stronger.\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 20\nDescription:\n   Weaken is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
37	shelp_dispel_object	-1	dispel object	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Dispel Object\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 15\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Dispel Object!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 60\n   - Cleric: level 70\n   - Psionicist: level 80\nDescription:\n   Dispel Object strips magical flags and all applied enchantments from a\n   carried item. The spell targets an item in the caster's inventory (or\n   passed via object targeting).\n\n   Flags removed by Dispel Object:\n     ITEM_EVIL      -- "X looks less evil."\n     ITEM_NODROP    -- Silently removed (item becomes droppable again).\n     ITEM_INVIS     -- "X fades back into view."\n     ITEM_MAGIC     -- "X looks less magical."\n     ITEM_BLESS     -- "X looks less Holy."\n     ITEM_NOREMOVE  -- Silently removed (item becomes removable again).\n\n   In addition to removing flags, ALL applied enchantments (first_apply /\n   last_apply linked list) are wiped from the item. This is permanent and\n   irreversible -- enchantments removed by Dispel Object cannot be\n   re-applied without re-enchanting the item from scratch.\n\n   Note: Because dispel object removes the apply list, it interacts with the\n   enchant command: an item that has been dispelled can be re-enchanted\n   normally, since the enchant system checks for existing enchantments before\n   allowing a new enchantment to be applied.\n\n   Primary use cases:\n     - Removing a curse (ITEM_NODROP) from an item without using Remove Curse.\n     - Stripping an invisible or evil-flagged item of its flags.\n     - Clearing an item's enchantments before re-enchanting with new stats.\n*******************************************************************************\n
38	shelp_dispel_evil	-1	dispel evil	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Dispel Evil\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 15\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Dispel Object!\nAcquisition:\n   - Not learnable by player classes.\nDescription:\n   Dispel Evil Channels holy power to damage evil entities and purge unholy influence.\n*******************************************************************************\n
39	shelp_hunt	-1	hunt	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Hunt\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_RESTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Hunt!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cipher: level 70\nDescription:\n   Hunt improves tracking, letting you follow trails across rooms and through doors more reliably.\n*******************************************************************************\n
40	shelp_stun	-1	stun	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Stun\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: None\nAcquisition:\n   - Not learnable by player classes.\nDescription:\n   Stun slams your current target and leaves them stunned for several rounds, interrupting their actions.\n*******************************************************************************\n
41	shelp_verdict	-1	verdict	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Verdict\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: verdict\n   Wear-Off: !Verdict!\nAcquisition:\n   - Sentinel: level 20\nDescription:\n   Verdict is the Sentinel's signature judgment strike. After observing and\n   analyzing a target through the Pale Ledger's framework, the Sentinel\n   delivers a decisive blow that represents the culmination of their\n   assessment. Verdict deals enhanced damage based on how thoroughly the\n   Sentinel has studied the target — if Read Opponent is active, the blow\n   is significantly more powerful.\n\n   Delivering a Verdict is a formal act in the Sentinel doctrine: it\n   closes the observational cycle and resets the Sentinel's assessment of\n   the opponent. The damage scales with combat intelligence gathered, making\n   it most devastating against targets who have been extensively analyzed.\n   The Sentinel should use Verdict as a finisher after setting up with\n   Read Opponent and other debuffing techniques.\n*******************************************************************************\n
42	shelp_magical_supremacy	-1	magical supremacy	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Magical Supremacy\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 12\n Wait Beats: 18\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: You no longer have magical supremacy.\nAcquisition:\n   - Egomancer: level 13\n   - Wizard: level 42\nDescription:\n   Magical Supremacy is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
43	shelp_living_bridge	-1	living bridge	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: living bridge\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n    HP Cost: 60\n Wait Beats: 18\n  Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: \nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 90\nDescription:\n   Creates a portal of living vines.\n*******************************************************************************\n
44	shelp_weapon_mastery	-1	weapon mastery	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Weapon Mastery\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage:\n   Wear-Off: Your weapon mastery fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Warden: level 5\nDescription:\n   Weapon Mastery is an innate passive ability granted to Wardens that\n   represents their exceptional proficiency with all weapon types. Applies\n   a permanent hit roll bonus (Warden level/8 + 2) and damage roll bonus\n   (Warden level/12 + 1) at all times. Cannot be trained; it improves\n   automatically as the Warden gains levels. This foundational skill\n   underpins the Warden's superior melee offense compared to other classes.\n*******************************************************************************\n
45	shelp_cancelhotreboot	-1	cancelhotreboot cancel hotreboot	*******************************************************************************\nCommand: CANCELHOTREBOOT\n   Syntax: cancelhotreboot\n   Access: Immortal (L_GOD)\n\nDescription:\n   Cancels a pending automated hotreboot that was triggered by the deployment\n   system (via the hotreboot trigger file). If a 60-second or 30-second warning\n   has already been broadcast to players, this command stops the countdown and\n   notifies all players that the reboot has been cancelled.\n\n   This command has no effect if no automated hotreboot is currently in\n   progress.\n\n   Note: This does not cancel a hotreboot initiated manually with the\n   HOTREBOOT command.\n*******************************************************************************\n
46	shelp_nerve_fire	-1	nerve fire	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Nerve Fire\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 50\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: nerve fire\n   Wear-Off: !Nerve Fire!\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 60\nDescription:\n   Nerve Fire is an area-of-effect psionic attack that simultaneously damages\n   all enemies in the caster's room. It represents the Psionicist reaching\n   out with concentrated mental force and igniting nerve pathways in every\n   hostile creature nearby.\n\n   Damage and targeting:\n     - Deals mental-element damage to every NPC in the room (if cast by a\n       player) or every player in the room (if cast by an NPC).\n     - Damage formula: level + dice(5, 20).\n     - Damage type: ELEMENT_MENTAL | NO_REFLECT | NO_ABSORB.\n       The NO_REFLECT and NO_ABSORB flags mean the damage bypasses magical\n       reflection shields and absorption cloaks entirely.\n     - Targets only enemies in the caster's room -- grouped or neutral\n       characters are not affected.\n\n   Area-wide warning:\n     - Characters in the same AREA but NOT in the caster's room receive a\n       subtle message: "You notice a slight burning feeling in your body."\n       This provides no mechanical effect; it is a warning/flavor notification.\n\n   When cast via an object (staff or scroll):\n     - The triggering object glows: "X glows with the power of Nerve Fire!"\n\n   Tactical notes:\n     The long wait time (24 beats) and high mana cost make Nerve Fire\n     expensive to spam, but its room-wide reach makes it uniquely powerful\n     when surrounded by multiple enemies. The NO_ABSORB flag makes it\n     effective against targets with cloak:absorption or similar defenses.\n*******************************************************************************\n
47	shelp_riposte	-1	riposte	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Riposte\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 80\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Riposte\n   Wear-Off: You are no longer in a position to riposte!\nAcquisition:\n   - Swordsman: level 30\nDescription:\n   Riposte is a prepared finisher stance that waits for an incoming skill attack, then interrupts and reflects damage back to the attacker.\n*******************************************************************************\n
