62	shelp_blindness	-1	blindness	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Blindness\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 5\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: You can see again.\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 16\nDescription:\n   Blindness is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
63	shelp_ventriloquate	-1	ventriloquate	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Ventriloquate\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 5\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Ventriloquate!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 3\nDescription:\n   Ventriloquate Projects your voice to a different source/location to misdirect other players.\n*******************************************************************************\n
64	shelp_leg_sweep	-1	leg sweep	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Leg Sweep\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 1\n Wait Beats: 18\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: leg sweep\n   Wear-Off: !Leg Sweep!\nAcquisition:\n   - Pugilist: level 18\nDescription:\n   Leg Sweep knocks the opponent off their feet with a low sweeping kick.\n   Deals damage (2d(level/4 + 1)) and applies an armor class debuff\n   (level/4) to the prone victim. The stumble also costs the target their\n   next action via WAIT_STATE. This short stagger window lets the Pugilist\n   land additional strikes before the opponent recovers. Effective crowd\n   control for buying time in extended fights.\n*******************************************************************************\n
65	shelp_summon_nightmare	-1	summon nightmare	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Summon Nightmare\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 1200\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: None\nAcquisition:\n   - Not learnable by player classes.\nDescription:\n   Summon Nightmare Summons a charmed nightmare mount/ally from infernal forces to aid in combat and mobility temporarily.\n*******************************************************************************\n
66	shelp_wraith_touch	-1	wraith touch	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Wraith Touch\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 120\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Wraith Touch\n   Wear-Off: !Wraith Touch!\nAcquisition:\n   - Necromancer: level 46\nDescription:\n   Wraith Touch is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
67	shelp_elemental_ward	-1	elemental ward	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Elemental Ward\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 50\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage:\n   Wear-Off: !Elemental Ward!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 55\nDescription:\n   Elemental Ward surrounds the Magi with defensive arcane energies that\n   resist elemental forces. Applies a saving throw bonus against spells\n   (-level/3) for a duration of level/5 hours. Cannot be stacked with\n   itself. The ward intercepts fire, ice, lightning, and other elemental\n   damage types before they reach the caster. A high-level defensive\n   cornerstone for Magi expecting heavy magical assault.\n*******************************************************************************\n
68	shelp_peek	-1	peek	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Peek\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Peek!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cipher: level 20\nDescription:\n   Peek is a tactical skill focused on stealth, positioning, or information advantage.\n*******************************************************************************\n
69	shelp_poison_quinine	-1	poison:quinine	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Poison:quinine\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 80\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Poison Quinine\n   Wear-Off: @@N$n feels much better!\nAcquisition:\n   - Warlock: level 21\n   - Assassin: level 56\nDescription:\n   Poison:quinine is a combat skill that attacks an enemy and deals poison-type physical or energy damage.\n*******************************************************************************\n
70	shelp_cistern_discipline	-1	cistern discipline	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Cistern Discipline\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: Your cistern discipline fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Pugilist: level 5\n   - Sentinel: level 5\nDescription:\n   Cistern Discipline is a foundational conditioning practice shared by\n   Pugilists and Sentinels. The warrior trains their body to absorb more\n   punishment by hardening their constitution through focused physical\n   conditioning regimens. While this discipline is active, the character\n   gains increased hit point regeneration and improved stamina.\n\n   The technique takes its name from the ancient training wells where fighters\n   would practice endurance by treading water for hours. Modern practitioners\n   use equivalent sustained physical drills to achieve the same metabolic\n   conditioning. The effect improves survivability in extended fights by\n   ensuring the warrior recovers between engagements.\n*******************************************************************************\n
71	shelp_pale_imprint	-1	pale imprint	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Pale Imprint\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 12\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: The Pale Ledger's imprint fades from your awareness.\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 10\nDescription:\n   Pale Imprint is a Psionicist utility spell that creates a persistent\n   mental snapshot of the current area's layout and inhabitants. By\n   impressing the surroundings onto a psionic "ledger" in their mind, the\n   Psionicist gains a detailed awareness of the room's magical properties\n   and hidden features.\n\n   The Pale Imprint allows the Psionicist to detect hidden objects and\n   doors more easily, notice subtle magical disturbances, and maintain\n   a mental map of nearby terrain. The imprint fades over time as new\n   information overwrites it. In practice, it is used by Psionicists who\n   need to navigate unfamiliar or trapped environments with greater safety\n   than their unaided senses would provide.\n*******************************************************************************\n
72	shelp_seal_room	-1	seal room	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Seal Room\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 75\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: The Energy web around this room fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 50\n   - Psionicist: level 50\n   - Magi: level 70\nDescription:\n   Seal Room Seals the room with warding magic to block movement and certain entry or exit effects.\n*******************************************************************************\n
73	shelp_climb	-1	climb	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Climb\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Climb!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cipher: level 25\nDescription:\n   Climb allows movement through exits marked as climb-only when you are not flying.\n*******************************************************************************\n
74	shelp_detect_evil	-1	detect evil	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Detect Evil\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 5\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: The red in your vision disappears.\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 8\n   - Magi: level 12\nDescription:\n   Detect Evil is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
75	shelp_pummel	-1	pummel	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Pummel\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 80\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Pummel\n   Wear-Off: !!Pummel!!\nAcquisition:\n   - Pugilist: level 66\nDescription:\n   Pummel is a basic chi-fighter attack that deals physical damage while building chi for stronger follow-up techniques.\n*******************************************************************************\n
76	shelp_infuse	-1	infuse	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Infuse\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_OBJ_INV\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 1000\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Infuse Soul!\nAcquisition:\n   - Necromancer: level 71\n   - Egomancer: level 71\nDescription:\n   Infuse Infuses a target with magical power to strengthen selected attributes or spell interactions.\n*******************************************************************************\n
77	shelp_read_opponent	-1	read opponent	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Read Opponent\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 8\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: You lose your read on your opponent.\nAcquisition:\n   - Sentinel: level 10\nDescription:\n   Read Opponent is one of the Sentinel's foundational analytical techniques.\n   The Sentinel studies their target's fighting style, identifying patterns,\n   tendencies, and weaknesses over the course of a few exchanges. Once a\n   read is established, the Sentinel gains improved accuracy and damage\n   against that specific opponent.\n\n   The benefit accumulates as long as the Sentinel maintains engagement with\n   the read target. The information gathered — stance preferences, telegraphed\n   attacks, habitual defenses — remains valid until the target significantly\n   changes their approach or the Sentinel disengages. Read Opponent is the\n   cornerstone of the Sentinel's adaptive combat philosophy: every fight\n   begins with observation and ends with exploitation of identified patterns.\n*******************************************************************************\n
78	shelp_beacon	-1	beacon	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Beacon\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 25\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Beacon!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 70\n   - Psionicist: level 70\nDescription:\n   Beacon Creates a magical beacon that can be used as a travel anchor or reference point for movement spells.\n*******************************************************************************\n
79	shelp_cognitive_flush	-1	cognitive flush	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Cognitive Flush\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_NOTSELF\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 15\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Cognitive Flush!\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 50\nDescription:\n   Cognitive Flush is an advanced Psionicist offensive ability that strips\n   magical buffs from a target by overwhelming their mental defenses with a\n   broad-spectrum psionic disruption. The Psionicist broadcasts a diffuse\n   wave of mental static that interferes with the cognitive processes\n   maintaining the target's magical protections, causing them to unravel.\n\n   Cognitive Flush functions similarly to a Dispel Magic, but is focused\n   specifically on a single opponent (not the room) and is delivered through\n   psionic means. The flush is particularly effective against psychic and\n   mental buffs, as these share the cognitive substrate the Psionicist\n   is disrupting. It is a targeted depuff tool that Psionicists use to\n   strip protected opponents before launching their main assault.\n*******************************************************************************\n
80	shelp_soul_net	-1	soul net	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Soul Net\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 350\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: @@NThe @@dSoul Net@@N dissipates.\nAcquisition:\n   - Necromancer: level 58\n   - Egomancer: level 58\nDescription:\n   Soul Net Ensnare souls in the area, hindering death/escape interactions and empowering soul-based magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
81	shelp_vigilance	-1	vigilance	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Vigilance\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Vigilance!\nAcquisition:\n   None (available to all — LEVELS_INIT)\nDescription:\n   Vigilance is an innate passive alertness shared by all characters at\n   some base level. For the Sentinel class, it is a core competency that\n   exceeds that of ordinary combatants, granting improved passive awareness\n   in all situations. Characters with Vigilance have a reduced chance of\n   being surprised, improved detection of hidden enemies, and a better\n   chance of acting first when combat initiates unexpectedly.\n\n   For Sentinels, Vigilance is a constant state of operational readiness\n   that reflects their role as witnesses and enforcers. They are never\n   caught fully off-guard, always maintaining situational awareness even\n   while resting. The passive benefit improves base detection, hit, and\n   initiative stats at all times.\n*******************************************************************************\n
82	shelp_field_patch	-1	field patch	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Field Patch\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage:\n   Wear-Off: !Field Patch!\nAcquisition:\n   - Warden: level 30\nDescription:\n   Field Patch applies basic battlefield medicine to restore hit points to\n   the Warden or a nearby ally. Cannot be used while in combat. Heals for\n   3d(Warden level) + 10 hit points. Defaults to self if no target is\n   specified; otherwise the target must be in the same room. Has a long\n   cooldown of 60 beats between uses. Provides the Warden with meaningful\n   self-sustain during or between encounters.\n   Syntax: field patch [target]\n*******************************************************************************\n
83	shelp_aurabolt	-1	aurabolt	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Aurabolt\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 80\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Aurabolt\n   Wear-Off: !!Aurabolt!!\nAcquisition:\n   - Monk: level 34\n   - Brawler: level 41\nDescription:\n   Aurabolt is a combo skill that deals direct damage to an enemy target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
84	shelp_ironpine_vigor	-1	ironpine vigor	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: ironpine vigor\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n    HP Cost: 20\n Wait Beats: 24\n  Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: \nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 36\nDescription:\n   Increases target max HP by 10%.\n*******************************************************************************\n
85	shelp_poison_arsenic	-1	poison:arsenic	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Poison:arsenic\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 80\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Poison Arsenic\n   Wear-Off: @@N$nFeels much better!\nAcquisition:\n   - Warlock: level 28\n   - Assassin: level 66\nDescription:\n   Poison:arsenic is a combat skill that attacks an enemy and deals poison-type physical or energy damage.\n*******************************************************************************\n
86	shelp_hex_ward	-1	hex ward	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Hex Ward\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: The hex ward eroding your defenses fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Nightblade: level 10\nDescription:\n   Hex Ward weaves shadow-compact entropy around the target, gradually\n   eroding their defenses by worsening their AC for several rounds. This\n   represents the Nightblade's "ward dissolution" doctrine -- applying hex\n   effects that "progressively degrade spiritual protective wards before\n   physical contact."\n\n   Costs: Movement (via subtract_energy_cost)\n   Cooldown: 20 rounds\n   Duration: 3 + (Nightblade level / 5) rounds\n   AC penalty to victim: +(Nightblade level * 4 + Warlock level * 2)\n\n   Distinct from Dispel Magic (instant all-or-nothing buff removal). Hex\n   Ward is gradual degradation that synergizes with the Nightblade's\n   sustained-pressure doctrine, softening targets for precision strikes.\n*******************************************************************************\n
87	shelp_summon	-1	summon	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Summon\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 50\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Summon!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 35\nDescription:\n   Summon Pulls a distant player or creature to the caster's room if summon rules and protections allow it.\n*******************************************************************************\n
88	shelp_condense_soul	-1	condense soul	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Condense Soul\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_OBJ_INV\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 800\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Soul Potion!\nAcquisition:\n   - Necromancer: level 78\n   - Egomancer: level 78\nDescription:\n   Condense Soul Condenses spiritual energy into a usable form for advanced soul magic rituals.\n*******************************************************************************\n
89	shelp_equip_fist	-1	equip fist	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Equip Fist\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Equip Fist!\nAcquisition:\n   - Monk: level 1\n   - Brawler: level 1\nDescription:\n   Equip Fist allows you to equip fist-type weapons.\n*******************************************************************************\n
90	shelp_hypnosis	-1	hypnosis	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Hypnosis\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 30\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Hypnosis!\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 14\nDescription:\n   Hypnosis is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
91	shelp_shadowshield	-1	shadowshield	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Shadowshield\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 400\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: @@NThe @@rshield@@N shatters!!\nAcquisition:\n   - Not learnable by player classes.\nDescription:\n   Shadowshield is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
92	shelp_compact_amplification	-1	compact amplification	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Compact Amplification\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Compact Amplification!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 20\nDescription:\n   Compact Amplification is a passive arcane refinement technique unique to\n   the Magi. Through intensive study of magical compression, the Magi learns\n   to compact more raw power into each spell without increasing its mana cost.\n   The technique involves folding magical resonance back into the casting\n   matrix, amplifying the output of every spell cast.\n\n   This passive skill increases the potency of the Magi's spells, effectively\n   raising their magical supremacy when this technique is mastered. It stacks\n   with other magical enhancement abilities. The Magi becomes capable of\n   achieving spell outputs that exceed what their raw mana pool would normally\n   allow, making each point of mana invested more efficient.\n*******************************************************************************\n
93	shelp_flurry	-1	flurry	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Flurry\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 80\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Flurry\n   Wear-Off: None\nAcquisition:\n   - Pugilist: level 45\nDescription:\n   Flurry converts stored chi into a rapid sequence of extra basic strikes, dumping your remaining chi into immediate melee pressure.\n*******************************************************************************\n
94	shelp_psychic_crush	-1	psychic crush	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Psychic Crush\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 33\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: psychic crush\n   Wear-Off: !Psychic Crush!\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 19\nDescription:\n   Psychic Crush is an offensive spell that inflicts psychic damage on an enemy target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
95	shelp_stalker	-1	stalker	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Stalker\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 100\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Stalker!\nAcquisition:\n   - Not learnable by player classes.\nDescription:\n   Stalker Summons a stealth-focused stalker ally to hunt and pressure enemies.\n*******************************************************************************\n
96	shelp_chakra	-1	chakra	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Chakra\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 80\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Chakra\n   Wear-Off: None\nAcquisition:\n   - Monk: level 55\nDescription:\n   Chakra spends chi to steady body and spirit, immediately restoring health and granting a short damroll boost for stronger follow-up attacks.\n*******************************************************************************\n
97	shelp_charter_challenge	-1	charter challenge	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Charter Challenge\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 18\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: charter challenge\n   Wear-Off: !Charter Challenge!\nAcquisition:\n   - Warden: level 12\nDescription:\n   Charter Challenge is the Warden's battlefield provocation technique. The\n   warrior issues a formal combat declaration that compels nearby enemies to\n   redirect their attention toward them. Targeted opponents are taunted into\n   focusing their attacks on the Warden rather than allies.\n\n   In addition to redirecting aggression, Charter Challenge temporarily lowers\n   the target's morale and combat efficiency, as the challenge undermines their\n   confidence and forces them into a reactive stance. It is an essential tool\n   for Wardens filling a protective role in group combat, enabling them to\n   shield weaker party members by drawing enemy focus.\n*******************************************************************************\n
98	shelp_roll_with_blow	-1	roll with blow	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Roll With Blow\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage:\n   Wear-Off: Your fluid stance fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Pugilist: level 12\nDescription:\n   Roll With Blow is an innate passive stance that reflects the Pugilist's\n   trained ability to absorb and redirect incoming strikes. Permanently\n   applies a dodge bonus (Pugilist level/4) and an armor class improvement\n   (-Pugilist level/6). Cannot be trained; improves automatically with\n   Pugilist level. Combined with Conditioning and natural unarmed defenses,\n   this makes the Pugilist surprisingly durable despite wearing lighter\n   protection than warrior classes.\n*******************************************************************************\n
99	shelp_two_handed	-1	two handed	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Two Handed\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Two Handed!\nAcquisition:\n   - Knight: level 6\n   - Swordsman: level 6\n   - Paladin: level 8\nDescription:\n   Two Handed allows you to equip and use two-handed weapons.\n*******************************************************************************\n
100	shelp_bare_hand	-1	bare hand	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Bare Hand\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Enhanced Sword!\nAcquisition:\n   - Monk: level 6\n   - Brawler: level 6\nDescription:\n   Bare Hand passively increases unarmed attack damage (normal hits, martial hits, and counters).\n*******************************************************************************\n
