104	shelp_visit	-1	visit	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Visit\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 50\n Wait Beats: 48\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !visit!\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 32\nDescription:\n   Visit Projects the caster's presence to another player/location to communicate or scout without full travel.\n*******************************************************************************\n
105	shelp_phase	-1	phase	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Phase\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 20\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: You feel solid again.\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 45\nDescription:\n   Phase is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
106	shelp_substrate_piercing	-1	substrate piercing	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Substrate Piercing\n       Kind: Skill (Passive)\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n    HP Cost: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n  Can Learn: FALSE\nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 20 (requires reincarnation)\nDescription:\n   A passive skill that allows your earth and poison spells to\n   bypass elemental resistance. Unlocked through reincarnation\n   as a Druid.\n*******************************************************************************\n
107	shelp_dispel_magic	-1	dispel magic	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Dispel Magic\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 15\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Dispel Magic!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 68\n   - Cleric: level 89\nDescription:\n   Dispel Magic Attempts to strip magical effects from a target, removing beneficial buffs or harmful debuffs based on dispel strength.\n*******************************************************************************\n
108	shelp_detect_invis	-1	detect invis	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Detect Invis\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 5\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: You no longer see invisible objects.\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 19\nDescription:\n   Detect Invis is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
109	shelp_reflex_disruption	-1	reflex disruption	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Reflex Disruption\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: Your reflexes return to normal.\nAcquisition:\n   - Nightblade: level 15\nDescription:\n   Reflex Disruption applies targeted hex interference to the victim's\n   combat reflexes, reducing their hitroll for several rounds. The target\n   remains functionally aware but cannot generate the specific defensive\n   responses needed to counter incoming attacks effectively.\n\n   Costs: Movement (via subtract_energy_cost)\n   Cooldown: 20 rounds\n   Duration: 2 + (Nightblade level / 5) rounds\n   Hitroll penalty to victim: -(Nightblade level * 3 + Assassin level * 2)\n\n   Named explicitly in the Nightblade lore: "targeted disruption of\n   specific reflex chains that the Assassin's chosen attack vector would\n   need to overcome. The target remains functionally aware; they simply\n   cannot generate the specific defensive response."\n*******************************************************************************\n
110	shelp_know_alignment	-1	know alignment	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Know Alignment\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 9\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Know Alignment!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 13\n   - Cleric: level 22\nDescription:\n   Know Alignment is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
111	shelp_berserk	-1	berserk	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Berserk\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: berserk\n   Wear-Off: You calm down!\nAcquisition:\n   - Warden: level 34\nDescription:\n   Berserk is a self-buff that calls on dark power for stronger offense and defenses in a fight, boosting hitroll, damroll, armor, and spell saves once it lands.\n*******************************************************************************\n
112	shelp_arcane_lock	-1	arcane lock	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Arcane Lock\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 15\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage:\n   Wear-Off: !Arcane Lock!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 18\nDescription:\n   Arcane Lock weaves magical wards across all exits in the current room,\n   preventing passage through those doors without dispelling the lock.\n   Cannot be cast if already active in the room. Duration: 6 hours. The\n   lock affects all exits simultaneously. Useful for securing a room\n   against intruders, blocking retreat routes, or containing enemies.\n   This is a passive room-effect spell that does not require combat.\n*******************************************************************************\n
113	shelp_arcaneshield	-1	arcaneshield	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Arcaneshield\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 350\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: None\nAcquisition:\n   - Brawler: level 48\nDescription:\n   Arcaneshield is the Brawler's signature remort shield. It encases the\n   caster in a shimmering arcane barrier that absorbs magical damage. Similar\n   in structure to iceshield, it is a purely defensive shield with no reactive\n   damage, but provides very high absorption and durability.\n\n   The key difference from iceshield is that arcaneshield ONLY absorbs\n   non-physical (magical) damage. Physical attacks pass through the barrier\n   entirely unaffected.\n\n   Shield properties:\n     - Type: ARCANE_SHIELD (can coexist with other shields)\n     - Reactive Damage: None (purely absorptive)\n     - Absorption: 50% + (pseudo_level / 6)% of magical damage absorbed\n     - Hit Points: 15,000 + (pseudo_level * 50) -- shield breaks when depleted\n     - Duration: pseudo_level / 15 rounds (halved on login)\n     - Physical Bypass: Physical damage is NOT absorbed\n\n   Arcaneshield can coexist with other shield effects.\n*******************************************************************************\n
114	shelp_rictus_curse	-1	rictus curse	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Rictus Curse\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 120\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Rictus Curse\n   Wear-Off: !Rictus Curse!\nAcquisition:\n   - Necromancer: level 100\n   - Egomancer: level 100\nDescription:\n   Rictus Curse is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
115	shelp_parry	-1	parry	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Parry\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Parry!\nAcquisition:\n   - Warden: level 10\n   - Cipher: level 52\nDescription:\n   Parry gives you a chance to deflect melee attacks when wielding a weapon.\n*******************************************************************************\n
116	shelp_enhanced_heal	-1	enhanced heal	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Enhanced Heal\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Enhanced Heal!\nAcquisition:\n   - Templar: level 1\nDescription:\n   Enhanced Heal is a passive healing mastery skill intended to improve restorative magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
117	shelp_thought_devourer	-1	thought devourer	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Thought Devourer\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 1200\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: None\nAcquisition:\n   - Egomancer: level 65\nDescription:\n   Thought Devourer Summons a thought devourer pet that attacks enemies and pressures their mental defenses.\n*******************************************************************************\n
118	shelp_mirror_image	-1	mirror image	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Mirror Image\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 25\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage:\n   Wear-Off: !Mirror Image!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 38\nDescription:\n   Mirror Image conjures flickering illusory duplicates of the caster that\n   confuse attackers and cause strikes to miss the real Magi. Applies a\n   dodge bonus (level/5) and an armor class improvement (-level/5) for\n   level/6 rounds. Cannot be stacked with itself. The images shift and\n   move with the caster, forcing enemies to guess which target is real.\n   Effective for surviving burst damage windows while higher-priority\n   defenses are refreshed.\n*******************************************************************************\n
119	shelp_sense_life	-1	sense life	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: sense life\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n    HP Cost: 5\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: \nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 11\nDescription:\n   Grants detect invisible.\n*******************************************************************************\n
120	shelp_pass_door	-1	pass door	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Pass Door\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 20\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: You feel solid again.\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 46\nDescription:\n   Pass Door is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
121	shelp_disks_word	-1	disk's word	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Disk's Word\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 50\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: disk's word\n   Wear-Off: !Disk's Word!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 60\nDescription:\n   Disk's Word is a high-level Cleric offensive ability invoking the divine\n   authority of Disk, the god of balance and judgment. The Cleric channels\n   the full weight of Disk's judgment as a spoken divine decree, calling\n   down retribution upon all enemies in the area. The spell deals massive\n   holy damage to every enemy in the room.\n\n   Disk's Word is the Cleric equivalent of a holy word — an area-effect\n   divine blast that demonstrates the Cleric's role as a conduit for divine\n   will rather than a mere healer. The spell does not discriminate between\n   enemies; all hostile entities in the presence of the Cleric when the Word\n   is spoken are struck. It represents the ultimate expression of Disk's\n   impartial, all-encompassing judgment delivered through their faithful servant.\n*******************************************************************************\n
122	shelp_cognitive_pressure	-1	cognitive pressure	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Cognitive Pressure\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 8\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: cognitive pressure\n   Wear-Off: !Cognitive Pressure!\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 1\nDescription:\n   Cognitive Pressure is the first technique in Psionicist training: focused\n   will directed at a surface cognitive pattern, pressing against it until\n   the subject flinches. In the tradition's mainstream doctrine this is\n   explicitly defensive in origin — taught as a way to interrupt a threat,\n   not pursue one. The technique matters more than the force it delivers.\n\n   Damage: 2d4 + level/4, mental elemental. A successful save halves damage.\n   Has no effect on mindless targets (ACT_NOMIND). Cannot be used on self.\n   Mana cost: 8. Available automatically at level 1.\n\n   Psionicists who need heavier mental offense should advance to Mind Flail\n   (level 4), which does not scale with level but applies tiered damage at\n   level thresholds.\n*******************************************************************************\n
123	shelp_fire_breath	-1	fire breath	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Fire Breath\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 4\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: blast of flame\n   Wear-Off: !Fire Breath!\nAcquisition:\n   - Not learnable by player classes.\nDescription:\n   Fire Breath is an offensive spell that inflicts fire damage on an enemy target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
124	shelp_mana_drain	-1	mana drain	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Mana Drain\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 150\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: @@NThe @@dMana Drain@@N dissipates.\nAcquisition:\n   - Sorcerer: level 11\n   - Wizard: level 11\n   - Necromancer: level 15\n   - Egomancer: level 15\nDescription:\n   Mana Drain Creates a room effect that drains mana over time from those within it.\n*******************************************************************************\n
125	shelp_shard_ward	-1	shard ward	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Shard Ward\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 15\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: shard ward\n   Wear-Off: !Shard Ward!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 36\nDescription:\n   Shard Ward is a Cleric mid-level offensive area spell. The Cleric calls\n   down a barrage of razor-edged divine shards onto all enemies in the room.\n   The shards are manifestations of divine judgment rendered as cutting force,\n   dealing holy-physical damage to every hostile target present.\n\n   Shard Ward is one of the Cleric's primary area-effect damage spells before\n   they reach the level required for Disk's Word and Jackal's Verdict. It\n   provides reliable multi-target damage in group encounters where the Cleric\n   needs to contribute offensively while maintaining their support role.\n   The shards have a secondary chance to reduce the target's armor class\n   as they embed themselves and restrict movement.\n*******************************************************************************\n
126	shelp_group_heal	-1	group heal	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Group Heal\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 50\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Group Heal!\nAcquisition:\n   - Paladin: level 5\n   - Priest: level 25\nDescription:\n   Group Heal is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
127	shelp_solar_brand	-1	solar brand	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Solar Brand\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 8\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: solar brand\n   Wear-Off: !Solar Brand!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 1\nDescription:\n   Solar Brand is the Dawn Liturgy's ritual opener: a mark of the Black Sun\n   Shard's authority pressed briefly into a target. In the Solar Court's\n   five-office tradition it is taught to all candidates as the first act of\n   channeled authority — not a prayer for aid but a direct expression of\n   cosmological function.\n\n   Damage: 2d4 + level/4, holy elemental. Against targets of corrupt\n   alignment (< -350), damage is increased by 50%. No save against the\n   damage. Mana cost: 8. Available automatically at level 1.\n\n   Solar Brand does not scale dramatically with level. Clerics who need\n   sustained offensive output should advance to Divine Strike (level 4).\n*******************************************************************************\n
128	shelp_earth_elemental	-1	earth elemental	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Earth Elemental\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 500\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !EARTH ELEMENTAL!\nAcquisition:\n   - Sorcerer: level 52\n   - Wizard: level 52\nDescription:\n   Earth Elemental Summons an earth elemental ally with high toughness and control presence.\n*******************************************************************************\n
129	shelp_sneak	-1	sneak	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Sneak\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: None\nAcquisition:\n   - Cipher: level 5\nDescription:\n   Sneak is a tactical skill focused on stealth, positioning, or information advantage.\n*******************************************************************************\n
130	shelp_sacred_ward	-1	sacred ward	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Sacred Ward\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE (room/group)\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 80\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: The sacred ward's warmth fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Templar: level 5\nDescription:\n   Sacred Ward calls forth holy power to bless the ground, applying a\n   heal-over-time (HOT) effect to all grouped allies in the room. This\n   reflects the Templar's role as a threshold guardian who "consecrates\n   spaces" -- securing and sanctifying contested locations.\n\n   Duration: 6 + (Templar level / 4) rounds\n   HOT modifier: Templar level * 3 + Paladin level + Priest level\n   Mana cost: 80\n\n   Distinct from the Cleric's "consecrate" spell (which grants hitroll/AC\n   to group and damages evil NPCs). Sacred Ward focuses on sustained\n   healing throughput for the group rather than offensive holy damage.\n*******************************************************************************\n
131	shelp_rend	-1	rend	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Rend\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 1\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: rend\n   Wear-Off: !Rend!\nAcquisition:\n   - Warden: level 36\nDescription:\n   Rend tears through the target's armor and defenses with a brutal weapon\n   strike. Deals physical damage (2d(Warden level/4 + 1)) and applies an\n   armor class debuff to the victim for 24 rounds, making them easier to\n   hit. The armor penalty scales with Warden level. Useful for softening\n   up heavily armored opponents before sustained attacks.\n*******************************************************************************\n
132	shelp_window	-1	window	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Window\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 100\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Window!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 70\n   - Psionicist: level 70\nDescription:\n   Window Opens a magical viewing window to observe a distant location.\n*******************************************************************************\n
133	shelp_general_purpose	-1	general purpose	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: General Purpose\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: general purpose ammo\n   Wear-Off: !General Purpose Ammo!\nAcquisition:\n   - Not learnable by player classes.\nDescription:\n   General Purpose is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
134	shelp_tidal_lash	-1	tidal lash	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Tidal Lash\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 120\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: tidal lash\n   Wear-Off: !tidal lash!\nAcquisition:\n   - Wizard: level 50\nDescription:\n   Tidal Lash is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
135	shelp_solar_censure	-1	solar censure	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Solar Censure\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 17\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: solar censure\n   Wear-Off: !Solar Censure!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 40\nDescription:\n   Solar Censure is a mid-level Cleric offensive spell invoking Disk's solar\n   aspect to censure a transgressor. The Cleric formally condemns the target\n   in Disk's name and channels solar divine energy as a focused bolt of\n   radiant judgment. The spell deals significant holy damage and carries\n   the weight of divine disapproval.\n\n   Solar Censure is the Cleric's strongest single-target offensive spell\n   before reaching the tier of Flamestrike and Disk's Word. It is more\n   powerful than Divine Strike and serves as the Cleric's primary offensive\n   tool in the mid-career range. The censure aspect of the spell means it\n   is particularly effective against targets who have committed transgressions\n   that Disk has noted — repeat offenders take increased damage.\n*******************************************************************************\n
136	shelp_bark_skin	-1	bark skin	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Bark Skin\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 20\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: Your skin feels softer.\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 20\nDescription:\n   Bark Skin is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
137	shelp_wall_of_fire	-1	wall of fire	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Wall of Fire\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 30\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: wall of fire\n   Wear-Off: !Wall of Fire!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 32\nDescription:\n   Wall of Fire erupts a curtain of roaring flames throughout the current\n   room, striking all enemies present. Deals fire elemental damage\n   (3d(level/4 + 2)) to each valid target. Saving throws apply for reduced\n   damage. Grouped allies are not harmed. A powerful area-of-effect spell\n   that excels against clustered enemies or when multiple NPCs are engaged\n   simultaneously. Use with caution in mixed-alignment groups.\n*******************************************************************************\n
138	shelp_summon_pegasus	-1	summon pegasus	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Summon Pegasus\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 1200\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: None\nAcquisition:\n   - Not learnable by player classes.\nDescription:\n   Summon Pegasus Summons a charmed pegasus mount/ally from holy light to aid movement and combat for a limited duration.\n*******************************************************************************\n
139	shelp_elemental_attunement	-1	elemental attunement	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Elemental Attunement\n       Kind: Passive Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: None\nAcquisition:\n   - Grand Magi: level 3\nDescription:\n   Elemental Attunement is a passive skill representing the Grand Magi's\n   deep understanding of multi-domain elemental interaction. Having this\n   skill reflects the Confluent Theorists' documentation that "formal proof\n   methodology applied to synthesis research would produce qualitatively\n   different results."\n\n   This passive grants awareness of elemental interactions that enhances\n   the Grand Magi's overall elemental spell effectiveness. The skill is\n   acquired automatically at Grand Magi level 3 and requires no activation.\n*******************************************************************************\n
140	shelp_enhanced_sword_damage	-1	enhanced sword damage	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Enhanced Sword Damage\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Enhanced Sword!\nAcquisition:\n   - Swordsman: level 20\nDescription:\n   Enhanced Sword Damage passively boosts your physical damage when wielding a sword.\n*******************************************************************************\n
141	shelp_flamestrike	-1	flamestrike	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Flamestrike\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 20\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: flamestrike\n   Wear-Off: !Flamestrike!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 54\nDescription:\n   Flamestrike is an offensive spell that inflicts fire damage on an enemy target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
142	shelp_spinfist	-1	spinfist	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Spinfist\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 80\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Spinfist\n   Wear-Off: !!SPINFIST!!\nAcquisition:\n   - Brawler: level 66\nDescription:\n   Spinfist is a chi-consuming spinning attack that attempts to strike multiple nearby enemies, making it a close-range area pressure tool.\n*******************************************************************************\n
