152	shelp_continual_light	-1	continual light	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Continual Light\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 7\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Continual Light!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 11\n   - Cleric: level 27\nDescription:\n   Continual Light Creates a long-lasting magical light source that illuminates rooms or objects.\n*******************************************************************************\n
153	shelp_detect_poison	-1	detect poison	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Detect Poison\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_OBJ_INV\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 5\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Detect Poison!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 10\nDescription:\n   Detect Poison Detects poison on creatures, food, drink, or objects.\n*******************************************************************************\n
154	shelp_momentum_drain	-1	momentum drain	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Momentum Drain\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 100\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: momentum drain\n   Wear-Off: Your momentum returns to normal.\nAcquisition:\n   - Kinetimancer: level 5\nDescription:\n   Momentum Drain redirects the target's combat momentum, applying hitroll\n   and damroll penalties that represent their force being siphoned away.\n   This reflects the Kinetic Formulists' momentum doctrine: "rather than\n   generating force from nothing, the practitioner identifies existing\n   force vectors and redirects them."\n\n   Duration: 3 + (Kinetimancer level / 5) rounds\n   Hitroll penalty: -(Kinetimancer level * 2 + Necromancer level\n                      + Egomancer level)\n   Damroll penalty: same as hitroll\n   Mana cost: 100\n\n   Refocused from mana-drain (which overlaps with existing Mana Drain\n   spell accessible via Necromancer/Egomancer prereqs) to combat-stat\n   drain, which better represents the momentum-redirection lore.\n*******************************************************************************\n
155	shelp_barkskin	-1	barkskin	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: barkskin\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n    HP Cost: 10\n Wait Beats: 24\n  Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: \nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 5\nDescription:\n   AC buff on self. Skin hardens into bark.\n*******************************************************************************\n
177	shelp_briar_volley	-1	briar volley	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: briar volley\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n    HP Cost: 18\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: briar volley\nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 20\nDescription:\n   A volley of thorny briars for earth damage.\n*******************************************************************************\n
157	shelp_shieldblock	-1	shieldblock	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Shieldblock\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 80\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Shieldblock\n   Wear-Off: You are no longer ready to shield block!\nAcquisition:\n   - Knight: level 57\n   - Paladin: level 83\nDescription:\n   Shieldblock is a prepared defensive finisher that improves armor and gives shield users a stronger chance to blunt incoming attacks.\n*******************************************************************************\n
158	shelp_solar_flare	-1	solar flare	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Solar Flare\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 25\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: solar flare\n   Wear-Off: !Solar Flare!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 50\nDescription:\n   Solar Flare unleashes a concentrated burst of holy solar light at a\n   single target. Deals holy elemental damage (4d10 + level/2). On a\n   failed saving throw (50% chance), the target is also blinded: AFF_BLIND\n   is applied for level/6 rounds, accompanied by a significant hit roll\n   penalty (-10 - level/4). The blindness component makes this spell\n   especially powerful when fighting opponents who rely on melee accuracy.\n*******************************************************************************\n
159	shelp_fist_of_the_interior_form	-1	fist of the interior form fist interior	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Fist of the Interior Form\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 80\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Fist of the Interior Form\n   Wear-Off: None\nAcquisition:\n   - Martial Artist: level 15\nDescription:\n   The Fist of the Interior Form is the Martial Artist tradition's ultimate\n   expression -- a single perfect strike that combines Monk internal energy\n   work with Brawler impact methodology at maximum intensity.\n\n   Requires exactly 20 chi to activate (near-full pool). Consumes 20 chi.\n   Deals massive damage with both Physical and Holy elements, representing\n   the chi integration's "mechanism that neither tradition's theoretical\n   framework fully explains."\n\n   Chi cost: 20 (fixed)\n   Cooldown: 30 rounds\n   Damage element: Physical + Holy\n   Damage formula: base pug damage * 20 * (10 + Martial Artist level) / 10\n\n   The high chi requirement forces a deliberate choice each fight: spend chi\n   incrementally on utility (chakra, chiblock, spinfist) or save for this\n   devastating finisher. The two-apprenticeship depth producing something\n   neither tradition could achieve alone.\n*******************************************************************************\n
160	shelp_entropic_shield	-1	entropic shield	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Entropic Shield\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 100\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: Your entropic shield dissipates.\nAcquisition:\n   - Kinetimancer: level 8\nDescription:\n   Entropic Shield manifests an entropy field that degrades incoming\n   attacks, providing an AC bonus that scales with Kinetimancer level\n   and Intelligence.\n\n   Duration: level / 8 hours\n   AC modifier: -(Kinetimancer level * 4 + Intelligence / 3)\n   Mana cost: 100\n\n   The Kinetic Formulists documented that "the equations describing how\n   will-imposition propagates through cognitive architecture were\n   structurally analogous to the equations describing how entropic force\n   propagates through biological systems." This defensive application uses\n   the entropy field to degrade incoming force rather than generate it.\n*******************************************************************************\n
161	shelp_gap_probe	-1	gap probe	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Gap Probe\n       Kind: Skill (active combat)\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 1\n Wait Beats: 18\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: gap probe\n   Wear-Off: !Gap Probe!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cipher: level 1\nDescription:\n   Gap Probe is the first application of Gap Intuition: before a gap in an\n   opponent's defense can be exploited, it must be found. This technique is\n   assessment. The Cipher delivers a testing strike that searches for\n   structural fault — a probe rather than a committed blow. At level 1 the\n   Cipher cannot yet exploit what they find, but the strike itself carries\n   force and begins building their read of the target.\n\n   Damage is calculated from pseudo-level and Strength (same as Warden\n   melee skills). The Cipher's deeper combat skills — backstab, circle,\n   mark target — build on the gap assessment this technique initiates.\n\n   Syntax: gap probe <target>\n   Requires POS_FIGHTING. Can be practiced to improve hit rate.\n*******************************************************************************\n
162	shelp_elemental_inferno	-1	elemental inferno	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Elemental Inferno\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 120\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: elemental inferno\n   Wear-Off: !elemental inferno!\nAcquisition:\n   - Grand Magi: level 1\nDescription:\n   Elemental Inferno is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
163	shelp_counter	-1	counter	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Counter\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: counter\n   Wear-Off: !Counter!\nAcquisition:\n   - Pugilist: level 20\nDescription:\n   Counter is a passive reactive combat skill that grants a chance to automatically strike back when enemies attack you, with stronger returns for high dexterity and speed.\n*******************************************************************************\n
164	shelp_mind_flail	-1	mind flail	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Mind Flail\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 12\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: mind flail\n   Wear-Off: !Mind Flail!\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 4\nDescription:\n   Mind Flail is an offensive spell that inflicts psychic damage on an enemy target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
165	shelp_giant_strength	-1	giant strength	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Giant Strength\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 20\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: You feel weaker.\nAcquisition:\n   - Sorcerer: level 18\n   - Wizard: level 18\nDescription:\n   Giant Strength is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
166	shelp_divine_intervention	-1	divine intervention	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Divine Intervention\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 150\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Intervention!\nAcquisition:\n   - Priest: level 12\n   - Paladin: level 67\nDescription:\n   Divine Intervention is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
167	shelp_ice_bolt	-1	ice bolt	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Ice Bolt\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 20\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Ice Bolt\n   Wear-Off: !Ice Bolt!\nAcquisition:\n   - Sorcerer: level 3\nDescription:\n   Ice Bolt is an offensive spell that inflicts ice damage on an enemy target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
168	shelp_precognition	-1	precognition	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Precognition\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 30\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage:\n   Wear-Off: !Precognition!\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 45\nDescription:\n   Precognition expands the Psionicist's awareness into the immediate\n   future, allowing them to anticipate and sidestep incoming attacks.\n   For level/5 rounds, applies a dodge bonus (level/5) and an armor\n   class improvement (-level/6). Cannot be stacked. The passive foresight\n   provides consistent evasion enhancement that complements the\n   Psionicist's other defensive abilities. Excellent when combined with\n   Mindwall for layered magical and physical defense.\n*******************************************************************************\n
169	shelp_iron_skin	-1	iron skin	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Iron Skin\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: Your iron skin fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Pugilist: level 22\nDescription:\n   Iron Skin is a passive conditioning technique mastered by experienced\n   Pugilists. Through years of repeated blows and deliberate skin-hardening\n   exercises, the fighter develops a natural resistance to physical damage.\n   The skin and underlying tissue become denser and more resilient, providing\n   a permanent reduction in damage taken from physical attacks.\n\n   Iron Skin is always active once learned — it does not need to be activated\n   and cannot be dispelled by normal means. The conditioning is physiological\n   rather than magical, meaning it persists regardless of magical suppression\n   effects. Combined with the Pugilist's other defensive techniques, Iron Skin\n   makes these fighters remarkably durable despite fighting without heavy armor.\n*******************************************************************************\n
170	shelp_leadership	-1	leadership	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Leadership\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 75\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Leadership\n   Wear-Off: !Leadership!\nAcquisition:\n   - Knight: level 12\n   - Paladin: level 24\nDescription:\n   Leadership inspires grouped allies with a hitroll bonus, functioning as a teamwide offensive support buff.\n*******************************************************************************\n
171	shelp_psionic_recovery	-1	psionic recovery	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Psionic Recovery\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 5\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: You feel less protected.\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 5\nDescription:\n   Psionic Recovery is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
172	shelp_ancient_bark	-1	ancient bark	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: ancient bark\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n    HP Cost: 35\n Wait Beats: 24\n  Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: \nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 68\nDescription:\n   Large AC buff plus thorns that damage attackers.\n*******************************************************************************\n
173	shelp_ledger_mark	-1	ledger mark	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Ledger Mark\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 12\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: ledger mark\n   Wear-Off: !Ledger Mark!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 14\nDescription:\n   Ledger Mark is a Cleric utility spell that inscribes a divine tracking\n   mark on a target in the name of Disk's accounting. The marked target is\n   registered in Disk's divine ledger, allowing the Cleric to locate them\n   or be aware of their presence. The spell is used for tracking enemies\n   of the faith, marking those who owe divine debts, or maintaining\n   awareness of important individuals.\n\n   While the mark is active, the Cleric gains enhanced perception regarding\n   the marked target and may have improved accuracy when targeting them with\n   subsequent spells. The Ledger Mark represents the Cleric's role as a\n   keeper of divine accounts — one who tracks and records all transgressions\n   and debts on behalf of their god.\n*******************************************************************************\n
174	shelp_chiblock	-1	chiblock	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Chiblock\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 80\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Chiblock\n   Wear-Off: You are no longer able to block with your chi!\nAcquisition:\n   - Brawler: level 84\n   - Monk: level 86\nDescription:\n   Chiblock converts chi into a temporary defensive stance, improving armor for several rounds as a monk-style block effect.\n*******************************************************************************\n
175	shelp_sap_mend	-1	sap mend	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: sap mend\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n    HP Cost: 8\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: \nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 3\nDescription:\n   Basic self heal (20-35 HP).\n*******************************************************************************\n
176	shelp_chain_lightning	-1	chain lightning	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Chain Lightning\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 25\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: lightening bolt\n   Wear-Off: !chain-light!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 65\nDescription:\n   Chain Lightning Launches lightning that arcs between multiple enemies, damaging each jump target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
178	shelp_equip_buckler	-1	equip buckler	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Equip Buckler\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Equip Buckler!\nAcquisition:\n   - Paladin: level 1\n   - Knight: level 1\n   - Swordsman: level 1\nDescription:\n   Equip Buckler allows you to wear bucklers that are otherwise restricted.\n*******************************************************************************\n
179	shelp_bash	-1	bash	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Bash\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: bash\n   Wear-Off: !bash!\nAcquisition:\n   - Warden: level 28\nDescription:\n   Bash is a straightforward heavy-body strike in the warrior combo chain, used to pressure targets and build toward combo-triggered follow-up attacks.\n*******************************************************************************\n
180	shelp_black_hand	-1	black hand	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Black Hand\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 50\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Black Hand\n   Wear-Off: The hand dissolves from around your throat into nothingness.\nAcquisition:\n   - Necromancer: level 7\n   - Egomancer: level 7\nDescription:\n   Black Hand is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
181	shelp_solar_invocation	-1	solar invocation	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Solar Invocation\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 25\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Solar Invocation!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 22\nDescription:\n   Solar Invocation is a Cleric prayer ritual that invokes Disk's solar\n   aspect, calling for divine blessing and empowerment through sustained\n   devotion. The Cleric enters a brief meditative invocation, and if their\n   faith is sufficient, Disk responds with a blessing that improves the\n   Cleric's overall combat and healing effectiveness.\n\n   Solar Invocation is the Cleric's primary self-buff prayer. The effect\n   enhances the potency of subsequent healing spells and slightly improves\n   the Cleric's divine combat capabilities. It represents the Cleric\n   entering a heightened state of divine alignment, where Disk's will flows\n   more freely through them. The invocation must be performed at rest\n   (standing position) as it requires focused devotional attention.\n*******************************************************************************\n
182	shelp_assertion_form	-1	assertion form	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Assertion Form\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 60\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: Your assertion form fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 60\nDescription:\n   Assertion Form is an advanced psionic self-enhancement technique. The\n   Psionicist enters a formalized combat trance, overlaying their normal\n   consciousness with a highly structured mental combat framework. In this\n   state, their perception sharpens, their reflexes are guided by predictive\n   psionic modeling, and they fight with unusual precision and efficiency.\n\n   While Assertion Form is active, the Psionicist gains bonuses to their\n   combat stats — improved attack, damage, and defense — reflecting the\n   enhanced mental engagement with every action. The form is difficult to\n   maintain under severe stress, and particularly powerful disruptions may\n   cause it to collapse. It is the Psionicist's equivalent of a martial\n   combat trance, achieved through mental rather than physical discipline.\n*******************************************************************************\n
183	shelp_root_touch	-1	root touch	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Root Touch\n       Kind: Spell (Overgrowth — costs HP, not mana)\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: root touch\n   Wear-Off: !Root Touch!\nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 1\nDescription:\n   Root Touch is the most basic expression of the Overgrowth Doctrine: the\n   Druid channels living-world vitality through their own body into a contact\n   strike. The life force of the living world briefly extends through the\n   practitioner's hands. At level 1 this is undirected and inefficient — the\n   technique costs more than the result justifies, which the tradition accepts\n   as a consequence of incomplete covenant.\n\n   Like all Druid spells, Root Touch costs hit points rather than mana\n   (Overgrowth mechanic, growth = 3 HP per cast). Damage: 2d4, earth\n   elemental. Does not scale with level — the Druid's control over this\n   technique is limited at early levels. A successful save halves damage.\n\n   Druids with higher constitution sustain this at lower relative cost.\n   Root Touch is superseded by Thornlash (level 3) for sustained offense.\n*******************************************************************************\n
184	shelp_feeble_body	-1	feeble body	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Feeble Body\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 12\n Wait Beats: 18\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: You are now moving quickly.\nAcquisition:\n   - Necromancer: level 45\nDescription:\n   Feeble Body is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
185	shelp_cloak_transcendence	-1	cloak:transcendence	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Cloak:transcendence\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 550\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: @@NThe @@Ccloak@@N around your body fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Assassin: level 48\nDescription:\n   Cloak:transcendence is the Assassin's signature remort cloak. It envelops\n   the caster in a shimmering aura of transcendent agility, granting a small\n   chance to completely avoid incoming physical attacks.\n\n   When the caster would take physical damage, there is a pseudo_level / 15\n   percent chance that the Assassin transcends the strike entirely, taking no\n   damage. For example, at pseudo-level 150, there is a 10% chance to avoid\n   each physical hit.\n\n   The cloak does not protect against non-physical (spell) damage. For\n   magical avoidance, see cloak:oathbreaker (Warlock).\n\n   Duration scales with pseudo-level (pseudo_level / 8 rounds).\n*******************************************************************************\n
186	shelp_thornhide	-1	thornhide	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: thornhide\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n    HP Cost: 15\n Wait Beats: 24\n  Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: \nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 14\nDescription:\n   Reflects melee damage to attackers.\n*******************************************************************************\n
187	shelp_heat_armor	-1	heat armor	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Heat Armor\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 350\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Heat Armor\n   Wear-Off: !Heat Armor!\nAcquisition:\n   - Sorcerer: level 57\n   - Wizard: level 57\n   - Necromancer: level 78\n   - Egomancer: level 78\nDescription:\n   Heat Armor is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
188	shelp_shield	-1	shield	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Shield\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 12\n Wait Beats: 18\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: Your force shield shimmers, then fades away.\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 9\nDescription:\n   Shield is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
189	shelp_gas_breath	-1	gas breath	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Gas Breath\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 4\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: blast of gas\n   Wear-Off: !Gas Breath!\nAcquisition:\n   - Not learnable by player classes.\nDescription:\n   Gas Breath Exhales a cloud of toxic gas that damages and can debilitate multiple targets.\n*******************************************************************************\n
190	shelp_withering_shadow	-1	withering shadow	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Withering Shadow\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 150\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: @@NThe @@dWithering Shadow@@N dissipates.\nAcquisition:\n   - Knight: level 17\n   - Swordsman: level 17\nDescription:\n   Withering Shadow Unleashes draining shadow energy that weakens the target while dealing damage over time.\n*******************************************************************************\n
191	shelp_purge_toxin	-1	purge toxin	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: purge toxin\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n    HP Cost: 10\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: \nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 22\nDescription:\n   Cures poison on the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
192	shelp_enhanced_damage	-1	enhanced damage	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Enhanced Damage\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Enhanced Damage!\nAcquisition:\n   - Warden: level 20\nDescription:\n   Enhanced Damage passively increases your physical damage, scaling with Strength.\n*******************************************************************************\n
