194	shelp_target	-1	target	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Target\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: target\n   Wear-Off: !target\nAcquisition:\n   - Monk: level 18\n   - Brawler: level 18\n   - Knight: level 20\n   - Swordsman: level 20\n   - Paladin: level 32\n   - Priest: level 32\nDescription:\n   Target is a focus opener that rapidly commits you to a selected victim with an immediate strike, useful for fast target swaps and pursuit pressure.\n*******************************************************************************\n
195	shelp_sap_strength	-1	sap strength	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: sap strength\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n    HP Cost: 15\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: \nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 18\nDescription:\n   Reduces target STR by 2.\n*******************************************************************************\n
196	shelp_testimonial_guard	-1	testimonial guard	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Testimonial Guard\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Testimonial Guard!\nAcquisition:\n   - Sentinel: level 12\nDescription:\n   Testimonial Guard is a passive defensive discipline of the Sentinel.\n   The warrior has internalized the core Pale Ledger principle that a\n   reliable witness must protect themselves to continue bearing testimony.\n   This translates into an instinctive defensive alertness that improves\n   the Sentinel's armor class and resistance to incoming attacks.\n\n   The passive benefit represents a constant state of careful situational\n   awareness — the Sentinel never fully relaxes their guard, always\n   maintaining the physical posture and mental alertness of someone who\n   expects to be tested at any moment. Combined with other Sentinel\n   defensive skills, Testimonial Guard makes these warriors difficult\n   targets despite their role as frontline combatants.\n*******************************************************************************\n
