220	shelp_summon_beast	-1	summon beast	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Summon Beast\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 1200\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: None\nAcquisition:\n   - Not learnable by player classes.\nDescription:\n   Summon Beast Calls a beast companion to assist the caster in battle.\n*******************************************************************************\n
232	shelp_enchant_weapon	-1	enchant weapon	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Enchant Weapon\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_OBJ_INV\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 100\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Enchant Weapon!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 39\nDescription:\n   Enchant Weapon Temporarily enchants a weapon with magical power to improve its combat effectiveness.\n*******************************************************************************\n
221	shelp_duty_strike	-1	duty strike	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Duty Strike\n       Kind: Skill (active combat)\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 1\n Wait Beats: 18\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: duty strike\n   Wear-Off: !Duty Strike!\nAcquisition:\n   - Warden: level 1\nDescription:\n   Duty Strike is the foundational combat technique of the Registry School\n   curriculum — a direct, committed blow delivered from a stable stance. In\n   Dunmar's Watch doctrine the first blow from held ground is not an attack;\n   it is a statement of position. The duty strike forces the enemy to\n   acknowledge that the ground is held.\n\n   Damage is calculated from pseudo-level and Strength, same as other Warden\n   melee attacks (kick, checkpoint break). This is not a finesse technique;\n   it is weight and commitment delivered correctly.\n\n   Syntax: duty strike <target>\n   Requires POS_FIGHTING. Can be practiced to improve hit rate.\n*******************************************************************************\n
222	shelp_thought_vise	-1	thought vise	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Thought Vise\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 200\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Thought Vise\n   Wear-Off: !Thought Vise!\nAcquisition:\n   - Egomancer: level 70\nDescription:\n   Thought Vise is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
223	shelp_dualwield	-1	dualwield	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Dualwield\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !DualWield!\nAcquisition:\n   - Assassin: level 5\n   - Warlock: level 5\nDescription:\n   Dualwield allows you to wield weapons in both hands at the same time.\n*******************************************************************************\n
224	shelp_oathshield	-1	oathshield	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Oathshield\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE (other)\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: The oathshield fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Templar: level 10\nDescription:\n   Oathshield extends the Templar's oath to shield an ally, granting them\n   an AC bonus for several rounds. This represents the Solar Court\n   auxiliaries' threshold-guardian role -- standing between danger and\n   those they protect.\n\n   Target: Must target another character (cannot self-cast)\n   Costs: Movement (via subtract_energy_cost)\n   Cooldown: 20 rounds\n   Duration: 3 + (Templar level / 5) rounds\n   AC modifier: -(Templar level * 4 + Paladin level * 2)\n\n   This is the only ally-targeted defensive buff in the adept system,\n   reflecting the Templar's unique position as both combatant and protector.\n*******************************************************************************\n
225	shelp_curse	-1	curse	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Curse\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 20\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: curse\n   Wear-Off: The curse wears off.\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 26\n   - Magi: level 35\nDescription:\n   Curse is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
226	shelp_know_terrain	-1	know terrain	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: know terrain\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n    HP Cost: 8\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: \nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 15\nDescription:\n   Reveals alignment of creatures. Like know alignment.\n*******************************************************************************\n
227	shelp_bad_breath	-1	bad breath	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Bad Breath\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 10\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: bad breath\n   Wear-Off: !Bad Breath!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 4\nDescription:\n   Bad Breath is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
228	shelp_seven_shade_hold	-1	seven shade hold	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Seven Shade Hold\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage:\n   Wear-Off: You release the Seven Shade Hold.\nAcquisition:\n   - Warden: level 22\nDescription:\n   Seven Shade Hold toggles a defensive combat posture named after the\n   Seven Shade Arches, the feat of positional engineering that defined\n   Dunmar's Watch doctrine. While active, the Warden gains an armor class\n   bonus (-Warden level/3) but suffers a reduced damage roll (-Warden\n   level/6). The posture persists indefinitely until toggled off by using\n   the skill again. Cannot be used while in combat. Best used when\n   expecting sustained fights or needing to hold position.\n   Syntax: seven shade hold\n*******************************************************************************\n
229	shelp_magic_missile	-1	magic missile	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Magic Missile\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 15\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: magic missile\n   Wear-Off: !Magic Missile!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 3\nDescription:\n   Magic Missile is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
230	shelp_fleche	-1	fleche	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Fleche\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 80\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Fleche\n   Wear-Off: !Fleche!\nAcquisition:\n   - Swordsman: level 45\nDescription:\n   Fleche is a high-impact finisher attack in the warrior combo system that deals boosted physical damage and can improve combo momentum when timed correctly.\n*******************************************************************************\n
231	shelp_adrenaline_bonus	-1	adrenaline bonus	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Adrenaline Bonus\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !ADRENALINE BONUS!\nAcquisition:\n   - Not learnable by player classes.\nDescription:\n   Adrenaline Bonus is a short-lived damroll buff triggered by Adrenaline after taking heavy damage.\n*******************************************************************************\n
234	shelp_cause_light	-1	cause light	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Cause Light\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 15\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: spell\n   Wear-Off: !Cause Light!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 4\nDescription:\n   Cause Light is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
235	shelp_forestsight	-1	forestsight	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: forestsight\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n    HP Cost: 5\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: \nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 7\nDescription:\n   Grants detect hidden.\n*******************************************************************************\n
236	shelp_crystal_burst	-1	crystal burst	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Crystal Burst\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 15\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: crystal burst\n   Wear-Off: !Crystal Burst!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 7\nDescription:\n   Crystal Burst is an early offensive spell available to the Magi. The\n   caster condenses arcane energy into sharp crystalline shards and projects\n   them at high velocity into the target. The crystals shatter on impact,\n   causing piercing and slashing damage from the explosion of razor fragments.\n\n   Crystal Burst is a staple early-game offensive tool for the Magi, offering\n   reliable physical-arcane hybrid damage at low mana cost. The spell is\n   straightforward in application and does not have secondary effects, making\n   it a solid damage option when more specialized spells are not appropriate\n   for the situation. Higher levels of Magi find it replaced by more powerful\n   fire and ice spells, but it remains useful in situations where elemental\n   resistance would reduce those spells' effectiveness.\n*******************************************************************************\n
237	shelp_enhanced_purify	-1	enhanced purify	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Enhanced Purify\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Enhanced Purify!\nAcquisition:\n   - Egomancer: level 44\nDescription:\n   Enhanced Purify upgrades Purify so it also attempts to cure blindness and remove curses in addition to clearing poison.\n*******************************************************************************\n
238	shelp_morale	-1	morale	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Morale\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 75\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Morale\n   Wear-Off: !Morale!\nAcquisition:\n   - Knight: level 10\n   - Paladin: level 21\nDescription:\n   Morale bolsters grouped allies with a damroll bonus, improving the party's overall damage potential.\n*******************************************************************************\n
239	shelp_seal_calculus	-1	seal calculus	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Seal Calculus\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 25\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Seal Calculus!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 79\nDescription:\n   Seal Calculus is a high-level Cleric utility spell that performs a\n   comprehensive divine calculation of all seals and testimonies present in\n   an area. The spell evaluates the spiritual state of the environment,\n   counting and categorizing active divine seals, testimonies, and ledger\n   marks, and reveals information about their strength and who placed them.\n\n   For Clerics who work extensively with the Pale Ledger's sealing system,\n   Seal Calculus is an invaluable administrative tool. It allows a senior\n   Cleric to audit the divine accounting of an area and identify any seals\n   that have been tampered with, weakened, or improperly placed. The spell\n   is rarely used in combat but is essential for advanced work with Disk's\n   judicial and archival systems.\n*******************************************************************************\n
240	shelp_road_sweep	-1	road sweep	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Road Sweep\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 1\n Wait Beats: 18\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: road sweep\n   Wear-Off: !Road Sweep!\nAcquisition:\n   - Warden: level 8\nDescription:\n   Road Sweep is a low-angled combat technique developed by Wardens who\n   train on uneven terrain. The warrior delivers a sweeping kick or strike\n   targeting the opponent's lower body — knees, shins, or ankles. The\n   blow trips or staggers the target, potentially knocking them off balance\n   and interrupting their next action.\n\n   Road Sweep is an early offensive skill that complements the Warden's\n   direct assault style. It deals physical damage and can interrupt the\n   target's positioning, making follow-up strikes easier to land. The\n   technique is most effective against opponents who rely on footwork and\n   mobility, as disrupting their stance negates much of their defensive\n   advantage.\n*******************************************************************************\n
241	shelp_bloody_tears	-1	bloody tears	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Bloody Tears\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 12\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Bloody Tears\n   Wear-Off: !Bloody Tears!\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 26\nDescription:\n   Bloody Tears is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
242	shelp_revenant	-1	revenant	.\n***** REVENANT *****\n\nName:          Revenant\nKind:          Spell\nTarget:        Object (NPC corpse in room)\nPosition:      Standing\nMin Mana:      75\nWait Beats:    24\nCan Learn:     No\n\nAcquisition:   Necromancer level 70, Ego level 70\n\nDescription:\n   Raises a permanent undead minion (revenant) from an NPC corpse.\n   The revenant inherits the original mob's full combat statistics,\n   capped at the caster's pseudo level (hard cap 150).\n\n   Better corpses produce stronger revenants.  Use the 'revenant'\n   command to manage tracks, feed soul points, and view status.\n\n   Only one revenant may be controlled at a time.\n\n   Replaces the old 'animate' spell with a more powerful and\n   customizable undead minion system.\n\nSee also: HELP REVENANT, HELP REVENANT TRACKS, HELP REVENANT INFUSE\n
243	shelp_frost_breath	-1	frost breath	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Frost Breath\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 4\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: blast of frost\n   Wear-Off: !Frost Breath!\nAcquisition:\n   - Not learnable by player classes.\nDescription:\n   Frost Breath is an offensive spell that inflicts frost damage on an enemy target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
244	shelp_convergence_shield	-1	convergence shield	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Convergence Shield\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 100\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: Your convergence shield dissipates.\nAcquisition:\n   - Grand Magi: level 8\nDescription:\n   Convergence Shield creates a rotating barrier of elemental forces around\n   the caster, providing an AC bonus that scales with Grand Magi level and\n   Intelligence.\n\n   Duration: level / 8 hours\n   AC modifier: -(Grand Magi level * 5 + Intelligence / 2)\n   Mana cost: 100\n\n   This reflects the Solar Court's original ceremonial purpose of\n   "demonstrating stability under pressure" -- showing that multiple\n   elemental forces can be held in organized simultaneous expression.\n   Distinct from Elemental Ward (which provides saving throw reduction);\n   Convergence Shield provides direct AC protection.\n*******************************************************************************\n
245	shelp_iceshield	-1	iceshield	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Iceshield\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 350\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: None\nAcquisition:\n   - Sorcerer: level 65\n   - Wizard: level 65\nDescription:\n   Iceshield encases the caster in a protective layer of magical ice. Unlike\n   fireshield and shockshield, iceshield is a purely defensive shield -- it\n   does not deal any reactive damage, but absorbs a much higher percentage\n   of incoming damage and has far more hit points.\n\n   Shield properties:\n     - Type: ICE_SHIELD (can coexist with other shields)\n     - Reactive Damage: None (purely absorptive)\n     - Absorption: 50% + (pseudo_level / 6)% of incoming damage absorbed\n     - Hit Points: 15,000 + (pseudo_level * 50) -- shield breaks when depleted\n     - Duration: pseudo_level / 15 rounds (halved on login)\n\n   Iceshield can coexist with other shield effects. Only duplicate iceshields\n   are prevented from stacking.\n*******************************************************************************\n
246	shelp_ashfall_strike	-1	ashfall strike	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Ashfall Strike\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 1\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Ashfall Strike!\nAcquisition:\n   - Warden: level 35\nDescription:\n   Ashfall Strike is a debilitating combat technique used by experienced Wardens.\n   The warrior delivers a powerful blow that leaves a residual ash-like coating on\n   the target, reducing their combat effectiveness. The strike applies a stacking\n   debuff that lowers the target's armor class and attack rolls for a short\n   duration.\n\n   Each application of Ashfall Strike refreshes and intensifies the debuff,\n   making it valuable to apply repeatedly in extended fights. The effect is\n   particularly potent against heavily armored foes, as the ashen coating\n   interferes with joint articulation and visibility.\n*******************************************************************************\n
247	shelp_dodge	-1	dodge	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Dodge\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Dodge!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cipher: level 7\n   - Pugilist: level 27\nDescription:\n   Dodge gives you a chance to evade incoming attacks entirely during combat.\n*******************************************************************************\n
248	shelp_sap_transfusion	-1	sap transfusion	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: sap transfusion\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_NOTSELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n    HP Cost: 10\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: \nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 80\nDescription:\n   Transfer HP from caster to target at 1:1 ratio.\n*******************************************************************************\n
249	shelp_tribunals_hand	-1	tribunal's hand	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Tribunal's Hand\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 20\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: tribunal's hand\n   Wear-Off: !Tribunal's Hand!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 58\nDescription:\n   Tribunal's Hand is a high-level Cleric offensive spell that invokes the\n   full authority of Disk's divine tribunal. The Cleric channels the\n   combined judgment of the celestial court, delivering a devastating\n   critical blow of divine force. The spell calls down Disk's hand as an\n   instrument of the tribunal's decision, crushing the target with the\n   weight of divine verdict.\n\n   Tribunal's Hand is one of the Cleric's most powerful single-target\n   offensive spells, dealing major holy damage. The tribunal aspect means\n   the spell has an enhanced critical chance — when the tribunal's decision\n   is delivered with full certainty, the blow lands with devastating force.\n   It is the culmination of the Cleric's role as an executor of divine\n   judgment rather than merely a healer.\n*******************************************************************************\n
250	shelp_haste	-1	haste	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Haste\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 12\n Wait Beats: 18\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: You are no longer moving quickly.\nAcquisition:\n   - Wizard: level 84\nDescription:\n   Haste is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
251	shelp_astral_projection	-1	astral projection	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Astral Projection\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 40\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage:\n   Wear-Off: !Astral Projection!\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 60\nDescription:\n   Astral Projection separates the Psionicist's consciousness from their\n   physical body. For level/8 rounds, the caster gains AFF_PASS_DOOR\n   (ability to move through closed doors and barriers) and an armor class\n   improvement (-level/3). Cannot be stacked with itself. While projected,\n   the Psionicist can navigate obstacles that would normally impede\n   movement. The highest-tier Psionicist utility spell, granting\n   extraordinary freedom of movement.\n*******************************************************************************\n
252	shelp_detect_magic	-1	detect magic	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Detect Magic\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 5\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: The detect magic wears off.\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 7\n   - Cleric: level 7\nDescription:\n   Detect Magic is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
253	shelp_cloak_flaming	-1	cloak:flaming	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Cloak:flaming\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 750\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: @@NThe @@ecloak@@N around your body fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Sorcerer: level 48\nDescription:\n   Cloak:flaming is the Sorcerer's signature remort cloak. It wraps the\n   caster in a cloak of searing flame. When the caster takes physical damage,\n   the cloak erupts and reflects 15% of the incoming damage back at the\n   attacker as fire-element damage.\n\n   The reflected damage bypasses reflection and absorption effects (it carries\n   NO_REFLECT and NO_ABSORB flags). The cloak only triggers against physical\n   attacks -- spells and non-physical damage do not activate it.\n\n   For a similar effect against non-physical damage, see cloak:elements\n   (Wizard).\n\n   Duration scales with pseudo-level (pseudo_level / 8 rounds).\n*******************************************************************************\n
254	shelp_spirit_curse	-1	spirit curse	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Spirit Curse\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 120\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Spirit Curse\n   Wear-Off: !Spirit Curse!\nAcquisition:\n   - Necromancer: level 77\n   - Egomancer: level 77\nDescription:\n   Spirit Curse is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
255	shelp_iron_golem	-1	iron golem	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Iron Golem\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 800\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !IRON GOLEM!\nAcquisition:\n   - Sorcerer: level 63\n   - Wizard: level 63\nDescription:\n   Iron Golem Summons an iron golem companion with strong durability for frontline fighting.\n*******************************************************************************\n
256	shelp_holyshield	-1	holyshield	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Holyshield\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 400\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: None\nAcquisition:\n   - Priest: level 48\nDescription:\n   Holyshield is the Priest's signature remort shield. It surrounds the\n   caster in a radiant aura of holy light that retaliates specifically\n   against magical attacks. Similar in structure to fireshield, it deals\n   reactive holy-element damage to spell-casting attackers while absorbing\n   a portion of incoming damage.\n\n   The key difference from fireshield is that holyshield's reactive damage\n   only triggers against non-physical (magical) attacks. Physical attacks\n   still have their damage absorbed by the shield, but do not provoke a\n   retaliatory strike.\n\n   Shield properties:\n     - Type: HOLY_SHIELD (cannot stack with other non-coexisting shields)\n     - Reactive Damage: 30% of incoming damage as holy damage (spells only)\n     - Absorption: 10% + (pseudo_level / 10)% of incoming damage absorbed\n     - Hit Points: 5,000 + (pseudo_level * 10) -- shield breaks when depleted\n     - Duration: pseudo_level / 10 rounds (halved on login)\n\n   The reactive holy damage bypasses cloak reflection and absorption effects.\n*******************************************************************************\n
257	shelp_summon_shadow	-1	summon shadow	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Summon Shadow\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 1200\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: None\nAcquisition:\n   - Not learnable by player classes.\nDescription:\n   Summon Shadow Summons a controllable shadow servant to fight for the caster for a limited time.\n*******************************************************************************\n
258	shelp_cure_serious	-1	cure serious	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Cure Serious\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 15\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Cure Serious!\nAcquisition:\n   - Not learnable by player classes.\nDescription:\n   Cure Serious is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
259	shelp_cloak_valor	-1	cloak:valor	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Cloak:valor\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 550\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: @@NThe @@Wcloak@@N around your body fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Paladin: level 48\nDescription:\n   Cloak:valor is the Paladin's signature remort cloak. It wraps the Paladin\n   in an aura of righteous fury that converts suffering into power. When the\n   Paladin is struck in combat, there is a chance the cloak will ignite with\n   holy energy, granting the Paladin a guaranteed critical hit on their next\n   attack or ability.\n\n   Proc mechanics:\n     - Trigger: Each hit taken has a pseudo_level / 10 percent chance to proc\n       (e.g. 10% at pseudo-level 100)\n     - Effect: Applies a "valor_crit" buff that guarantees the Paladin's next\n       damage-dealing action is a critical hit\n     - The buff lasts up to 2 rounds if not consumed\n     - The buff does not stack -- if already active, it will not re-proc\n\n   This cloak leans heavily into the Paladin's support identity, rewarding\n   the Paladin for taking hits and converting defense into powerful offensive\n   moments.\n\n   Duration scales with pseudo-level (pseudo_level / 8 rounds).\n*******************************************************************************\n
260	shelp_chill_touch	-1	chill touch	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Chill Touch\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 15\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: chilling touch\n   Wear-Off: You feel less cold.\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 8\nDescription:\n   Chill Touch is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
261	shelp_rockburst	-1	rockburst	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: rockburst\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n    HP Cost: 15\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: rockburst\nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 10\nDescription:\n   A burst of stone shards for earth damage.\n*******************************************************************************\n
283	shelp_poison	-1	poison	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Poison\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 10\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: poison\n   Wear-Off: You feel less sick.\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 31\nDescription:\n   Poison is an offensive spell that inflicts poison damage on an enemy target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
262	shelp_restoration	-1	restoration	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Restoration\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 50\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !restoration!\nAcquisition:\n   - Not learnable by player classes.\nDescription:\n   Restoration is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
263	shelp_turn_undead	-1	turn undead	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Turn Undead\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 20\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage:\n   Wear-Off: !Turn Undead!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 15\nDescription:\n   Turn Undead channels divine power outward against undead and evil\n   creatures (alignment < -200) in the room. Targets that fail their\n   saving throw take full damage (4d(level)); those who save take\n   reduced damage. A room-wide holy attack targeting only evil-aligned\n   NPCs. Cannot be trained; its effectiveness scales automatically with\n   Cleric level. An essential tool when fighting undead-heavy areas or\n   demonic content.\n*******************************************************************************\n
264	shelp_laser_bolt	-1	laser bolt	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Laser Bolt\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 35\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: laserbolt\n   Wear-Off: !laserbolt!\nAcquisition:\n   - Not learnable by player classes.\nDescription:\n   Laser Bolt is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
265	shelp_detect_undead	-1	detect undead	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Detect Undead\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 8\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: You no longer sense undead beings.\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 8\nDescription:\n   Detect Undead is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
266	shelp_psishield	-1	psishield	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Psishield\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 400\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: None\nAcquisition:\n   - Egomancer: level 48\nDescription:\n   Psishield is the Egomancer's signature remort shield. It surrounds the\n   caster in a pulsing psionic field that assaults the minds of attackers.\n   Similar in structure to fireshield, it deals reactive mental-element\n   damage while absorbing a portion of incoming damage.\n\n   Shield properties:\n     - Type: PSI_SHIELD (cannot stack with other non-coexisting shields)\n     - Reactive Damage: 30% of incoming damage dealt back as mental damage\n     - Absorption: 10% + (pseudo_level / 10)% of incoming damage absorbed\n     - Hit Points: 5,000 + (pseudo_level * 10) -- shield breaks when depleted\n     - Duration: pseudo_level / 10 rounds (halved on login)\n\n   The reactive mental damage bypasses cloak reflection and absorption\n   effects. Creatures without minds are immune to the reactive component.\n*******************************************************************************\n
267	shelp_fissure	-1	fissure	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: fissure\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n    HP Cost: 25\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: fissure\nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 46\nDescription:\n   The ground splits for massive earth damage.\n*******************************************************************************\n
268	shelp_terra_rend	-1	terra rend	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Terra Rend\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 120\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: terra rend\n   Wear-Off: !terra rend!\nAcquisition:\n   - Wizard: level 40\nDescription:\n   Terra Rend is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
269	shelp_gate	-1	gate	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Gate\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 50\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Gate!\nAcquisition:\n   - Not learnable by player classes.\nDescription:\n   Gate is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
270	shelp_teleport	-1	teleport	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Teleport\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 35\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Teleport!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 40\nDescription:\n   Teleport is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
271	shelp_harbor_dust	-1	harbor dust	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Harbor Dust\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 1\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Harbor Dust!\nAcquisition:\n   - Pugilist: level 47\nDescription:\n   Harbor Dust is an advanced Pugilist technique derived from dockside\n   brawling traditions. The fighter reaches into a concealed pouch and hurls\n   a mixture of fine abrasive dust directly into the opponent's face.\n   The dust blinds and disorients the target, temporarily reducing their\n   accuracy and ability to dodge.\n\n   The technique requires no special tool — experienced Pugilists always\n   carry a supply of the mixture. The dust cloud briefly surrounds the\n   target's head, causing eye irritation and disorientation. While it deals\n   no direct damage, the debilitating effect often turns the tide of a close\n   fight by creating an opening for the Pugilist to deliver decisive blows.\n   The effect is short-lived as most opponents can clear their eyes quickly.\n*******************************************************************************\n
272	shelp_black_curse	-1	black curse	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Black Curse\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 120\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Black Curse\n   Wear-Off: !Black Curse!\nAcquisition:\n   - Necromancer: level 65\n   - Egomancer: level 65\nDescription:\n   Black Curse is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
273	shelp_flee_timer	-1	flee timer	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Flee Timer\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: Your anti-flee timer has expired!\nAcquisition:\n   - Not learnable by player classes.\nDescription:\n   Flee Timer is the temporary cooldown effect applied after fleeing, preventing immediate repeated flee attempts.\n*******************************************************************************\n
274	shelp_interior_discipline	-1	interior discipline	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Interior Discipline\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 80\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: interior discipline\n   Wear-Off: You lose your interior discipline focus.\nAcquisition:\n   - Pugilist: level 21\nDescription:\n   Interior Discipline is a Pugilist technique that harnesses internal energy\n   to deliver a powerful focused strike. The fighter channels their internal\n   training into a single devastating blow, targeting the opponent's core\n   or internal organs to cause maximum disruption.\n\n   The technique is derived from pressure-point fighting methods that focus\n   on disrupting the opponent's internal alignment rather than simply\n   delivering surface damage. A successful Interior Discipline strike can\n   impair the target's regeneration or reduce their combat effectiveness\n   as their body struggles to compensate for the internal impact. The\n   focus required means this skill has a longer cooldown than basic attacks.\n*******************************************************************************\n
275	shelp_strangling_vines	-1	strangling vines	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: strangling vines\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n    HP Cost: 35\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: strangling vines\nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 65\nDescription:\n   Earth damage plus a DEX-lowering snare.\n*******************************************************************************\n
276	shelp_bless	-1	bless	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Bless\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 5\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: You feel less righteous.\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 8\nDescription:\n   Bless is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
277	shelp_thoughtsteal	-1	thoughtsteal	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Thoughtsteal\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 30\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: thoughtsteal\n   Wear-Off: !Thoughtsteal!\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 40\nDescription:\n   Thoughtsteal tears cognitive fragments from the victim's mind, weakening\n   their intellect while bolstering the caster's. The stolen INT amount is\n   level/8 (minimum 1). The victim suffers an INT debuff (-stolen amount)\n   and a saving throw penalty (+level/6) for level/6 rounds, reducing both\n   mental acuity and spell resistance. The caster gains an INT buff\n   (+stolen/2) for the same duration. A unique dual-action spell that\n   simultaneously harms and buffs through a single cast.\n*******************************************************************************\n
278	shelp_grapple	-1	grapple	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Grapple\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 1\n Wait Beats: 18\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: grapple\n   Wear-Off: !Grapple!\nAcquisition:\n   - Pugilist: level 15\nDescription:\n   Grapple seizes the opponent in a clinch during melee combat. Both the\n   Pugilist and the victim suffer an armor class debuff (-level/5) for 2\n   rounds due to the tangle. The victim also has AFF_HOLD applied,\n   restricting their movement and actions. The mutual disadvantage rewards\n   Pugilists with high natural armor and hit points who can weather the\n   exchange better than their opponents.\n*******************************************************************************\n
279	shelp_primary_motion	-1	primary motion	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Primary Motion\n       Kind: Skill (active combat)\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 1\n Wait Beats: 18\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: primary motion\n   Wear-Off: !Primary Motion!\nAcquisition:\n   - Pugilist: level 1\nDescription:\n   Primary Motion is the first thing taught in Pugilist training: a single,\n   clean, efficient strike. Economy of Motion holds that no movement should\n   be wasted — every action deliberate, every step purposeful. Primary Motion\n   is not powerful. It is correct. The pyramid-construction labor tradition\n   that produces Pugilists does not celebrate force; it celebrates precision\n   of application. This is where that application begins.\n\n   Damage is calculated from pseudo-level and Constitution (pug_attack\n   helper, same as palmstrike, pummel). As the Pugilist advances, Primary\n   Motion gives way to more specialized techniques from the Interior Forms\n   curriculum.\n\n   Syntax: primary motion <target>\n   Requires POS_FIGHTING. Can be practiced to improve hit rate.\n*******************************************************************************\n
280	shelp_creeping_blight	-1	creeping blight	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: creeping blight\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n    HP Cost: 40\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: \nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 78\nDescription:\n   Reduces STR and CON by 3 and impairs healing.\n*******************************************************************************\n
281	shelp_portal	-1	portal	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Portal\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 100\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Portal!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 80\nDescription:\n   Portal Creates a temporary magical portal for rapid travel between locations.\n*******************************************************************************\n
282	shelp_planergy	-1	planergy	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Planergy\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 25\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: energy\n   Wear-Off: !planergy!\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 5\nDescription:\n   Planergy is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
284	shelp_lightning_breath	-1	lightning breath	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Lightning Breath\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 4\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: blast of lightning\n   Wear-Off: !Lightning Breath!\nAcquisition:\n   - Not learnable by player classes.\nDescription:\n   Lightning Breath is an offensive spell that inflicts lightning damage on an enemy target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
285	shelp_cloak_absorption	-1	cloak:absorption	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Cloak:absorption\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 500\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: @@NThe @@lcloak@@N around your body fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Not learnable by player classes.\nDescription:\n   Cloak:absorption surrounds the caster in a shimmering cloak that has a\n   chance to absorb offensive spells cast against them. When a spell hits the\n   caster, there is a (pseudo_level - 55) percent chance that the cloak will\n   absorb the spell entirely, negating its damage.\n\n   When a spell is absorbed, the mana cost of that spell is restored to the\n   caster's mana pool (up to their maximum mana), effectively turning enemy\n   spells into fuel.\n\n   The cloak only triggers against offensive targeted spells (TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE).\n\n   Duration scales with pseudo-level (pseudo_level / 8 rounds).\n*******************************************************************************\n
286	shelp_cage	-1	cage	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Cage\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 150\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: @@NThe @@rCage@@N dissipates.\nAcquisition:\n   - Necromancer: level 13\n   - Egomancer: level 13\n   - Sorcerer: level 18\n   - Wizard: level 18\n   - Knight: level 19\n   - Swordsman: level 19\n   - Paladin: level 31\n   - Priest: level 31\n   - Assassin: level 40\n   - Warlock: level 40\nDescription:\n   Cage Traps a target inside a magical cage, restricting movement and isolating them from the fight.\n*******************************************************************************\n
287	shelp_dunmars_call	-1	dunmar's call	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Dunmar's Call\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: dunmar's call\n   Wear-Off: !Dunmar's Call!\nAcquisition:\n   - Warden: level 10\nDescription:\n   Dunmar's Call is the Warden's battle cry, named after the legendary\n   warrior-general Dunmar whose voice was said to fortify entire armies.\n   The Warden unleashes a powerful war shout that bolsters their own fighting\n   spirit and temporarily intimidates nearby opponents.\n\n   The call grants the Warden a short-term bonus to combat stats and may\n   cause weaker enemies to falter in their attacks. In group settings, the\n   cry can provide a morale boost to nearby allies. The technique requires\n   full physical commitment — the Warden must be in a stable standing\n   position to project the full force of the call. It is an early-career\n   cornerstone of the Warden's arsenal, useful both in solo combat and\n   when leading a group charge.\n*******************************************************************************\n
288	shelp_shock_storm	-1	shock storm	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Shock Storm\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 100\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Shock Storm\n   Wear-Off: !Shock Storm!\nAcquisition:\n   - Sorcerer: level 42\n   - Necromancer: level 68\n   - Egomancer: level 68\nDescription:\n   Shock Storm is an offensive spell that inflicts lightning damage on an enemy target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
289	shelp_wither_limbs	-1	wither limbs	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: wither limbs\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n    HP Cost: 20\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: \nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 40\nDescription:\n   Reduces target DEX by 2.\n*******************************************************************************\n
290	shelp_cure_light	-1	cure light	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Cure Light\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 10\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Cure Light!\nAcquisition:\n   - Not learnable by player classes.\nDescription:\n   Cure Light is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
291	shelp_binding_strike	-1	binding strike	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Binding Strike\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 5\n Wait Beats: 18\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: binding strike\n   Wear-Off: Your movements are no longer impaired.\nAcquisition:\n   - Sentinel: level 22\nDescription:\n   Binding Strike is a precise, targeted attack that hampers the opponent's\n   ability to move freely. The Sentinel exploits openings in the target's\n   defenses, striking joints, tendons, or pressure points to reduce their\n   mobility. The target's movement and evasion are impaired for the duration\n   of the effect.\n\n   Binding Strike deals physical damage in addition to applying the movement\n   debuff. It synergizes well with other Sentinel techniques that rely on\n   catching a hindered opponent, such as Verdict and Ninth Descent. The\n   impairment affects flee attempts and dodge chances.\n*******************************************************************************\n
292	shelp_heartwood_balm	-1	heartwood balm	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: heartwood balm\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n    HP Cost: 15\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: \nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 50\nDescription:\n   Cures blindness and poison in one cast.\n*******************************************************************************\n
293	shelp_ego_whip	-1	ego whip	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Ego Whip\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 35\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: ego whip\n   Wear-Off: !Ego Whip!\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 25\nDescription:\n   Ego Whip is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
294	shelp_momentum_chain	-1	momentum chain	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Momentum Chain\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: Your momentum fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Crusader: level 5\nDescription:\n   Momentum Chain activates the Crusader's escalating-pressure doctrine,\n   granting a damroll bonus that represents each strike building on the\n   momentum of the last. The buff reflects the lore's core principle:\n   "chain the Knight's body-strikes into the Swordsman's building\n   momentum, and the accumulated force exceeds what either path sustains\n   alone."\n\n   Costs: Movement (via subtract_energy_cost)\n   Cooldown: 20 rounds\n   Duration: 5 + (Crusader level / 4) rounds\n   Damroll modifier: (Crusader level * 3) + (Knight level * 2)\n                     + (Swordsman level * 2)\n\n   Designed to be activated before building a combo sequence, amplifying\n   the damage of each war_attack skill used during the chain.\n*******************************************************************************\n
295	shelp_choke_hold	-1	choke hold	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Choke Hold\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 1\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: choke hold\n   Wear-Off: !Choke Hold!\nAcquisition:\n   - Pugilist: level 30\nDescription:\n   Choke Hold seizes the victim's throat, cutting off blood flow to the\n   brain. Deals damage (1d(Pugilist level/4 + 1)) and applies AFF_SLEEP,\n   temporarily incapacitating the target for 2 rounds. The incapacitated\n   target cannot act, fight back, or flee during this window. A powerful\n   control skill at high levels, but the brief duration requires follow-up\n   strikes to capitalize on the opening.\n*******************************************************************************\n
296	shelp_curse_of_decay	-1	curse of decay	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: curse of decay\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n    HP Cost: 30\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: \nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 62\nDescription:\n   Applies both curse and poison to the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
297	shelp_overwhelming_assault	-1	overwhelming assault	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Overwhelming Assault\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 80\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Overwhelming Assault\n   Wear-Off: None\nAcquisition:\n   - Crusader: level 15\nDescription:\n   Overwhelming Assault is an alternative combo finisher that replaces the\n   normal combo burst trigger. When the combo sequence is ready for a\n   finisher (all but the last slot filled with unique war_attack skills),\n   using Overwhelming Assault delivers a single devastating blow instead\n   of the normal random-attack burst.\n\n   Requires: is_valid_finisher(ch) == TRUE (combo at max-1 slots filled)\n   Resets combo on use.\n   Cooldown: 20 rounds\n   Damage element: Physical\n   Damage formula: war_attack base damage * combo_damage_multiplier\n                   * (10 + Crusader level) / 10\n\n   This gives Crusaders a deliberate choice: normal combo trigger (many\n   random hits + stun chance) vs. Overwhelming Assault (one enormous hit).\n   The lore's "decisive finishing blows" doctrine made mechanical --\n   channeling all accumulated momentum into a single overwhelming impact.\n\n   Works with the combo system: uses get_max_combo(), reset_combo(),\n   is_valid_finisher(), and combo_damage_multiplier_for_max_combo().\n*******************************************************************************\n
298	shelp_holy_light	-1	holy light	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Holy Light\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 75\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: Holy Light\n   Wear-Off: !Holy Light!\nAcquisition:\n   - Priest: level 14\n   - Paladin: level 43\n   - Wizard: level 82\nDescription:\n   Holy Light Unleashes a burst of holy light that harms dark-aligned enemies and supports allies.\n*******************************************************************************\n
299	shelp_shadowform	-1	shadowform	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Shadowform\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: None\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 9\nDescription:\n   Shadowform applies a sneak effect, helping you move with reduced visibility.\n*******************************************************************************\n
300	shelp_holy_armor	-1	holy armor	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Holy Armor\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 100\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: Your armor is no longer blessed.\nAcquisition:\n   - Priest: level 19\n   - Paladin: level 30\nDescription:\n   Holy Armor is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
301	shelp_asset_flag	-1	asset flag	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Asset Flag\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: Your asset flag fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Cipher: level 15\nDescription:\n   Asset Flag is a covert intelligence technique unique to the Cipher. The\n   operative mentally designates a target as a tracked asset, establishing a\n   persistent awareness of their presence and movements. While the flag is\n   active, the Cipher gains enhanced combat information against the flagged\n   target.\n\n   Asset Flag is primarily a setup skill used before engaging a priority target.\n   The flagged designation improves the Cipher's accuracy and damage against\n   that specific opponent, reflecting the operational intelligence gathered on\n   the asset before engagement. The flag fades after a set duration or when the\n   Cipher flags a different target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
314	shelp_mindwall	-1	mindwall	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Mindwall\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 25\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage:\n   Wear-Off: !Mindwall!\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 22\nDescription:\n   Mindwall erects a psionic barrier within the caster's mind that\n   intercepts and diffuses incoming mental and magical attacks. For\n   level/5 rounds, applies a saving throw improvement against spells\n   (-level/4) and an armor class bonus (-level/8). Cannot be stacked.\n   The spell defense component makes this particularly valuable when\n   facing enemy spellcasters or psionic enemies. A fundamental defensive\n   spell for the Psionicist class.\n*******************************************************************************\n
302	shelp_ember_spark	-1	ember spark	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Ember Spark\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 8\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: ember spark\n   Wear-Off: !Ember Spark!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 1\nDescription:\n   Ember Spark is the first practical exercise in the Wizard's Keep curriculum\n   — a small, directed burst of Ember Canon fire. Producing it requires\n   controlled ignition: proof of will applied to elemental principle. The\n   Keep teaches this not as a weapon but as a demonstration of control.\n\n   Damage: 2d4 + level/4, fire elemental. A successful save halves damage.\n   Mana cost: 8. Available automatically at level 1.\n\n   As a Magi advances, Ember Spark is superseded by Magic Missile and the\n   deeper Ember Canon curriculum (Fireball, Wall of Fire, Lifesteal). It\n   remains the first fire the Magi ever commands.\n*******************************************************************************\n
303	shelp_punch	-1	punch	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Punch\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 1\n Wait Beats: 18\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: punch\n   Wear-Off: !Punch!\nAcquisition:\n   - Warden: level 5\nDescription:\n   Punch is a core warrior combo strike for steady melee damage and combo progression.\n*******************************************************************************\n
304	shelp_static	-1	static	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Static\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 40\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: discharge\n   Wear-Off: !static!\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 20\nDescription:\n   Static is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
305	shelp_mystical_focus	-1	mystical focus	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Mystical Focus\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 200\n Wait Beats: 10\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: Your lose your mystical focus.\nAcquisition:\n   - Wizard: level 45\n   - Egomancer: level 47\n   - Necromancer: level 48\n   - Sorcerer: level 55\nDescription:\n   Mystical Focus is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
306	shelp_dissolution	-1	dissolution	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Dissolution\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 20\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: dissolution\n   Wear-Off: !Dissolution!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 50\nDescription:\n   Dissolution is an advanced Magi offensive spell that channels raw arcane\n   entropy to dissolve the target's physical integrity. The spell projects\n   a stream of corrosive arcane energy that breaks down organic and inorganic\n   matter at the molecular level, causing severe acid-like damage as the\n   target's substance is literally dissolved.\n\n   Dissolution is one of the Magi's high-tier single-target offensive spells,\n   offering strong damage with no secondary effects. It is reliable in\n   situations where elemental immunities would reduce fire or ice spells'\n   effectiveness, as the dissolution energy bypasses conventional elemental\n   resistances by attacking the fundamental coherence of matter rather than\n   delivering thermal or kinetic force.\n*******************************************************************************\n
307	shelp_purify	-1	purify	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Purify\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 5\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: Purify\n   Wear-Off: !Purify!\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 19\nDescription:\n   Purify is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
308	shelp_identify	-1	identify	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Identify\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_OBJ_INV\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 12\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Identify!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 9\nDescription:\n   Identify Reveals detailed magical properties of an item, including enchantments and requirements.\n*******************************************************************************\n
309	shelp_poison_nightshade	-1	poison:nightshade	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Poison:nightshade\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 80\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Poison Nightshade\n   Wear-Off: @@N$nFeels much better!\nAcquisition:\n   - Nightblade: level 2\nDescription:\n   Poison:nightshade is a combat skill that attacks an enemy and deals poison-type physical or energy damage.\n*******************************************************************************\n
310	shelp_entangling_growth	-1	entangling growth	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: entangling growth\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n    HP Cost: 25\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: \nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 52\nDescription:\n   Snares target, reducing DEX by 4.\n*******************************************************************************\n
311	shelp_refuge	-1	refuge	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Refuge\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 75\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: The rainbow aura around your body fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Paladin: level 32\n   - Priest: level 32\nDescription:\n   Refuge is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
312	shelp_smash	-1	smash	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Smash\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !smash!\nAcquisition:\n   - Warden: level 30\nDescription:\n   Smash is a utility breaching skill used to force open closed or locked doors, trading finesse for immediate entry.\n*******************************************************************************\n
313	shelp_find_doors	-1	find doors	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Find Doors\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Find Doors!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cipher: level 16\nDescription:\n   Find Doors reveals hidden closed exits (without door keywords) when you look at room exits.\n*******************************************************************************\n
315	shelp_sleep	-1	sleep	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Sleep\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 15\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: You feel less tired.\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 9\nDescription:\n   Sleep is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
316	shelp_dissolution_protocol	-1	dissolution protocol	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Dissolution Protocol\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Dissolution Protocol!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cipher: level 38\nDescription:\n   Dissolution Protocol is the Cipher's advanced survival technique. When\n   activated, the operative executes a controlled collapse, appearing to all\n   observers as if they have been killed or incapacitated. The Cipher enters\n   a state of feigned death, removing themselves from combat entirely until\n   they choose to reengage.\n\n   While in this state the Cipher is ignored by enemies and ticks no combat\n   timers. The protocol is a calculated strategic withdrawal rather than an\n   actual retreat — the operative uses the brief window to assess the\n   situation, recover slightly, and choose the optimal moment to reveal\n   their continued presence. Enemies must be successfully deceived for the\n   protocol to take effect; highly aware opponents may see through the ruse.\n*******************************************************************************\n
317	shelp_sonic_blast	-1	sonic blast	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Sonic Blast\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 140\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Sonic Blast\n   Wear-Off: @@N$nFeels much better!\nAcquisition:\n   - Egomancer: level 67\nDescription:\n   Sonic Blast is an offensive spell that inflicts sonic damage on an enemy target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
318	shelp_rot	-1	rot	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: rot\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n    HP Cost: 40\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: rot\nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 75\nDescription:\n   Heavy poison nuke spell.\n*******************************************************************************\n
319	shelp_circle	-1	circle	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Circle\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 1\n Wait Beats: 18\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: circle\n   Wear-Off: !circle!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cipher: level 19\nDescription:\n   Circle is the in-combat rogue follow-up to backstab: a piercing flank strike that can be used mid-fight and can consume active poisons for bonus damage.\n*******************************************************************************\n
320	shelp_suffocate	-1	suffocate	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Suffocate\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 30\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: a choking hand\n   Wear-Off: !Suffocate!\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 46\nDescription:\n   Suffocate is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
321	shelp_cloak_oathbreaker	-1	cloak:oathbreaker	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Cloak:oathbreaker\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 550\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: @@NThe @@dcloak@@N around your body fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Warlock: level 48\nDescription:\n   Cloak:oathbreaker is the Warlock's signature remort cloak. It shrouds the\n   caster in dark, oath-defying energy that grants a chance to completely\n   avoid incoming magical (spell) damage.\n\n   When the caster would take non-physical damage that does not have\n   NO_REFLECT or NO_ABSORB flags, there is a pseudo_level / 10 percent chance\n   that the cloak shatters the incoming magic harmlessly. For example, at\n   pseudo-level 100, there is a 10% chance to avoid each spell hit entirely.\n\n   The cloak does not protect against physical damage. For physical avoidance,\n   see cloak:transcendence (Assassin).\n\n   Duration scales with pseudo-level (pseudo_level / 8 rounds).\n*******************************************************************************\n
322	shelp_seam_snare	-1	seam snare	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Seam Snare\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Seam Snare!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cipher: level 35\nDescription:\n   Seam Snare is an advanced trap-setting technique unique to the Cipher.\n   The operative exploits structural seams — gaps between surfaces, cracks\n   in floors, doorway thresholds — to place a nearly invisible snare that\n   triggers when an opponent passes through. The snare entangles the target,\n   immobilizing them briefly and leaving them vulnerable to attack.\n\n   Unlike conventional traps, the Seam Snare is placed with such precision\n   that it is extremely difficult to detect. The snare material is threaded\n   through existing environmental gaps, meaning it leaves no visible\n   apparatus. The Cipher can then position themselves for an ambush or simply\n   use the immobilization to create distance if they need to escape. The\n   snare can only catch one target before it must be re-set.\n*******************************************************************************\n
323	shelp_vigil_strike	-1	vigil strike	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Vigil Strike\n       Kind: Skill (active combat)\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 1\n Wait Beats: 18\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: vigil strike\n   Wear-Off: !Vigil Strike!\nAcquisition:\n   - Sentinel: level 1\nDescription:\n   Vigil Strike is the Sentinel's foundational combat technique: a deliberate\n   blow delivered from a watched position. The Sentinel sees the opening\n   before they take it. This is not a reactive attack — it is a strike made\n   from a posture of sustained observation, placed at the moment the\n   practitioner has already identified.\n\n   Damage is calculated from pseudo-level and Strength (war_attack helper,\n   same as Warden melee skills). The Sentinel shares a physical combat\n   foundation with the Warden tradition, though the doctrinal emphasis\n   differs: where a Warden holds ground, a Sentinel watches it.\n\n   Syntax: vigil strike <target>\n   Requires POS_FIGHTING. Can be practiced to improve hit rate.\n*******************************************************************************\n
324	shelp_peripheral_extension	-1	peripheral extension	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Peripheral Extension\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 17\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: Your peripheral awareness returns to its normal range.\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 19\nDescription:\n   Peripheral Extension is a Psionicist sensory enhancement spell. The\n   psionicist expands the range of their psionic perception beyond normal\n   physiological limits, effectively granting enhanced night vision and\n   improved peripheral awareness. The caster can see clearly in darkness\n   and has a wider effective field of view.\n\n   This is the Psionicist's version of infravision, derived from psionic\n   amplification of sensory processing rather than enhanced biological\n   heat detection. The extended peripheral awareness also improves the\n   Psionicist's ability to detect hidden enemies approaching from the sides\n   or behind, making them harder to surprise during combat. The spell is\n   particularly valuable in dungeon environments with limited lighting.\n*******************************************************************************\n
325	shelp_detect_hidden	-1	detect hidden	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Detect Hidden\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 5\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: You feel less aware of your suroundings.\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 16\n   - Magi: level 17\nDescription:\n   Detect Hidden is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
326	shelp_cure_blindness	-1	cure blindness	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Cure Blindness\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 5\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Cure Blindness!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 28\nDescription:\n   Cure Blindness is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
327	shelp_energy_drain	-1	energy drain	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Energy Drain\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 12\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: energy drain\n   Wear-Off: !Energy Drain!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 7\n   - Cipher: level 8\n   - Psionicist: level 9\n   - Warden: level 11\n   - Pugilist: level 13\n   - Magi: level 15\nDescription:\n   Energy Drain is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
328	shelp_dual_fist	-1	dual fist	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Dual Fist\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Dual Fist!\nAcquisition:\n   - Monk: level 35\n   - Brawler: level 35\nDescription:\n   Dual Fist allows you to dual-wield fist weapons in both hands.\n*******************************************************************************\n
329	shelp_cloak_elements	-1	cloak:elements	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Cloak:elements\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 750\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: @@NThe @@lcloak@@N around your body fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Wizard: level 48\nDescription:\n   Cloak:elements is the Wizard's signature remort cloak. It surrounds the\n   caster in a crackling aura of raw elemental power. When the caster takes\n   non-physical (spell) damage, the cloak lashes back and reflects 15% of the\n   incoming damage at the attacker as water-element damage.\n\n   The reflected damage bypasses reflection and absorption effects (it carries\n   NO_REFLECT and NO_ABSORB flags). The cloak only triggers against non-\n   physical damage that does not already have NO_REFLECT or NO_ABSORB set --\n   physical attacks do not activate it.\n\n   For a similar effect against physical damage, see cloak:flaming (Sorcerer).\n\n   Duration scales with pseudo-level (pseudo_level / 8 rounds).\n*******************************************************************************\n
330	shelp_weapon_bond	-1	weapon bond	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Weapon Bond\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Weapon Bond!\nAcquisition:\n   - Swordmaster: level 1\nDescription:\n   Weapon Bond is the foundational passive skill of the Swordmaster class.\n   From the moment of their initiation, Swordmasters form a deep kinesthetic\n   bond with their weapon, treating it as an extension of their body rather\n   than a tool. This bond improves all aspects of their swordsmanship:\n   accuracy, damage, critical rate, and fluidity of technique all benefit\n   from the bond's presence.\n\n   The bond is forged through thousands of hours of dedicated practice with\n   a single weapon type. A Swordmaster who fights without their bonded\n   weapon type fights at reduced effectiveness. Weapon Bond scales with\n   level, meaning senior Swordmasters have a deeper, more powerful bond than\n   novices. It is always active and cannot be suppressed by normal magical\n   means.\n*******************************************************************************\n
331	shelp_sanctuary	-1	sanctuary	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Sanctuary\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 75\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: The white aura around your body fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 70\nDescription:\n   Sanctuary is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
332	shelp_jackals_verdict	-1	jackal's verdict	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Jackal's Verdict\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 15\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: jackal's verdict\n   Wear-Off: !Jackal's Verdict!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 78\nDescription:\n   Jackal's Verdict is a high-level Cleric area-effect divine offensive\n   spell. Named for the jackal — divine herald of death and transition in\n   the Disk theology — the spell invokes the god's judgment against all\n   enemies present, dealing holy damage to every hostile target in the room.\n\n   The jackal aspect of Disk governs the transition between life and death,\n   and this spell channels that transitory force as a weapon. It is the\n   Cleric's signature high-level AoE divine blast, available at a later\n   tier than Disk's Word and dealing a different flavor of divine damage.\n   Jackal's Verdict is particularly devastating against undead and unholy\n   creatures, who are especially vulnerable to the divine transitional energy\n   the spell channels.\n*******************************************************************************\n
333	shelp_cloak_iron	-1	cloak:iron	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Cloak:iron\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 550\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: @@NThe @@Wcloak@@N around your body fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Knight: level 48\nDescription:\n   Cloak:iron is the Knight's signature remort cloak. It encases the caster\n   in an aura of hardened iron, providing a flat reduction to all incoming\n   physical damage. The reduction amount is equal to pseudo_level / 2.\n\n   For example, at pseudo-level 100, every physical hit against the Knight\n   is reduced by 50 damage. This reduction is applied before other damage\n   modifiers such as sanctuary or elemental resistance.\n\n   The cloak does not affect non-physical (magical) damage. For magical\n   damage reduction, see cloak:mental (Monk).\n\n   Duration scales with pseudo-level (pseudo_level / 8 rounds).\n*******************************************************************************\n
334	shelp_cleave	-1	cleave	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Cleave\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: cleave\n   Wear-Off: !Cleave!\nAcquisition:\n   - Warden: level 25\nDescription:\n   Cleave executes a wide sweeping weapon strike that hits all NPCs in the\n   room currently engaged in combat with the Warden. Each target is struck\n   once for physical damage. The broad swing doubles the normal wait time\n   (48 beats total) due to the effort required. Ideal for crowd control\n   when surrounded by multiple enemies. Has no effect if only one opponent\n   is engaged.\n*******************************************************************************\n
335	shelp_upheaval	-1	upheaval	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: upheaval\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n    HP Cost: 50\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: upheaval\nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 85\nDescription:\n   Major area earth damage from the earth rising in fury.\n*******************************************************************************\n
336	shelp_frenzy	-1	frenzy	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Frenzy\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: frenzy\n   Wear-Off: !FRENZY!\nAcquisition:\n   - Knight: level 27\n   - Swordsman: level 28\n   - Priest: level 41\nDescription:\n   Frenzy is an area melee finisher that sends you into an aggressive burst, attempting attacks against multiple nearby enemies in the room.\n*******************************************************************************\n
337	shelp_arc_lightning	-1	arc lightning	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Arc Lightning\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 120\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: arc lightning\n   Wear-Off: !arc lightning!\nAcquisition:\n   - Wizard: level 30\nDescription:\n   Arc Lightning is an offensive spell that deals air elemental damage to an enemy target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
338	shelp_checkpoint_break	-1	checkpoint break	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Checkpoint Break\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 1\n Wait Beats: 18\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: checkpoint break\n   Wear-Off: !Checkpoint Break!\nAcquisition:\n   - Warden: level 6\nDescription:\n   Checkpoint Break is a fundamental Warden offensive technique. The warrior\n   drives a powerful headbutt or shoulder charge into the opponent, targeting\n   their guard and breaking through their defensive positioning. The attack\n   deals physical damage and can momentarily stagger the target.\n\n   As the Warden's earliest active combat skill, Checkpoint Break serves as\n   a bread-and-butter melee attack that supplements regular weapon strikes.\n   The blow is forceful enough to interrupt spellcasting when it connects,\n   making it valuable against caster opponents. The technique requires the\n   Warden to commit to a forward rush, leaving them briefly vulnerable if\n   the attack misses.\n*******************************************************************************\n
339	shelp_natures_ward	-1	natures ward	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: natures ward\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n    HP Cost: 25\n Wait Beats: 24\n  Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: \nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 55\nDescription:\n   Grants resistance to poison and earth damage.\n*******************************************************************************\n
340	shelp_enhanced_critical	-1	enhanced critical	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Enhanced Critical\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Enhanced Crit!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cipher: level 20\nDescription:\n   Enhanced Critical passively increases physical critical hit chance and critical damage.\n*******************************************************************************\n
341	shelp_hellspawn	-1	hellspawn	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Hellspawn\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 50\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: HellSpawn\n   Wear-Off: !Hellspawn!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 43\nDescription:\n   Hellspawn is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
342	shelp_shocking_grasp	-1	shocking grasp	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Shocking Grasp\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 15\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: shocking grasp\n   Wear-Off: !Shocking Grasp!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 5\nDescription:\n   Shocking Grasp is an offensive spell that inflicts lightning damage on an enemy target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
355	shelp_room_dispel	-1	room dispel	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Room Dispel\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 120\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: None\nAcquisition:\n   - Sorcerer: level 22\n   - Wizard: level 22\n   - Necromancer: level 34\n   - Egomancer: level 34\nDescription:\n   Room Dispel Disrupts active room-wide magical effects in the current room, such as persistent field spells.\n*******************************************************************************\n
343	shelp_fireshield	-1	fireshield	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Fireshield\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 400\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: None\nAcquisition:\n   - Sorcerer: level 80\n   - Wizard: level 80\nDescription:\n   Fireshield surrounds the caster in a blazing shield of flame. It is the\n   most aggressive of the magic shields, dealing significant reactive fire\n   damage to any attacker while also absorbing a portion of incoming damage.\n\n   Shield properties:\n     - Type: FLAME_SHIELD (cannot stack with other non-coexisting shields)\n     - Reactive Damage: 30% of incoming damage dealt back as fire damage\n     - Absorption: 10% + (pseudo_level / 10)% of incoming damage absorbed\n     - Hit Points: 5,000 + (pseudo_level * 10) -- shield breaks when depleted\n     - Duration: pseudo_level / 10 rounds (halved on login)\n\n   The reactive fire damage bypasses cloak reflection and absorption effects.\n   Only one non-coexisting shield may be active at a time (fireshield,\n   shockshield, etc). Iceshield and arcaneshield may coexist with it.\n*******************************************************************************\n
344	shelp_psychic_thrust	-1	psychic thrust	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Psychic Thrust\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 22\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: psychic thrust\n   Wear-Off: !Physic Thrust!\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 7\nDescription:\n   Psychic Thrust is an offensive spell that inflicts psychic damage on an enemy target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
345	shelp_mend_wounds	-1	mend wounds	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: mend wounds\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n    HP Cost: 12\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: \nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 12\nDescription:\n   Moderate target heal (25-45 HP).\n*******************************************************************************\n
346	shelp_unit_tactics	-1	unit tactics	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Unit Tactics\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: Unit Tactics\n   Wear-Off: !Unit Tactics!\nAcquisition:\n   - Knight: level 16\n   - Swordsman: level 16\nDescription:\n   Unit Tactics is a command-and-control passive that increases how many charmed followers you can maintain, improving summon/charm group capacity.\n*******************************************************************************\n
