348	shelp_roothold	-1	roothold	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: roothold\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n    HP Cost: 12\n Wait Beats: 24\n  Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: \nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 9\nDescription:\n   Prevents being forced to flee.\n*******************************************************************************\n
349	shelp_travel	-1	travel	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Travel\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 50\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Travel!\nAcquisition:\n   - Not learnable by player classes.\nDescription:\n   Travel is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
350	shelp_know_critical	-1	know critical	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Know Critical\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 15\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: You are less aware of critical damage points.\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 28\nDescription:\n   Know Critical is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
351	shelp_feint	-1	feint	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Feint\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 18\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage:\n   Wear-Off: Your feint bonus fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Pugilist: level 25\nDescription:\n   Feint sacrifices the current round's attack to set up a powerful\n   follow-through. The Pugilist forgoes their immediate action (one\n   PULSE_VIOLENCE wait) but gains a hit roll bonus (Pugilist level/4 + 3)\n   and an armor class improvement (-Pugilist level/5) for the next 2\n   rounds. Best used as a setup move before a high-value strike like\n   Pressure Point or Choke Hold to ensure the follow-up lands cleanly.\n*******************************************************************************\n
352	shelp_refresh_mana	-1	refresh mana	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Refresh Mana\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 12\n Wait Beats: 18\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: refresh mana\n   Wear-Off: !Refresh mana!\nAcquisition:\n   - Not learnable by player classes.\nDescription:\n   Refresh Mana is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
353	shelp_water_elemental	-1	water elemental	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Water Elemental\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 80\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Stalker!\nAcquisition:\n   - Sorcerer: level 6\n   - Wizard: level 6\nDescription:\n   Water Elemental Summons a water elemental ally that fights alongside the caster.\n*******************************************************************************\n
354	shelp_locate_object	-1	locate object	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Locate Object\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 20\n Wait Beats: 18\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Locate Object!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 16\n   - Cleric: level 30\nDescription:\n   Locate Object Searches for a named object and reveals where it can be found if it is within the spell's reach.\n*******************************************************************************\n
356	shelp_fungal_eruption	-1	fungal eruption	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: fungal eruption\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n    HP Cost: 30\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: fungal eruption\nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 55\nDescription:\n   Area poison damage from erupting fungi.\n*******************************************************************************\n
357	shelp_phantomfist	-1	phantomfist	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Phantomfist\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 80\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Phantomfist (bugged)\n   Wear-Off: You no longer move like a phantom\nAcquisition:\n   - Brawler: level 34\n   - Monk: level 51\nDescription:\n   Phantomfist is a chi focus technique that increases your speed for a short duration and helps set up faster offensive tempo.\n*******************************************************************************\n
358	shelp_mass_invis	-1	mass invis	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Mass Invis\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 20\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Mass Invis!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 60\nDescription:\n   Mass Invis Makes the caster's group invisible, enabling coordinated stealth movement.\n*******************************************************************************\n
359	shelp_consecrate	-1	consecrate	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Consecrate\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 50\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage:\n   Wear-Off: !Consecrate!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 35\nDescription:\n   Consecrate channels divine power into the ground. Its effect depends\n   on those present in the room: evil NPCs (alignment < -200) are struck\n   for holy damage (2d(level/4)) from the sanctified earth, while grouped\n   allies receive a combat blessing granting a hit roll bonus (level/10)\n   and armor class improvement (-level/10) for 12 hours. Cannot be stacked\n   on allies. A versatile support spell that provides both offensive and\n   defensive utility in a single cast.\n*******************************************************************************\n
360	shelp_spore_cloud	-1	spore cloud	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: spore cloud\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n    HP Cost: 18\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: \nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 30\nDescription:\n   Blinds the target with a cloud of spores.\n*******************************************************************************\n
361	shelp_cognitive_fault	-1	cognitive fault	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Cognitive Fault\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Cognitive Fault!\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 20\nDescription:\n   Cognitive Fault is a passive mental discipline that enhances the\n   Psionicist's ability to strike critical vulnerabilities in an opponent's\n   mind. Through deep training, the Psionicist learns to recognize the subtle\n   cognitive fault lines in an adversary's mental architecture, directing\n   psionic attacks with greater precision.\n\n   This passive skill increases the critical strike rate of the Psionicist's\n   spells, allowing psionic attacks to deal significantly amplified damage\n   when those fault lines are exploited. The damage bonus on critical strikes\n   is also improved, reflecting the cascading psychological damage caused when\n   the attack penetrates the deepest layers of the target's consciousness.\n*******************************************************************************\n
362	shelp_gap_transit	-1	gap transit	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Gap Transit\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage:\n   Wear-Off: !Gap Transit!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cipher: level 45\nDescription:\n   Gap Transit allows the Cipher to instantly move to an adjacent room in\n   the specified direction (north, east, south, west, up, down) without\n   triggering normal movement delays or aggro checks. Cannot be used while\n   in combat. The technique exploits seams between mapped routes — gaps\n   that exist in every system of control — making it ideal for\n   repositioning or pursuing fleeing targets.\n   Syntax: gap transit <direction>\n*******************************************************************************\n
363	shelp_thornlash	-1	thornlash	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: thornlash\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n    HP Cost: 12\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: thornlash\nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 3\nDescription:\n   Lashes enemy with thorny vines for earth damage.\n*******************************************************************************\n
364	shelp_rune_fire	-1	rune:fire	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Rune:fire\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 150\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: The rune dissipates.\nAcquisition:\n   - Sorcerer: level 40\n   - Wizard: level 40\nDescription:\n   Rune:fire Places a fire rune trap that explodes into flame when triggered.\n*******************************************************************************\n
365	shelp_quake	-1	quake	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: quake\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n    HP Cost: 30\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: quake\nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 60\nDescription:\n   Area earth damage from a devastating earthquake.\n*******************************************************************************\n
375	shelp_valor_crit	-1	valor_crit	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Valor Crit\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: Your righteous fury fades.\nAcquisition:\n   None (internal affect holder)\nDescription:\n   Valor Crit is an internal affect holder associated with the Cloak:Valor\n   ability used by Paladins. It tracks and applies the guaranteed critical\n   strike proc that Cloak:Valor periodically grants. When this affect is\n   active, the Paladin's next attack is guaranteed to critically strike.\n\n   This is not a castable ability. The affect is applied automatically by\n   the Cloak:Valor system when its proc condition is met. Staff may see\n   this affect on players who have Cloak:Valor active and have accumulated\n   sufficient righteous fury charges. The wear-off message "Your righteous\n   fury fades" indicates that the guaranteed critical window has passed\n   without being consumed.\n*******************************************************************************\n
366	shelp_cloak_precision	-1	cloak:precision	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Cloak:precision\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 550\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: @@NThe @@ycloak@@N around your body fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Swordsman: level 48\nDescription:\n   Cloak:precision is the Swordsman's signature remort cloak. Rather than\n   providing damage reduction or avoidance like other cloaks, it instead\n   reduces the effectiveness of critical hits against the Swordsman.\n\n   The cloak provides two benefits:\n     - Critical Chance Reduction: Enemies' critical hit chance against the\n       Swordsman is reduced by pseudo_level / 5 percentage points. At\n       pseudo-level 100, this is a 20% reduction in crit chance.\n     - Critical Damage Reduction: When an enemy does land a critical hit,\n       the bonus critical damage is reduced by 25%.\n\n   Both effects apply to physical and spell criticals alike. This makes the\n   Swordsman exceptionally resilient against burst damage from critical\n   strikes.\n\n   Duration scales with pseudo-level (pseudo_level / 8 rounds).\n*******************************************************************************\n
367	shelp_cloak_reflection	-1	cloak:reflection	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Cloak:reflection\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 500\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: @@NThe @@lc@@el@@ro@@ya@@ak@@N around your body fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Not learnable by player classes.\nDescription:\n   Cloak:reflection surrounds the caster in a shimmering, multi-hued cloak\n   that has a chance to reflect offensive spells back at the original caster.\n   When a spell hits the caster, there is a (pseudo_level - 70) percent\n   chance that the cloak will reflect the spell, dealing its full damage back\n   to the attacker instead.\n\n   The cloak only triggers against offensive targeted spells\n   (TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE) and does not activate if the caster is targeting\n   themselves. Reflected spells deal their original damage to the attacker.\n\n   Duration scales with pseudo-level (pseudo_level / 8 rounds).\n*******************************************************************************\n
368	shelp_ninth_descent	-1	ninth descent	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Ninth Descent\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 25\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: Your heightened awareness fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Sentinel: level 35\nDescription:\n   Ninth Descent is an advanced Sentinel awareness technique named for the\n   ninth and deepest level of the Pale Ledger's observational hierarchy. The\n   Sentinel enters a heightened state of perceptual acuity, processing the\n   flow of combat at an accelerated rate. For a brief window, the Sentinel\n   can perceive openings and threats before they fully materialize.\n\n   While active, Ninth Descent improves the Sentinel's dodge and parry rates\n   significantly, as their enhanced perception allows them to anticipate\n   attacks before they land. The technique also amplifies the damage of any\n   counter-attacks made during this window, as the Sentinel can direct their\n   responses to precisely targeted weak points. The heightened state is\n   mentally taxing and cannot be sustained indefinitely.\n*******************************************************************************\n
369	shelp_nodisarm	-1	nodisarm	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Nodisarm\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !nodisarm!\nAcquisition:\n   - Warden: level 30\n   - Cipher: level 40\nDescription:\n   Nodisarm gives you resistance against disarm attempts.\n*******************************************************************************\n
370	shelp_reach_remedy	-1	reach remedy	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Reach Remedy\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: reach remedy\n   Wear-Off: !Reach Remedy!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cipher: level 27\nDescription:\n   Reach Remedy is a Cipher field medicine technique. The operative has\n   trained to rapidly neutralize toxins and poisons using a compact kit of\n   antidotes always kept within easy reach. When deployed, the Reach Remedy\n   removes poison effects from the Cipher without requiring them to leave\n   combat or seek outside assistance.\n\n   The technique reflects the Cipher's professional preparation for\n   operating in environments where they may be subjected to poisons —\n   whether from enemy casters, trapped objects, or poisoned weapons. The\n   remedies are applied rapidly enough that the Cipher can detoxify\n   mid-combat. More advanced toxins may require a full dose of the kit\n   and cannot be countered by partial application.\n*******************************************************************************\n
371	shelp_heal	-1	heal	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Heal\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 50\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Heal!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 5\nDescription:\n   Heal is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
372	shelp_blight_touch	-1	blight touch	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: blight touch\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n    HP Cost: 20\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: blight touch\nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 25\nDescription:\n   Poison damage with a damage-over-time effect.\n*******************************************************************************\n
373	shelp_creature_bond	-1	creature bond	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Creature Bond\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 100\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: None\nAcquisition:\n   - Necromancer: level 55\n   - Wizard: level 60\n   - Sorcerer: level 77\nDescription:\n   Creature Bond is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
374	shelp_corrupt_bond	-1	corrupt bond	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Corrupt Bond\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 100\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: None\nAcquisition:\n   - Necromancer: level 33\n   - Egomancer: level 50\nDescription:\n   Corrupt Bond is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
376	shelp_infravision	-1	infravision	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Infravision\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 5\n Wait Beats: 18\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: You no longer see in the dark.\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 20\nDescription:\n   Infravision is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
377	shelp_primal_restoration	-1	primal restoration	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: primal restoration\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n    HP Cost: 35\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: \nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 70\nDescription:\n   Large heal plus cure poison, blindness, and curse.\n*******************************************************************************\n
378	shelp_detection	-1	detection	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Detection\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 12\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Detection!\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 22\nDescription:\n   Detection Heightens magical perception so hidden presences, illusions, or magical disturbances are easier to notice.\n*******************************************************************************\n
379	shelp_rootway	-1	rootway	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: rootway\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n    HP Cost: 30\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: \nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 58\nDescription:\n   Teleports to a random location via root network.\n*******************************************************************************\n
380	shelp_condemn	-1	condemn	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Condemn\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 15\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: The weight of condemnation lifts from you.\nAcquisition:\n   - Sentinel: level 45\nDescription:\n   Condemn is the Sentinel's highest judgment technique. The warrior formally\n   condemns the target, invoking the Pale Ledger's authority to mark them as\n   a declared enemy. The condemned target suffers a persistent debuff that\n   reduces all their combat stats, representing the psychological and\n   metaphysical weight of being formally condemned.\n\n   While Condemned, the target takes increased damage from Sentinel attacks\n   and has reduced effectiveness in all combat actions. The effect of Condemn\n   is difficult to remove, as it represents a formal ruling rather than a\n   temporary magical effect. Condemn is most powerful as a sustained pressure\n   tool in lengthy battles where the cumulative debuff significantly shifts\n   the balance of combat.\n*******************************************************************************\n
381	shelp_applied_understanding	-1	applied understanding	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Applied Understanding\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 1\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: applied understanding\n   Wear-Off: !Applied Understanding!\nAcquisition:\n   - Pugilist: level 35\nDescription:\n   Applied Understanding strikes a vital nerve cluster using Interior\n   Forms knowledge — the Pugilist tradition's doctrine that the body's\n   systems can be interrupted at precise junctions. The effect applied\n   is chosen randomly each use from three possibilities: a Strength\n   debuff (-level/6), a Dexterity debuff (-level/6), or a damage roll\n   reduction (-level/5). All effects last 3 rounds. Useful for hampering\n   powerful melee opponents or weakening spellcasters who rely on stats.\n   Deals 1d(level/4 + 1) physical damage.\n*******************************************************************************\n
382	shelp_poison_weapon	-1	poison weapon	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Poison Weapon\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_OBJ_INV\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 100\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Enchant Weapon!\nAcquisition:\n   - Warlock: level 5\n   - Assassin: level 25\nDescription:\n   Poison Weapon Coats a weapon with venom so successful hits can poison enemies.\n*******************************************************************************\n
383	shelp_earth_shatter	-1	earth shatter	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Earth Shatter\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 100\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Earth Shatter\n   Wear-Off: !Earth Shatter!\nAcquisition:\n   - Sorcerer: level 60\nDescription:\n   Earth Shatter is an offensive spell that inflicts earth damage on an enemy target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
384	shelp_pick_lock	-1	pick lock	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Pick Lock\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Pick!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cipher: level 25\nDescription:\n   Pick Lock allows you to unlock lockable doors and containers without keys.\n*******************************************************************************\n
385	shelp_lightning_bolt	-1	lightning bolt	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Lightning Bolt\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 15\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: lightning bolt\n   Wear-Off: !Lightning Bolt!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 24\nDescription:\n   Lightning Bolt is an offensive spell that inflicts lightning damage on an enemy target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
386	shelp_phoenix_flare	-1	phoenix flare	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Phoenix Flare\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 120\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: phoenix flare\n   Wear-Off: !phoenix flare!\nAcquisition:\n   - Wizard: level 60\nDescription:\n   Phoenix Flare is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
387	shelp_gap_hold	-1	gap hold	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Gap Hold\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Gap Hold!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cipher: level 8\nDescription:\n   Gap Hold is a foundational concealment technique for the Cipher. The\n   operative identifies a tactical gap — a blind spot, shadow, or structural\n   feature of the environment — and uses it to maintain a concealed position\n   without full stealth movement. Unlike active sneak, Gap Hold is a passive\n   ability that allows the Cipher to remain hidden while stationary.\n\n   The technique is most effective in complex terrain where environmental\n   features provide natural cover. A Cipher using Gap Hold can observe\n   enemies without being observed themselves, setting up ambushes or\n   gathering information before engaging. The hold breaks if the Cipher\n   moves or takes any aggressive action.\n*******************************************************************************\n
388	shelp_hide	-1	hide	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Hide\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_RESTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Hide!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cipher: level 12\nDescription:\n   Hide is a tactical skill focused on stealth, positioning, or information advantage.\n*******************************************************************************\n
389	shelp_martial_arts	-1	martial arts	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Martial Arts\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 0\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Martial Arts!\nAcquisition:\n   - Pugilist: level 10\nDescription:\n   Martial Arts unlocks unarmed martial strikes and provides extra damage for martial attacks.\n*******************************************************************************\n
390	shelp_nettlesting	-1	nettlesting	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: nettlesting\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n    HP Cost: 12\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: nettlesting\nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 6\nDescription:\n   Stinging nettles erupt to poison the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
391	shelp_cure_critical	-1	cure critical	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Cure Critical\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 20\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Cure Critical!\nAcquisition:\n   - Not learnable by player classes.\nDescription:\n   Cure Critical is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
392	shelp_tremor	-1	tremor	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: tremor\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n    HP Cost: 20\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: tremor\nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 32\nDescription:\n   The earth trembles for heavy earth damage.\n*******************************************************************************\n
393	shelp_prism_mark	-1	prism mark	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Prism Mark\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 5\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: prism mark\n   Wear-Off: The crystal outline around you fractures and fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 3\nDescription:\n   Prism Mark is the Magi's first defensive utility spell. The caster marks\n   a target — typically themselves — with a glittering crystalline outline\n   of magical energy. The mark provides a small absorption shield that\n   intercepts a portion of incoming damage before the target's health is\n   reduced.\n\n   Prism Mark is the Magi's earliest access to magical protection, available\n   at the very beginning of their career. While the absorption value is\n   modest compared to later shields, it provides meaningful damage mitigation\n   at low levels where every point of absorption matters. The crystal outline\n   shatters and fades when fully depleted, indicating the mark has been\n   consumed by absorbed damage.\n*******************************************************************************\n
394	shelp_backstab	-1	backstab	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Backstab\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 1\n Wait Beats: 18\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: backstab\n   Wear-Off: !Backstab!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cipher: level 10\nDescription:\n   Backstab is a precision dagger strike that opens from stealth or advantage, delivering high burst damage and consuming applied rogue poisons for extra effects.\n*******************************************************************************\n
395	shelp_cloak_misery	-1	cloak:misery	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Cloak:misery\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 550\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: @@NThe @@Rcloak@@N around your body fades.\nAcquisition:\n   - Necromancer: level 73\n   - Egomancer: level 73\n   - Assassin: level 80\n   - Warlock: level 80\nDescription:\n   Cloak:misery is a shared higher-level cloak available to several remort\n   classes. It wraps the caster in a dark aura of suffering. When the caster\n   is struck in combat, there is a 35% chance the cloak will activate and\n   shroud the attacker in misery.\n\n   The effect applies a short curse to the attacker (1 round duration):\n     - Hitroll: -1\n     - Damroll: -1\n     - AC: -5\n\n   While the individual debuffs are small, they can stack with repeated\n   procs, steadily weakening an opponent over a prolonged fight.\n\n   Duration scales with pseudo-level (pseudo_level / 8 rounds).\n*******************************************************************************\n
396	shelp_creeping_rot	-1	creeping rot	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: creeping rot\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n    HP Cost: 22\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: creeping rot\nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 38\nDescription:\n   Poison DoT that reduces healing effectiveness.\n*******************************************************************************\n
397	shelp_deflect_weapon	-1	deflect weapon	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Deflect Weapon\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 25\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: Your mind shield melts away.\nAcquisition:\n   - Necromancer: level 22\n   - Egomancer: level 22\nDescription:\n   Deflect Weapon is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
398	shelp_recurrence_loop	-1	recurrence loop	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Recurrence Loop\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 40\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: recurrence loop\n   Wear-Off: !Recurrence Loop!\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 35\nDescription:\n   Recurrence Loop is a Psionicist offensive area spell. The caster\n   establishes a recursive psionic feedback pattern that bounces between\n   all enemies in the room, dealing psychic damage to each target it hits\n   before looping back and repeating. The loop strikes multiple times,\n   accumulating damage with each recurrence.\n\n   The recurrence effect makes this spell valuable in fights with multiple\n   opponents, as the looping damage can strike each enemy several times in\n   a single casting. The number of loops and the intensity of each pass\n   scales with the Psionicist's level and psionic power. The loop eventually\n   dissipates when the feedback energy is fully expended, but a well-timed\n   Recurrence Loop can deal enormous total damage spread across an entire\n   enemy group.\n*******************************************************************************\n
399	shelp_elemental_shock	-1	elemental shock	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Elemental Shock\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 120\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: elemental shock\n   Wear-Off: !elemental shock!\nAcquisition:\n   - Grand Magi: level 5\nDescription:\n   Elemental Shock is an offensive spell that inflicts lightning damage on an enemy target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
400	shelp_elemental_deluge	-1	elemental deluge	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Elemental Deluge\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 120\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: elemental deluge\n   Wear-Off: !elemental deluge!\nAcquisition:\n   - Grand Magi: level 10\nDescription:\n   Elemental Deluge is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
401	shelp_emotion_control	-1	emotion control	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Emotion Control\n       Kind: Skill\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 0\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: emotion control\n   Wear-Off: !EMOTION CONTROL!\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 75\nDescription:\n   Emotion Control is a passive alignment-control discipline that reduces how much killing alters your alignment, helping maintain your intended moral path over time.\n*******************************************************************************\n
402	shelp_passage	-1	passage	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: passage\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_SELF\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n    HP Cost: 12\n Wait Beats: 12\n  Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: \nAcquisition:\n   - Druid: level 24\nDescription:\n   Allows passing through doors. Like pass door.\n*******************************************************************************\n
403	shelp_retributive_strike	-1	retributive strike	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Retributive Strike\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_IGNORE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 800\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: Retributive strike\n   Wear-Off: !Retributive Strike!\nAcquisition:\n   - Sorcerer: level 72\n   - Wizard: level 72\n   - Necromancer: level 78\n   - Egomancer: level 78\nDescription:\n   Retributive Strike Places a retaliatory holy effect that punishes attackers when they strike the protected target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
404	shelp_fireball	-1	fireball	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Fireball\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 15\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: fireball\n   Wear-Off: !Fireball!\nAcquisition:\n   - Magi: level 28\nDescription:\n   Fireball is an offensive spell that inflicts fire damage on an enemy target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
405	shelp_exorcism	-1	exorcism	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Exorcism\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 25\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: TRUE\nNoun Damage: exorcism\n   Wear-Off: !Exorcism!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 55\nDescription:\n   Exorcism is the Cleric's most powerful targeted holy spell, unleashing\n   righteous divine wrath on a single target. Base damage is 3d(level/3)\n   holy elemental. Against evil targets (alignment < -200), damage is\n   tripled, making it catastrophically effective against undead, demons,\n   and other dark creatures. Less effective against neutral or good-aligned\n   targets. A high-level spell that rewards specialization against evil\n   enemies and areas.\n*******************************************************************************\n
406	shelp_enhance_weapon	-1	enhance weapon	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Enhance Weapon\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_OBJ_INV\n   Position: POS_STANDING\n   Min Mana: 50\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Enhance Weapon!\nAcquisition:\n   - Not learnable by player classes.\nDescription:\n   Enhance Weapon Greatly enhances a weapon with magical bonuses beyond basic enchantment.\n*******************************************************************************\n
407	shelp_cure_poison	-1	cure poison	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Cure Poison\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_DEFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 5\n Wait Beats: 12\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: None\n   Wear-Off: !Cure Poison!\nAcquisition:\n   - Cleric: level 32\nDescription:\n   Cure Poison is a protective/support spell that strengthens, restores, or safeguards the target.\n*******************************************************************************\n
408	shelp_phobia	-1	phobia	*******************************************************************************\n       Name: Phobia\n       Kind: Spell\n     Target: TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE\n   Position: POS_FIGHTING\n   Min Mana: 32\n Wait Beats: 24\n Can Learn: FALSE\nNoun Damage: phobia attack\n   Wear-Off: !phobia!\nAcquisition:\n   - Psionicist: level 10\nDescription:\n   Phobia is an offensive spell used to damage an enemy target with direct magic.\n*******************************************************************************\n
